a|cash} come from and go?* (**liquidity and solvency**)","5. **Notes**: accounting policies, judgements and details. *How were the numbers made?*","! The statement of cash flows is about **liquidity and solvency**, not profitability (that’s P&L) and not gearing (that’s the balance sheet)."],"id":"rule-1lm9ul","sect":3,"part":"The complete set of statements"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"statements","lo":1,"title":"Five statements, five questions","intro":"Each statement answers one question. Learn the pairs and the “role of the statement” MCQs are free marks.","notes":{"sfp":"{a|Assets}, {l|liabilities} and {e|equity} at one date.","pl":"{i|Income} and {x|expenses} for the period, split between profit or loss and OCI.","soce":"{e|Share issues}, {e|dividends}, profit, OCI: every movement in each {e|equity component}.","scf":"{a|Cash} in and out, grouped into operating, investing and financing.","notes":"Accounting policies, judgements, estimates and the detail behind each line.","q4":"The exam’s favourite pair: cash flows → **liquidity and solvency**.","q1":"{l|Debt} against {e|equity} (gearing) is read from here, not from the cash flow statement.","q2":"Profitability lives in P&L."},"walk":[{"nodes":["sfp","q1"],"text":"**Financial position:** what it owns and owes at a date. Gearing comes from here."},{"nodes":["pl","q2"],"text":"**Profit or loss and OCI:** how it performed over the period."},{"nodes":["soce","q3"],"text":"**Changes in equity:** what happened to the {e|owners’ stake}: profit, dividends, share issues."},{"nodes":["scf","q4"],"text":"**Cash flows:** liquidity and solvency. The pair the exam tests."},{"nodes":["notes","q5"],"text":"**Notes:** how the numbers were made."}],"caption":"Profitability → P&L. Gearing → financial position. Liquidity and solvency → cash flows.","id":"diagram-17uju3","sect":3,"part":"The complete set of statements","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:344px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 313.00 258.00\" xmlns