pecial purpose. Its shareholders can’t demand a tailored report, so it is general purpose."},{"t":"A schedule of covenant ratios prepared in the format the company’s bank specified in the loan agreement","ok":true,"why":"One user set the format and terms: special purpose."},{"t":"The financial statements of an SGX-listed company","why":"General purpose, under SFRS(I)."},{"t":"The annual financial statements of the CPF Board","why":"General purpose financial statements of a statutory board, under SB-FRS."}],"id":"mcq-16dbxa","sect":4,"part":"Four kinds of financial statements"},{"type":"map","id":"map-5-roles","bucket":"roles","sect":5,"part":"Who does what, and the ASC"},{"type":"think","bucket":"roles","lo":2,"scenario":"After Kopi Kakis publishes its audited financial statements, a shareholder finds an error in them. The CEO says: “Not our problem, the auditors signed them off.”","prompt":"Is the CEO right? Who is responsible for the financial statements?","answer":["No. **Management and the directors** prepare the financial statements and are **responsible** for them. The Companies Act requires FS that comply with the accounting standards.","The **auditors** only give an **opinion** on whether they are true and fair. Blaming the auditor for your own accounts is like blaming the exam marker for your answers."],"id":"think-75zi14","sect":5,"part":"Who does what, and the ASC"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"roles","lo":2,"title":"Who does what in the reporting process","body":["The CEO tried to pass the blame to the auditors. To see why that fails, map who does what, from writing the rules to signing the accounts.","1. **Standard setters** write the rules: the **IASB** internationally, the **ASC** in Singapore, which adopts IFRS as SFRS(I).","2. **Preparers**, management and directors, prepare the FS and are **responsible** for them.","3. **Auditors**, independent public accountants, give an opinion on whether the FS are **true and fair**.","4. **Regulators and enforcers** monitor compliance: **ACRA** (its financial reporting surveillance), and SGX and MAS for listed entities.","5. **Users** (investors, lenders, creditors and others) make decisions with the FS.","! The auditor does not prepare the financial statements, and is not responsible for them."],"id":"rule-7u299x","sect":5,"part":"Who does what, and the ASC"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"roles","lo":3,"title":"Who does what in Singapore financial reporting","intro":"This is the chart from your notes. Follow the solid arrows from the rule writers down to the users; ACRA watches from the side.","notes":{"iasb":"The **IASB** writes IFRS, for the world.","asc":"The **ASC** (now within ACRA) adopts IFRS as SFRS(I), almost word for word, and also prescribes FRS, SFRS for Small Entities and the CAS.","dir":"Directors and management **prepare** the FS and are **responsible** for them.","aud":"Auditors give an **opinion**: true and fair or not.","users":"Investors, lenders and other creditors make their decisions.","acra":"ACRA (SGX and MAS for listed entities) **enforces** compliance, e.g. through financial reporting surveillance."},"walk":[{"nodes":["iasb","asc"],"text":"**IASB writes → ASC adopts.** Singapore takes IFRS largely word for word as SFRS(I)."},{"nodes":["dir"],"text":"**Directors prepare** the financial statements and are responsible for them."},{"nodes":["aud"],"text":"**Auditors check**, and give an opinion on whether the FS are true and fair."},{"nodes":["users"],"text":"**Users decide**: buy, hold, sell, lend, vote."},{"nodes":["acra","dir"],"text":"**ACRA enforces**: it monitors whether companies comply. Not the ASC’s job."}],"caption":"IASB writes → ASC adopts → directors prepare → auditors check → ACRA enforces → users decide.","id":"diagram-10t778","sect":5,"part":"Who does what, and the ASC","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:486px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 442.00 295.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 284.44)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-284.44 431.45,-284.44 431.45,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>iasb\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e8eef6\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M326.9,-273.64C326.9,-273.64 254.12,-273.64 254.12,-273.64 248.12,-273.64 242.12,-267.64 242.12,-261.64 242.12,-261.64 242.12,-249.64 242.12,-249.64 242.12,-243.64 248.12,-237.64 254.12,-237.64 254.12,-237.64 326.9,-237.64 326.9,-237.64 332.9,-237.64 338.9,-243.64 338.9,-249.64 338.9,-249.64 338.9,-261.64 338.9,-261.64 338.9,-267.64 332.9,-273.64 326.9,-273.64\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"250.76\" y=\"-252.19\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">IASB\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"277.76\" y=\"-252.19\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\"> &#160;\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"283.76\" y=\"-252.19\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">writes IFRS\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node2\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>asc\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e8eef6\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M408.65,-214.64C408.65,-214.64 172.38,-214.64 172.38,-214.64 166.38,-214.64 160.38,-208.64 160.38,-202.64 160.38,-202.64 160.38,-190.64 160.38,-190.64 160.38,-184.64 166.38,-178.64 172.38,-178.64 172.38,-178.64 408.65,-178.64 408.65,-178.64 414.65,-178.64 420.65,-184.64 420.65,-190.64 420.65,-190.64 420.65,-202.64 420.65,-202.64 420.65,-208.64 414.65,-214.64 408.65,-214.64\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"242.51\" y=\"-197.19\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight