369.32,-212 369.32,-212 369.32,-224 369.32,-224 369.32,-230 363.32,-236 357.32,-236\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"273.84\" y=\"-218.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">The constraint\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"286.59\" y=\"-209.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">over all QCs\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge5\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>cst&#45;&gt;con\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M115.49,-218C154.32,-218 205.83,-218 246.19,-218\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"246.08,-220.1 252.08,-218 246.08,-215.9 246.08,-220.1\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"179.33\" y=\"-219.75\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> is \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"type":"mcq","bucket":"enhancing","lo":6,"q":"Which statement about the cost constraint is correct?","options":[{"t":"Cost is an enhancing qualitative characteristic","why":"Cost is a constraint, not a QC."},{"t":"Each company decides for itself whether the cost of each disclosure is justified","why":"The judgement is made for reporting in general, mainly by standard setters."},{"t":"The benefits of reporting information must justify the costs of providing and using it","ok":true,"why":"That is the cost constraint."},{"t":"Only preparers bear the cost of financial information","why":"Users bear costs too: lower returns, analysis, and estimating what isn’t reported."}],"id":"mcq-55kegn","sect":2,"part":"Enhancing characteristics and the cost constraint"},{"type":"map","id":"map-3-position","bucket":"position","sect":3,"part":"Assets, liabilities and equity"},{"type":"think","bucket":"position","lo":7,"scenario":"Sunrise Bakery lists what makes it successful: (1) its ovens, owned outright; (2) a 5-year registered trademark; (3) its team of highly skilled bakers, who can resign on one month’s notice; (4) a contract under which a supplier must deliver flour at a fixed price next year.","prompt":"Which of these meet the definition of an asset? What is the test that knocks one out?","answer":["An {a|asset} is a **present economic resource controlled by the entity as a result of past events**. An economic resource is a **right** that has the **potential** to produce economic benefits.","The **{a|ovens}**, the **{a|trademark}** and the **{a|flour contract}** are rights Sunrise controls, from past events, with the potential to produce benefits.","The **bakers** fail on **control**: Sunrise can’t direct their skills or stop them taking those skills to a competitor next month. A great team, but not an asset."],"id":"think-1t61vo","sect":3,"part":"Assets, liabilities and equity"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"position","lo":7,"title":"Asset, liability, equity: learn the words","body":["Sunrise Bakery’s list showed that “valuable to the business” isn’t the same as “an {a|asset}”. The Framework’s definitions give the precise tests.","1. **{a|Asset}:** a **present economic resource controlled** by the entity **as a result of past events**. (An economic resource is a **right** that has the **potential** to produce economic benefits.)","2. **{l|Liability}:** a **present obligation** of the entity to **transfer an economic resource** as a result of past events.","3. **{e|Equity}:** the **residual interest** in the {a|assets} of the entity after deducting all its {l|liabilities}.","Key words:","- **right**; **potential**: benefits don’t have to be certain, or even likely","- **control**: the present ability to direct the use of the resource and get its benefits","- **obligation**: a duty the entity has **no practical ability to avoid**, legal or constructive","- **past event**: no past event, no {a|asset} or {l|liability} yet","> {a|Assets} − {l|Liabilities} = {e|Equity}"],"id":"rule-1xb2m6","sect":3,"part":"Assets, liabilities and equity"},{"type":"tree","bucket":"position","lo":7,"title":"Is it an asset?","scenario":"Sunrise Bakery’s team of highly skilled bakers, who can resign on one month’s notice. Does the team meet the definition of an asset?","expect":"noctl","start":"a1","nodes":{"a1":{"q":"Is there a right with the potential to produce economic benefits?","why":"An economic resource is a right with potential. The benefits needn’t be certain or even likely.","opts":[{"t":"Yes","to":"a2"},{"t":"No potential for benefits at all","to":"nopot"}]},"a2":{"q":"Does the entity control it: can it direct its use, get the benefits, and stop others getting them?","why":"Control is what makes the resource *this entity’s* {a|asset} rather than someone else’s.","opts":[{"t":"Yes","to":"a3"},{"t":"No, e.g. staff who can leave and take their skills","to":"noctl"}]},"a3":{"q":"Does it exist now, as a result of a past event?","why":"A plan or an intention is not a past event.","opts":[{"t":"Yes, e.g. it was bought, built or contracted","to":"asset"},{"t":"No, it is only planned","to":"nopast"}]},"nopot":{"result":"Not an asset: no economic resource","body":["Without potential to produce economic benefits there is no economic resource."]},"noctl":{"result":"Not an asset: not controlled","body":["The bakery can’t direct the bakers’ skills or stop them leaving with them. The team may be valuable, but it is not the entity’s asset.","! A skilled workforce is the classic “valuable but not an asset” example."]},"nopast":{"result":"Not an asset (yet): no past event","body":["A planned purchase is not a present resource. It becomes an {a|asset} when the past event (purchase, contract) happens."]},"asset":{"result":"Meets the definition of an asset","body":["A present economic resource controlled by the entity as a result of past events.","- Whether it is then **recognised** and how it is **measured** are separate questions."]}},"id":"tree-w5ccd6","sect":3,"part":"Assets, liabilities and equity","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:495px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 450.00 363.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 352.08)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-352.08 439.58,-352.08 439.58,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>a1\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#b45309\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M328.78,-341.28C328.78,-341.28 226,-341.28 226,-341.28 220,-341.28 214,-335.28 214,-329.28 214,-329.28 214,-308.64 214,-308.64 214,-302.64 220,-296.64 226,-296.64 226,-296.64 328.78,-296.64 328.78,-296.64 334.78,-296.64 340.78,-302.64 340.78,-308.64 340.78,-308.64 340.78,-329.28 340.78,-329.28 340.78,-335.28 334.78,-341.28 328.78,-341.28\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"277.39\" y=\"-326.51\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Is there a right with the\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"277.39\" y=\"-314.51\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">potential to produce\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"277.39\" y=\"-302.51\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">economic benefits?\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node2\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>a2\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#b45309\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M254.28,-248.14C254.28,-248.14 142.5,-248.14 142.5,-248.14 136.5,-248.14 130.5,-242.14 130.5,-236.14 130.5,-236.14 130.5,-203.5 130.5,-203.5 130.5,-197.5 136.5,-191.5 142.5,-191.5 142.5,-191.5 254.28,-191.5 254.28,-191.5 260.28,-191.5 266.28,-197.5 266.28,-203.5 266.28,-203.5 266.28,-236.1