-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"207.39\" y=\"-19.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Meets the definition of an\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"207.39\" y=\"-7.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">asset\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge5\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>a3&#45;&gt;asset\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M159.07,-95.44C163.82,-91.59 168.5,-87.29 172.39,-82.75 182.51,-70.94 191,-55.73 197.08,-43.14\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"198.93,-44.14 199.56,-37.81 195.12,-42.36 198.93,-44.14\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"229.42\" y=\"-73.25\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> Yes, e.g. it was\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"229.42\" y=\"-62\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\">bought, built or\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"229.42\" y=\"-50.75\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\">contracted \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"type":"think","bucket":"position","lo":7,"scenario":"At year end Sunrise Bakery has: (1) a bank loan outstanding; (2) a board decision to buy a new oven next year; (3) a policy, published on its website and always honoured, of refunding any customer who isn’t happy.","prompt":"Which of these is a present obligation, and which is just a plan?","answer":["The **{l|loan}** is a **legal** obligation from a past event (borrowing the money): a {l|liability}.","The **oven plan** is not an obligation. Sunrise can still change its mind, so it has the **practical ability to avoid** paying: no {l|liability}.","The **refund policy** creates a {l|**constructive** obligation}: customers reasonably expect it, and in practice Sunrise can’t avoid honouring it."],"id":"think-crdwp1","sect":3,"part":"Assets, liabilities and equity"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"position","lo":7,"title":"Old wording vs the 2018 Framework","body":["The refund policy counted as an {l|obligation} even without a contract. That follows from the 2018 wording, which differs from what older textbooks say.","- Older textbooks define {a|assets} by “**future** economic benefits **expected** to flow” and {l|liabilities} by a “**probable**” outflow.","- The **2018** Framework, which SFRS(I) uses, removed probability from the definitions. Uncertainty is now handled when deciding on **recognition and measurement**.","- Elements of the statement of financial position: **{a|assets}, {l|liabilities}, {e|equity}**. Of financial performance: **{i|income} and {x|expenses}**.","! Practice Q2 offers “arises from an increase in assets or reduction in liabilities” for **{e|equity}**. That wording belongs to **{i|income}**."],"id":"rule-wsg225","sect":3,"part":"Assets, liabilities and equity"},{"type":"mcq","bucket":"position","lo":7,"q":"Under the 2018 Conceptual Framework, which statement about the definition of an asset is correct?","options":[{"t":"Future economic benefits must be probable before an item meets the definition","why":"That is the pre-2018 wording. Probability is no longer part of the definition."},{"t":"An economic resource is a right that has the potential to produce economic benefits; the benefits need not be certain or even likely","ok":true,"why":"The 2018 definition. Uncertainty is handled at recognition and measurement."},{"t":"An asset must be legally owned by the entity","why":"The test is control, not legal ownership."},{"t":"An asset is the residual interest after deducting liabilities","why":"That is the definition of {e|equity}."}],"id":"mcq-1cbmtj","sect":3,"part":"Assets, liabilities and equity"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"position","lo":7,"title":"The five elements and how they connect","intro":"Three elements describe position at a date; two describe performance over the period. {e|Equity} is where they meet, and owners have their own door.","notes":{"a":"A present economic resource controlled by the entity as a result of past events.","l":"A present obligation to transfer an economic resource as a result of past events.","e":"The residual interest: {a|assets} minus {l|liabilities}. It has no definition of its own beyond that.","i":"Increases in {a|assets} or decreases in {l|liabilities} that increase {e|equity}, **other than** contributions from owners.","x":"Decreases in {a|assets} or increases in {l|liabilities} that decrease {e|equity}, **other than** distributions to owners.","own":"{e|Share issues} (contributions) and {e|dividends} (distributions) change {e|equity} but are **not** {i|income} or {x|expenses}."},"walk":[{"nodes":["a","l","e"],"text":"**Position:** {a|assets} minus {l|liabilities} equals {e|equity}, at a date."},{"nodes":["i","x","e"],"text":"**Performance:** {i|income} pushes {e|equity} up, {x|expenses} push it down."},{"nodes":["own","e"],"text":"**Owners** also move {e|equity}, through contributions and distributions. Those are never {i|income} or {x|expenses}."}],"caption":"{i|Income} and {x|expenses} are changes in {e|equity} that don’t come from owners.","id":"diagram-9h29kd","sect":3,"part":"Assets, liabilities and equity","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:640px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 670.00 201.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 190.12)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-190.12 659.69,-190.12 659.69,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\u003cg id=\"clust1\" class=\"cluster\">\n\u003ctitle>cluster_sfp\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"white\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,2\" d=\"M20,-8C20,-8 263,-8 