e observable market transactions, not the entity’s own assumptions."},{"t":"It is not fair value, because no identical building was sold","why":"Fair value does not need an identical sale; the hierarchy exists for exactly this."}],"sect":3,"part":"Fair value (SFRS(I) 13)"},{"type":"map","id":"map-4-viu","bucket":"viu","sect":4,"part":"Value in use and current cost"},{"id":"think-qdkxri","type":"think","bucket":"viu","lo":8,"scenario":"Tiong Bahru Kopi, a café, owns a coffee roaster. The second-hand market would pay little for it, but the shop expects it to generate $20,000 of net cash a year for 4 more years, and to sell it for scrap at $10,000 at the end.","prompt":"How would you put a number on what the roaster is worth **to Tiong Bahru Kopi**? Why can’t you just add up the cash?","answer":["Forecast the cash the entity expects from **using** the asset and from its **ultimate disposal**, then **discount** it to today. Money in four years is worth less than money now.","That present value is **value in use**. It is entity-specific: it reflects how **this** shop will use the roaster, not what the market would pay."],"sect":4,"part":"Value in use and current cost"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"viu","lo":8,"title":"Value in use (and fulfilment value)","body":["Fair value ignores what the entity plans to do. Value in use is the opposite: it values the asset the way **this** entity will use it.","**Value in use** = the **present value** of the cash flows, or other economic benefits, that an entity expects to derive from the **use** of an asset and from its **ultimate disposal**.","- **Entity-specific**: it reflects the entity’s own expectations, not the market’s.","- An **exit**-type value: it measures the benefits of using up and then disposing of the asset.","- For **{l|liabilities}**, the equivalent is **fulfilment value**: the present value of what the entity expects to transfer as it fulfils the {l|liability}.","! Exam favourite (practice Q7): \"the present value of the cash flows… from the use of an asset and from its ultimate disposal\" is **value in use**, not fair value. Fair value is a **market** selling price, not the entity’s forecast."],"id":"rule-1bzoig","sect":4,"part":"Value in use and current cost"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"viu","lo":8,"title":"Value in use on a timeline","intro":"The roaster’s expected cash flows, each pulled back to today at the discount rate.","notes":{"today":"PV of the 4 yearly inflows 63,397 + PV of disposal 6,830 = 70,227.","y1":"Net cash from **using** the roaster in year 1. Discounted one year: 20,000 ÷ 1.10.","y2":"Each later year is discounted one more year.","y3":"The entity’s own forecast, not a market’s.","y4":"The last year of use. Discounted 4 years.","scrap":"The **ultimate disposal** counts too: 10,000 × 0.6830 = 6,830."},"walk":[{"nodes":["y1","y2","y3","y4"],"text":"Step 1: the cash the entity expects from **using** the asset: 20,000 a year for 4 years."},{"nodes":["scrap"],"text":"Step 2: add the cash from **ultimate disposal**: 10,000 at the end."},{"nodes":["today"],"text":"Step 3: discount everything to today at 10%. Value in use = **70,227**, not the undiscounted 90,000."}],"caption":"Use + ultimate disposal, discounted. That’s the whole definition.","id":"diagram-1nga1a","sect":4,"part":"Value in use and current cost","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:640px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 618.00 61.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 50.44)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-50.44 607.11,-50.44 607.11,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>today\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e6f4f1\" stroke=\"#0f766e\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M54.78,-39.64C54.78,-39.64 12,-39.64 12,-39.64 6,-39.64 0,-33.64 0,-27.64 0,-27.64 0,-