t-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\">consumed in the\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"293.25\" y=\"-155.14\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\">job \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node7\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>ppe\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e6f4f1\" stroke=\"#0f766e\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M103.53,-36C103.53,-36 12,-36 12,-36 6,-36 0,-30 0,-24 0,-24 0,-12 0,-12 0,-6 6,0 12,0 12,0 103.53,0 103.53,0 109.53,0 115.53,-6 115.53,-12 115.53,-12 115.53,-24 115.53,-24 115.53,-30 109.53,-36 103.53,-36\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"57.76\" y=\"-13.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">PPE (SFRS(I) 1&#45;16)\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge6\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>n3&#45;&gt;ppe\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M106.32,-95.17C103.23,-91.09 100.1,-86.83 97.26,-82.75 88.32,-69.84 79.03,-54.94 71.71,-42.79\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"73.52,-41.72 68.64,-37.65 69.91,-43.88 73.52,-41.72\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"132.51\" y=\"-73.25\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> Yes: machines,\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"132.51\" y=\"-62\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\">buildings,\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"132.51\" y=\"-50.75\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\">vehicles \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node8\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>ip\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e6f4f1\" stroke=\"#0f766e\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M234.03,-36C234.03,-36 145.5,-36 145.5,-36 139.5,-36 133.5,-30 133.5,-24 133.5,-24 133.5,-12 133.5,-12 133.5,-6 139.5,0 145.5,0 145.5,0 234.03,0 234.03,0 240.03,0 246.03,-6 246.03,-12 246.03,-12 246.03,-24 246.03,-24 246.03,-30 240.03,-36 234.03,-36\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"189.76\" y=\"-19.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Investment property\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"189.76\" y=\"-7.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">(SFRS(I) 1&#45;40)\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge7\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>n3&#45;&gt;ip\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M156.15,-95.44C160.45,-91.58 164.5,-87.32 167.76,-82.75 176.07,-71.12 181.46,-56.09 184.82,-43.55\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"186.8,-44.29 186.21,-37.96 182.72,-43.28 186.8,-44.29\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"221.66\" y=\"-73.25\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> No: it is land or\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"221.66\" y=\"-62\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\">a building held\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"221.66\" y=\"-50.75\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\">for rent or growth \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"type":"mcq","bucket":"classify","lo":11,"q":"A bakery owns the following. Which is inventory?","options":[{"t":"The ovens it bakes with","why":"Used over many years to produce goods: {a|PPE}."},{"t":"The flour, sugar and butter in its store room","ok":true,"why":"Materials to be consumed in production: {a|raw materials} inventory."},{"t":"The delivery van","why":"Used to run the business over several periods: {a|PPE}."},{"t":"A flat above the shop it rents out to a tenant","why":"Held to earn rent: {a|investment property}."}],"id":"mcq-7vrel8","sect":1,"part":"Classify"},{"type":"compare","bucket":"classify","preamble":"Inventory, PPE and investment property can be the very same kind of thing (a building, a machine). What separates them is **purpose**: sell it, use it, or hold it for rent and growth.","lo":11,"special":"{a|Inventory} is the asset you mean to **get rid of**: sell it, or use it up making something to sell, all within the normal operating cycle.","id":"compare-1kumyt","sect":1,"part":"Classify"},{"type":"map","id":"map-2-recognise","bucket":"recognise","sect":2,"part":"Recognise"},{"type":"think","bucket":"recognise","lo":11,"scenario":"Changi Gadgets (year end 31 Dec) orders speakers from a supplier in Shenzhen. They are shipped on 29 Dec on terms that pass ownership **when the goods are loaded at the supplier’s port** (FOB shipping point). They arrive on 4 Jan.","prompt":"On 31 Dec the speakers are on a ship in the South China Sea. Whose inventory are they?","answer":["**Changi Gadgets’.** Control passed when the goods were loaded, so at 31 Dec they are its {a|inventory} (and it owes the supplier a {l|payable}), even though no one in Singapore has seen them yet.","If the terms had been FOB **destination**, control would pass on arrival: on 31 Dec they would still be the supplier’s.","Rule of thumb: {a|inventory} belongs to whoever **controls** it, not whoever happens to be holding it."],"id":"think-j2ybt3","sect":2,"part":"Recognise"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"recognise","lo":11,"title":"Recognise inventory when you control it","body":["Once we know something *is* {a|inventory}, the next question is *whose* it is, and from when. The speakers on the ship showed that being physically present is not the test; this rule says what is.","{a|Inventory} goes on the balance sheet when **control** of the goods passes to the entity, usually with legal title.","- **FOB shipping point:** the buyer controls the goods from shipment. Goods in transit at year end are the **buyer’s**.","- **FOB destination:** the seller keeps control until delivery. Goods in transit are still the **seller’s**.","- **Consignment:** goods held by an agent to sell on the owner’s behalf stay in the **owner’s** (consignor’s) {a|inventory}, not the agent’s.","! At a year-end count, the warehouse is not the whole story: add goods in transit you control, and leave out goods you hold for others."],"id":"rule-lzpkk9","sect":2,"part":"Recognise"},{"type":"mcq","bucket":"recognise","lo":11,"q":"At 31 December, a retailer holds goods costing $8,000 on consignment for a supplier, to sell on the supplier’s behalf for a commission. How should the retailer treat them?","options":[{"t":"Include them in its {a|inventory} at $8,000","why":"The supplier still controls them; the retailer is only an agent."},{"t":"Exclude them: they are the supplier’s {a|inventory}","ok":true,"why":"Consigned goods stay in the consignor’s (supplier’s) {a|inventory} until sold to a customer."},{"t":"Include them, with a matching {l|liability} to the supplier","why":"There is no purchase. The retailer never controls the goods."},{"t":"Include only the expected commission as {a|inventory}","why":"Commission is {i|revenue} when earned, not {a|inventory}."}],"id":"mcq-diomkh","sect":2,"part":"Recognise"},{"type":"map","id":"map-3-initial","bucket":"initial","sect":3,"part":"Initial measurement"},{"type":"think","bucket":"initial","lo":11,"scenario":"Changi Gadgets imports 500 speakers at a list price of $80 each, less a 10% trade discount. It also pays import duty of $1,800, GST of $3,402 (which it can claim back as input tax), freight from the port of $1,200 and insurance in transit of $300. Once they arrive it pays $900 to store them in a warehouse until sold, and $700 to deliver them to customers.","prompt":"Which of these belong in the cost of the speakers? A hint: what did it take to get them *onto the shelf, ready to sell*?","answer":["In: the price after the trade discount (40,000 − 4,000 = 36,000), **import duty**, **freight-in** and **insurance in transit**. All needed to bring the speakers to their present location and condition.","**Recoverable GST** is out: it comes back from IRAS, so it is a {a|GST receivable}, not a cost.","**Storage** after arrival and **delivery to customers** are out: they happen after the goods are ready to sell. They are {x|selling and distribution costs}.","{a|Cost} = 36,000 + 1,800 + 1,200 + 300 = **$39,300**, or $78.6 a speaker."],"id":"think-13m7m3","sect":3,"part":"Initial measurement"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"initial","lo":11,"title":"What goes into the cost of inventory","body":["The speakers showed the idea: cost is everything it took to get the goods **ready to sell**, and nothing after. Here is the full list, so the same test works for a manufacturer as well as a trader.","> {a|Cost} = {a|costs of purchase} + {a|costs of conversion} + {a|other costs} to bring it to its present location and condition","1. **Purchase:** price + import duties and **non-recoverable** taxes + transport and handling − **trade discounts** and rebates.","2. **Conversion** (manufacturers): direct labour + production overheads.","3. **Other costs:** only if needed to bring the goods to their present location and condition.","Expensed, not cost:","- {x|**abnormal** waste} of materials, labour or overheads","- {x|**storage**}, unless it is needed in the production process (think whisky ageing in casks)","- {x|**admin** overheads} not related to production","- {x|**selling** costs}, including {x|**freight-out**}","+ Memory hook: **freight-IN goes IN to {a|inventory}; freight-OUT goes OUT as an {x|expense}.**"],"id":"rule-4u0wa6","sect":3,"part":"Initial measurement"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"initial","lo":11,"title":"Changi Gadgets: what goes into cost","intro":"The same answer as a picture. Four amounts build the {a|cost} of the speakers; the GST becomes a {a|receivable}; two costs go straight to profit or loss.","notes":{"price":"List 40,000 less the 10% **trade discount** 4,000. Trade discounts reduce cost.","duty":"Import duty is a non-recoverable tax: part of cost.","frt":"Transport to get the goods to the shop or warehouse: part of cost.","ins":"Insurance while the goods are on their way to you: part of cost.","cost":"36,000 + 1,800 + 1,200 + 300 = 39,300, or 39,300 ÷ 500 = 78.6 a unit.","gst":"GST registered businesses claim input tax back, so it is not a cost.","gstr":"A {a|GST receivable} until it is offset against output tax.","sto":"Storing goods that are **already ready to sell** is not part of cost. Expense it.","fout":"Delivery **to customers** is a {x|selling cost}.","pl":"{x|Storage} and {x|freight-out} are expensed in the period."},"walk":[{"nodes":["price","cost"],"text":"Start with the purchase price, **after** the trade discount."},{"nodes":["duty","frt","ins","cost"],"text":"Add what it took to get the goods here: duty, freight-in and insurance in transit."},{"nodes":["cost"],"text":"{a|Cost} = **39,300**, 78.6 per speaker."},{"nodes":["gst","gstr"],"text":"Recoverable GST is not cost: it is an {a|asset} you will get back."},{"nodes":["sto","fout","pl"],"text":"{x|Storage after arrival} and {x|delivery to customers} happen after the goods are ready to sell: expense them."}],"caption":"Ask of each cost: did it bring the goods to their present location and condition?","id":"diagram-1jirmz","sect":3,"part":"Initial measurement","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:334px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 304.00 382.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 370.8)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-370.8 292.86,-370.8 292.86,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>price\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e8eef6\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width