roke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M209.9,-95C209.9,-95 151.38,-95 151.38,-95 145.38,-95 139.38,-89 139.38,-83 139.38,-83 139.38,-71 139.38,-71 139.38,-65 145.38,-59 151.38,-59 151.38,-59 209.9,-59 209.9,-59 215.9,-59 221.9,-65 221.9,-71 221.9,-71 221.9,-83 221.9,-83 221.9,-89 215.9,-95 209.9,-95\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"148.01\" y=\"-73.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Keep at cost\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge2\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>q&#45;&gt;cost\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M203.2,-131.35C199.61,-122.84 195.04,-112.04 190.95,-102.38\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"192.94,-101.7 188.67,-96.99 189.07,-103.34 192.94,-101.7\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"205.13\" y=\"-107.75\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> no \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node4\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>wd\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#ffe4e6\" stroke=\"#be123c\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M361.78,-95C361.78,-95 269.5,-95 269.5,-95 263.5,-95 257.5,-89 257.5,-83 257.5,-83 257.5,-71 257.5,-71 257.5,-65 263.5,-59 269.5,-59 269.5,-59 361.78,-59 361.78,-59 367.78,-59 373.78,-65 373.78,-71 373.78,-71 373.78,-83 373.78,-83 373.78,-89 367.78,-95 361.78,-95\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"266.14\" y=\"-77.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Write down to NRV\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"268.39\" y=\"-68.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Dr COGS / Cr Inventory\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge3\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>q&#45;&gt;wd\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M227.14,-135.25C242.15,-125.54 264.18,-111.29 282.5,-99.44\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"283.39,-101.36 287.29,-96.34 281.11,-97.84 283.39,-101.36\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"283.01\" y=\"-107.75\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> yes \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node6\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>rm\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#f3f4f6\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M479.78,-166.89C479.78,-166.89 345.5,-166.89 345.5,-166.89 339.5,-166.89 333.5,-160.89 333.5,-154.89 333.5,-154.89 333.5,-140.25 333.5,-140.25 333.5,-134.25 339.5,-128.25 345.5,-128.25 345.5,-128.25 479.78,-128.25 479.78,-128.25 485.78,-128.25 491.78,-134.25 491.78,-140.25 491.78,-140.25 491.78,-154.89 491.78,-154.89 491.78,-160.89 485.78,-166.89 479.78,-166.89\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"342.14\" y=\"-154.07\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Raw materials:\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"411.14\" y=\"-154.07\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#111827\"> no write&#45;down if\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"354.89\" y=\"-144.07\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#111827\">the finished goods still sell\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"377.39\" y=\"-134.07\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#111827\">at or above cost\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge5\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>q&#45;&gt;rm\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" stroke-dasharray=\"1,5\" d=\"M263.56,-147.57C286.76,-147.57 309.95,-147.57 333.15,-147.57\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node5\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>rev\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#dcfce7\" stroke=\"#166534\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M388.03,-36C388.03,-36 243.25,-36 243.25,-36 237.25,-36 231.25,-30 231.25,-24 231.25,-24 231.25,-12 231.25,-12 231.25,-6 237.25,0 243.25,0 243.25,0 388.03,0 388.03,0 394.03,0 400.03,-6 400.03,-12 400.03,-12 400.03,-24 400.03,-24 400.03,-30 394.03,-36 388.03,-36\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"239.89\" y=\"-19.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">NRV recovers later?\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"344.89\" y=\"-19.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\"> Reverse,\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"240.64\" y=\"-8.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">but only back up to original cost\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge4\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>wd&#45;&gt;rev\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,2\" d=\"M315.64,-58.59C315.64,-53.84 315.64,-48.6 315.64,-43.53\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"317.74,-43.82 315.64,-37.82 313.54,-43.82 317.74,-43.82\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"id":"calc-vp8fos","type":"calc","bucket":"subsequent","lo":9,"q":"Jurong Furniture has 200 unfinished dining tables in {a|work in progress}, costing $170 each so far. Finishing each table will cost another $40. Each sells for $220, and the sales agent takes a 10% commission on the selling price. What write-down is needed?","answer":2400,"unit":"$","working":["Commission = 220 × 10% = 22.","NRV per table = 220 − 40 (to complete) − 22 (to sell) = 158.","Cost to date 170 vs NRV 158: write down 12 a table.","{x|Write-down} = 200 × 12 = **$2,400**. {a|WIP} is carried at 200 × 158 = 31,600.","Trap: forget the costs to complete and NRV looks like 198, well above cost: no write-down. That is the classic trap."],"sect":4,"part":"Subsequent measurement"},{"type":"think","bucket":"subsequent","lo":9,"scenario":"A gadget shop holds three product lines. Phones cost $12,000 (NRV $15,000), tablets cost $8,000 (NRV $6,500), smartwatches cost $5,000 (NRV $4,200).","prompt":"In total, cost is $25,000 and NRV is $25,700. So no write-down is needed... right?","answer":["Wrong. The profit expected on phones would be hiding the {x|losses} already suffered on tablets and smartwatches.","Apply the test **item by item**. Tablets and smartwatches go down to NRV; phones stay at cost (they are never written **up**).","Netting a {i|gain} you haven’t made against a {x|loss} you have is exactly what the rule is there to stop."],"id":"think-1bs9rf","sect":4,"part":"Subsequent measurement"},{"id":"visual-mqqwya","type":"visual","bucket":"subsequent","lo":9,"title":"Item by item, line by line","html":"\u003cp>The gadget shop’s three lines, tested one at a time. Each row takes the lower of its own cost and NRV, so a \u003cspan class=\"el el-i\">gain\u003c/span> on one line can’t hide a \u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">loss\u003c/span> on another.\u003c/p>\n    \u003cdiv class=\"tbl-wrap\">\u003ctable class=\"tbl num reveal-rows\">\u003cthead>\u003ctr>\u003cth>Item\u003c/th>\u003cth>Cost\u003c/th>\u003cth>NRV\u003c/th>\u003cth>Lower\u003c/th>\u003c/tr>\u003c/thead>\u003ctbody>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>Phones\u003c/td>\u003ctd>12,000\u003c/td>\u003ctd>15,000\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cb>12,000\u003c/b>\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>Tablets\u003c/td>\u003ctd>8,000\u003c/td>\u003ctd>6,500\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cb>6,500\u003c/b>\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>Smartwatches\u003c/td>\u003ctd>5,000\u003c/td>\u003ctd>4,200\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cb>4,200\u003c/b>\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003cb>Total\u003c/b>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>25,000\u003c/td>\u003ctd>25,700\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cb>22,700\u003c/b>\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n    \u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\u003c/div>\n    \u003cp class=\"cap\">Item by item: \u003cstrong>22,700\u003c/strong>, a \u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">write-down\u003c/span> of 2,300. Comparing totals would give 25,000 and no write-down at all. Grouping is allowed only for similar or related items (e.g. the same product line), \u003cstrong>never\u003c/strong> a whole category such as “all finished goods”.\u003c/p>","sect":4,"part":"Subsequent measurement"},{"id":"mcq-1jsdah","type":"mcq","bucket":"subsequent","lo":9,"q":"Three items: P cost $30,000, NRV $26,000; Q cost $14,000, NRV $19,000; R cost $9,000, NRV $9,500. At what amount is {a|inventory} reported?","options":[{"t":"$53,000","why":"Compares total cost (53,000) with total NRV (54,500). The test is item by item."},{"t":"$49,000","ok":true,"why":"26,000 + 14,000 + 9,000 = 49,000. Only P is written down."},{"t":"$54,500","why":"Writes Q and R up to NRV. {a|Inventory} is never carried above cost."},{"t":"$49,500","why":"Carries R at its NRV, which is above its cost. Only P is written down; Q and R stay at cost."}],"sect":4,"part":"Subsequent measurement"},{"type":"think","bucket":"subsequent","lo":9,"scenario":"Cocoa Co makes chocolate bars. It holds cocoa beans that cost $50,000; their replacement cost has dropped to $42,000. A finished bar costs $120 to make and still sells for $150.","prompt":"The beans are now “worth” less than they cost. Write them down?","answer":["No. The {a|beans} aren’t going to be sold as beans: they will be turned into bars that still sell **above** cost (150 vs 120). The full cost of the beans will be recovered.","Only if the fall in material prices meant the **finished bars** would sell below cost would the beans be written down, and then replacement cost may be the best measure of their NRV."],"id":"think-1s8qwn","sect":4,"part":"Subsequent measurement"},{"type":"tree","bucket":"subsequent","lo":9,"title":"Write it down or not?","scenario":"Cocoa Co’s cocoa beans: cost $50,000, replacement cost now $42,000. The chocolate bars made from them cost $120 and sell for $150.","expect":"keepRm","start":"r1","nodes":{"r1":{"q":"What kind of inventory is it?","why":"Raw materials get a special test; everything else is compared with its own NRV.","opts":[{"t":"Finished goods, merchandise or WIP","to":"r2"},{"t":"Raw materials held for production","to":"r3"}]},"r2":{"q":"Is NRV (selling price − costs to complete − costs to sell) below cost?","why":"Inventory must not be carried above what it will bring in.","opts":[{"t":"Yes","to":"wd"},{"t":"No","to":"keep"}]},"r3":{"q":"Will the finished goods it goes into sell at or above cost?","why":"If the end product recovers its full cost, so do the materials inside it.","opts":[{"t":"Yes","to":"keepRm"},{"t":"No, they will sell below cost","to":"wdRm"}]},"keep":{"result":"Keep at cost","body":["NRV is at or above cost: no adjustment. Never write inventory up to NRV."]},"wd":{"result":"Write down to NRV","body":["> Dr {x|Cost of goods sold} / Cr {a|Inventory}","- Reassess at the next reporting date; reverse (up to cost) if NRV recovers."]},"keepRm":{"result":"Raw materials stay at cost","body":["The bars still sell above cost, so the {a|beans} stay at 50,000 even though replacement cost fell to 42,000.","! A fall in replacement cost alone is not a reason to write materials down."]},"wdRm":{"result":"Write the raw materials down","body":["The finished goods will sell below cost, so the materials are written down. **Replacement cost** may be the best available measure of their NRV."]}},"id":"tree-ep8vq2","sect":4,"part":"Subsequent measurement","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:593px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 539.00 235.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 224.44)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-224.44 528.58,-224.44 528.58,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node