0.64\" y=\"-13.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Write down to NRV\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge3\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>r2&#45;&gt;wd\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M144.66,-83.91C145.78,-71.76 147.17,-56.61 148.34,-44\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"150.43,-44.2 148.89,-38.04 146.24,-43.82 150.43,-44.2\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"159.07\" y=\"-56.38\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> Yes \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node6\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>keepRm\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e6f4f1\" stroke=\"#0f766e\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M359.28,-36C359.28,-36 240,-36 240,-36 234,-36 228,-30 228,-24 228,-24 228,-12 228,-12 228,-6 234,0 240,0 240,0 359.28,0 359.28,0 365.28,0 371.28,-6 371.28,-12 371.28,-12 371.28,-24 371.28,-24 371.28,-30 365.28,-36 359.28,-36\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"299.64\" y=\"-13.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Raw materials stay at cost\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge5\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>r3&#45;&gt;keepRm\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M302.63,-83.91C302.07,-71.76 301.37,-56.61 300.79,-44\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"302.89,-43.94 300.52,-38.04 298.7,-44.13 302.89,-43.94\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"313.25\" y=\"-56.38\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> Yes \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node7\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>wdRm\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e6f4f1\" stroke=\"#0f766e\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M505.78,-36C505.78,-36 401.5,-36 401.5,-36 395.5,-36 389.5,-30 389.5,-24 389.5,-24 389.5,-12 389.5,-12 389.5,-6 395.5,0 401.5,0 401.5,0 505.78,0 505.78,0 511.78,0 517.78,-6 517.78,-12 517.78,-12 517.78,-24 517.78,-24 517.78,-30 511.78,-36 505.78,-36\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"453.64\" y=\"-19.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Write the raw materials\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"453.64\" y=\"-7.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">down\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge6\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>r3&#45;&gt;wdRm\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M341.49,-83.91C364.66,-70.5 394.15,-53.44 417.07,-40.17\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"417.9,-42.11 422.04,-37.29 415.8,-38.48 417.9,-42.11\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"438.71\" y=\"-62\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> No, they will sell\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"438.71\" y=\"-50.75\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\">below cost \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"type":"je","bucket":"subsequent","lo":10,"q":"Year 1. Goods cost $10,000. Expected selling price $9,500, costs to complete $600, selling costs $400. Record the write-down.","accounts":["Inventory","Accounts payable","Accounts receivable","Cash","GST receivable","Sales revenue","Cost of goods sold","Purchases","Freight-in","Purchase returns","Purchase discounts","Freight-out expense","Storage expense","Revaluation surplus (OCI)","Retained earnings"],"lines":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Cost of goods sold","amount":1500},{"side":"Cr","account":"Inventory","amount":1500}],"why":"NRV = 9,500 − 600 − 400 = 8,500. {x|Write-down} = 10,000 − 8,500 = 1,500, expensed in the period (here inside {x|COGS}). Never to OCI: {a|inventory} has no {e|revaluation surplus}.","id":"je-72j083","sect":4,"part":"Subsequent measurement"},{"id":"think-5vxshz","type":"think","bucket":"subsequent","lo":10,"scenario":"Goods that cost $10,000 were written down to their NRV of $8,500 at the end of year 1. At the end of year 2 they are still on hand. Demand has bounced back and their NRV is now $11,000.","prompt":"The goods are carried at $8,500. Can the write-down be reversed? By how much: 1,500 or 2,500?","answer":["Yes, SFRS(I) allows the reversal, because the reason for the write-down has gone. But only **1,500**, back to the original cost of 10,000.","Reversing 2,500 would carry the goods at 11,000, above cost: that would be recognising profit before the sale.","Down any amount, back up only to cost. Inventory can recover, but it can’t get a promotion."],"sect":4,"part":"Subsequent measurement"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"subsequent","lo":10,"title":"Write-downs and reversals","body":["A write-down is not forever: NRV is reassessed every reporting date, and the last page showed it can bounce back. This rule sets out both directions, and the ceiling on the way back up.","1. **Reassess NRV at each reporting date.**","2. **{x|Write-down}** = cost − NRV (only when NRV is lower). Expense it in the period the {x|loss} occurs.","3. **Reversal** when the circumstances that caused the write-down no longer exist (or there is clear evidence NRV has risen). Cap it at the original write-down, so the new {a|carrying amount} is never above **original cost**.","4. The reversal **reduces the {x|inventory expense}** recognised in that period.","> Write-down: Dr {x|Cost of goods sold} / Cr {a|Inventory}. Reversal: Dr {a|Inventory} / Cr {x|Cost of goods sold}","! US GAAP (your FA book) **forbids** reversals. SFRS(I) **allows** them, up to original cost. Expect an MCQ on this."],"id":"rule-phlh06","sect":4,"part":"Subsequent measurement"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"subsequent","lo":10,"title":"Down any amount, back up only to cost","intro":"The notes’ example on a timeline. Watch the {a|carrying amount} follow NRV down, then hit the ceiling on the way back up.","notes":{"y0":"Cost 10,000: the ceiling for the life of these goods.","y1":"NRV = 9,500 − 600 − 400 = 8,500, below cost: carry at 8,500.","wd":"10,000 − 8,500 = 1,500, expensed in year 1.","y2":"NRV 11,000 is above cost, so the {a|carrying amount} goes back to cost, 10,000.","rev":"Reverse 1,500, exactly the earlier write-down. It reduces year 2 {x|COGS}.","cap":"Carrying the goods at 11,000 would recognise 1,000 of profit before any sale. Not allowed."},"walk":[{"nodes":["y0"],"text":"Bought at 10,000."},{"nodes":["y1","wd"],"text":"Year 1: NRV 8,500. Write down 1,500 to profit or loss."},{"nodes":["y2","rev"],"text":"Year 2: NRV 11,000. Reverse 1,500, back to cost."},{"nodes":["cap"],"text":"Not to 11,000: original cost is the ceiling."}],"caption":"The reversal is capped at the original write-down.","id":"diagram-1sx2b9","sect":4,"part":"Subsequent measurement","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:640px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 598.00 140.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 129.62)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-129.62 587.17,-129.62 587.17,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>y0\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M60.78,-117C60.78,-117 12,-117 12,-117 6,-117 0,-111 0,-105 0,-105 0,-93 0,-93 0,-87 6,-81 12,-81 12,-81 60.78,-81 60.78,-81 66.78,-81 72.78,-87 72.78,-93 72.78,-93 72.78,-105 72.78,-105 72.78,-111 66.78,-117 60.78,-117\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"16.89\" y=\"-100.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"white\">Bought\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=