id=\"edge8\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>wa&#45;&gt;wc\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M222.83,-60.62C222.21,-55.38 221.51,-49.53 220.85,-43.91\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"222.93,-43.68 220.14,-37.97 218.76,-44.17 222.93,-43.68\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node10\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>wk\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e6f4f1\" stroke=\"#0f766e\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M312.78,-36C312.78,-36 279,-36 279,-36 273,-36 267,-30 267,-24 267,-24 267,-12 267,-12 267,-6 273,0 279,0 279,0 312.78,0 312.78,0 318.78,0 324.78,-6 324.78,-12 324.78,-12 324.78,-24 324.78,-24 324.78,-30 318.78,-36 312.78,-36\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"275.64\" y=\"-19.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Closing\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"282.39\" y=\"-8.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">1,755\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge9\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>wa&#45;&gt;wk\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M245.81,-60.62C253.11,-54.55 261.41,-47.65 269.12,-41.25\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"270.44,-42.88 273.71,-37.43 267.75,-39.65 270.44,-42.88\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"type":"visual","bucket":"derecognise","lo":12,"title":"FIFO vs moving average, sale by sale","html":"\u003cp>The same January for Tiong Bahru Tea, as a perpetual system sees it: two purchases and two sales. Watch \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">inventory\u003c/span> build up with each delivery and drop with each sale. The drops differ, because each formula sends a different cost to \u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">COGS\u003c/span>.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"wg\" data-wg=\"roll\" data-key=\"tea-b11\" data-cfg=\"{&quot;panels&quot;:[{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;FIFO&quot;,&quot;sub&quot;:&quot;oldest costs leave first&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;bal&quot;:&quot;Inventory&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:1000,&quot;startCap&quot;:&quot;1 Jan: 100 tins × $10 = {a|opening inventory 1,000}.&quot;,&quot;years&quot;:[{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;5–10 Jan&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;purchase&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:2600,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;5 Jan: buy 200 × $13 = {a|+2,600}. The same in both columns.&quot;},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;cost of sale&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-1650,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;10 Jan: sell 150 tins. FIFO takes the **oldest** layers first: {x|COGS 1,650}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20–25 Jan&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;purchase&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:1800,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;20 Jan: buy 100 × $18 = {a|+1,800}. The same in both columns.&quot;},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;cost of sale&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-1560,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;25 Jan: sell 120 tins. FIFO takes the **oldest** layers first: {x|COGS 1,560}.&quot;}]}]},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Moving average&quot;,&quot;sub&quot;:&quot;average after each purchase&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;bal&quot;:&quot;Inventory&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:1000,&quot;startCap&quot;:&quot;1 Jan: 100 tins × $10 = {a|opening inventory 1,000}.&quot;,&quot;years&quot;:[{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;5–10 Jan&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;purchase&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:2600,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;5 Jan: buy 200 × $13 = {a|+2,600}. The same in both columns.&quot;},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;cost of sale&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-1800,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;10 Jan: sell 150 tins at the running average 12: 150 × 12 = {x|COGS 1,800}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20–25 Jan&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;purchase&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:1800,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;20 Jan: buy 100 × $18 = {a|+1,800}. The same in both columns.&quot;},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;cost of sale&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-1728,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;25 Jan: sell 120 tins at the running average 14.4: 120 × 14.4 = {x|COGS 1,728}.&quot;}]}]}],&quot;notes&quot;:{&quot;start&quot;:&quot;Same tins, same purchases, same sales. Only the cost formula differs. Press Play or Next.&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[&quot;A purchase adds its cost to {a|inventory}: identical under both formulas.&quot;,&quot;A sale moves cost out to {x|COGS}. **This** is where the formulas disagree: which cost leaves?&quot;],&quot;end&quot;:&quot;Prices rose, so FIFO sends the cheaper, older costs out: {x|COGS} 3,210 vs 3,528, leaving {a|closing inventory} 2,190 vs 1,872. Both add up to goods available of 5,400.&quot;}}\">\u003c/div>","id":"visual-v7pbr7","sect":5,"part":"Derecognise / transfer"},{"id":"calc-g2nnbw","type":"calc","bucket":"derecognise","lo":12,"q":"Tiong Bahru Tea’s January: 100 tins on hand at $10 on 1 Jan; bought 200 at $13 on 5 Jan; sold 150 on 10 Jan; bought 100 at $18 on 20 Jan; sold 120 on 25 Jan. 130 tins are left. What is {a|closing inventory} under FIFO?","answer":2190,"unit":"$","working":["FIFO: the oldest costs have gone to {x|COGS}, so the 130 tins left carry the **latest** costs.","30 × 13 = 390; 100 × 18 = 1,800.","{a|Closing inventory} = **$2,190**. {x|COGS} = 5,400 − 2,190 = 3,210."],"sect":5,"part":"Derecognise / transfer"},{"type":"mcq","bucket":"derecognise","lo":12,"q":"Prices have risen steadily all year. Compared with weighted average, which is true of FIFO?","options":[{"t":"Higher {x|COGS}, lower {a|closing inventory}, lower profit","why":"That is weighted average compared with FIFO."},{"t":"Lower {x|COGS}, higher {a|closing inventory}, higher profit","ok":true,"why":"FIFO sends the older, cheaper costs to {x|COGS} and keeps the newer, dearer ones in {a|closing stock}."},{"t":"The same {x|COGS}, because total {x|purchases} are the same","why":"Total goods available is the same, but the split between {x|COGS} and {a|closing inventory} differs."},{"t":"Lower {x|COGS}, lower {a|closing inventory}, higher profit","why":"{x|COGS} and {a|closing inventory} must add up to goods available, so if one is lower the other is higher."}],"id":"mcq-vricq2","sect":5,"part":"Derecognise / transfer"},{"id":"think-1c0fue","type":"think","bucket":"derecognise","lo":11,"scenario":"At the 31 Dec 20X1 stock count, a pallet worth $5,000 was counted twice. Nobody noticed. Reported profit was $80,000 for 20X1 and $70,000 for 20X2.","prompt":"Which years’ profits are wrong, and by how much? Is {e|retained earnings} wrong at the end of 20X2?","answer":["**20X1:** {a|closing inventory} is 5,000 too high, so {x|COGS} is 5,000 too low and profit is **overstated** by 5,000 (true profit 75,000).","**20X2:** that same {a|closing figure} is now {a|**opening** inventory}, 5,000 too high, so {x|COGS} is too high and profit is **understated** by 5,000 (true profit 75,000).","**{e|Retained earnings} at the end of 20X2 is correct again:** the two errors cancel. A counting error is like a bad joke: it comes back the next year, and then it’s over."],"sect":5,"part":"Derecognise / transfer"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"derecognise","lo":11,"title":"An inventory error ripples for two years","intro":"One overstated {a|closing figure}, two wrong profits, and a self-correcting {e|balance} by the end of year 2.","notes":{"err":"The pallet counted twice: {a|closing inventory} is too high.","c1":"{x|COGS} = {a|opening} + {x|purchases} − {a|closing}. A bigger {a|closing figure} means smaller {x|COGS}.","p1":"Smaller {x|COGS} → profit too high in 20X1 (and {e|closing retained earnings} too).","o2":"Last year’s {a|closing balance} is this year’s {a|opening balance}, error included.","c2":"A bigger {a|opening figure} means bigger {x|COGS} in 20X2.","p2":"Bigger {x|COGS} → profit too low in 20X2.","re":"+5,000 then −5,000: by the end of 20X2 {e|retained earnings} is right again."},"walk":[{"nodes":["err","c1","p1"],"text":"20X1: {a|closing} too high → {x|COGS} too low → profit **over** by 5,000."},{"nodes":["o2"],"text":"The error becomes next year’s {a|opening inventory}."},{"nodes":["o2","c2","p2"],"text":"20X2: {a|opening} too high → {x|COGS} too high → profit **under** by 5,000."},{"nodes":["re"],"text":"After two years the errors cancel: {e|retained earnings} is correct."}],"caption":"{a|Closing inventory} and profit move in the same direction; {a|opening inventory} and profit move in opposite directions.","id":"diagram-rp7eib","sect":5,"part":"Derecognise / transfer","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:607px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 552.00 138.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 126.8)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-126.8 541.17,-126.8 541.17,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>err\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M128.66,-116C128.66,-116 13.88,-116 13.88,-116 7.88,-116 1.88,-110 1.88,-104 1.88,-104 1.88,-92 1.88,-92 1.88,-86 7.88,-80 13.88,-80 13.88,-80 128.66,-80 128.66,-80 134.66,-80 140.66,-86 140.66,-92 140.66,-92 140.66,-104 140.66,-104 140.66,-110 134.66,-116 128.66,-116\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"10.52\" y=\"-99.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"white\">Closing inventory 20X1\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"31.14\" y=\"-88.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"white\">overstated 5,000\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node2\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>c1\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e