>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#ffe4e6\" stroke=\"#be123c\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M93.78,-286C93.78,-286 48,-286 48,-286 42,-286 36,-280 36,-274 36,-274 36,-262 36,-262 36,-256 42,-250 48,-250 48,-250 93.78,-250 93.78,-250 99.78,-250 105.78,-256 105.78,-262 105.78,-262 105.78,-274 105.78,-274 105.78,-280 99.78,-286 93.78,-286\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"44.64\" y=\"-268.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">GST\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"67.14\" y=\"-268.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\"> 8,550\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"46.51\" y=\"-259.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">recoverable\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node9\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>rec\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e8eef6\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M315.81,-286C315.81,-286 243.78,-286 243.78,-286 237.78,-286 231.78,-280 231.78,-274 231.78,-274 231.78,-262 231.78,-262 231.78,-256 237.78,-250 243.78,-250 243.78,-250 315.81,-250 315.81,-250 321.81,-250 327.81,-256 327.81,-262 327.81,-262 327.81,-274 327.81,-274 327.81,-280 321.81,-286 315.81,-286\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"240.42\" y=\"-268.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">GST receivable\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"247.17\" y=\"-259.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">claim from IRAS\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge6\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>gst&#45;&gt;rec\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M106.06,-268C138.12,-268 186.63,-268 224.08,-268\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"223.9,-270.1 229.9,-268 223.9,-265.9 223.9,-270.1\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node7\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>train\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#ffe4e6\" stroke=\"#be123c\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M103.9,-336C103.9,-336 37.87,-336 37.87,-336 31.87,-336 25.87,-330 25.87,-324 25.87,-324 25.87,-312 25.87,-312 25.87,-306 31.87,-300 37.87,-300 37.87,-300 103.9,-300 103.9,-300 109.9,-300 115.9,-306 115.9,-312 115.9,-312 115.9,-324 115.9,-324 115.9,-330 109.9,-336 103.9,-336\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"34.51\" y=\"-314.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Training\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"77.26\" y=\"-314.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\"> 2,500\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node10\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>pl\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#b45309\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M301.19,-336C301.19,-336 258.41,-336 258.41,-336 252.41,-336 246.41,-330 246.41,-324 246.41,-324 246.41,-312 246.41,-312 246.41,-306 252.41,-300 258.41,-300 258.41,-300 301.19,-300 301.19,-300 307.19,-300 313.19,-306 313.19,-312 313.19,-312 313.19,-324 313.19,-324 313.19,-330 307.19,-336 301.19,-336\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"257.3\" y=\"-318.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Expense\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"255.05\" y=\"-309.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">profit or loss\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge7\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>train&#45;&gt;pl\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M116.28,-318C152.64,-318 203.64,-318 238.76,-318\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"238.49,-320.1 244.49,-318 238.49,-315.9 238.49,-320.1\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"id":"je-1qossf","type":"je","bucket":"initial","lo":14,"q":"A machine costs $95,000 after trade discount. The company also pays import duty $3,000, delivery $2,000 and installation and testing $5,500: $105,500 in {a|cash} in total. It must dismantle the machine and restore the site later; the present value of that {l|obligation} is $5,000. Record the machine on the day it is ready for use, showing only the capitalised amounts (recoverable GST and staff training are recorded separately).","accounts":["Machine (PPE)","Building (PPE)","Land (PPE)","Accumulated depreciation: machine","Accumulated depreciation: building","Cash","GST receivable","Provision for dismantling","Revaluation surplus (OCI)","Retained earnings","Depreciation expense","Revaluation loss (P&L)","Loss on disposal","Gain on disposal","Revenue","Training expense"],"lines":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Machine (PPE)","amount":110500,"el":"a"},{"side":"Cr","account":"Cash","amount":105500,"el":"a"},{"side":"Cr","account":"Provision for dismantling","amount":5000,"el":"l"}],"why":"Every cost of getting it ready is capitalised (110,500). The dismantling obligation is a {l|liability} from day one, so 5,000 is credited to the {l|provision} rather than paid in {a|cash}. {a|GST} and {x|training} are recorded separately.","sect":3,"part":"Initial measurement"},{"type":"think","bucket":"initial","lo":14,"scenario":"Jurong Solar installs solar panels on a leased rooftop for $900,000 plus $60,000 installation. The lease says it must remove them and restore the roof in 10 years, at an estimated cost of $200,000. The discount rate is 5%.","prompt":"Should the panels’ cost include $200,000, something less, or nothing until the removal happens?","answer":["The obligation exists **now** (the panels are up), so it belongs in cost now. But $200,000 paid in 10 years is worth less today, so use the **present value**.","PV = 200,000 ÷ 1.05^10 = **$122,783**. {a|Cost} = 900,000 + 60,000 + 122,783 = $1,082,783.","The same amount is credited to a {l|Provision for dismantling}. Future-you pays the bill; present-you books the asset."],"id":"think-1mau0k","sect":3,"part":"Initial measurement"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"initial","lo":14,"title":"Dismantling: one estimate, two balances","intro":"The dismantling estimate splits into an asset and a liability on day one, and each has its own life after that.","notes":{"est":"What the company expects to pay to remove the panels and restore the roof.","pv":"200,000 ÷ 1.05^10 = 122,783.","asset":"Panels 900,000 + installation 60,000 + 122,783 = 1,082,783.","prov":"A {l|liability} from day one: the obligation already exists.","dep":"1,082,783 ÷ 10 years = 108,278 (nearest dollar). So the dismantling cost reaches P&L through {x|depreciation}.","unw":"Each year the {l|provision} grows by the discount rate: 122,783 × 5% = {x|6,139} of {x|finance cost} in year 1. Beyond your notes, but worth knowing.","end":"By year 10 the {l|provision} has grown to the full 200,000, ready to be paid."},"walk":[{"nodes":["est","pv"],"text":"Discount the future cost to today."},{"nodes":["pv","asset","prov"],"text":"Debit {a|PPE}, credit a {l|provision}: same amount, both sides."},{"nodes":["asset","dep"],"text":"The higher {a|asset cost} is depreciated over the asset’s life."},{"nodes":["prov","unw","end"],"text":"The {l|provision} unwinds (grows) each year as a {x|finance cost}, until it reaches the full amount."}],"caption":"Dismantling hits P&L twice over the years: through {x|depreciation} and through {x|unwinding}.","id":"diagram-18jdek","sect":3,"part":"Initial measurement","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:344px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 313.00 327.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 316.33)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"no