\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"249.14\" y=\"-78.19\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">600,000 a year\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge6\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>cab&#45;&gt;dc\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M280.35,-125.22C280.97,-119.86 281.65,-113.96 282.3,-108.33\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"284.38,-108.61 282.98,-102.41 280.21,-108.13 284.38,-108.61\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node8\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>tot\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#b45309\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M214.53,-39.64C214.53,-39.64 123.75,-39.64 123.75,-39.64 117.75,-39.64 111.75,-33.64 111.75,-27.64 111.75,-27.64 111.75,-12 111.75,-12 111.75,-6 117.75,0 123.75,0 123.75,0 214.53,0 214.53,0 220.53,0 226.53,-6 226.53,-12 226.53,-12 226.53,-27.64 226.53,-27.64 226.53,-33.64 220.53,-39.64 214.53,-39.64\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"122.64\" y=\"-25.87\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Total depreciation\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"128.64\" y=\"-14.87\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">3,780,000 a year\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"120.39\" y=\"-5.77\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">vs 2,400,000 on one life\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge7\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>db&#45;&gt;tot\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M83.85,-64.05C96.58,-57.6 111.17,-50.2 124.64,-43.37\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"125.4,-45.35 129.8,-40.76 123.5,-41.6 125.4,-45.35\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge8\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>de&#45;&gt;tot\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M169.14,-64.05C169.14,-58.84 169.14,-53.01 169.14,-47.37\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"171.24,-47.37 169.14,-41.37 167.04,-47.37 171.24,-47.37\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge9\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>dc&#45;&gt;tot\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M251.59,-64.05C239.39,-57.66 225.44,-50.34 212.51,-43.56\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"213.5,-41.7 207.21,-40.78 211.54,-45.42 213.5,-41.7\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"id":"calc-b96mla","type":"calc","bucket":"subsequent","lo":14,"q":"A machine cost $110,500, with a residual value of $10,500 and a 5-year life, depreciated straight-line. At the start of year 3 the company decides it has only 2 more years of use, and a residual value of $6,500. What is the depreciation charge for year 3?","answer":32000,"unit":"$","working":["{a|Carrying amount} after 2 years = 110,500 − 2 × 20,000 = 70,500.","Prospective {x|depreciation}: (70,500 − 6,500) ÷ 2 remaining years = **$32,000**.","Years 1 and 2 are not restated: it is a change in estimate."],"sect":4,"part":"Subsequent measurement"},{"type":"visual","bucket":"subsequent","lo":14,"title":"A change in estimate, step by step","html":"\u003cp>What does “prospective” look like? On the left, the machine follows its original plan (cost $110,500, 5 years, residual $10,500). On the right, the estimate changes at the start of year 3 to 2 more years and a $6,500 residual. The first two years stay exactly as they were; only the slope from year 3 onwards changes.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"wg\" data-wg=\"roll\" data-key=\"estimate-b12\" data-cfg=\"{&quot;panels&quot;:[{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Original estimate&quot;,&quot;sub&quot;:&quot;5 years, residual 10,500&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;bal&quot;:&quot;Carrying amount&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:110500,&quot;startCap&quot;:&quot;Cost {a|110,500}.&quot;,&quot;years&quot;:[{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Yr 1&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-20000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 1: (110,500 − 10,500) ÷ 5 = {x|20,000}, leaving {a|90,500}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Yr 2&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-20000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 2: (110,500 − 10,500) ÷ 5 = {x|20,000}, leaving {a|70,500}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Yr 3&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-20000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 3: (110,500 − 10,500) ÷ 5 = {x|20,000}, leaving {a|50,500}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Yr 4&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-20000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 4: (110,500 − 10,500) ÷ 5 = {x|20,000}, leaving {a|30,500}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Yr 5&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-20000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 5: (110,500 − 10,500) ÷ 5 = {x|20,000}, leaving {a|10,500}. It stops at the {a|residual value 10,500}.&quot;}]}]},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Revised in year 3&quot;,&quot;sub&quot;:&quot;2 more years, residual 6,500&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;bal&quot;:&quot;Carrying amount&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:110500,&quot;startCap&quot;:&quot;Same machine, same cost {a|110,500}.&quot;,&quot;years&quot;:[{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Yr 1&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-20000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 1: the same {x|20,000}: nothing has changed yet. {a|Carrying amount} {a|90,500}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Yr 2&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-20000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 2: the same {x|20,000}: nothing has changed yet. {a|Carrying amount} {a|70,500}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Yr 3&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-32000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 3: new estimate: 2 years left, residual 6,500. ({a|70,500} − 6,500) ÷ 2 = {x|32,000}, leaving {a|38,500}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Yr 4&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-32000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 4: ({a|70,500} − 6,500) ÷ 2 = {x|32,000}, leaving {a|6,500}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Yr 5&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:0,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 5: already retired at its {a|new residual value 6,500}. No {x|depreciation}.&quot;}]}]}],&quot;notes&quot;:{&quot;start&quot;:&quot;Same machine. On the right, the estimate changes at the start of year 3. Press Play or Next.&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[&quot;Each year the {x|depreciation} charge comes off the {a|carrying amount}.&quot;],&quot;end&quot;:&quot;**Prospective, not retrospective.** Years 1 and 2 are left alone. From year 3 the {a|carrying amount} of {a|70,500} is spread over the 2 remaining years: a steeper slope, landing on the new residual 6,500 two years early.&quot;}}\">\u003c/div>","id":"visual-7gh3jj","sect":4,"part":"Subsequent measurement"},{"type":"mcq","bucket":"subsequent","lo":14,"q":"A machine is ready for use on 1 March but stands idle until 1 July while the factory waits for orders. When does depreciation start?","options":[{"t":"1 July, when production starts","why":"Depreciation starts when the asset is available for use, not when it is first used."},{"t":"1 March, when it is available for use","ok":true,"why":"Available for use is the trigger, even if it sits idle."},{"t":"The date it was ordered","why":"It is not available for use until it is delivered, installed and ready."},{"t":"The start of the next financial year","why":"There is no such rule; depreciate from the date it is available for use."}],"id":"mcq-1b103f","sect":4,"part":"Subsequent measurement"},{"type":"map","id":"map-5-subsequent","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"revaluation","sect":5,"part":"Subsequent measurement · revaluation"},{"type":"think","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"revaluation","lo":15,"scenario":"A company’s head office was bought 20 years ago and is carried at depreciated cost. Its market value is now three times that. The directors want the balance sheet to show what the building is really worth.","prompt":"Is that allowed? And if the building goes up in value, should the gain be in this year’s profit?","answer":["Yes: the **revaluation model** carries {a|PPE} at **fair value**. But it is a choice for a whole **class**, not one favourite building.","The gain is **not** profit. The company hasn’t sold the building and still uses it to run the business. So it goes to **OCI**, into a {e|Revaluation surplus} in equity.","Compare {a|investment property} under the fair value model, where {i|gains} do go to P&L. Different standard, different home."],"id":"think-1snlmv","sect":5,"part":"Subsequent measurement · revaluation"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"revaluation","lo":15,"title":"Two models, chosen per class","body":["So far every number came from cost. Now the head office asks to show what the building is really worth. The standard allows that, with guard rails: a whole class at once, and gains kept out of profit.","Choose a model for **each class** of PPE. If one item is revalued, the **whole class** must be.","1. **Cost model:** {a|cost} − {a|accumulated depreciation} − {a|accumulated impairment losses}.","2. **Revaluation model:** **fair value at the revaluation date** − {a|later accumulated depreciation} − {a|later impairment}. Revalue often enough that the {a|carrying amount} stays close to fair value.","On revaluation, {a|accumulated depreciation} is either **eliminated** against the {a|gross amount} (used in exams) or restated proportionately.","> {e|Revaluation surplus} = Fair value − {a|Carrying amount} at the revaluation date","! Compare fair value with the **{a|carrying amount}**, not the original cost."],"id":"rule-19f7yn","sect":5,"part":"Subsequent measurement · revaluation"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"revaluation","lo":15,"title":"Where a revaluation goes","intro":"This is the chart from your notes. Every revaluation starts by comparing fair value with the carrying amount.","notes":{"s":"Fair value at the revaluation date vs {a|carrying amount} (cost or last valuation, less depreciation since).","up":"Fair value is above the {a|carrying amount}.","dn":"Fair value is below the {a|carrying amount}.","up1":"Did this same asset have an earlier **{x|revaluation loss}** that went to P&L?","up2":"Reverse the earlier {x|loss} in P&L first, then the rest goes to the {e|Revaluation surplus}.","up3":"The normal case: the whole increase goes to OCI.","dn1":"Is there a {e|revaluation surplus} left **for this asset**? Surpluses on other assets don’t count.","dn2":"Use up this asset’s {e|surplus} in OCI first, then the rest is a {x|loss} in P&L.","dn3":"No {e|surplus} to absorb it, so the whole decrease is a {x|P&L loss}."},"walk":[{"nodes":["s"],"text":"Compare fair value with the {a|carrying amount}."},{"nodes":["up","up1","up3"],"text":"An **increase** normally goes to **OCI**, building up the {e|revaluation surplus}."},{"nodes":["up1","up2"],"text":"Unless it reverses an earlier {x|P&L loss} on the same asset: then P&L first, up to that loss."},{"nodes":["dn","dn1","dn2"],"text":"A **decrease** uses up that asset’s {e|surplus} in OCI first, then hits P&L."},{"nodes":["dn1","dn3"],"text":"No {e|surplus}? The whole decrease goes to P&L."}],"caption":"Up → OCI, down → P&L. Each first cancels the other’s earlier effect on the same asset.","id":"diagram-1gh13y","sect":5,"part":"Subsequent measurement · revaluation","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:619px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 563.00 245.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 234.05)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-234.05 551.94,-234.05 551.94,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>s\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M460.4,-223.25C460.4,-223.25 245.88,-223.25 245.88,-223.25 239.88,-223.25 233.88,-217.25 233.88,-211.25 233.88,-211.25 233.88,-199.25 233.88,-199.25 233.88,-193.25 239.88,-187.25 245.88,-187.25 245.88,-187.25 460.4,-187.25 460.4,-187.25 466.4,-187.25 472.4,-193.25 472.4,-199.25 472.4,-199.25 472.4,-211.25 472.4,-211.25 472.4,-217.25 466.4,-223.25 460.4,-223.25\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"242.51\" y=\"-201.8\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"white\">Revaluation: fair value vs carrying amount\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node2\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>up\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#dcfce7\" stroke=\"#166534\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M331.9,-164.25C331.9,-164.25 294.38,-164.25 294.38,-164.25 288.38,-164.25 282.38,-158.25 282.38,-152.25 282.38,-152.25 282.38,-140.25 282.38,-140.25 282.38,-134.25 288.38,-128.25 294.38,-128.25 294.38,-128.25 331.9,-128.25 331.9,-128.25 337.9,-128.25 343.9,-134.25 343.9,-140.25 343.9,-140.25 343.9,-152.25 343.9,-152.25 343.9,-158.25 337.9,-164.25 331.9,-164.25\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"291.01\" y=\"-142.8\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Increase\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge1\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>s&#45;&gt;up\u003c/title>\n\u003cpat