"intro":["A typical exam question: you get the cost, the life and one or two fair values, and must give the entries or the P&L hit. Remember two things:","- Always compare fair value with the {a|carrying amount} on that date, never with the original cost.","- After a revaluation, {x|depreciation} restarts from the revalued amount over the remaining life, and a later fall uses up **this asset’s** {e|surplus} before it touches P&L.","Then follow these steps: carrying amount → revalue up → depreciate and transfer → carrying amount and surplus left → revalue down."],"steps":[{"h":"Find the carrying amount at 31 Dec 20X2.","t":"{a|Carrying amount} = {a|cost 100,000} − 2 × {x|10,000} = **{a|80,000}**"},{"h":"Revalue up: the gain goes to OCI.","t":["{e|Surplus} = fair value 120,000 − {a|carrying amount 80,000} = **{e|40,000}**","Eliminate the {a|accumulated depreciation} (20,000); the {a|building’s gross amount} goes from 100,000 to 120,000."],"je":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Accumulated depreciation: building","amount":20000,"el":"a"},{"side":"Dr","account":"Building (PPE)","amount":20000,"el":"a"},{"side":"Cr","account":"Revaluation surplus (OCI)","amount":40000,"el":"e"}]},{"h":"Depreciate the revalued amount and transfer the excess.","t":["{x|Depreciation} = 120,000 ÷ 8 remaining years = **{x|15,000}** a year in 20X3 and 20X4","Excess over {x|depreciation on cost} = 15,000 − 10,000 = **5,000**, moved from the {e|surplus} to {e|retained earnings}: equity to equity, never through P&L."],"je":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Depreciation expense","amount":15000,"el":"x"},{"side":"Cr","account":"Accumulated depreciation: building","amount":15000,"el":"a"},{"side":"Dr","account":"Revaluation surplus (OCI)","amount":5000,"el":"e"},{"side":"Cr","account":"Retained earnings","amount":5000,"el":"e"}],"after":"This entry is made in 20X3 and again in 20X4."},{"h":"Find the carrying amount and the surplus left at 31 Dec 20X4.","t":["{a|Carrying amount} = 120,000 − 2 × {x|15,000} = **{a|90,000}**","{e|Surplus left} = 40,000 − 2 × 5,000 = **{e|30,000}**"]},{"h":"Revalue down: surplus first, then P&L.","t":["Fall = {a|carrying amount 90,000} − fair value 50,000 = **40,000**","The {e|surplus left} absorbs **{e|30,000}** (OCI); the remaining **{x|10,000}** is a {x|revaluation loss in P&L}."],"je":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Accumulated depreciation: building","amount":30000,"el":"a"},{"side":"Dr","account":"Revaluation surplus (OCI)","amount":30000,"el":"e"},{"side":"Dr","account":"Revaluation loss (P&L)","amount":10000,"el":"x"},{"side":"Cr","account":"Building (PPE)","amount":70000,"el":"a"}],"after":"The {a|building’s gross amount} is now 50,000 with no {a|accumulated depreciation}. The {e|surplus} cushion took the first 30,000 of the fall; P&L caught the rest."}],"id":"worked-128jz1","sect":5,"part":"Subsequent measurement · revaluation"},{"id":"je-17mxpa","type":"je","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"revaluation","lo":15,"q":"Your turn, with two lines filled in. A building bought on 1 Jan 20X1 for $600,000 (12-year life, no residual value, straight-line) is revalued to $540,000 on 31 Dec 20X3. {a|Accumulated depreciation} is eliminated. Complete the entry.","accounts":["Machine (PPE)","Building (PPE)","Land (PPE)","Accumulated depreciation: machine","Accumulated depreciation: building","Cash","GST receivable","Provision for dismantling","Revaluation surplus (OCI)","Retained earnings","Depreciation expense","Revaluation loss (P&L)","Loss on disposal","Gain on disposal","Revenue","Training expense"],"given":[0,1],"lines":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Accumulated depreciation: building","amount":150000,"el":"a"},{"side":"Cr","account":"Building (PPE)","amount":60000,"el":"a"},{"side":"Cr","account":"Revaluation surplus (OCI)","amount":90000,"el":"e"}],"why":"{a|Accumulated depreciation} 600,000 ÷ 12 × 3 = 150,000; {a|carrying amount} 450,000. Fair value 540,000 → {e|surplus} 90,000 to OCI. The {a|building’s gross amount} falls from 600,000 to 540,000, a credit of 60,000.","sect":5,"part":"Subsequent measurement · revaluation"},{"id":"je-7d8phl","type":"je","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"revaluation","lo":15,"q":"Now a blank one. A machine bought on 1 Jan 20X2 for $320,000 has a residual value of $20,000 and a 6-year life (straight-line). On 31 Dec 20X4 it is revalued to $210,000, eliminating {a|accumulated depreciation}. Record the revaluation.","accounts":["Machine (PPE)","Building (PPE)","Land (PPE)","Accumulated depreciation: machine","Accumulated depreciation: building","Cash","GST receivable","Provision for dismantling","Revaluation surplus (OCI)","Retained earnings","Depreciation expense","Revaluation loss (P&L)","Loss on disposal","Gain on disposal","Revenue","Training expense"],"lines":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Accumulated depreciation: machine","amount":150000,"el":"a"},{"side":"Cr","account":"Machine (PPE)","amount":110000,"el":"a"},{"side":"Cr","account":"Revaluation surplus (OCI)","amount":40000,"el":"e"}],"why":"{x|Depreciation} (320,000 − 20,000) ÷ 6 = 50,000 a year × 3 = {a|accumulated depreciation} 150,000. {a|Carrying amount} 170,000. Fair value 210,000 → {e|surplus} 40,000. {a|Gross amount} 320,000 → 210,000: credit 110,000. Forget the residual value and every number is wrong.","sect":5,"part":"Subsequent measurement · revaluation"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"revaluation","lo":15,"title":"The building on a timeline","intro":"The worked example as a timeline. Watch the surplus fill up, drain a little each year, then cushion the fall.","notes":{"y0":"Bought for 100,000, depreciated 10,000 a year.","y2":"{a|Carrying amount} 80,000; fair value 120,000.","oci1":"120,000 − 80,000 = 40,000 into the {e|Revaluation surplus}.","y3":"{x|Depreciation} is now on the revalued amount: 120,000 ÷ 8 = 15,000.","re":"Excess depreciation 15,000 − 10,000 = 5,000 moves from the {e|surplus} to {e|Retained earnings}. Optional, and never through P&L.","y4":"{a|Carrying amount} 90,000; fair value 50,000; fall 40,000.","oci2":"{e|Surplus} left 30,000 absorbs the first part of the fall.","pl":"The rest, 40,000 − 30,000 = 10,000, is a {x|loss} in P&L."},"walk":[{"nodes":["y0","y2","oci1"],"text":"Value rises: 40,000 to OCI."},{"nodes":["y3","re"],"text":"{x|Depreciation} goes up to 15,000; 5,000 a year of {e|surplus} moves to {e|retained earnings}."},{"nodes":["y4","oci2","pl"],"text":"Value falls by 40,000: 30,000 uses up the {e|surplus}, 10,000 hits P&L."}],"caption":"Green = equity (OCI, retained earnings); amber = profit or loss.","id":"diagram-9fh5xq","sect":5,"part":"Subsequent measurement · revaluation","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:640px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 705.00 175.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 163.8)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-163.8 694.45,-163.8 694.45,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>y0\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M66.78,-65C66.78,-65 12,-65 12,-65 6,-65 0,-59 0,-53 0,-53 0,-41 0,-41 0,-35 6,-29 12,-29 12,-29 66.78,-29 66.78,-29 72.78,-29 78.78,-35 78.78,-41 78.78,-41 78.78,-53 78.78,-53 78.78,-59 72.78,-65 66.78,-65\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"11.26\" y=\"-48.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"white\">1 Jan 20X1\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"8.64\" y=\"-37.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"white\">cost 100,000\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node2\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>y2\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e8eef6\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M233.56,-65C233.56,-65 115.78,-65 115.78,-65 109.78,-65 103.78,-59 103.7