" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\"> −10,000\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"610.13\" y=\"-68.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">revaluation loss\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge7\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>y4&#45;&gt;pl\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#b45309\" d=\"M576.47,-91.25C582.3,-89.97 588.11,-88.69 593.74,-87.46\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#b45309\" stroke=\"#b45309\" points=\"593.85,-89.58 599.26,-86.24 592.95,-85.48 593.85,-89.58\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"type":"visual","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"revaluation","lo":15,"title":"Cost model vs revaluation model, step by step","html":"\u003cp>The worked example's building again (cost $100,000 on 1 Jan 20X1, 10-year life), next to the same building under the cost model. Step through the four years and watch where each model's \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">carrying amount\u003c/span> goes.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"wg\" data-wg=\"roll\" data-key=\"reval-b12\" data-cfg=\"{&quot;panels&quot;:[{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Cost model&quot;,&quot;sub&quot;:&quot;100,000 ÷ 10 years&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;bal&quot;:&quot;Carrying amount&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:100000,&quot;startCap&quot;:&quot;1 Jan 20X1: bought for {a|100,000}, 10-year life, no residual value.&quot;,&quot;years&quot;:[{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X1&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-10000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;20X1: {x|depreciation} 100,000 ÷ 10 = {x|10,000}, so {a|carrying amount} = {a|90,000}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X2&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-10000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;20X2: {x|depreciation} 100,000 ÷ 10 = {x|10,000}, so {a|carrying amount} = {a|80,000}.&quot;}],&quot;hold&quot;:&quot;Cost model: fair value is ignored. The building stays at {a|80,000}.&quot;},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X3&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-10000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;20X3: {x|depreciation} 100,000 ÷ 10 = {x|10,000}, so {a|carrying amount} = {a|70,000}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X4&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-10000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;20X4: {x|depreciation} 100,000 ÷ 10 = {x|10,000}, so {a|carrying amount} = {a|60,000}.&quot;}],&quot;hold&quot;:&quot;Cost model: the fall in value is ignored too. It ends 20X4 at {a|60,000}: cost less four years of {x|depreciation}.&quot;}]},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Revaluation model&quot;,&quot;sub&quot;:&quot;fair value 120,000 (20X2), 50,000 (20X4)&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;bal&quot;:&quot;Carrying amount&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:100000,&quot;startCap&quot;:&quot;1 Jan 20X1: the same building, same {a|100,000} cost.&quot;,&quot;years&quot;:[{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X1&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-10000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;20X1: {x|depreciation} {x|10,000}, the same as the cost model.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X2&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-10000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;20X2: {x|depreciation} {x|10,000} again, leaving {a|carrying amount 80,000}.&quot;},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;revaluation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;e&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:40000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;31 Dec 20X2: fair value 120,000 − {a|80,000} = {e|+40,000} to the {e|revaluation surplus} (OCI), not profit.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X3&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-15000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;20X3: {x|depreciation} restarts from the revalued amount: 120,000 ÷ 8 = {x|15,000}. 5,000 of {e|surplus} moves to {e|retained earnings}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X4&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-15000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;20X4: {x|depreciation} {x|15,000} again, leaving {a|carrying amount 90,000}. {e|Surplus left}: 40,000 − 2 × 5,000 = {e|30,000}.&quot;},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;surplus used&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;e&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-30000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;31 Dec 20X4: fair value 50,000 is 40,000 below. The first {e|30,000} uses up this building’s {e|surplus} (OCI).&quot;},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;P&amp;L loss&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-10000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;The other {x|10,000} is a {x|revaluation loss in P&amp;L}. The building now sits at fair value {a|50,000}.&quot;}]}]}],&quot;notes&quot;:{&quot;start&quot;:&quot;One building, two models, four years. Press Play or Next.&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[&quot;{x|Depreciation} takes the {a|carrying amount} down every year.&quot;,&quot;A **rise** goes to the {e|revaluation surplus} (OCI); a **fall** uses up that {e|surplus} first…&quot;,&quot;…and only the rest is a {x|loss} in P&amp;L.&quot;],&quot;end&quot;:&quot;**Same building, different stories.** Cost model: {x|40,000} of {x|depreciation} in P&amp;L, ending at {a|60,000}. Revaluation model: {x|60,000} in P&amp;L (higher {x|depreciation} after the revaluation, plus the {x|10,000} loss), ending at fair value {a|50,000}. The {e|40,000} surplus is all gone: 10,000 transferred to {e|retained earnings}, 30,000 used by the fall.&quot;}}\">\u003c/div>","id":"visual-ynu8vz","sect":5,"part":"Subsequent measurement · revaluation"},{"id":"think-1awjfp","type":"think","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"revaluation","lo":15,"scenario":"A building is carried under the revaluation model. Its revaluation at 31 Dec 20X2 created a {e|surplus} of $40,000. With yearly excess-depreciation transfers of $5,000, only $30,000 was left by 31 Dec 20X4, when fair value fell $40,000 below the {a|carrying amount}. Now suppose the company **never** made those transfers. The value still falls by $40,000.","prompt":"How much now goes to OCI and how much to P&L?","answer":["The {e|surplus} would still be the full 40,000, enough to absorb the whole 40,000 fall. So **40,000 to OCI and 0 to P&L**.","Always read whether transfers are made. The size of the cushion decides the P&L hit."],"sect":5,"part":"Subsequent measurement · revaluation"},{"id":"tree-qe2knv","type":"tree","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"revaluation","lo":15,"title":"Where does this revaluation go?","scenario":"A building under the revaluation model, at 31 Dec 20X4: {a|carrying amount} $90,000, fair value $50,000, {e|surplus} left on this building $30,000. Tap your way through.","expect":"dnSplit","start":"r1","nodes":{"r1":{"q":"Is fair value above or below the {a|carrying amount}?","why":"Increases and decreases have different homes.","opts":[{"t":"Above: an increase","to":"r2"},{"t":"Below: a decrease","to":"r3"}]},"r2":{"q":"Does it reverse an earlier {x|revaluation loss} on this asset that went to P&L?","why":"P&L took the earlier hit, so P&L gets the recovery, up to that amount.","opts":[{"t":"Yes","to":"upSplit"},{"t":"No","to":"upOci"}]},"r3":{"q":"Is there a {e|revaluation surplus} left for this same asset?","why":"A decrease first uses up that asset’s own {e|surplus}. Surpluses on other assets can’t be used.","opts":[{"t":"Yes, and it covers the whole fall","to":"dnOci"},{"t":"Yes, but less than the fall","to":"dnSplit"},{"t":"No","to":"dnPl"}]},"upSplit":{"result":"P&L up to the earlier {x|loss}, the rest to OCI","body":["Reverse the old {x|loss} in P&L first; anything above that builds the {e|Revaluation surplus}."]},"upOci":{"result":"All to OCI ({e|revaluation surplus})","body":["The normal increase: credit the {e|Revaluation surplus (OCI)}."]},"dnOci":{"result":"All to OCI","body":["The {e|surplus} is big enough to absorb the whole fall. Nothing in P&L."]},"dnSplit":{"result":"OCI up to the {e|surplus}, the rest to P&L","body":["Here: 30,000 debited to the {e|revaluation surplus}, 10,000 to P&L as a {x|revaluation loss}."]},"dnPl":{"result":"All to P&L","body":["No {e|surplus} to absorb it: the whole decrease is a {x|Revaluation loss (P&L)}."]}},"sect":5,"part":"Subsequent measurement · revaluation","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:640px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 602.00 224.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 213.19)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-213.19 591.58,-213.19 591.58,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>r1\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#b45309\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M335.4,-202.39C335.4,-202.39 210.88,-202.39 210.88,-202.39 204.88,-202.39 198.88,-196.39 198.88,-190.39 198.88,-190.39 198.88,-178.39 198.88,-178.39 198.88,-172.39 204.88,-166.39 210.88,-166.39 210.88,-166.39 335.4,-166.39 335.4,-166.39 341.4,-166.39 347.4,-172.39 347.4,-178.39 347.4,-178.39 347.4,-190.39 347.4,-190.39 347.4,-196.39 341.4,-202.39 335.4,-202.39\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"273.14\" y=\"-185.94\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Is fair value above or below\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"273.14\" y=\"-173.94\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">the carrying amount?\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node2\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>r2\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#b45309\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M253.15,-129.14C253.15,-129.14 139.12,-129.14 139.12,-129.14 133.12,-129.14 127.12,-123.14 127.12,-117.14 127.12,-117.1