ew {x|depreciation}: 480,000 ÷ 15 = 32,000. Old: 20,000.","Excess = 32,000 − 20,000 = **$12,000** (the same as 180,000 ÷ 15 years)."],"sect":5,"part":"Subsequent measurement · revaluation"},{"id":"mcq-11cx6a","type":"mcq","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"revaluation","lo":15,"q":"Last year a revalued machine fell in value, and a $40,000 {x|loss} went to P&L (it had no {e|surplus}). This year its {a|carrying amount} is $300,000 and fair value is $370,000. How is the increase treated?","options":[{"t":"$70,000 to OCI","why":"Part of the increase reverses last year’s {x|P&L loss} on this asset, so that part goes to P&L."},{"t":"$40,000 to P&L, $30,000 to OCI","ok":true,"why":"The first 40,000 reverses the earlier {x|P&L loss}; the remaining 30,000 goes to the {e|revaluation surplus}."},{"t":"$70,000 to P&L","why":"Only the reversal of the earlier loss goes to P&L; the rest builds a {e|surplus} in OCI."},{"t":"No entry: the machine stays at its {a|carrying amount}","why":"Under the revaluation model the asset is carried at fair value."}],"sect":5,"part":"Subsequent measurement · revaluation"},{"type":"map","id":"map-6-subsequent","bucket":"subsequent","sect":6,"part":"Subsequent measurement"},{"type":"compare","bucket":"subsequent","preamble":"PPE and investment property both allow a value-based model, but the gains land in different places: OCI for PPE, P&L for investment property. A lessee’s ROU asset is depreciated just like PPE.","lo":15,"special":"PPE is **depreciated by components**, and under the **revaluation model** gains go to **OCI**, falls use up that asset’s {e|surplus} first, and the surplus drains to {e|retained earnings}, never P&L.","id":"compare-1kumyt-2","sect":6,"part":"Subsequent measurement"},{"type":"map","id":"map-7-derecognise","bucket":"derecognise","sect":7,"part":"Derecognise / transfer"},{"id":"think-byk1jn","type":"think","bucket":"derecognise","lo":14,"scenario":"A machine (cost $110,500, {x|depreciation} $20,000 a year since it was bought at the start of year 1) is sold at the end of year 3 for $45,000 {a|cash}.","prompt":"{i|Gain} or {x|loss}? And what do you compare the {a|cash} with?","answer":["Compare with the **{a|carrying amount}**, not cost: 110,500 − 3 × 20,000 = 50,500.","45,000 − 50,500 = **{x|loss of 5,500}** in profit or loss.","Remove both the {a|cost} and its {a|accumulated depreciation} from the books."],"sect":7,"part":"Derecognise / transfer"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"derecognise","lo":14,"title":"Disposal","body":["The machine’s life ends with a sale. This exit rule is the same for every asset class: compare what you get with what is still on the books.","Derecognise PPE on **disposal**, or when no future benefits are expected from its use or disposal.","> {i|Gain} or {x|loss} = {a|Net disposal proceeds} − {a|Carrying amount} → profit or loss","1. Remove the **{a|cost}** (credit the {a|asset}).","2. Remove its **{a|accumulated depreciation}** (debit).","3. Record the {a|proceeds}; the balancing figure is the {i|gain} or {x|loss}.","- A {i|gain} is **not revenue**.","- For a revalued asset, any **{e|revaluation surplus}** left may go **directly to {e|retained earnings}**. It is never recycled through P&L."],"id":"rule-1lclg8","sect":7,"part":"Derecognise / transfer"},{"id":"je-i1bvxp","type":"je","bucket":"derecognise","lo":14,"q":"A machine cost $110,500 and is depreciated straight-line at $20,000 a year. Record its sale at the end of year 3 for $45,000 cash.","accounts":["Machine (PPE)","Building (PPE)","Land (PPE)","Accumulated depreciation: machine","Accumulated depreciation: building","Cash","GST receivable","Provision for dismantling","Revaluation surplus (OCI)","Retained earnings","Depreciation expense","Revaluation loss (P&L)","Loss on disposal","Gain on disposal","Revenue","Training expense"],"lines":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Cash","amount":45000,"el":"a"},{"side":"Dr","account":"Accumulated depreciation: machine","amount":60000,"el":"a"},{"side":"Dr","account":"Loss on disposal","amount":5500,"el":"x"},{"side":"Cr","account":"Machine (PPE)","amount":110500,"el":"a"}],"why":"{a|Accumulated depreciation} 3 × 20,000 = 60,000. {a|Carrying amount} 50,500. 45,000 − 50,500 = {x|loss} of 5,500.","sect":7,"part":"Derecognise / transfer"},{"type":"visual","bucket":"derecognise","lo":14,"title":"The disposal in three bars","html":"\u003cp>The sale you just recorded, as layers. The top bar is the machine’s \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">cost\u003c/span>: the hatched part has already been written off as \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">accumulated depreciation\u003c/span> (a \u003cstrong>contra-asset\u003c/strong> account, so it is coloured like the asset it reduces), and the solid part is what is left, the \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">carrying amount\u003c/span>. Only the carrying amount is compared with the \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">cash\u003c/span>: the gap is the \u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">loss\u003c/span>.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"cbars\">\n    \u003cdiv class=\"cb-year\">\u003cdiv class=\"cb-cap\">\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">Cost\u003c/span> 110,500 = \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">accumulated depreciation\u003c/span> 60,000 + \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">carrying amount\u003c/span> 50,500\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-track\">\u003ci class=\"seg out-a\" style=\"width:54.30%\">\u003c/i>\u003ci class=\"seg a\" style=\"width:45.70%\">\u003c/i>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\n    \u003cdiv class=\"cb-year\">\u003cdiv class=\"cb-cap\">\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">Carrying amount\u003c/span> 50,500\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-track\">\u003ci class=\"seg a\" style=\"width:45.70%\">\u003c/i>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\n    \u003cdiv class=\"cb-year\">\u003cdiv class=\"cb-cap\">\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">Proceeds\u003c/span> 45,000 + \u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">loss\u003c/span> 5,500\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-track\">\u003ci class=\"seg a\" style=\"width:40.72%\">\u003c/i>\u003ci class=\"seg x\" style=\"width:4.98%\">\u003c/i>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\n    \u003cdiv class=\"cb-key\">\u003cspan>\u003ci class=\"seg out-a\">\u003c/i>\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">accumulated depreciation\u003c/span> (contra asset: already written off)\u003c/span>\u003cspan>\u003ci class=\"seg a\">\u003c/i>\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">carrying amount\u003c/span> / \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">cash\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan>\u003ci class=\"seg x\">\u003c/i>\u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">loss on disposal\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\u003cp class=\"cap\">Both layers of the top bar leave the books: credit \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">Machine (PPE)\u003c/span> 110,500, debit \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">accumulated depreciation\u003c/span> 60,000.\u003c/p>","id":"visual-12p6j0","sect":7,"part":"Derecognise / transfer"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"derecognise","lo":14,"title":"Disposal: what goes where","intro":"Selling PPE moves up to two things: the {i|gain} or {x|loss} goes to P&L, and any old {e|revaluation surplus} stays in equity.","notes":{"cash":"{a|Net disposal proceeds}: price less any selling costs.","ca":"{a|Cost} less {a|accumulated depreciation}: 110,500 − 60,000 = 50,500.","gl":"45,000 − 50,500 = {x|(5,500)}.","pl":"{i|Gains} and {x|losses} on disposal go to profit or loss. A {i|gain} is {i|other income}, not revenue.","rs":"Only if the asset was revalued and some {e|surplus} is left.","re":"Moved straight to {e|Retained earnings}."},"walk":[{"nodes":["cash","ca","gl"],"text":"{a|Proceeds} − {a|carrying amount} = {x|loss} of 5,500."},{"nodes":["gl","pl"],"text":"The {i|gain} or {x|loss} goes to profit or loss."},{"nodes":["rs","re"],"text":"Any {e|revaluation surplus} may move directly to {e|retained earnings}…"},{"nodes":["rs","pl"],"text":"…but never through P&L."}],"caption":"Same exit rule for every asset: {a|proceeds} vs {a|carrying amount}.","id":"diagram-14p9eg","sect":7,"part":"Derecognise / transfer","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:571px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 519.00