"-23.87\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Investment property\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"325.92\" y=\"-23.87\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\"> (SFRS(I) 1&#45;40)\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"259.54\" y=\"-14.77\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">to earn rentals, for capital\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"268.92\" y=\"-5.77\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">appreciation, or both\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge4\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>q&#45;&gt;ip\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M101.37,-82.25C110.7,-78.56 120.52,-74.82 129.78,-71.57 162.37,-60.12 198.85,-49.11 230.41,-40.14\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"230.83,-42.21 236.03,-38.55 229.68,-38.16 230.83,-42.21\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"161.65\" y=\"-73.32\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> rent / growth \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"type":"think","bucket":"classify","lo":17,"scenario":"Orchid Realty owns a 10-storey building. It uses 1 floor as its own head office and leases the other 9 floors to tenants. It also provides security guards and cleaning of the lobby for all tenants.","prompt":"Is the building investment property, PPE, or both? And do the security and cleaning services change anything?","answer":["If the floors **could be sold or leased out separately**, split it: 9 floors are {a|investment property}, 1 floor is {a|PPE}.","If they could not be separated, the whole building is {a|investment property} **only if the owner-occupied part is insignificant**. Otherwise all of it is {a|PPE}.","Security and cleaning are **insignificant** services. They don’t change the answer. Compare a **hotel**: the owner provides significant services to guests, so a hotel is owner-occupied {a|PPE}."],"id":"think-1w6ayg","sect":1,"part":"Classify"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"classify","lo":17,"title":"Mixed use and services to occupants","body":["Real buildings are messy: part rented, part used, often with services thrown in. These rules decide what happens when one building does two jobs at once.","- **Part owner-occupied:** if the parts could be sold or leased out separately, account for them separately. If not, it is {a|investment property} only if the owner-occupied part is **insignificant**.","- **Services to occupants:** insignificant (security, maintenance, cleaning of an office block) → still {a|investment property}. Significant (a hotel run by its owner) → {a|PPE}.","- **Within a group:** a building a parent leases to its subsidiary can be {a|investment property} in the parent’s own financial statements, but it is owner-occupied {a|PPE} in the group’s consolidated statements."],"id":"rule-t1clmf","sect":1,"part":"Classify"},{"id":"tree-jpcafe","type":"tree","bucket":"classify","lo":17,"title":"Which standard? Classify a property","scenario":"Orchid Realty owns a 10-storey building: 1 floor used as its own head office, 9 floors leased to tenants under operating leases. Each floor can be leased out separately. Orchid provides security and lobby cleaning. Tap your way to the answer.","expect":"split","start":"n1","nodes":{"n1":{"q":"Is it land or a building (or part of one)?","why":"Investment property is only ever land or buildings. Equipment, even if rented out, falls under other standards.","opts":[{"t":"Yes","to":"n2"},{"t":"No, it is equipment or another asset","to":"other"}]},"n2":{"q":"Is it held for sale in the ordinary course of business?","why":"A developer’s stock earns its profit when sold, so it is inventory however long it sits unsold.","opts":[{"t":"Yes, it is stock we build or buy to sell","to":"inv"},{"t":"No","to":"n3"}]},"n3":{"q":"Does the entity use it itself (production, services, admin, staff housing)?","why":"Property used in operations wears out as it is used, so it follows the PPE rules.","opts":[{"t":"Yes, all of it","to":"ppe"},{"t":"Partly: some own use, some leased out","to":"n4"},{"t":"No","to":"n6"}]},"n4":{"q":"Could the parts be sold or leased out separately?","why":"If the parts are separable, each part gets the accounting that fits its own use.","opts":[{"t":"Yes","to":"split"},{"t":"No","to":"n5"}]},"n5":{"q":"Is the owner-occupied part insignificant?","why":"An inseparable building gets one classification, so the main use decides.","opts":[{"t":"Yes, only a small part is used by the owner","to":"ip"},{"t":"No","to":"ppe"}]},"n6":{"q":"Is it leased out under a finance lease?","why":"Under a finance lease the lessor has, in substance, sold the property on credit.","opts":[{"t":"Yes","to":"rec"},{"t":"No: operating lease, vacant, or held for growth","to":"n7"}]},"n7":{"q":"What services does the owner provide to the occupants?","why":"Significant services (a hotel) mean the business is really running an operation, not holding an investment.","opts":[{"t":"None, or insignificant ones (security, cleaning)","to":"ip"},{"t":"Significant ones, as in a hotel","to":"hotel"}]},"other":{"result":"Not investment property","body":["SFRS(I) 1-40 covers land and buildings only. Rented-out equipment stays under SFRS(I) 1-16 (and SFRS(I) 16 for the lease)."]},"inv":{"result":"Inventory (SFRS(I) 1-2)","body":["Held for sale in the ordinary course of business. Measured at the lower of cost and net realisable value.","! A developer’s unsold units are inventory, not investment property, even while they wait for a buyer."]},"ppe":{"result":"PPE (SFRS(I) 1-16)","body":["Owner-occupied: used to make goods, supply services or for administration, including housing for staff.","- Cost or revaluation model, depreciated."]},"split":{"result":"Split: the leased floors are investment property, the head-office floor is PPE","body":["The parts can be leased out separately, so each part follows its own use.","- 9 floors → {a|Investment property} (SFRS(I) 1-40).","- 1 floor → {a|PPE} (SFRS(I) 1-16).","Security and lobby cleaning are insignificant services, so they don’t change this."]},"ip":{"result":"Investment property (SFRS(I) 1-40)","body":["Held to earn rentals, for capital appreciation, or both.","- Initially at {a|cost}; afterwards the fair value model or the cost model."]},"rec":{"result":"Lease receivable (lessor, SFRS(I) 16)","body":["A finance lease transfers substantially all the risks and rewards. The lessor derecognises the property and recognises a {a|Lease receivable}."]},"hotel":{"result":"PPE (owner-occupied)","body":["Significant services such as a hotel’s make the property part of an operating business, so it is owner-occupied {a|PPE}."]}},"sect":1,"part":"Classify","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:640px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 667.00 589.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 578.08)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-578.08 655.82,-578.08 655.82,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>n1\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#b45309\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M346.52,-567.28C346.52,-567.28 235.49,-567.28 235.49,-567.28 229.49,-567.28 223.49,-561.28 223.49,-555.28 223.49,-555.28 223.49,-543.28 223.49,-543.28 223.49,-537.28 229.49,-531.28 235.49,-531.28 235.49,-531.28 346.52,-531.28 346.52,-531.28 352.52,-531.28 358.52,-537.28 358.52,-543.28 358.52,-543.28 358.52,-555.28 358.52,-555.28 358.52,-561.28 352.52,-567.28 346.52,-567.28\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"291\" y=\"-550.83