03ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"211.5\" y=\"-50.75\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> Below \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"id":"worked-8y9t7d","type":"worked","bucket":"derecognise","lo":18,"title":"Worked example: PPE → investment property","q":"On 30 Jun 20X3 Lim Holdings vacates its office ({a|cost} $1,000,000, {a|accumulated depreciation} to that date $200,000) and leases it out. Fair value is $950,000. At 31 Dec 20X3, fair value is $1,000,000. Fair value model.","intro":["A typical exam question: an owner moves out of its building and leases it out, and you must give the transfer entry and the year-end entry. Remember two things:","- Up to the date of change it is still {a|PPE}: depreciate it to that date, then compare fair value with the {a|carrying amount}.","- The increase on the transfer is treated as a **PPE revaluation** ({e|revaluation surplus}, OCI). Every change **after** the transfer goes to **profit or loss**.","Then follow these steps: depreciate to the date of change → compare → transfer entry → year-end remeasurement."],"steps":[{"h":"Depreciate up to the date of change.","t":"The building is {a|PPE} until 30 Jun 20X3, so it is depreciated to that date. {a|Accumulated depreciation} is then {a|200,000}."},{"h":"Compare fair value with the carrying amount.","t":["{a|Carrying amount} = {a|cost 1,000,000} − {a|accumulated depreciation 200,000} = **{a|800,000}**","Increase = fair value 950,000 − {a|800,000} = **{e|150,000}**"]},{"h":"Record the transfer.","t":"Treat the increase as a PPE revaluation: it goes to the {e|revaluation surplus} in OCI. Remove the {a|PPE cost} and its {a|accumulated depreciation}; bring in the {a|investment property} at fair value.","je":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Investment property","amount":950000,"el":"a"},{"side":"Dr","account":"Accumulated depreciation: building","amount":200000,"el":"a"},{"side":"Cr","account":"Building (PPE)","amount":1000000,"el":"a"},{"side":"Cr","account":"Revaluation surplus (OCI)","amount":150000,"el":"e"}]},{"h":"Remeasure at the year end.","t":"Now it is {a|investment property} under the fair value model: 1,000,000 − 950,000 = **{i|50,000}**, a {i|fair value gain} in **profit or loss**. No more {x|depreciation}.","je":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Investment property","amount":50000,"el":"a"},{"side":"Cr","account":"Fair value gain on investment property","amount":50000,"el":"i"}],"after":"Two different homes for two gains on the same building: the gain while it was {a|PPE} goes to the {e|revaluation surplus} (OCI); the gain after it became {a|investment property} is {i|income} in P&L. Same bricks, new job, new rules."}],"sect":5,"part":"Derecognise / transfer"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"derecognise","lo":18,"title":"Lim’s building on a timeline","intro":"The worked example as a timeline. Watch the home for the gain change on the day the use changes.","notes":{"ppe":"PPE rules apply right up to the date of change: depreciate to 30 Jun. {a|Carrying amount} 1,000,000 − 200,000 = 800,000.","move":"The **date of change in use**: the property is remeasured to fair value and becomes {a|investment property}.","oci":"950,000 − 800,000 = 150,000. Treated as a PPE revaluation, so it goes to the {e|Revaluation surplus (OCI)}.","ye":"Now {a|investment property} under the fair value model: remeasure at each year end, no {x|depreciation}.","pl":"1,000,000 − 950,000 = 50,000, a {i|Fair value gain on investment property} in P&L."},"walk":[{"nodes":["ppe"],"text":"Until the use changes, it is {a|PPE}: depreciate up to the date of change."},{"nodes":["move","oci"],"text":"On the date of change, remeasure to fair value. The 150,000 increase goes to the {e|revaluation surplus} in **OCI**, like a PPE revaluation."},{"nodes":["ye","pl"],"text":"From then on it is {a|investment property}: the 50,000 year-end {i|gain} goes to **P&L**."},{"nodes":["oci","pl"],"text":"Same building, two gains, two homes. The date of change is the dividing line."}],"caption":"Before the change: PPE rules. After it: investment property rules.","id":"diagram-xcpnm9","sect":5,"part":"Derecognise / transfer","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:592px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 538.00 144.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 133.44)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-133.44 526.89,-133.44 526.89,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>ppe\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e8eef6\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M99.78,-122.64C99.78,-122.64 12,-122.64 12,-122.64 6,-122.64 0,-116.64 0,-110.64 0,-110.64 0,-95 0,-95 0,-89 6,-83 12,-83 12,-83 99.78,-83 99.78,-83 105.78,-83 111.78,-89 111.78,-95 111.78,-95 111.78,-110.64 111.78,-110.64 111.78,-116.64 105.78,-122.64 99.78,-122.64\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"8.64\" y=\"-108.87\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Up to 30 Jun 20X3\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"13.51\" y=\"-97.87\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">PPE, depreciated\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"31.51\" y=\"-88.77\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">CA 800,000\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node2\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>move\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M291.06,-122.64C291.06,-122.64 215.28,-122.64 215.28,-122.64 209.28,-122.64 203.28,-116.64 203.28,-110.64 203.28,-110.64 203.28,-95 203.28,-95 203.28,-89 209.28,-83 215.28,-83 215.28,-83 291.06,-83 291.06,-83 297.06,-83 303.06