 transfer","Loss on transfer","Revaluation surplus (OCI)","Retained earnings","Depreciation expense","Rental income","Legal fees expense"],"given":[0,2],"lines":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Investment property","amount":2100000},{"side":"Dr","account":"Accumulated depreciation: building","amount":600000},{"side":"Cr","account":"Building (PPE)","amount":2400000},{"side":"Cr","account":"Revaluation surplus (OCI)","amount":300000}],"why":"{a|Carrying amount} 2,400,000 − 600,000 = 1,800,000. Fair value 2,100,000 → increase {e|300,000} to the {e|revaluation surplus} (OCI), as for a PPE revaluation.","sect":5,"part":"Derecognise / transfer"},{"type":"je","bucket":"derecognise","lo":18,"q":"Now a blank one. Sengkang Pte Ltd bought its office building on 1 Jan 20X1 for $1,500,000 (building only, 50-year life, no residual value, straight-line). On 1 Jan 20X6, it moves out and leases the building to a tenant. Fair value at that date is $1,800,000. Fair value model. Record the transfer.","accounts":["Investment property","Building (PPE)","Accumulated depreciation: building","Inventory","Cash","Fair value gain on investment property","Fair value loss on investment property","Gain on transfer","Loss on transfer","Revaluation surplus (OCI)","Retained earnings","Depreciation expense","Rental income","Legal fees expense"],"lines":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Investment property","amount":1800000},{"side":"Dr","account":"Accumulated depreciation: building","amount":150000},{"side":"Cr","account":"Building (PPE)","amount":1500000},{"side":"Cr","account":"Revaluation surplus (OCI)","amount":450000}],"why":"{a|Accumulated depreciation} = 1,500,000 ÷ 50 × 5 years = 150,000. {a|Carrying amount} 1,350,000; fair value 1,800,000 → increase 450,000 to the {e|revaluation surplus} (OCI).","id":"je-1rgsw1","sect":5,"part":"Derecognise / transfer"},{"id":"mcq-14maki","type":"mcq","bucket":"derecognise","lo":18,"q":"An owner-occupied building ({a|cost} $900,000, {a|accumulated depreciation} $150,000) is leased out. It has never been revalued. Fair value at the date of change is $700,000. Fair value model. How is the difference treated?","options":[{"t":"50,000 debited to the {e|revaluation surplus} (OCI)","why":"There is no {e|surplus} on this building to use up, so the decrease cannot go to OCI."},{"t":"50,000 recognised as a {x|loss} in profit or loss","ok":true,"why":"{a|Carrying amount} 750,000 − fair value 700,000 = 50,000. As for a PPE revaluation decrease, it is a {x|loss} in P&L (there is no earlier {e|surplus} on this building)."},{"t":"No loss: the property is transferred at its {a|carrying amount}","why":"That is the cost-model treatment. Under the fair value model it comes in at fair value."},{"t":"50,000 debited directly to {e|retained earnings}","why":"A {x|loss} is never taken straight to {e|retained earnings}."}],"sect":5,"part":"Derecognise / transfer"},{"id":"think-1q9j1j","type":"think","bucket":"derecognise","lo":18,"scenario":"A developer has an unsold flat in {a|inventory} at $600,000. Instead of waiting for a buyer, it signs an operating lease with a tenant. Fair value is $680,000. It uses the fair value model.","prompt":"The flat is now investment property. Where does the $80,000 difference go: OCI, like a PPE transfer, or profit or loss?","answer":["**Profit or loss.** The flat was trading stock ({a|inventory}). Had the developer sold it, the margin would have been profit; moving it to fair value recognises that same profit as a {i|gain}.","Only property the entity **used itself** ({a|PPE}) sends its transfer gain to the {e|revaluation surplus} (OCI)."],"sect":5,"part":"Derecognise / transfer"},{"id":"je-1lsiv0","type":"je","bucket":"derecognise","lo":18,"q":"A developer carries an unsold flat in {a|inventory} at $600,000. It signs an operating lease with a tenant, so the flat becomes investment property; fair value at that date is $680,000. It uses the fair value model. Record the transfer.","accounts":["Investment property","Building (PPE)","Accumulated depreciation: building","Inventory","Cash","Fair value gain on investment property","Fair value loss on investment property","Gain on transfer","Loss on transfer","Revaluation surplus (OCI)","Retained earnings","Depreciation expense","Rental income","Legal fees expense"],"lines":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Investment property","amount":680000},{"side":"Cr","account":"Inventory","amount":600000},{"side":"Cr","account":"Gain on transfer","amount":80000}],"why":"Fair value 680,000 − {a|carrying amount} 600,000 = {i|80,000 gain}, to profit or loss.","sect":5,"part":"Derecognise / transfer"},{"type":"visual","bucket":"derecognise","lo":18,"title":"Two ways into investment property, step by step","html":"\u003cp>Both properties become \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">investment property\u003c/span> at fair value, and both carrying amounts go \u003cstrong>up\u003c/strong> on the day. The bars show the same jump; the colour shows where the other side of the entry goes. Left, Lim’s former office (from \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">PPE\u003c/span>): the increase is an \u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">equity\u003c/span> layer in the \u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">revaluation surplus\u003c/span> (OCI), then a later \u003cspan class=\"el el-i\">gain\u003c/span> in P&amp;L. Right, the developer’s flat (from \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">inventory\u003c/span>): the increase is \u003cspan class=\"el el-i\">income\u003c/span> in P&amp;L straight away.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"wg\" data-wg=\"roll\" data-key=\"transfers-b13\" data-cfg=\"{&quot;panels&quot;:[{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;PPE → IP&quot;,&quot;sub&quot;:&quot;Lim’s office&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;bal&quot;:&quot;Carrying amount&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:800000,&quot;startCap&quot;:&quot;30 Jun 20X3, still {a|PPE}: {a|cost 1,000,000} − {a|accumulated depreciation 200,000} = {a|800,000}.&quot;,&quot;years&quot;:[{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X3&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;transfer to fair value&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;e&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:150000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;30 Jun: up to fair value 950,000. The {e|150,000} increase goes to the {e|revaluation surplus} (OCI), like a PPE revaluation.&quot;},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;year-end gain&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;i&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:50000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;31 Dec: now {a|investment property}. 1,000,000 − 950,000 = {i|50,000 gain} in **P&amp;L**. {a|Closing} = {a|1,000,000}.&quot;}]}]},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Inventory → IP&quot;,&quot;sub&quot;:&quot;developer’s flat&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;bal&quot;:&quot;Carrying amount&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:600000,&quot;startCap&quot;:&quot;Unsold flat in {a|inventory} at {a|600,000}.&quot;,&quot;years&quot;:[{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X3&quot;,&quot;hold&quot;:&quot;From here on it is ordinary {a|investment property}: any later change in fair value goes to P&amp;L too.&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;transfer to fair value&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;i&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:80000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Operating lease signed: up to fair value 680,000. The {i|80,000} increase is a {i|gain} in **P&amp;L**: the profit it would have made selling it.&quot;}]}]}],&quot;notes&quot;:{&quot;start&quot;:&quot;Two properties move into investment property under the fair value model. Press Play or Next.&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[&quot;Step 1, the date of change: remeasure to fair value. **Where it came from** decides where the increase goes.&quot;,&quot;Step 2, the year end: once it is {a|investment property}, every change in fair value goes to **P&amp;L**, whatever its past.&quot;],&quot;end&quot;:&quot;**Same jump, different homes.** From {a|PPE}: 150,000 to {e|OCI}, then 50,000 to {i|P&amp;L}. From {a|inventory}: 80,000 to {i|P&amp;L} at once. Only used-by-the-owner property gets the OCI treatment on the way in.&quot;}}\">\u003c/div>","id":"visual-1eel42","sect":5,"part":"Derecognise / transfer"},{"id":"think-1fqdo0","type":"think","bucket":"derecognise","lo":18,"scenario":"A company has carried a building as {a|investment property} at fair value, $3,000,000 at 31 Dec 20X4. On 1 Jul 20X5, it moves its own head office in. Fair value that day is $3,120,000.","prompt":"It is PPE now, and PPE is depreciated from its cost. But what is its “cost”?","answer":["1. Remeasure it to fair value at the date of change: the 120,000 increase is a {i|fair value gain} in P&L, like any fair value change on {a|investment property}.","2. That fair value, $3,120,000, becomes the **{a|PPE’s deemed cost}**. The original purchase price is no longer relevant. {x|Depreciation} runs from 1 Jul 20X5 on 3,120,000."],"sect":5,"part":"Derecognise / transfer"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"derecognise","lo":18,"title":"Transfers out of investment property","body":["We have seen properties come **into** investment property. Going the other way is simpler: the fair value on the day of the move becomes the new starting cost.","- **IP → PPE** (owner-occupation starts) and **IP → inventory** (development with a view to sale starts): fair value at the date of change becomes the **{a|deemed cost}**.","- A decision to **sell without development** is not a change in use: the property stays {a|investment property} until it is sold.","- **Cost model:** every transfer is at **{a|carrying amount}**, so nothing is remeasured.","! After IP → PPE, depreciate the {a|PPE} from the **fair value at the date of change**, not from the {a|original cost}."],"id":"rule-1jle3r","sect":5,"part":"Derecognise / transfer"},{"id":"calc-1q8qbf","type":"calc","bucket":"derecognise","lo":18,"q":"A building carried as {a|investment property} under the fair value model ($3,000,000 at 31 Dec 20X4) becomes the owner’s head office on 1 Jul 20X5, when its fair value is $3,120,000. It has a remaining useful life of 30 years from that date (building only, no residual value, straight-line). What is its {a|carrying amount} as {a|PPE} at 31 Dec 20X5?","answer":3068000,"unit":"$","working":["{a|Deemed cost} = fair value at the date of change = 3,120,000.","{x|Depreciation} for 6 months = 3,120,000 ÷ 30 × 6/12 = 52,000.","{a|Carrying amount} = 3,120,000 − 52,000 = **$3,068,000**."],"sect":5,"part":"Derecognise / transfer"},{"type":"visual","bucket":"derecognise","lo":18,"title":"IP → PPE: the building’s 20X5, step by step","html":"\u003cp>The calculation you just did, as a picture. One building, two regimes in one year: while it is \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">investment property\u003c/span> it moves with fair value; from 1 Jul 20X5 it is \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">PPE\u003c/span>, and \u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">depreciation\u003c/span> starts eating into the \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">deemed cost\u003c/span>.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"wg\" data-wg=\"roll\" data-key=\"ip-ppe-b13\" data-cfg=\"{&quot;panels&quot;:[{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;IP → PPE on 1 Jul 20X5&quot;,&quot;sub&quot;:&quot;then 30-year life&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;bal&quot;:&quot;Carrying amount&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:3000000,&quot;startCap&quot;:&quot;31 Dec 20X4: {a|investment property} at fair value {a|3,000,000}.&quot;,&quot;years&quot;:[{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;to 1 Jul&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;fair value gain&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;i&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:120000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;1 Jul 20X5: remeasure to fair value 3,120,000. The {i|120,000 gain} goes to P&amp;L, like any IP fair value change. {a|3,120,000} is now the {a|PPE’s deemed cost}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;to 31 Dec&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-52000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Now {a|PPE}: {x|depreciation} = {a|3,120,000} ÷ 30 × 6/12 = {x|52,000}. {a|Carrying amount} at 31 Dec 20X5 = {a|3,068,000}.&quot;}]}]}],&quot;notes&quot;:{&quot;start&quot;:&quot;Press Play or Next to follow the building through 20X5.&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[&quot;Each step is one regime: fair value while it is {a|investment property}, {x|depreciation} once it is {a|PPE}.&quot;],&quot;end&quot;:&quot;**The fair value on the day becomes the cost.** The original purchase price never comes back; {x|depreciation} runs on 3,120,000.&quot;}}\">\u003c/div>","id":"visual-1a26wn","sect":5,"part":"Derecognise / transfer"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"derecognise","lo":18,"title":"Disposal","body":["The last stop of the journey: the property is sold. Under the fair value model most of the profit has already been booked year by year, so the sale itself is usually an anticlimax.","Derecognise {a|investment property} when it is **disposed of**, or when it is permanently withdrawn from use and no future benefits are expected from its disposal.","> {i|Gain} or {x|loss} = {a|net disposal proceeds} − {a|carrying amount} → profit or loss","- Under the fair value model, the {a|carrying amount} is the latest fair value, so the {i|gain on sale} is usually small: most of the increase was recognised year by year. P&L has already eaten most of the cake, one slice a year.","Example: Bayfront sells its building (carried at fair value $2,100,000) for $2,180,000 and pays agents $30,000. {i|Gain} = (2,180,000 − 30,000) − 2,100,000 = **$50,000** in profit or loss.","- If the property came from PPE with a {e|Revaluation surplus (OCI)}, that {e|surplus} may be transferred **directly to {e|retained earnings}** on disposal. It is **not** reclassified to profit or loss."],"id":"rule-1lclg8","sect":5,"part":"Derecognise / transfer"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"derecognise","lo":18,"title":"Disposal: two flows, two homes","intro":"Selling the property moves two things. The {i|gain on sale} goes to P&L; any old {e|revaluation surplus} stays inside equity.","notes":{"net":"{a|Cash} in, net: sale price less selling costs (agents’ fees): 2,180,000 − 30,000 = 2,150,000.","ca":"The {a|carrying amount}: under the fair value model this is the last fair value, so most of the rise was already in P&L year by year.","gain":"2,150,000 − 2,100,000 = {i|50,000 gain}. Usually small under the fair value model.","pl":"The {i|gain} or {x|loss on disposal} is recognised in profit or loss.","rs":"The {e|revaluation surplus} exists only if the property came from PPE and had an increase on transfer (or earlier PPE revaluations).","re":"The {e|surplus} may be moved straight to {e|Retained earnings}, without passing through P&L."},"walk":[{"nodes":["net","ca","gain"],"text":"{i|Gain} = {a|net proceeds} − {a|carrying amount} = 2,150,000 − 2,100,000 = **50,000**."},{"nodes":["gain","pl"],"text":"The {i|gain} goes to **profit or loss**."},{"nodes":["rs","re"],"text":"If the property came from PPE, its **{e|revaluation surplus}** may be transferred directly to {e|retained earnings}."},{"nodes":["rs","pl"],"text":"It is **never** recycled through profit or loss."}],"caption":"Bayfront’s sale: 50,000 {i|gain} in P&L.","id":"diagram-1n5s3q","sect":5,"part":"Derecognise / transfer","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:576px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 524.00 165.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 154.62)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-154.62 513.64,-154.62 513.64,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>net\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e8eef6\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M99.03,-143.82C99.03,-143.82 12,-143.82 12,-143.82 6,-143.82 0,-137.82 0,-131.82 0,-131.82 0,-114.18 0,-114.18 0,-108.18 6,-102.18 12,-102.18 12,-102.18 99.03,-102.18 99.03,-102.18 105.03,-102.18 111.03,-108.18 111.03,-114.18 111.03,-114.18 111.03,-131.82 111.03,-131.82 111.03,-137.82 105.03,-143.82 99.03,-143.82\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"20.64\" y=\"-130.05\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"