35.82 282.53,-235.82 282.53,-218.18 282.53,-218.18 282.53,-212.18 288.53,-206.18 294.53,-206.18 294.53,-206.18 481.31,-206.18 481.31,-206.18 487.31,-206.18 493.31,-212.18 493.31,-218.18 493.31,-218.18 493.31,-235.82 493.31,-235.82 493.31,-241.82 487.31,-247.82 481.31,-247.82\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"325.29\" y=\"-234.05\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Shortcut: annuity factor\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"291.17\" y=\"-223.05\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">0.94340 + 0.89000 + 0.83962 ≈ 2.67301\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"325.67\" y=\"-212.05\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">5,000 × 2.67301 = 13,365\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge10\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>af&#45;&gt;pc\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,2\" d=\"M417.14,-205.69C427.97,-193.52 428.76,-181.35 419.5,-169.17\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"421.1,-167.81 415.55,-164.71 417.96,-170.59 421.1,-167.81\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"id":"calc-chfuan","type":"calc","bucket":"initial","lo":20,"q":"A 3-year bond has a face value of $100,000 and pays a 5% coupon at the end of each year. Similar bonds yield 6%. At 6%, the 3-year annuity factor is 2.67301 and the 3-year discount factor is 0.83962. What does the investor pay for the bond?","answer":97327,"unit":"$","working":["Coupon = 100,000 × 5% = 5,000 a year","PV of coupons = 5,000 × 2.67301 = 13,365","PV of face value = 100,000 × 0.83962 = 83,962","Price = 13,365 + 83,962 = **$97,327**, a discount of 2,673."],"sect":3,"part":"Initial measurement"},{"type":"compare","bucket":"initial","preamble":"Financial assets and financial liabilities are exact mirrors here: an asset **adds** transaction costs, a liability **deducts** them.","special":"Transaction costs are capitalised for amortised cost and FVOCI, but expensed on day one for FVTPL.","id":"compare-1kumyt-2","sect":3,"part":"Initial measurement"},{"type":"map","id":"map-4-subsequent","bucket":"subsequent","sect":4,"part":"Subsequent measurement"},{"id":"think-15vbt8","type":"think","bucket":"subsequent","lo":21,"scenario":"On 1 Jan 20X1 an investor pays $97,327 for a 3-year bond: face $100,000, coupon 5% paid each 31 Dec, market (effective) rate 6%. It holds the bond to collect (amortised cost). It will receive $5,000 a year and $100,000 at the end.","prompt":"Is the {i|yearly income} just the $5,000 coupon? Where does the extra $2,673 it gets back at maturity go?","answer":["The investor’s true return is 6% on what it paid, so {i|year 1 income} is 97,327 × 6% = **$5,840**, not $5,000.","The $840 above the coupon is not received in {a|cash}; it is added to the {a|bond}. Year by year the {a|carrying amount} climbs to $100,000, so the $2,673 discount is earned as {i|interest} over the 3 years."],"sect":4,"part":"Subsequent measurement"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"subsequent","lo":21,"title":"Amortised cost: the effective interest method","body":["> {i|Interest income} = {a|opening carrying amount} × effective interest rate","> {a|Closing carrying amount} = {a|opening carrying amount} + {i|interest income} − {a|coupon cash received}","- The **effective rate** is the rate that discounts the expected cash flows exactly to the {a|initial amount} (including transaction costs). For a bond bought at market price with no costs, it is the market rate.","- **Each year’s {a|closing} is next year’s {a|opening}**, so {i|interest income} changes every year.","- **Discount bond:** {i|interest} is more than the coupon. The gap (the discount unwinding) is added to the {a|bond}, so the {a|carrying amount} and next year’s {i|interest income} both **rise** towards face value.","- **Premium bond:** {i|interest} is less than the coupon, so the {a|carrying amount} and {i|interest income} both **fall** towards face value.","! {i|Interest} is the **effective rate × {a|carrying amount}**, never the coupon rate × face value. The coupon is the {a|cash} in your hand; the effective rate is what you actually earn. Don’t let the coupon catfish you."],"id":"rule-17mqg0","sect":4,"part":"Subsequent measurement"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"subsequent","lo":21,"title":"The effective interest roll-forward","intro":"The notes bond in 20X1: bought for $97,327, face $100,000, coupon 5%, effective rate 6%.","notes":{"open":"{a|Opening carrying amount} = what was paid (fair value + any transaction costs): {a|97,327}, a discount of 2,673 below face.","int":"{i|Interest income} = {a|opening carrying amount} × **effective** rate: 97,327 × 6% = 5,840. Not the coupon.","cpn":"The {a|cash} actually received: face × coupon rate = 5,000. It reduces the {a|asset} because part of what you were owed has been paid.","close":"{a|97,327} + {i|5,840} − {a|5,000} = {a|98,167}. The 840 gap between {i|interest} and {a|cash} is added to {a|Investment in bonds}.","pl":"{i|Interest income} of 5,840 goes to profit or loss under amortised cost **and** FVOCI debt.","cash":"Dr {a|Cash} 5,000.","next":"{a|Closing} becomes next year’s {a|opening}, so {i|interest} grows: 5,890 in 20X2. The final year is rounded so the bond reaches exactly 100,000 at maturity."},"walk":[{"nodes":["open"],"text":"Start from the {a|opening carrying amount}, $97,327."},{"nodes":["int","pl"],"text":"Add {i|interest} at the **effective** rate: 97,327 × 6% = $5,840, credited to P&L."},{"nodes":["cpn","cash"],"text":"Take off the {a|coupon cash received}: $5,000."},{"nodes":["close"],"text":"{a|Closing} = {a|97,327} + {i|5,840} − {a|5,000} = {a|$98,167}. A discount bond climbs towards face value."},{"nodes":["close","next"],"text":"Roll forward: the {a|closing balance} is next year’s {a|opening}, so 20X2 {i|interest} is $5,890."}],"caption":"{a|Opening} + {i|interest} (effective rate) − {a|cash} (coupon) = {a|closing}.","id":"diagram-hxxmn5","sect":4,"part":"Subsequent measurement","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:304px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 276.00 327.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(14.4 312.65)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-14.4,14.4 -14.4,-312.65 261.18,-312.65 261.18,14.4 -14.4,14.4\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>open\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M129.03,-298.25C129.03,-298.25 21,-298.25 21,-298.25 15,-298.25 9,-292.25 9,-286.25 9,-286.25 9,-274.25 9,-274.25 9,-268.25 15,-262.25 21,-262.25 21,-262.25 129.03,-262.25 129.03,-262.25 135.03,-262.25 141.03,-268.25 141.03,-274.25 141.03,-274.25 141.03,-286.25 141.03,-286.25 141.03,-292.25 135.03,-298.25 129.03,-298.25\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"34.89\" y=\"-280.8\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"white\">Opening 97,327\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"17.64\" y=\"-271.7\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"white\">1 Jan 20X1 carrying amount\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node2\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>int\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e6f4f1\" stroke=\"#0f766e\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M111.41,-235.25C111.41,-235.25 38.63,-235.25 38.63,-235.25 32.63,-235.25 26.63,-229.25 26.63,-223.25 26.63,-223.25 26.63,-211.25 26.63,-211.25 26.63,-205.25 32.63,-199.25 38.63,-199.25 38.63,-199.25 111.41,-199.25 111.41,-199.25 117.41,-199.25 123.41,-205.25 123.41,-211.25 123.41,-211.25 123.41,-223.25 123.41,-223.25 123.41,-229.25 117.41,-235.25 111.41,-235.25\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserv