\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"394.88\" y=\"-6.2\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">asset 99,000\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge3\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>bond&#45;&gt;fvtpl\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M288.43,-132.23C304.56,-125.14 322.94,-116.56 339.12,-107.75 340.75,-106.86 342.39,-105.96 344.03,-105.03\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"344.92,-106.94 349.09,-102.14 342.84,-103.3 344.92,-106.94\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"type":"compare","bucket":"subsequent","preamble":"FVOCI works like a PPE revaluation (gains wait in OCI), FVTPL like investment property at fair value (gains straight to P&L), and amortised cost like a financial liability in reverse.","special":"One asset, three routes: amortised cost (effective interest), FVOCI (fair value on the balance sheet, interest in P&L, the rest in OCI) and FVTPL (everything in P&L).","id":"compare-1kumyt-3","sect":4,"part":"Subsequent measurement"},{"type":"map","id":"map-5-derecognise","bucket":"derecognise","sect":5,"part":"Derecognise / transfer"},{"id":"think-1cb9jt","type":"think","bucket":"derecognise","lo":21,"scenario":"A company bought 10,000 shares at $2.00 on 1 Jan 20X1 (FVTPL) and remeasured them to $2.30 at 31 Dec 20X1. In 20X2 it sells 4,000 of them at $2.20.","prompt":"Is this a gain (sold above the $2.00 cost) or a loss? Against what amount should the proceeds be compared?","answer":["A **{x|loss}**. The {i|gain} from $2.00 to $2.30 was already recognised last year. The {a|shares} are carried at $2.30, so selling at $2.20 loses 4,000 × 0.10 = **$400**.","Always compare {a|proceeds} with the **{a|carrying amount}** (the last fair value), never the original cost."],"sect":5,"part":"Derecognise / transfer"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"derecognise","lo":21,"title":"Derecognition and the gain or loss on sale","body":["Derecognise a financial asset when the contractual rights to its cash flows **expire** (e.g. the bond matures), or when it is **transferred** with substantially all the risks and rewards (e.g. sold outright).","> {i|Gain} or {x|loss} = {a|proceeds} − {a|carrying amount} of the part sold","- **Partial sale:** take out the {a|carrying amount} of the shares sold only (number sold × last fair value).","- **FVTPL:** the {i|gain} or {x|loss} goes to P&L.","! Using **original cost** for the part sold double-counts the {i|gain} already recognised. That’s celebrating the same birthday twice."],"id":"rule-8rxqli","sect":5,"part":"Derecognise / transfer"},{"id":"je-168phg","type":"je","bucket":"derecognise","lo":21,"q":"A company holds 10,000 shares at FVTPL, carried at $2.30 each (their 31 Dec 20X1 fair value). In 20X2 it sells 4,000 of them at $2.20 for cash. Record the sale.","accounts":["Investment in shares","Cash","Transaction costs expense","Fair value gain (P&L)","Fair value loss (P&L)","Fair value reserve (OCI)","Dividend income","Retained earnings","Accruals"],"lines":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Cash","amount":8800},{"side":"Dr","account":"Fair value loss (P&L)","amount":400},{"side":"Cr","account":"Investment in shares","amount":9200}],"why":"{a|Carrying amount} out = 4,000 × 2.30 = 9,200; {a|proceeds} 8,800; {x|loss} 400 to P&L. The other 6,000 shares stay at 2.30 until the next remeasurement.","sect":5,"part":"Derecognise / transfer"},{"id":"think-1sguie","type":"think","bucket":"derecognise","lo":21,"scenario":"Two FVOCI assets are sold. (1) An FVOCI bond with {a|amortised cost} $98,167, carried at fair value $99,000 with $833 sitting in the {e|fair value reserve}, is sold on 1 Jan 20X2 for $99,000. (2) Shares under the equity election, with a gain sitting in the {e|reserve}, are sold too.","prompt":"The gains in OCI have now been realised in cash. Should they move into profit or loss?","answer":["**The bond: yes.** Its {e|OCI balance} is **recycled** (reclassified) to P&L. Total profit on the bond then equals what amortised cost would have given: {a|proceeds} 99,000 − {a|amortised cost} 98,167 = 833.","**The shares: no, never.** What happens in OCI stays in OCI: that was the price of the election. The cumulative gain may be **transferred within equity** to {e|retained earnings}, but it never passes through P&L."],"sect":5,"part":"Derecognise / transfer"},{"id":"je-97j2j9","type":"je","bucket":"derecognise","lo":21,"q":"A bond held at FVOCI has {a|amortised cost} $98,167 and is carried at fair value $99,000, with $833 in the {e|fair value reserve}. On 1 Jan 20X2 it is sold for $99,000 cash. Record the sale, including the recycling.","accounts":["Investment in bonds","Cash","Interest income","Fair value reserve (OCI)","Fair value gain (P&L)","Gain on disposal (P&L)","Loss allowance","Trade receivables","Accruals"],"lines":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Cash","amount":99000},{"side":"Cr","account":"Investment in bonds","amount":99000},{"side":"Dr","account":"Fair value reserve (OCI)","amount":833},{"side":"Cr","account":"Gain on disposal (P&L)","amount":833}],"why":"Sold at {a|carrying amount}, so no new {i|gain}. The 833 in the {e|reserve} is reclassified to P&L (it appears as a negative item in OCI for the year).","sect":5,"part":"Derecognise / transfer"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"derecognise","lo":21,"title":"Timeline: an FVOCI bond, held then sold","intro":"The notes bond in a collect-and-sell portfolio, from purchase to sale. Follow the {e|OCI balance}.","notes":{"buy":"Paid 97,327 (fair value; no transaction costs). Classified FVOCI: SPPI met, model is collect and sell.","ye":"Two things happen: the effective interest roll-forward takes {a|amortised cost} to 98,167, then the {a|asset} is remeasured to fair value 99,000.","int":"97,327 × 6% = {i|5,840} to P&L, the same as amortised cost would give.","oci":"{a|Fair value} − {a|amortised cost} = 99,000 − 98,167 = 833, credited to {e|Fair value reserve (OCI)}. Measured from amortised cost, not from original cost.","sell":"Sold at the {a|carrying amount} 99,000, so no new {i|gain} arises on the sale itself.","rec":"Dr {e|Fair value reserve (OCI)} 833, Cr {i|Gain on disposal (P&L)} 833. The gain that waited in OCI now reaches profit.","tot":"Profit over the bond’s life = 5,840 + 833 = 6,673: exactly the FVTPL profit. FVOCI debt only changes the **timing**."},"walk":[{"nodes":["buy"],"text":"1 Jan 20X1: buy the bond for $97,327."},{"nodes":["ye","int"],"text":"31 Dec 20X1: {i|interest} $5,840 to P&L, taking {a|amortised cost} to $98,167."},{"nodes":["ye","oci"],"text":"Same date: remeasure to fair value $99,000. The $833 above {a|amortised cost} goes to OCI."},{"nodes":["sell","rec","oci"],"text":"1 Jan 20X2: sell for $99,000. No new gain, but the $833 waiting in OCI is **recycled** to P&L."},{"nodes":["int","rec","tot"],"text":"Total profit $6,673, the same as FVTPL. Recycling makes sure debt gains reach profit in the end."}],"id":"diagram-1coakj","sect":5,"part":"Derecognise / transfer","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:403px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 366.00 317.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(14.4 302.4)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-14.4,14.4 -14.4,-302.4 351.68,-302.4 351.68,14.4 -14.4,14.4\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>buy\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M177.28,-288C177.28,-288 127.75,-288 127.75,-288 121.75,-288 115.75,-282 115.75,-276 115.75,-276 115.75,-264 115.75,-264 115.75,-258 121.75,-252 127.75,-252 127.75,-252 177.28,-252 177.28,-252 183.28,-252 189.28,-258 189.28,-264 189.28,-264 189.28,-276 189.28,-276 189.28,-282 183.28,-288 177.28,-288\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"124.39\" y=\"-271.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,san