.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Each period\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"250.18\" y=\"-15.49\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">− depreciation over the shorter of\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"266.3\" y=\"-6.49\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">lease term and useful life\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge5\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>rou&#45;&gt;rou2\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,2\" d=\"M317.3,-65.33C317.3,-59.93 317.3,-53.83 317.3,-47.92\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"319.75,-48 317.3,-41 314.85,-48 319.75,-48\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"type":"map","id":"map-4-subsequent","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"lessee","sect":4,"part":"Subsequent measurement · lessee"},{"id":"think-12epdj","type":"think","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"lessee","lo":23,"scenario":"Kopi Co’s {l|lease liability} was $33,121 on 1 Jan 20X1 (4 payments of $10,000 in arrears, rate implicit in the lease 8%). It is now 31 Dec 20X1, and Kopi Co pays RoastPro the first $10,000.","prompt":"Does the {l|liability} fall by the full $10,000? What happened to it during the year before the payment?","answer":["1. During the year it **grew by {x|interest}**: $33,121 × 8% = $2,650. That is an {x|expense}.","2. The payment then reduces it: $33,121 + $2,650 − $10,000 = {l|closing liability} **$25,771**. Only $7,350 of the payment repaid “principal”."],"sect":4,"part":"Subsequent measurement · lessee"},{"id":"visual-14mvhm","type":"visual","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"lessee","lo":23,"title":"The lease liability over 4 years (arrears)","html":"\u003cp>Kopi Co’s \u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">lease liability\u003c/span> ($33,121 on 1 Jan 20X1, 4 payments of $10,000 in arrears, 8%) rolled forward to the end of the lease. Each row repeats the year-1 pattern: \u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">opening\u003c/span> + \u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">interest\u003c/span> − \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">payment\u003c/span> = \u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">closing\u003c/span>.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"tbl-wrap\">\u003ctable class=\"tbl num reveal-rows\">\u003cthead>\u003ctr>\u003cth>Year\u003c/th>\u003cth>Opening\u003c/th>\u003cth>Interest 8%\u003c/th>\u003cth>Payment (31 Dec)\u003c/th>\u003cth>Closing\u003c/th>\u003c/tr>\u003c/thead>\u003ctbody>\u003ctr>\u003ctd>20X1\u003c/td>\u003ctd>33,121\u003c/td>\u003ctd>2,650\u003c/td>\u003ctd>(10,000)\u003c/td>\u003ctd>25,771\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\u003ctr>\u003ctd>20X2\u003c/td>\u003ctd>25,771\u003c/td>\u003ctd>2,062\u003c/td>\u003ctd>(10,000)\u003c/td>\u003ctd>17,833\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\u003ctr>\u003ctd>20X3\u003c/td>\u003ctd>17,833\u003c/td>\u003ctd>1,427\u003c/td>\u003ctd>(10,000)\u003c/td>\u003ctd>9,260\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\u003ctr>\u003ctd>20X4\u003c/td>\u003ctd>9,260\u003c/td>\u003ctd>740\u003c/td>\u003ctd>(10,000)\u003c/td>\u003ctd>0\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\u003c/div>\u003cp class=\"cap\">\u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">Interest\u003c/span> totals $6,879, which is exactly $40,000 minus the $33,121 borrowed. \u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">Interest\u003c/span> is highest in year 1 because the \u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">balance\u003c/span> is highest. Final-year \u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">interest\u003c/span> is rounded so the \u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">balance\u003c/span> ends at 0.\u003c/p>","sect":4,"part":"Subsequent measurement · lessee"},{"id":"je-oouv30","type":"je","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"lessee","lo":23,"q":"Kopi Co’s {l|lease liability} is $33,121 on 1 Jan 20X1: 4 payments of $10,000 in arrears, rate implicit in the lease 8%. Record Kopi Co’s {x|interest} and payment on 31 Dec 20X1 (one entry, all lines).","accounts":["Right-of-use asset","Lease liability","Cash","Prepaid lease payments","Interest expense","Depreciation expense","Lease expense","Legal fees expense","Accumulated depreciation: ROU asset","Accruals"],"lines":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Interest expense","amount":2650},{"side":"Dr","account":"Lease liability","amount":7350},{"side":"Cr","account":"Cash","amount":10000}],"alt":"Recording it as two entries (Dr {x|Interest expense} / Cr {l|Lease liability}, then Dr {l|Lease liability} / Cr {a|Cash}) is equally correct. The net effect is the same.","why":"{x|Interest} 2,650; the remaining 7,350 of the payment reduces the {l|liability}.","sect":4,"part":"Subsequent measurement · lessee"},{"id":"think-h7iqte","type":"think","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"lessee","lo":23,"scenario":"Kopi Co leases a coffee roaster from RoastPro for 4 years from 1 Jan 20X1 and recognises a {a|right-of-use asset}. The roaster’s useful life is 6 years, but Kopi Co must hand it back after 4. Ownership does not transfer and there is no purchase option.","prompt":"Over how many years should Kopi Co depreciate the {a|ROU asset}?","answer":["**4 years**. Kopi Co only gets to use it for the lease term, so the shorter of lease term and useful life.","If ownership transferred at the end, or a purchase option were reasonably certain, it would use the **useful life** (6 years) instead, because it will keep the machine."],"sect":4,"part":"Subsequent measurement · lessee"},{"id":"calc-qn47ns","type":"calc","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"lessee","lo":23,"q":"Kopi Co’s {a|ROU asset} cost $34,121 on 1 Jan 20X1. The lease term is 4 years; the roaster’s useful life is 6 years; ownership does not transfer and there is no purchase option. Straight-line, no residual value. What is the 20X1 {x|depreciation}?","answer":8530,"unit":"$","working":["$34,121 ÷ 4 years = $8,530","Total 20X1 {x|expense} = {x|interest} 2,650 + {x|depreciation} 8,530 = $11,180, more than the $10,000 {a|cash} paid. The {x|expense} is front-loaded."],"sect":4,"part":"Subsequent measurement · lessee"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"lessee","lo":23,"title":"Kopi Co’s first year","intro":"Two balances move separately. Both feed profit or loss.","notes":{"open":"The {l|lease liability}: the PV of the four payments on day 1.","int":"33,121 × 8% = 2,650. {x|Interest expense} (a finance cost), added to the {l|liability}.","pay":"Only 7,350 of the {a|cash} repays {l|principal}; the rest pays the {x|interest}.","close":"{l|33,121} + {x|2,650} − {a|10,000} = {l|25,771}.","rou":"{l|Liability} plus initial direct costs.","dep":"Over 4 years: the lease term is shorter than the 6-year life and ownership does not transfer.","nbv":"{a|Carrying amount} after one year of {x|depreciation}.","pl":"{x|Interest} is highest early, so the total {x|expense} is front-loaded."},"walk":[{"nodes":["open","int"],"text":"The {l|liability} grows by {x|interest} at 8% on the {l|opening balance}."},{"nodes":["pay","close"],"text":"The {a|payment} reduces it. {l|Closing} = {l|opening} + {x|interest} − {a|payment}."},{"nodes":["rou","dep","nbv"],"text":"Separately, the {a|ROU asset} is depreciated straight-line over the lease term."},{"nodes":["pl"],"text":"P&L gets {x|interest} + {x|depreciation} = 11,180, more than the {a|cash} paid. That is the front-loading."}],"id":"diagram-jj001a","sect":4,"part":"Subsequent measurement · lessee","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:442px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 402.00 253.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(14.4 238.48)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-14.4,14.4 -14.4,-238.48 387.12,-238.48 387.12,14.4 -14.4,14.4\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>open\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#ffe4e6\" stroke=\"#be123c\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M155.85,-224.08C155.85,-224.08 69.75,-224.08 69.75,-224.08 63.75,-224.08 57.75,-218.08 57.75,-212.08 57.75,-212.08 57.75,-200.08 57.75,-20