50.57 241.55,-43.57 239.1,-50.57 244,-50.57\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"id":"visual-oee94k","type":"visual","bucket":"initial","blabel":"lessee · in advance","lo":23,"title":"Arrears vs advance","html":"\u003cp>The timeline and the numbers side by side. The PV of all four payments is higher in advance (no wait for the first), but the \u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">liability\u003c/span> is lower, because one payment is already made.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"timeline\">\n      \u003cdiv class=\"tl-row\">\u003cb>Arrears\u003c/b>\u003cspan class=\"tick\">1 Jan X1\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"tick pay\">31 Dec X1\u003cbr>$10k\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"tick pay\">X2\u003cbr>$10k\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"tick pay\">X3\u003cbr>$10k\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"tick pay\">X4\u003cbr>$10k\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\n      \u003cdiv class=\"tl-row\">\u003cb>Advance\u003c/b>\u003cspan class=\"tick pay\">1 Jan X1\u003cbr>$10k\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"tick pay\">1 Jan X2\u003cbr>$10k\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"tick pay\">X3\u003cbr>$10k\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"tick pay\">X4\u003cbr>$10k\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"tick\">31 Dec X4\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\n    \u003c/div>\n    \u003cdiv class=\"tbl-wrap\">\u003ctable class=\"tbl num\">\u003cthead>\u003ctr>\u003cth>\u003c/th>\u003cth>Arrears\u003c/th>\u003cth>Advance\u003c/th>\u003c/tr>\u003c/thead>\u003ctbody>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>PV of all 4 payments\u003c/td>\u003ctd>33,121\u003c/td>\u003ctd>35,771\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>Paid on day 1\u003c/td>\u003ctd>0\u003c/td>\u003ctd>10,000\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">Lease liability\u003c/span> on day 1\u003c/td>\u003ctd>33,121\u003c/td>\u003ctd>25,771\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>20X1 \u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">interest\u003c/span> (8%)\u003c/td>\u003ctd>2,650\u003c/td>\u003ctd>2,062\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n    \u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\u003c/div>\n    \u003cp class=\"cap\">Annuity due factor = 1 + the annuity factor for one period fewer.\u003c/p>","sect":5,"part":"Initial measurement · lessee · in advance"},{"type":"visual","bucket":"initial","blabel":"lessee · in advance","lo":23,"title":"Arrears vs advance, step by step","html":"\u003cp>The same lease paid two ways. Step through the four years and watch each \u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">lease liability\u003c/span> grow by \u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">interest\u003c/span> and fall with each \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">payment\u003c/span>. In the advance lease, each payment lands on 1 January, a day after the year’s \u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">interest\u003c/span> is accrued.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"wg\" data-wg=\"roll\" data-key=\"lease-timing\" data-cfg=\"{&quot;panels&quot;:[{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Arrears&quot;,&quot;sub&quot;:&quot;pay 31 Dec · 4 × 10,000 · 8%&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;l&quot;,&quot;bal&quot;:&quot;Lease liability&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:33121,&quot;startCap&quot;:&quot;1 Jan 20X1: nothing paid yet, so the {l|liability} is the PV of all 4 payments, {l|33,121}.&quot;,&quot;years&quot;:[{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X1&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;interest&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:2650,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;20X1: {x|interest} = {l|opening 33,121} × 8% = {x|2,650}.&quot;},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;payment&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-10000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;31 Dec 20X1: {a|payment 10,000} leaves {l|25,771}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X2&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;interest&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:2062,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;20X2: {x|interest} = {l|opening 25,771} × 8% = {x|2,062}.&quot;},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;payment&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-10000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;31 Dec 20X2: {a|payment 10,000} leaves {l|17,833}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X3&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;interest&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:1427,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;20X3: {x|interest} = {l|opening 17,833} × 8% = {x|1,427}.&quot;},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;payment&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-10000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;31 Dec 20X3: {a|payment 10,000} leaves {l|9,260}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X4&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;interest&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:740,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;20X4: {x|interest} = {l|opening 9,260} × 8% = {x|740}. (Rounded so the balance ends at 0.)&quot;},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;payment&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-10000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;31 Dec 20X4: {a|payment 10,000} leaves {l|0}. Paid off.&quot;}]}]},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Advance&quot;,&quot;sub&quot;:&quot;pay 1 Jan · 4 × 10,000 · 8%&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;l&quot;,&quot;bal&quot;:&quot;Lease liability&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:25771,&quot;startCap&quot;:&quot;1 Jan 20X1: the first 10,000 is paid on day 1 and goes into the {a|ROU asset}, so the {l|liability} is the PV of the other 3, {l|25,771}.&quot;,&quot;years&quot;:[{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X1&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;interest&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:2062,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;20X1: {x|interest} = {l|opening 25,771} × 8% = {x|2,062}, accrued at 31 Dec. No {a|cash} yet.&quot;},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;payment&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-10000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;1 Jan 20X2: {a|payment 10,000} leaves {l|17,833}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X2&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;interest&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:1427,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;20X2: {x|interest} = {l|opening 17,833} × 8% = {x|1,427}, accrued at 31 Dec. No {a|cash} yet.&quot;},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;payment&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-10000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;1 Jan 20X3: {a|payment 10,000} leaves {l|9,260}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X3&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;interest&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:740,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;20X3: {x|interest} = {l|opening 9,260} × 8% = {x|740}, accrued at 31 Dec. No {a|cash} yet.&quot;},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;payment&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-10000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;1 Jan 20X4: {a|payment 10,000} leaves {l|0}. Paid off.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X4&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;interest&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:0,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;20X4: nothing left to owe, so no {x|interest}. The last payment was made on 1 Jan 20X4.&quot;},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;payment&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:0,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Lease over. The advance {l|liability} hit zero a year earlier.&quot;}]}]}],&quot;notes&quot;:{&quot;start&quot;:&quot;Same four payments of $10,000 at 8%. Only the timing differs. Press Play or Next.&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[&quot;Step 1 each year: {x|interest} = 8% × the {l|opening liability}. It adds to what is owed.&quot;,&quot;Step 2: a {a|payment} reduces the {l|liability}. What is left is next year’s {l|opening}.&quot;],&quot;end&quot;:&quot;**Advance = arrears, one year further on.** The advance {l|liability} starts at 25,771, exactly where the arrears one is after its first year, and is paid off a year sooner. Total {x|interest}: 6,879 in arrears vs 4,229 in advance; the gap of 2,650 is the arrears lease’s first-year {x|interest}.&quot;}}\">\u003c/div>","id":"visual-88bjeq","sect":5,"part":"Initial measurement · lessee · in advance"},{"id":"mcq-sj1gjp","type":"mcq","bucket":"initial","blabel":"lessee · in advance","lo":23,"q":"Kopi Co leases a roaster from 1 Jan 20X1: 4 annual payments of $10,000 in advance (each 1 January, the first on 1 Jan 20X1), rate 8%. Annuity factors at 8%: 3 years 2.5771, 4 years 3.3121. What is Kopi Co’s {l|lease liability} immediately after the 1 Jan 20X1 payment?","options":[{"t":"$35,771","why":"That is the PV of all four payments, before the day-1 payment is made."},{"t":"$25,771","ok":true,"why":"PV of the three remaining payments. The first was paid on day 1, so it never sat in the {l|liability}."},{"t":"$33,121","why":"That is the PV for payments in arrears."},{"t":"$30,000","why":"Undiscounted. The {l|liability} is measured at present value."}],"sect":5,"part":"Initial measurement · lessee · in advance"},{"id":"worked-1vu1d4","type":"worked","bucket":"initial","blabel":"lessee · in advance","lo":23,"title":"Worked: Kopi Co pays in advance","q":"Kopi Co leases a coffee roaster from RoastPro for 4 years from 1 Jan 20X1 at $10,000 a year, paid in advance on each 1 January (the first on 1 Jan 20X1). Rate implicit in the lease 8% (3-year annuity factor 2.5771); legal fees $1,000 paid in {a|cash}; the roaster’s useful life is 6 years, with no purchase option. Record day 1 and the 20X1 year-end entries.","intro":["A typical exam question: a lease paid in advance, and you must give the day-1 entry and the year-end entries. Remember two things:","- The day-1 payment is already paid, so it is **not in the {l|liability}**. It goes into the {a|ROU asset}’s cost instead.","- At 31 Dec the next payment is not due until 1 January, so {x|interest} is **accrued** onto the {l|liability}, with no {a|cash}.","Then follow these steps: liability → ROU asset → day-1 entry → interest → depreciation → check."],"steps":[{"h":"Measure the lease liability.","t":"After the 1 Jan 20X1 payment only 3 payments are unpaid: {l|liability} = 10,000 × 2.5771 = **{l|$25,771}**."},{"h":"Build the ROU asset.","t":"{a|ROU asset} = {l|liability 25,771} + payment at commencement 10,000 + initial direct costs 1,000 = **{a|$36,771}**."},{"h":"Record the 1 Jan 20X1 entry.","t":"{a|Cash} out = first payment 10,000 + legal fees 1,000 = {a|11,000}.","je":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Right-of-use asset","amount":36771},{"side":"Cr","account":"Lease liability","amount":25771},{"side":"Cr","account":"Cash","amount":11000}]},{"h":"Accrue the 20X1 interest.","t":"{x|Interest} = {l|25,771} × 8% = **{x|2,062}**, added to the {l|liability}. No {a|cash} today: the next payment is on 1 Jan 20X2.","je":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Interest expense","amount":2062},{"side":"Cr","account":"Lease liability","amount":2062}]},{"h":"Depreciate the ROU asset.","t":"Over the 4-year lease term (shorter than the 6-year life, and no ownership transfer): {a|36,771} ÷ 4 = **{x|9,193}**.","je":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Depreciation expense","amount":9193},{"side":"Cr","account":"Accumulated depreciation: ROU asset","amount":9193}]},{"h":"Check the closing liability.","t":"{l|Liability at 31 Dec 20X1} = {l|25,771} + {x|2,062} = **{l|27,833}**.","after":"The next day’s $10,000 payment takes it to {l|17,833}."}],"sect":5,"part":"Initial measurement · lessee · in advance"},{"id":"je-ucaye5","type":"je","bucket":"initial","blabel":"lessee · in advance","lo":23,"q":"Your turn, with help. Kopi Co leases a delivery van from 1 Jan 20X2: 5 annual payments of $8,000 in advance, the first on 1 Jan 20X2. Rate implicit in the lease 6% (4-year annuity factor 3.4651). Kopi Co pays $600 of initial direct costs in {a|cash}. The {l|lease liability} line is filled in. Complete the day-1 entry, with one Cash line.","accounts":["Right-of-use asset","Lease liability","Cash","Prepaid lease payments","Interest expense","Depreciation expense","Lease expense","Legal fees expense","Accumulated depreciation: ROU asset","Accruals"],"given":[1],"lines":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Right-of-use asset","amount":36321},{"side":"Cr","account":"Lease liability","amount":27721},{"side":"Cr","account":"Cash","amount":8600}],"why":"{l|Liability} = 8,000 × 3.4651 = 27,721: the 4 payments still unpaid. {a|ROU asset} = 27,721 + first payment 8,000 + initial direct costs 600 = 36,321. {a|Cash} = 8,000 + 600 = 8,600.","sect":5,"part":"Initial measurement · lessee · in advance"},{"id":"je-6sbbme","type":"je","bucket":"initial","blabel":"lessee · in advance","lo":23,"q":"On your own. Kopi Co leases a café unit from 1 Jul 20X2 for 3 years at $36,000 a year in advance, the first payment on 1 Jul 20X2. The implicit rate is not readily determinable; Kopi Co’s incremental borrowing rate is 5% (2-year annuity factor 1.8594). It pays agent’s fees of $2,000 in {a|cash}, and must restore the unit at the end: the {l|restoration provision} is $3,000 at present value. Record the day-1 entry, with one Cash line.","accounts":["Right-of-use asset","Lease liability","Cash","Prepaid lease payments","Interest expense","Depreciation expense","Lease expense","Legal fees expense","Accumulated depreciation: ROU asset","Accruals","Provision for restoration"],"lines":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Right-of-use asset","amount":107939},{"side":"Cr","account":"Lease liability","amount":66939},{"side":"Cr","account":"Cash","amount":38000},{"side":"Cr","account":"Provision for restoration","amount":3000}],"why":"{l|Liability} = PV of the 2 unpaid payments at the 5% incremental borrowing rate = 66,939. {a|ROU asset} = 66,939 + first payment 36,000 + agent’s fees 2,000 + restoration {l|provision} 3,000 = 107,939. {a|Cash} = 36,000 + 2,000.","sect":5,"part":"Initial measurement · lessee · in advance"},{"type":"compare","id":"compare-initial","bucket":"initial","preamble":"A lessee’s lease is two cousins at once: an asset used like **PPE** and a loan repaid like a **financial liability**.","blabel":"lessee · in advance","lo":23,"special":"Here the {a|asset}’s cost is built from a {l|liability}: the {a|ROU asset} starts at the PV of the lease payments, then adds day-1 payments, initial direct costs and restoration, less incentives.","sect":5,"part":"Initial measurement · lessee · in advance"},{"type":"map","id":"map-6-classify","bucket":"classify","blabel":"lessor","sect":6,"part":"Classify · lessor"},{"type":"think","bucket":"classify","blabel":"lessor","lo":23,"scenario":"Now sit in RoastPro’s chair. It leased Kopi Co a roaster for 4 of its 6 years of life, and the payments are worth about what the machine is worth today.","prompt":"Economically, has RoastPro rented the machine out, or has it effectively sold it on credit?","answer":["Effectively **sold it on credit**. Kopi Co gets most of the machine’s useful life and RoastPro recovers about its full value. Most of the **risks and rewards of ownership** have passed.","So unlike the lessee, the **lessor still classifies**: this looks like a **finance lease**. RoastPro is basically a bank in a coffee-machine costume."],"id":"think-hxh11z","sect":6,"part":"Classify · lessor"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"classify","blabel":"lessor","lo":23,"title":"Lessor: finance or operating?","body":["Switch to the other side of the contract. The lessee has one model, but the lessor still asks the old question: is this really renting, or selling on credit?","A lease is a **finance lease** if it transfers **substantially all the risks and rewards** of ownership; otherwise it is an **operating lease**.","Indicators of a finance lease:","- ownership transfers to the lessee by the end","- a **bargain purchase option** reasonably certain to be exercised","- lease term is the **major part of the economic life**","- PV of lease payments is **substantially all of the fair value**","- the asset is so **specialised** only the lessee can use it without major changes","! Only the **lessor** classifies. The lessee always uses the single on-balance-sheet model."],"id":"rule-1rjfvh","sect":6,"part":"Classify · lessor"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"classify","blabel":"lessor","lo":23,"title":"Lessor: finance or operating?","intro":"Any of these indicators points to a finance lease. The question behind them is always risks and rewards.","notes":{"own":"If the lessee ends up owning it, the lessor has in effect sold it.","bpo":"An option priced so low that the lessee is reasonably certain to buy: same effect as ownership transfer.","life":"The lessee uses up most of the asset’s life, so little is left for the lessor.","pv":"The lessor recovers about the asset’s full value through the payments.","spec":"Nobody else could use it without major changes, so the lessor has no real other use for it.","rr":"The test itself. The indicators are evidence; judge the substance of the deal.","fin":"Derecognise the {a|asset}; recognise a {a|Lease receivable} at the net investment; earn {i|Finance income}.","op":"Keep the {a|asset} and depreciate it; recognise {i|Lease income}, usually straight-line."},"walk":[{"nodes":["own","bpo"],"text":"Will the lessee end up owning it? A transfer of title or a bargain purchase option."},{"nodes":["life","pv"],"text":"Does the lessee get most of the asset’s life, and pay about its full value?"},{"nodes":["spec"],"text":"Is the asset so specialised only the lessee can use it?"},{"nodes":["rr","fin"],"text":"If so, substantially all risks and rewards have passed: a finance lease."},{"nodes":["op"],"text":"If not, the lessor keeps them: an operating lease. (The lessee never makes this call.)"}],"id":"diagram-1bd43w","sect":6,"part":"Classify · lessor","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:530px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 482.00 257.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(14.4 242.4)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-14.4,14.4 -14.4,-242.4 467.45,-242.4 467.45,14.4 -14.4,14.4\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>own\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e8eef6\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M127.73,-228C127.73,-228 23.62,-228 23.62,-228 17.62,-228 11.63,-222 11.63,-216 11.63,-216 11.63,-204 11.63,-204 11.63,-198 17.63,-192 23.63,-192 23.63,-192 127.73,-192 127.73,-192 133.73,-192 139.73,-198 139.73,-204 139.73,-204 139.73,-216 139.73,-216 139.73,-222 133