e\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M441.05,-108C441.05,-108 361.7,-108 361.7,-108 355.7,-108 349.7,-102 349.7,-96 349.7,-96 349.7,-84 349.7,-84 349.7,-78 355.7,-72 361.7,-72 361.7,-72 441.05,-72 441.05,-72 447.05,-72 453.05,-78 453.05,-84 453.05,-84 453.05,-96 453.05,-96 453.05,-102 447.05,-108 441.05,-108\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"360.5\" y=\"-90.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Operating lease\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"371.38\" y=\"-81.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">like renting out\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge7\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>rr&#45;&gt;op\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M299.15,-105.4C312.69,-103.34 327.19,-101.14 340.86,-99.06\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"341.21,-101.48 347.76,-98.01 340.47,-96.64 341.21,-101.48\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"324.33\" y=\"-104.47\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> no\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"type":"mcq","bucket":"classify","blabel":"lessor","lo":23,"q":"A lessor leases a machine for 2 years. It has a 10-year economic life; payments are worth about 25% of its fair value; title stays with the lessor. How does the lessor classify it?","options":[{"t":"Finance lease, because there is a written contract","why":"Every lease has a contract. Classification depends on risks and rewards."},{"t":"Operating lease","ok":true,"why":"Short term relative to life, PV far below fair value, no transfer of title. The lessor keeps the risks and rewards."},{"t":"Finance lease, because the lessee recognises an {a|ROU asset}","why":"The lessee recognises an {a|ROU asset} regardless. That doesn’t drive the lessor’s classification."},{"t":"No classification needed under SFRS(I) 16","why":"That is true for lessees only. Lessors still classify."}],"id":"mcq-1tewb0","sect":6,"part":"Classify · lessor"},{"type":"compare","id":"compare-classify","bucket":"classify","preamble":"A lessor’s finance lease turns the asset into a **receivable**, which is why financial assets sit in this table.","blabel":"lessor","lo":23,"special":"Two questions, not one: is it a lease at all (the three tests), and then, for the lessor only, finance or operating by risks and rewards. The lessee never classifies.","sect":6,"part":"Classify · lessor"},{"type":"map","id":"map-7-initial","bucket":"initial","blabel":"lessor","sect":7,"part":"Initial measurement · lessor"},{"id":"visual-17stdj","type":"visual","bucket":"initial","blabel":"lessor","lo":23,"title":"Lessor: the two models side by side","html":"\u003cp>Classification done; here is what each answer means for the lessor’s books. A finance lease swaps the machine for a \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">receivable\u003c/span>; an operating lease keeps the machine and collects rent.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"tbl-wrap\">\u003ctable class=\"tbl\">\u003cthead>\u003ctr>\u003cth>\u003c/th>\u003cth>Finance lease\u003c/th>\u003cth>Operating lease\u003c/th>\u003c/tr>\u003c/thead>\u003ctbody>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>Underlying asset\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cstrong>Derecognise\u003c/strong> it\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cstrong>Keep\u003c/strong> it and charge \u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">Depreciation expense\u003c/span>\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>On day 1\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">Lease receivable\u003c/span> = net investment (PV of payments + PV of unguaranteed residual)\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Nothing new\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>Income\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cspan class=\"el el-i\">Finance income\u003c/span> at a constant rate on the net investment\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cspan class=\"el el-i\">Lease income\u003c/span>, usually \u003cstrong>straight-line\u003c/strong>\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>Feels like…\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Selling on credit\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Renting out\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n    \u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\u003c/div>","sect":7,"part":"Initial measurement · lessor"},{"id":"calc-1j39mc","type":"calc","bucket":"initial","blabel":"lessor","lo":23,"q":"A lessor leases a machine for 3 years at $15,000 a year in arrears; rate implicit in the lease 9%. It expects the machine back worth $4,000, which the lessee does not guarantee. It is a finance lease. What is the {a|lease receivable} (net investment) on day 1? (3-year annuity factor 2.5313; 3-year discount factor 0.7722.)","answer":41058,"unit":"$","working":["PV of lease payments: 15,000 × 2.5313 = 37,969","PV of the unguaranteed residual: 4,000 × 0.7722 = 3,089","Net investment ({a|lease receivable}) = 37,969 + 3,089 = **$41,058**","The residual is unguaranteed, so the lessor bears the risk on it, but it still expects to recover it. That is why it sits in the {a|receivable}."],"sect":7,"part":"Initial measurement · lessor"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"initial","blabel":"lessor","lo":23,"title":"Lessor finance lease: asset out, receivable in","intro":"The numbers from the calculation you just did, drawn.","notes":{"cls":"Finance or operating, by risks and rewards.","eq":"The lessor no longer controls the economics of the machine, so it comes off the balance sheet.","pvp":"15,000 × 2.5313 = 37,969.","pvr":"4,000 × 0.7722 = 3,089. The lessor expects the machine back, so the residual is part of what it will recover.","ni":"37,969 + 3,089 = {a|41,058}. Dr {a|Lease receivable}.","yr":"The mirror of the lessee’s {l|liability}: {i|interest} at the implicit rate adds to the {a|receivable}, {a|receipts} reduce it.","fi":"{i|Finance income} at a constant rate on the {a|net investment}.","op":"The other model: nothing new on day 1, {i|Lease income} usually straight-line, plus {x|Depreciation expense}."},"walk":[{"nodes":["cls","eq"],"text":"Finance lease: the {a|equipment} leaves the lessor’s balance sheet."},{"nodes":["pvp","pvr","ni"],"text":"In its place: a {a|lease receivable} = PV of payments + PV of the unguaranteed residual = 41,058."},{"nodes":["yr","fi"],"text":"Each year the {a|receivable} earns {i|finance income} and falls with each {a|receipt}."},{"nodes":["op"],"text":"Operating lease instead: keep the {a|equipment} and earn straight-line {i|lease income}."}],"id":"diagram-1v0u71","sect":7,"part":"Initial measurement · lessor","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:539px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 490.00 358.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(14.4 343.14)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-14.4,14.4 -14.4,-343.14 475.38,-343.14 475.38,14.4 -14.4,14.4\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>cls\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#b45309\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M291.73,-328.74C291.73,-328.74 156.88,-328.74 156.88,-328.74 150.88,-328.74 144.88,-322.74 144.88,-316.74 144.88,-316.74 144.88,-304.74 144.88,-304.74 144.88,-298.74 150.88,-292.74 156.88,-292.74 156.88,-292.74 291.73,-292.74 291.73,-292.74 297.73,-292.74 303.73,-298.74 303.73,-304.74 303.73,-304.74 303.73,-316.74 303.73,-316.74 303.73,-322.74 297.73,-328.74 291.73,-328.74\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"155.68\" y=\"-307.29\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Lessor classifies the lease\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node2\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>eq\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#dcfce7\" stroke=\"#166534\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,2\" d=\"M66.6,-252.95C66.6,-252.95 12,-252.95 12,-252.95 6,-252.95 0,-246.95 0,-240.95 0,-240.95 0,-228.95 0,-228.95 0,-222.95 6,-216.95 12,-216.95 12,-216.95