"bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"lessor","lo":23,"title":"The lease receivable, step by step","html":"\u003cp>The same lessor finance lease: 3 receipts of $15,000 in arrears at 9%, and a machine expected back worth $4,000 (unguaranteed). Step through the years and see where the \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">receivable\u003c/span> ends up.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"wg\" data-wg=\"roll\" data-key=\"lease-lessor-ni\" data-cfg=\"{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;v&quot;:4000,&quot;label&quot;:&quot;residual 4,000&quot;},&quot;panels&quot;:[{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Lessor: lease receivable&quot;,&quot;sub&quot;:&quot;3 × 15,000 in arrears · 9% · residual 4,000&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;bal&quot;:&quot;Lease receivable&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:41058,&quot;startCap&quot;:&quot;Day 1: {a|net investment} = PV of payments 37,969 + PV of residual 3,089 = {a|41,058}.&quot;,&quot;years&quot;:[{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Year 1&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;finance income&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;i&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:3695,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 1: {i|finance income} = {a|opening 41,058} × 9% = {i|3,695}.&quot;},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;receipt&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-15000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;{a|Cash received} 15,000 leaves {a|29,753}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Year 2&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;finance income&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;i&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:2678,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 2: {i|finance income} = {a|opening 29,753} × 9% = {i|2,678}.&quot;},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;receipt&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-15000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;{a|Cash received} 15,000 leaves {a|17,431}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Year 3&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;finance income&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;i&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:1569,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 3: {i|finance income} = {a|opening 17,431} × 9% = {i|1,569}. (Rounded.)&quot;},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;receipt&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-15000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;{a|Cash received} 15,000 leaves {a|4,000}. That is the residual: the machine comes back.&quot;}]}]}],&quot;notes&quot;:{&quot;start&quot;:&quot;The lessee’s {l|liability} in reverse: the lessor’s {a|receivable} earns {i|income} and is collected in {a|cash}. Press Play or Next.&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[&quot;Step 1: {i|finance income} at the implicit rate on the {a|opening receivable}.&quot;,&quot;Step 2: the {a|receipt} reduces the {a|receivable}.&quot;],&quot;end&quot;:&quot;**It doesn’t end at zero.** After the last receipt 4,000 is left: the unguaranteed residual, recovered by taking the machine back. Total {i|finance income} 7,942 = receipts 45,000 + residual 4,000 − {a|net investment} 41,058.&quot;}}\">\u003c/div>","id":"visual-1ggfi4","sect":8,"part":"Subsequent measurement · lessor"},{"id":"je-178jah","type":"je","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"lessor","lo":23,"q":"RoastPro leases a roaster to Kopi Co from 1 Jan 20X1: 4 payments of $10,000 in arrears, rate implicit in the lease 8%. It is a finance lease; the {a|lease receivable} on day 1 is $33,121, equal to the machine’s {a|carrying amount}, so there is no selling profit. Record RoastPro’s receipt of the first $10,000 on 31 Dec 20X1.","accounts":["Lease receivable","Equipment","Cash","Finance income","Lease income","Depreciation expense","Lease liability","Retained earnings"],"lines":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Cash","amount":10000},{"side":"Cr","account":"Finance income","amount":2650},{"side":"Cr","account":"Lease receivable","amount":7350}],"why":"The lessor’s schedule mirrors the lessee’s: 2,650 is {i|finance income}, 7,350 reduces the {a|receivable}. (On day 1: Dr {a|Lease receivable} 33,121, Cr {a|Equipment} 33,121.)","sect":8,"part":"Subsequent measurement · lessor"},{"id":"think-11jdh6","type":"think","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"lessor","lo":23,"scenario":"A landlord leases a café unit to Kopi Co for 3 years under an operating lease. To win the tenant, year 1 is **rent-free**; years 2 and 3 are $9,000 each.","prompt":"Should the landlord recognise zero {i|income} in year 1?","answer":["No. The landlord gave the use of the unit for all three years, so {i|income} should match that. Free rent isn’t free; it’s spread over the whole term.","Operating {i|lease income} is recognised **straight-line**: total $18,000 ÷ 3 years."],"sect":8,"part":"Subsequent measurement · lessor"},{"id":"calc-v0l94q","type":"calc","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"lessor","lo":23,"q":"A landlord leases a café unit for 3 years under an operating lease. Year 1 is rent-free; years 2 and 3 are $9,000 each. What {i|lease income} does the landlord recognise in year 1?","answer":6000,"unit":"$","working":["($9,000 × 2) ÷ 3 = $6,000 each year.","Year 1 entry: Dr {a|Accrued lease income} (an asset) 6,000, Cr {i|Lease income} 6,000. The landlord also keeps charging {x|depreciation} on the unit."],"sect":8,"part":"Subsequent measurement · lessor"},{"type":"compare","id":"compare-subsequent","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"lessor","lo":23,"special":"Lessee: {x|interest} on the {l|liability} plus {x|depreciation} of the {a|ROU asset}, so the {x|expense} is front-loaded. Lessor: {i|finance income} at a constant rate on the {a|receivable} (finance lease), or straight-line {i|lease income} plus {x|depreciation} (operating lease).","sect":8,"part":"Subsequent measurement · lessor"},{"type":"map","id":"map-9-derecognise","bucket":"derecognise","blabel":"sale & leaseback","sect":9,"part":"Derecognise / transfer · sale & leaseback"},{"id":"think-6q0cp0","type":"think","bucket":"derecognise","blabel":"sale & leaseback","lo":24,"scenario":"A company sells its head office for more than its {a|carrying amount}, then immediately leases it back for 10 years and carries on working there.","prompt":"It still uses the building every day. Should it book the whole profit on the sale?","answer":["Not all of it. It has only really given up part of the building: the years after the leaseback ends (the buyer’s share). You can’t sell the cake, keep eating most of it, and book a profit on the whole thing.","So the {i|gain} is recognised only on the **rights transferred** to the buyer. And first, check whether it is really a sale at all."],"sect":9,"part":"Derecognise / transfer · sale & leaseback"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"derecognise","blabel":"sale & leaseback","lo":24,"title":"Sale and leaseback","body":["Now the seller becomes a lessee of its own asset. Two standards meet here: SFRS(I) 15 decides whether there was a sale, and SFRS(I) 16 limits the {i|gain} to what was really given up.","First ask: **is the transfer a sale** under SFRS(I) 15? (Has control passed to the buyer?)","- **Yes, a sale:** derecognise the {a|asset}. Measure the {a|ROU asset} at the **share of the {a|old carrying amount}** kept. Recognise {i|gain} only on the rights **transferred**.","- **Not a sale:** keep the {a|asset}. The {a|cash} received is a {l|financial liability}: it is really a loan.","> {a|Right-of-use asset} = {a|carrying amount} × (PV of leaseback payments ÷ fair value)","Notes example: {a|CA} $600,000, sold at FV $1,000,000, PV of leaseback $400,000. {a|ROU} = $240,000; {i|gain} recognised = $240,000 (of the total $400,000).","! A sale price above fair value is **extra financing** from the buyer; below fair value it is a **prepayment** of lease payments."],"id":"rule-1i3b09","sect":9,"part":"Derecognise / transfer · sale & leaseback"},{"id":"calc-9wvbid","type":"calc","bucket":"derecognise","blabel":"sale & leaseback","lo":24,"q":"A building with {a|carrying amount} $400,000 is sold at its fair value of $500,000 (a genuine sale) and leased back. PV of leaseback payments is $200,000. What {i|gain} does the seller-lessee recognise?","answer":60000,"unit":"$","working":["Total {i|gain} = 500,000 − 400,000 = 100,000.","Share transferred = (500,000 − 200,000) ÷ 500,000 = 60%.","{i|Gain} recognised = 100,000 × 60% = **$60,000**.","Check: {a|ROU} = 400,000 × 200,000/500,000 = 160,000. Dr {a|Cash} 500,000, Dr {a|ROU asset} 160,000; Cr {a|Building} 400,000, Cr {l|Lease liability} 200,000, Cr {i|Gain} 60,000."],"sect":9,"part":"Derecognise / transfer · sale & leaseback"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"derecognise","blabel":"sale & leaseback","lo":24,"title":"Sale and leaseback: the split","intro":"The calculation you just did, drawn. The fair value splits into rights kept and rights sold.","notes":{"sale":"Apply SFRS(I) 15: has control of the asset passed to the buyer?","no":"No sale: no derecognition and no {i|gain}. The {a|cash} is in substance a secured loan ({l|financial liability}).","fv":"If the price differs from fair value, the difference is extra financing ({l|liability}, above FV) or a {a|prepayment} of rent (below FV).","kept":"The seller keeps the right to use the asset for the leaseback period: this share was never really sold.","tr":"The buyer’s share: the years after the leaseback ends.","rou":"Measured at the retained share of the old {a|carrying amount}, not at the PV of 200,000. The {i|gain} on this part (40,000) is never recognised.","gain":"Only the {i|gain} on the rights transferred reaches profit or loss."},"walk":[{"nodes":["sale","no"],"text":"First: is it really a sale? If not, keep the {a|asset} and treat the {a|cash} as a loan ({l|financial liability})."},{"nodes":["fv"],"text":"If it is a sale: the asset is sold at fair value 500,000, for a total {i|gain} of 100,000."},{"nodes":["kept","rou"],"text":"Rights retained (40%): become the {a|ROU asset} at 40% of the {a|old carrying amount}."},{"nodes":["tr","gain"],"text":"Rights transferred (60%): only this share of the {i|gain} is recognised, 60,000."}],"id":"diagram-1bwqz9","sect":9,"part":"Derecognise / transfer · sale & leaseback","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:440px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 400.00 267.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xl