.18,-76\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"221.02,-78.45 228.02,-76 221.02,-73.55 221.02,-78.45\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node6\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>oci\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#f3f4f6\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,2\" d=\"M311.7,-36C311.7,-36 247.35,-36 247.35,-36 241.35,-36 235.35,-30 235.35,-24 235.35,-24 235.35,-12 235.35,-12 235.35,-6 241.35,0 247.35,0 247.35,0 311.7,0 311.7,0 317.7,0 323.7,-6 323.7,-12 323.7,-12 323.7,-24 323.7,-24 323.7,-30 317.7,-36 311.7,-36\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"269.77\" y=\"-18.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#374151\">OCI\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"246.15\" y=\"-9.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#374151\">tax on OCI items\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge5\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>def&#45;&gt;oci\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" stroke-dasharray=\"1,5\" d=\"M127.68,-58.91C159.21,-50.36 196.91,-40.13 226.74,-32.05\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"227.35,-34.42 233.47,-30.22 226.07,-29.69 227.35,-34.42\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"172.35\" y=\"-55.65\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> if OCI item \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"type":"map","id":"map-6-recognise","bucket":"recognise","sect":6,"part":"Recognise"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"recognise","lo":28,"title":"Recognition and measurement","body":["You can now compute both halves of Lim’s tax. This page pulls them into one formula and adds the two questions every balance raises: do we recognise it at all, and at which rate?","> {x|Tax expense} = {x|current tax} + (closing deferred tax − opening deferred tax)","- **{x|Current tax}:** taxable profit × rate. Unpaid → {l|Current tax payable}; overpaid → {a|current tax **asset**}.","- {l|Deferred tax liability}: recognise for **all** taxable temporary differences (narrow exceptions, e.g. goodwill on initial recognition).","- {a|Deferred tax asset}: recognise **only to the extent future taxable profit is probable**.","- **Rate:** the rate **enacted or substantively enacted** by the reporting date for when the difference reverses. **Never discount** deferred tax.","! A rate the government has only *proposed* is not used."],"id":"rule-16i10c","sect":6,"part":"Recognise"},{"type":"mcq","bucket":"recognise","lo":28,"q":"Which statement about **recognising** deferred tax is correct?","options":[{"t":"A {l|DTL} is recognised only if it is probable that the tax will be paid","why":"There is no probability test for a DTL. It is recognised for (almost) all taxable temporary differences."},{"t":"A {a|DTA} is recognised for every deductible temporary difference","why":"Only to the extent that future taxable profit is probable. That test is what makes DTAs different."},{"t":"A {l|DTL} is recognised for all taxable temporary differences, with narrow exceptions such as goodwill on initial recognition","ok":true,"why":"That is the rule. The probable-profit test applies only to the asset side."},{"t":"Deferred tax is recognised only for differences that reverse within 12 months","why":"When a difference reverses affects the rate used, not whether it is recognised. And deferred tax is never discounted or split by timing."}],"id":"mcq-3ux680","sect":6,"part":"Recognise"},{"type":"map","id":"map-7-subsequent","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"P&L or OCI","sect":7,"part":"Subsequent measurement · P&L or OCI"},{"id":"think-1u5fzw","type":"think","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"P&L or OCI","lo":28,"scenario":"Lim revalues its building upward by $50,000. The gain goes to the {e|revaluation surplus} in OCI. The tax base is unchanged and the tax rate is 17%.","prompt":"The revaluation creates a taxable difference. Where should the deferred tax on it go: P&L or OCI?","answer":["**OCI.** Deferred tax follows the item like a shadow: the revaluation went to OCI, so its tax goes there too.","{l|DTL} = 50,000 × 17% = $8,500. {e|Net surplus} in equity = $41,500. Nothing touches P&L."],"sect":7,"part":"Subsequent measurement · P&L or OCI"},{"id":"je-1fquyk","type":"je","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"P&L or OCI","lo":28,"q":"Lim revalues its building upward by $50,000, with the gain in the {e|revaluation surplus} (OCI); the tax base is unchanged and the rate is 17%. The revaluation itself is already booked. Record the deferred tax on it.","accounts":["Current tax expense","Current tax payable","Deferred tax expense","Deferred tax income","Deferred tax liability","Deferred tax asset","Revaluation surplus (OCI)","Property, plant and equipment","Cash","Retained earnings","Accruals"],"lines":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Revaluation surplus (OCI)","amount":8500},{"side":"Cr","account":"Deferred tax liability","amount":8500}],"why":"50,000 × 17% = 8,500, charged against the {e|surplus} in OCI, not to {x|deferred tax expense}.","sect":7,"part":"Subsequent measurement · P&L or OCI"},{"type":"visual","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"P&L or OCI","lo":28,"title":"Where the revaluation gain ends up","html":"\u003cp>Two layers: the 50,000 gain splits into the tax that will be due when the value is recovered (\u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">DTL\u003c/span>) and what is left for owners (\u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">net surplus\u003c/span>). Both sit outside P&amp;L.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"cbars\">\u003cdiv class=\"cb-key\">\u003cspan>\u003cspan class=\"seg l\">\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">deferred tax liability\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan>\u003cspan class=\"seg e\">\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">net revaluation surplus\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\n    \u003cdiv class=\"cb-year\">\u003cdiv class=\"cb-cap\">Gain in OCI: \u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">50,000\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-track\">\u003cspan class=\"seg e\" style=\"flex:none;width:100.00%\">\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-year\">\u003cdiv class=\"cb-cap\">Split: \u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">8,500\u003c/span> + \u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">41,500\u003c/span> = 50,000\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-track\">\u003cspan class=\"seg l\" style=\"flex:none;width:17.00%\">\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"seg e\" style=\"flex:none;width:83.00%\">\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\n  \u003c/div>\u003cp class=\"cap\">17% of the gain is owed to the taxman later, so it sits in the \u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">DTL\u003c/span>; the \u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">revaluation surplus\u003c/span> keeps the other 83%.\u003c/p>","id":"visual-is0z1j","sect":7,"part":"Subsequent measurement · P&L or OCI"},{"type":"map","id":"map-8-subsequent","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"movement","sect":8,"part":"Subsequent measurement · movement"},{"id":"visual-1uc7lp","type":"visual","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"movement","lo":29,"title":"The balance sheet liability approach in five steps","html":"\u003cp>So far we have built the pieces one by one. This is the whole method in order, the routine you run on every balance at every year end.\u003c/p>\u003col class=\"flow\">\n      \u003cli class=\"q\">\u003cb>1 · For each asset and liability\u003c/b>\u003cspan>compare carrying amount with tax base\u003c/span>\u003c/li>\n      \u003cli class=\"q\">\u003cb>2 · Temporary difference\u003c/b>\u003cspan>carrying amount − tax base: taxable or deductible?\u003c/span>\u003c/li>\n      \u003cli class=\"q\">\u003cb>3 · Multiply by the enacted rate\u003c/b>\u003cspan>taxable → \u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">Deferred tax liability\u003c/span>; deductible → \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">Deferred tax asset\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/li>\n      \u003cli class=\"q\">\u003cb>4 · DTA test\u003c/b>\u003cspan>recognise a \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">DTA\u003c/span> only to the extent future taxable profit is probable\u003c/span>\u003c/li>\n      \u003cli class=\"end\">\u003cstrong>5 · Movement = closing − opening\u003c/strong> (remeasure the opening balance if the rate changed). Goes to P&amp;L, or OCI/equity if the item went there.\u003c/li>\n    \u003c/ol>","sect":8,"part":"Subsequent measurement · movement"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"movement","lo":29,"title":"Deferred tax in five steps","intro":"The chart from your notes (master.pdf). Tap a box, or walk through it.","notes":{"s1":"Go through the statement of financial position item by item. For each one, find its carrying amount and its tax base.","s2":"Temporary difference = carrying amount − tax base. Permanent items never get here.","tx":"Taxable: more tax later. {a|Asset} carried above its tax base (e.g. fast allowances, a revaluation), or a {l|liability} below it.","dd":"Deductible: less tax later. {a|Asset} below its tax base, a {l|liability} above it (e.g. a {l|provision}), or unused tax losses.","dtl":"{l|DTL} = difference × the rate enacted or substantively enacted for when it reverses. No probability test.","dta":"{a|DTA} = difference × enacted rate, but only to the extent future taxable profit is probable (step 4).","mv":"Work out the closing balance first. The movement is closing − opening; if the rate changed, the opening balance is remeasured too.","pl":"Most movements go to P&L as {x|deferred tax expense} or {i|income}.","oci":"If the item went to OCI or equity (e.g. a {e|revaluation surplus}), its deferred tax goes there too."},"walk":[{"nodes":["s1","s2"],"text":"Steps 1–2: for each item, carrying amount − tax base = temporary difference."},{"nodes":["tx","dd"],"text":"Is it taxable (tax later) or deductible (tax saved later)?"},{"nodes":["dtl","dta"],"text":"Step 3: × enacted rate. Step 4: a {a|DTA} only if future taxable profit is probable."},{"nodes":["mv"],"text":"Step 5: the {x|expense} is the movement, closing − opening, not the closing balance."},{"nodes":["pl","oci"],"text":"The movement follows the item: P&L for most, OCI for a revaluation."}],"caption":"Closing balance first; the {x|expense} falls out as the movement.","id":"diagram-1filyx","sect":8,"part":"Subsequent measurement · movement","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:515px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 468.00 360.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(14.4 345.4)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-14.4,14.4 -14.4,-345.4 453.88,-345.4 453.88,14.4 -14.4,14.4\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>s1\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e8eef6\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M283.6,-331C283.6,-331 134.5,-331 134.5,-331 128.5,-331 122.5,-325 122.5,-319 122.5,-319 122.5,-307 122.5,-307 122.5,-301 128.5,-295 134.5,-295 134.5,-295 283.6,-295 283.6,-295 289.6,-295 295.6,-301 295.6,-307 295.6,-307 295.6,-319 295.6,-319 295.6,-325 289.6,-331 283.6,-331\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"133.3\" y=\"-313.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">1 &#160;For each asset and liability\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"152.05\" y=\"-304.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">carrying amount vs tax base\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node2\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>s2\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e8eef6\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M341.35,-272C341.35,-272 76.75,-272 76.75,-272 70.75,-272 64.75,-266 64.75,-260 64.75,-260 64.75,-248 64.75,-248 64.75,-242 70.75,-236 76.75,-236 76.75,-236 341.35,-236 341.35,-236 347.35,-236 353.35,-242 353.35,-248 353.35,-248 353.35,-260 353.35,-260 353.35,-266 347.35,-272 341.35,-272\"/>\n\u003c