ement**: 5,100 − 4,250 = **$850**.","Under the balance sheet approach you work out the {l|closing balance} first, then the {x|expense} falls out as the difference. Balance first, P&L gets the leftovers."],"sect":8,"part":"Subsequent measurement · movement"},{"id":"visual-337158","type":"visual","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"movement","lo":29,"title":"Deferred tax worksheet: machine","html":"\u003cp>The answer above, as the worksheet you would actually draw: one row per year end, the \u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">DTL\u003c/span> computed fresh each time, and the \u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">expense\u003c/span> taken as the change.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"tbl-wrap\">\u003ctable class=\"tbl num\">\u003cthead>\u003ctr>\u003cth>\u003c/th>\u003cth>Carrying amount\u003c/th>\u003cth>Tax base\u003c/th>\u003cth>Difference\u003c/th>\u003cth>DTL 17%\u003c/th>\u003c/tr>\u003c/thead>\u003ctbody>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>End of year 1\u003c/td>\u003ctd>75,000\u003c/td>\u003ctd>50,000\u003c/td>\u003ctd>25,000\u003c/td>\u003ctd>4,250\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>End of year 2\u003c/td>\u003ctd>50,000\u003c/td>\u003ctd>20,000\u003c/td>\u003ctd>30,000\u003c/td>\u003ctd>5,100\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003cth scope=\"row\">Year-2 movement\u003c/th>\u003ctd>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cb>850\u003c/b>\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n    \u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\u003c/div>\n    \u003cp class=\"cap\">Year-2 entry: Dr \u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">Deferred tax expense\u003c/span> 850, Cr \u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">Deferred tax liability\u003c/span> 850.\u003c/p>","sect":8,"part":"Subsequent measurement · movement"},{"id":"calc-rlvo1p","type":"calc","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"movement","lo":29,"q":"{l|Opening DTL} $4,250. At year end the taxable difference is $30,000 at 17%. What is the **{x|deferred tax expense}** for the year?","answer":850,"unit":"$","working":["{l|Closing DTL} = 30,000 × 17% = 5,100.","{x|Expense} = 5,100 − 4,250 = $850."],"sect":8,"part":"Subsequent measurement · movement"},{"id":"think-ppe9lz","type":"think","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"movement","lo":29,"scenario":"Lim’s machine has a taxable temporary difference of $25,000 at the end of year 1, and Lim has been using the 17% rate. Suppose that before the year end, a new tax rate of 15% is enacted for future years.","prompt":"Which rate should Lim use, and what does that do to the deferred tax balance?","answer":["Use the **enacted** 15%, because that is the rate when the difference reverses. {l|DTL} = 25,000 × 15% = $3,750.","If Lim had already booked $4,250 at 17%, it remeasures: a $500 **{i|credit}** to P&L. A rate cut reduces a {l|DTL}."],"sect":8,"part":"Subsequent measurement · movement"},{"id":"mcq-116pln","type":"mcq","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"movement","lo":29,"q":"A company has an {l|opening DTL} of $4,250 (a $25,000 difference at 17%). During the year a rate of 15% is substantively enacted and the difference is unchanged. What is the effect on profit or loss?","options":[{"t":"No effect: deferred tax is measured at the rate when it first arose","why":"Deferred tax is remeasured at each reporting date using the enacted rate."},{"t":"{i|Deferred tax credit} of $500","ok":true,"why":"{l|New DTL} 3,750 vs 4,250: the 500 reduction goes to P&L (the original difference arose there)."},{"t":"{x|Deferred tax expense} of $500","why":"Wrong direction: a lower rate reduces a {l|liability}, which is a credit."},{"t":"Credit of $500 to OCI","why":"The difference arose in P&L (allowances vs depreciation), so the rate effect goes to P&L."}],"sect":8,"part":"Subsequent measurement · movement"},{"id":"worked-1uxtdt","type":"worked","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"movement","lo":29,"title":"Worked example: a year of tax with a rate change","q":"Kallang Engineering’s taxable profit for 20X2 is $400,000, taxed at 17%. At the end of 20X1 its plant had a taxable temporary difference of $40,000 ({l|DTL} $6,800 at 17%). At the end of 20X2 the difference is $70,000. During 20X2 a 15% rate was enacted for 20X3 onwards. Record the tax for 20X2.","intro":["A typical exam question: you get taxable profit, the opening and closing temporary differences, and a rate change, and must give the entry or the {x|tax expense}. Remember two things:","- {x|Current tax} uses **this year’s** rate; the {l|closing DTL} uses the rate **enacted for when the difference reverses**.","- The {x|deferred tax expense} is the **movement** ({l|closing} − {l|opening}), never the closing balance itself.","Then follow these steps: current tax → closing DTL → movement → check → entry."],"steps":[{"h":"Calculate the current tax.","t":"20X2 profit is still taxed at 17%: {x|Current tax} = 400,000 × 17% = **{x|68,000}**."},{"h":"Measure the closing DTL at the enacted rate.","t":"The difference reverses from 20X3, when 15% applies: {l|Closing DTL} = 70,000 × 15% = **{l|10,500}**."},{"h":"Take the movement as the deferred tax expense.","t":"{x|Deferred tax expense} = {l|closing 10,500} − {l|opening 6,800} = **{x|3,700}**."},{"h":"Check the movement in two parts.","t":["Rate cut on the opening difference: 40,000 × 2% = {i|800 credit}.","New difference at the new rate: 30,000 × 15% = {x|4,500 charge}.","Net: 4,500 − 800 = **{x|3,700}**. It ties."]},{"h":"Record the entry and the total tax expense.","je":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Current tax expense","amount":68000},{"side":"Dr","account":"Deferred tax expense","amount":3700},{"side":"Cr","account":"Current tax payable","amount":68000},{"side":"Cr","account":"Deferred tax liability","amount":3700}],"after":"{x|Total tax expense} = {x|68,000} + {x|3,700} = **{x|71,700}**."}],"sect":8,"part":"Subsequent measurement · movement"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"movement","lo":29,"title":"The DTL roll-forward","intro":"Kallang’s {l|DTL} from opening to closing. Each step says where its movement goes.","notes":{"open":"Last year’s {l|balance}, measured at last year’s rate: 40,000 × 17% = $6,800.","rate":"The opening difference is remeasured at the new 15% rate: 40,000 × 2% = $800 less. A rate cut reduces a {l|DTL}: a {i|credit}.","grow":"The difference grew by 30,000. At the new rate: × 15% = $4,500 more.","ocim":"Movements on items that went to OCI, such as a {e|revaluation surplus}. Kallang has none.","close":"Check: 70,000 × 15% = $10,500. Always compute the {l|closing balance} directly.","pl":"Net P&L {x|deferred tax expense} = 4,500 − 800 = $3,700 ({l|closing} 10,500 − {l|opening} 6,800).","oci":"Deferred tax on OCI items goes to OCI, not P&L."},"walk":[{"nodes":["open"],"text":"Start from the {l|opening DTL}: $6,800 at 17%."},{"nodes":["rate","pl"],"text":"Rate change first: remeasure the opening difference at 15%, a $800 {i|credit} to P&L."},{"nodes":["grow","pl"],"text":"Then the new difference: 30,000 × 15% = $4,500, a {x|charge} to P&L."},{"nodes":["ocim","oci"],"text":"OCI items (a revaluation) would add here, with their tax in OCI. None for Kallang."},{"nodes":["close","pl"],"text":"{l|Closing DTL} $10,500. Net P&L {x|charge} $3,700."}],"caption":"{l|Opening} + rate change + new differences (P&L) + OCI items = {l|closing}.","id":"diagram-zzu0z4","sect":8,"part":"Subsequent measurement · movement","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:349px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 317.00 309.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(14.4 294.4)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-14.4,14.4 -14.4,-294.4 302.75,-294.4 302.75,14.4 -14.4,14.4\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>open\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e8eef6\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M239.23,-280C239.23,-280 151.62,-280 151.62,-280 145.62,-280 139.62,-274 139.62,-268 139.62,-268 139.62,-256 139.62,-256 139.62,-250 145.62,-244 151.62,