t-anchor=\"start\" x=\"25.8\" y=\"-18.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"white\">Closing DTL\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"10.8\" y=\"-9.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"white\">70,000 × 15% = 10,500\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge4\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>ocim&#45;&gt;close\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M95.81,-60.62C90.79,-55.03 85.13,-48.73 79.77,-42.76\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"81.62,-41.16 75.12,-37.59 77.98,-44.43 81.62,-41.16\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node7\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>oci\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e6f4f1\" stroke=\"#0f766e\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M180.43,-36C180.43,-36 150.43,-36 150.43,-36 144.43,-36 138.43,-30 138.43,-24 138.43,-24 138.43,-12 138.43,-12 138.43,-6 144.43,0 150.43,0 150.43,0 180.43,0 180.43,0 186.43,0 192.43,-6 192.43,-12 192.43,-12 192.43,-24 192.43,-24 192.43,-30 186.43,-36 180.43,-36\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"155.68\" y=\"-14.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">OCI\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge7\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>ocim&#45;&gt;oci\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,2\" d=\"M127.33,-60.62C132.56,-54.91 138.46,-48.46 144.02,-42.38\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"145.5,-44.4 148.42,-37.58 141.89,-41.09 145.5,-44.4\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"type":"visual","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"movement","lo":29,"title":"What the rate cut did to Kallang’s DTL","html":"\u003cp>The roll-forward above, animated, next to a twin where the rate stayed at 17%. Two movements each: first the \u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">opening balance\u003c/span> is remeasured, then the year’s new difference is added. Only the left panel has anything to remeasure.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"wg\" data-wg=\"roll\" data-key=\"it-rate\" data-cfg=\"{&quot;panels&quot;:[{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Rate cut to 15%&quot;,&quot;sub&quot;:&quot;enacted during 20X2&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;l&quot;,&quot;bal&quot;:&quot;Deferred tax liability&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:6800,&quot;startCap&quot;:&quot;{l|Opening DTL} 40,000 × 17% = {l|6,800}.&quot;,&quot;years&quot;:[{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X2&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;rate change&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;i&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-800,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Remeasure the {l|opening} difference at 15%: 40,000 × 2% = {i|800 credit}. {l|DTL} now {l|6,000}.&quot;},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;new difference&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:4500,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;The difference grew by 30,000, × 15% = {x|4,500 charge}. {l|Closing DTL} = 70,000 × 15% = {l|10,500}.&quot;}]}]},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;If 17% had stayed&quot;,&quot;sub&quot;:&quot;no rate change&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;l&quot;,&quot;bal&quot;:&quot;Deferred tax liability&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:6800,&quot;startCap&quot;:&quot;Same opening: {l|6,800}.&quot;,&quot;years&quot;:[{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X2&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;rate change&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;i&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:0,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;No new rate, so nothing to remeasure. The balance holds still.&quot;},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;new difference&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:5100,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;30,000 × 17% = {x|5,100 charge}. {l|Closing DTL} = 70,000 × 17% = {l|11,900}.&quot;}]}]}],&quot;notes&quot;:{&quot;start&quot;:&quot;Kallang’s plant: taxable difference 40,000 at the start of 20X2, 70,000 at the end. Left: the 15% rate enacted in 20X2. Right: what would have happened without it.&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[&quot;Step 1: remeasure the **opening** balance at the new rate.&quot;,&quot;Step 2: the year’s new difference, at the new rate too.&quot;],&quot;end&quot;:&quot;**The rate cut is worth 1,400.** That is 70,000 × 2%: the whole closing difference at the lower rate. P&amp;L: {x|3,700} with the cut vs {x|5,100} without.&quot;}}\">\u003c/div>","id":"visual-ci000v","sect":8,"part":"Subsequent measurement · movement"},{"id":"je-q90nc0","type":"je","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"movement","lo":29,"given":[0,1],"q":"Bedok Bakery’s {x|current tax} for 20X5 is $51,000 (already filled in). The taxable temporary difference on its ovens fell from $60,000 to $45,000 during the year. The rate is 17% throughout. Complete the entry.","accounts":["Current tax expense","Current tax payable","Deferred tax expense","Deferred tax income","Deferred tax liability","Deferred tax asset","Revaluation surplus (OCI)","Property, plant and equipment","Cash","Retained earnings","Accruals"],"lines":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Current tax expense","amount":51000},{"side":"Cr","account":"Current tax payable","amount":51000},{"side":"Dr","account":"Deferred tax liability","amount":2550},{"side":"Cr","account":"Deferred tax income","amount":2550}],"why":"{l|Closing DTL} 45,000 × 17% = 7,650 vs {l|opening} 10,200. The {l|DTL} falls by 2,550, which is a {i|deferred tax credit} in P&L.","sect":8,"part":"Subsequent measurement · movement"},{"id":"je-pdfxqe","type":"je","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"movement","lo":29,"q":"Serangoon Retail’s taxable profit for 20X3 is $250,000, taxed at 17%. It has {l|warranty provisions} that are deductible when paid. The deductible temporary difference was $30,000 at the start of the year ({a|DTA} $5,100 at 17%) and $50,000 at the end. During 20X3 a 15% rate was enacted for 20X4 onwards. Future profits are probable. Record the tax for 20X3.","accounts":["Current tax expense","Current tax payable","Deferred tax expense","Deferred tax income","Deferred tax liability","Deferred tax asset","Revaluation surplus (OCI)","Property, plant and equipment","Cash","Retained earnings","Accruals"],"lines":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Current tax expense","amount":42500},{"side":"Cr","account":"Current tax payable","amount":42500},{"side":"Dr","account":"Deferred tax asset","amount":2400},{"side":"Cr","account":"Deferred tax income","amount":2400}],"why":"{x|Current tax} 250,000 × 17% = 42,500. {a|Closing DTA} 50,000 × 15% = 7,500 vs {a|opening} 5,100, so the {a|DTA} rises by 2,400: a {i|deferred tax credit}. The rate cut shrinks the {a|DTA}, but the bigger difference more than makes up for it.","sect":8,"part":"Subsequent measurement · movement"},{"type":"compare","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"movement","lo":29,"special":"No fair value and no amortisation: the balance is recomputed from scratch at each year end (difference × enacted rate), and the movement goes to P&L or OCI, wherever the underlying item went.","id":"compare-1kumyt-2","sect":8,"part":"Subsequent measurement · movement"},{"type":"map","id":"map-9-derecognise","bucket":"derecognise","blabel":"reversal","sect":9,"part":"Derecognise / transfer · reversal"},{"id":"think-olnuzy","type":"think","bucket":"derecognise","blabel":"reversal","lo":29,"scenario":"Lim Trading bought a machine (cost $100,000) at the start of year 1, depreciated over 4 years. At the end of year 2 its {a|carrying amount} is $50,000 and its tax base $20,000, so the {l|DTL} is $5,100 at 17%. In year 3 Lim charges $25,000 of {x|depreciation} but claims only the last $20,000 of allowances. By the end of year 4 the machine is fully depreciated and every allowance has been claimed.","prompt":"What happens to Lim’s {l|deferred tax liability} over years 3 and 4, and where does the change go?","answer":["It **unwinds to nil**: the IOU gets paid off. {x|Depreciation} is now bigger than allowances, so taxable profit and {x|current tax} are higher than accounting profit suggests. Releasing the {l|DTL} offsets that.","End of year 3: 25,000 − 0 = 25,000, so {l|DTL} $4,250, down $850. End of year 4: both are nil, so the last $4,250 is released. Each release is {i|Deferred tax income} in P&L.","If the machine were sold instead, its {a|carrying amount} and tax base would both leave the balance sheet and the {l|DTL} would be released the same way. Any tax on the sale itself (such as a balancing charge) is {x|current tax}."],"sect":9,"part":"Derecognise / transfer · reversal"},{"type":"visual","bucket":"derecognise","blabel":"reversal","lo":29,"title":"The gap opens, then closes","html":"\u003cp>Lim’s machine over its whole life, in the books and for tax, on the same scale. The vertical gap between the two panels each year is the taxable temporary difference behind the \u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">DTL\u003c/span>.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"wg\" data-wg=\"roll\" data-key=\"it-gap\" data-cfg=\"{&quot;panels&quot;:[{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;In the books&quot;,&quot;sub&quot;:&quot;{x|depreciation} 25,000 a year&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;bal&quot;:&quot;Carrying amount&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:100000,&quot;startCap&quot;:&quot;Bought for {a|100,000}. The {a|carrying amount} starts at cost.&quot;,&quot;years&quot;:[{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Yr 1&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-25000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 1: {x|depreciation} 25,000 takes the {a|carrying amount} to {a|75,000}. Gap over the tax base: 25,000, so {l|DTL} = 25,000 × 17% = {l|4,250}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Yr 2&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-25000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 2: {x|depreciation} 25,000 takes the {a|carrying amount} to {a|50,000}. Gap over the tax base: 30,000, so {l|DTL} = 30,000 × 17% = {l|5,100}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Yr 3&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-25000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 3: {x|depreciation} 25,000 takes the {a|carrying amount} to {a|25,000}. Gap over the tax base: 25,000, so {l|DTL} = 25,000 × 17% = {l|4,250}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Yr 4&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-25000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 4: {x|depreciation} 25,000 takes the {a|carrying amount} to {a|0}. Gap over the tax base: 0, so {l|DTL} = 0 × 17% = {l|0}.&quot;}]}]},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;For tax&quot;,&quot;sub&quot;:&quot;capital allowances, front-loaded&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;bal&quot;:&quot;Tax base&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:100000,&quot;startCap&quot;:&quot;For tax the machine also starts at its cost, 100,000: all of it is still to be claimed.&quot;,&quot;years&quot;:[{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Yr 1&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;allowances&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;n&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-50000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 1: {n|allowances} of 50,000 take the tax base to 50,000. Faster than depreciation: the gap **widens**.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Yr 2&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;allowances&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;n&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-30000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 2: {n|allowances} of 30,000 take the tax base to 20,000. Faster than depreciation: the gap **widens**.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Yr 3&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;allowances&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;n&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-20000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 3: {n|allowances} of 20,000 take the tax base to 0. Slower than depreciation: the gap **narrows**.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Yr 4&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;allowances&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;n&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:0,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 4: no {n|allowances} left to claim. The tax base stays at 0 while the books catch up.&quot;}]}]}],&quot;notes&quot;:{&quot;start&quot;:&quot;Lim’s machine, cost 100,000. Same machine, two sets of rules. Press Play or Next and watch the gap between the panels.&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[&quot;Each year: the books take off {x|depreciation}, tax takes off {n|capital allowances}. The gap between the two balances is the taxable temporary difference.&quot;],&quot;end&quot;:&quot;**Both end at 0.** Allowances ran ahead (50,000, 30,000, 20,000, 0) while {x|depreciation} stayed at 25,000, so the gap opened (25,000 → 30,000 → 25,000 → 0) and then closed. Over the life both total 100,000: pure timing.&quot;}}\">\u003c/div>","id":"visual-i9kmr3","sect":9,"part":"Derecognise / transfer · reversal"},{"id":"calc-afu65j","type":"calc","bucket":"derecognise","blabel":"reversal","lo":29,"q":"At the start of year 4 Lim’s {l|DTL} on the machine is $4,250. At the end of year 4 the {a|carrying amount} and tax base are both $0. How much **{i|deferred tax income}** goes to P&L in year 4?","answer":4250,"unit":"$","working":["{l|Closing DTL} = 0 × 17% = 0.","Movement = 0 − 4,250: the whole $4,250 is released as {i|deferred tax income}."],"sect":9,"part":"Derecognise / transfer · reversal"},{"type":"visual","bucket":"derecognise","blabel":"reversal","lo":29,"title":"Lim’s DTL, built up and unwound","html":"\u003cp>The same four years, seen from the \u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">deferred tax liability\u003c/span>. Each step is one year’s movement: growth is \u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">deferred tax expense\u003c/span>, release is \u003cspan class=\"el el-i\">deferred tax income\u003c/span>.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"wg\" data-wg=\"roll\" data-key=\"it-dtl\" data-cfg=\"{&quot;panels&quot;:[{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Lim’s DTL&quot;,&quot;sub&quot;:&quot;difference × 17% each year end&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;l&quot;,&quot;bal&quot;:&quot;Deferred tax liability&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:0,&quot;startCap&quot;:&quot;Before the machine arrives there is no difference and no {l|DTL}.&quot;,&quot;years&quot;:[{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Yr 1&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;deferred tax expense&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:4250,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 1: difference 25,000 × 17% = {l|closing DTL 4,250}, so the movement is 4,250 − 0 = {x|4,250 expense} in P&amp;L.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Yr 2&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;deferred tax expense&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:850,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 2: difference 30,000 × 17% = {l|closing DTL 5,100}, so the movement is 5,100 − 4,250 = {x|850 expense} in P&amp;L.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Yr 3&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;deferred tax income&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;i&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-850,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 3: difference 25,000 × 17% = {l|closing DTL 4,250}, so the movement is 4,250 − 5,100 = {i|850 income} in P&amp;L.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Yr 4&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;deferred tax income&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;i&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-4250,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 4: difference 0 × 17% = {l|closing DTL 0}, so the movement is 0 − 4,250 = {i|4,250 income} in P&amp;L.&quot;}]}]}],&quot;notes&quot;:{&quot;start&quot;:&quot;The balance sheet approach in motion: work out the {l|closing DTL} each year, and let the P&amp;L take the movement.&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[&quot;Each year: {x|deferred tax expense} when the {l|DTL} grows, {i|deferred tax income} when it shrinks.&quot;],&quot;end&quot;:&quot;**The IOU is paid off.** The {l|DTL} builds to 5,100 while allowances run ahead, then unwinds to 0. The movements (4,250, 850, (850), (4,250)) sum to nil over the machine’s life.&quot;}}\">\u003c/div>","id":"visual-1m01jb","sect":9,"part":"Derecognise / transfer · reversal"},{"type":"map","id":"map-10-recognise","bucket":"recognise","blabel":"tax losses","sect":10,"part":"Recognise · tax losses"},{"id":"think-46ie71","type":"think","bucket":"recognise","blabel":"tax losses","lo":30,"scenario":"Tembusu Pte Ltd has a tax loss of $300,000 that it can carry forward. Its budgets show taxable profits of only about $200,000 over the next few years that are probable. The tax rate is 17%.","prompt":"Is the tax loss an asset? If so, how much of it?","answer":["Yes, but only partly. A loss is only worth something if there will be **profits to set it against**, like a discount voucher that’s useless unless you actually go shopping.","Recognise a {a|Deferred tax asset} on the $200,000 that is probable: 200,000 × 17% = **$34,000**. The other $100,000 is disclosed as unrecognised."],"sect":10,"part":"Recognise · tax losses"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"recognise","blabel":"tax losses","lo":30,"title":"Unused tax losses","body":["Tembusu’s loss is a future deduction with no {a|carrying amount} behind it, so it gets the same treatment as a deductible difference. The catch is the one every {a|DTA} faces: it is only worth something if profits turn up to use it.","- Carried-forward losses work like a **deductible** temporary difference: they will cut future tax.","- Recognise a {a|DTA} **only to the extent future taxable profit is probable**. A history of **recent losses** is strong evidence against, unless there is convincing other evidence.","- Evidence for: taxable temporary differences that will reverse, forecast profits, tax-planning opportunities, losses from causes unlikely to recur.","- **Reassess every reporting date:** write the {a|DTA} down if profit is no longer probable, or recognise a previously unrecognised {a|DTA} if it now is.","! Singapore: unused trade losses can be carried forward **indefinitely**, but only if the **shareholding test** is met (broadly the same substantial shareholders)."],"id":"rule-feids1","sect":10,"part":"Recognise · tax losses"},{"type":"visual","bucket":"recognise","blabel":"tax losses","lo":30,"title":"Tembusu’s loss, sliced","html":"\u003cp>The loss splits into two layers: the part probable profits will absorb, and the rest. Only the first layer is multiplied by 17% and booked as a \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">DTA\u003c/span>.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"cbars\">\u003cdiv class=\"cb-key\">\u003cspan>\u003cspan class=\"seg a\">\u003c/span>covered by probable profit (and the \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">DTA\u003c/span> on it)\u003c/span>\u003cspan>\u003cspan class=\"seg out\">\u003c/span>not covered (disclosed only)\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\n    \u003cdiv class=\"cb-year\">\u003cdiv class=\"cb-cap\">Unused loss 300,000 = 200,000 + 100,000\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-track\">\u003cspan class=\"seg a\" style=\"flex:none;width:66.67%\">\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"seg out\" style=\"flex:none;width:33.33%\">\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-year\">\u003cdiv class=\"cb-cap\">\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">DTA\u003c/span> = 200,000 × 17% = \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">34,000\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-track\">\u003cspan class=\"seg a\" style=\"flex:none;width:11.33%\">\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\n  \u003c/div>\u003cp class=\"cap\">Only the covered slice becomes an asset. The hatched slice waits in the notes until profits make it probable.\u003c/p>","id":"visual-bn73tr","sect":10,"part":"Recognise · tax losses"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"recognise","blabel":"tax losses","lo":30,"title":"Can a tax loss be a DTA?","intro":"The recognition test for unused losses, with Tembusu’s numbers.","notes":{"loss":"Tembusu’s carried-forward tax loss: $300,000. It works like a deductible temporary difference.","ttd":"First source of profit: taxable temporary differences (e.g. a {l|DTL} on plant) that reverse in the periods the loss can be used. Tembusu has none.","prof":"Second source: forecast taxable profit that is probable. A history of recent losses is strong evidence against, unless there is convincing other evidence.","rec":"Recognise a {a|DTA} on the part covered: 200,000 × 17% = $34,000. Dr {a|Deferred tax asset}, Cr {i|Deferred tax income}.","dis":"The other $100,000 gets no {a|DTA}. It is disclosed as unused losses with no {a|DTA} recognised.","re":"Reassess at every reporting date: write the {a|DTA} down if profit is no longer probable, or recognise more if it now is."},"walk":[{"nodes":["loss"],"text":"Tembusu has $300,000 of unused losses. Is any of it worth an asset?"},{"nodes":["ttd"],"text":"Taxable differences reversing at the right time support a {a|DTA}. None here."},{"nodes":["prof","rec"],"text":"Probable profits of $200,000 support a {a|DTA} of $34,000."},{"nodes":["dis"],"text":"The rest, $100,000, is disclosed, not booked."},{"nodes":["re"],"text":"Every year end, test again."}],"caption":"A {a|DTA} only to the extent future taxable profit is probable.","id":"diagram-qpussv","sect":10,"part":"Recognise · tax losses","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:362px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 329.00 337.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(14.4 322.9)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-14.4,14.4 -14.4,-322.9 314.61,-322.9 314.61,14.4 -14.4,14.4\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>loss\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e8eef6\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M203.47,-308.5C203.47,-308.5 121.88,-308.5 121.88,-308.5 115.88,-308.5 109.88,-302.5 109.88,-296.5 109.88,-296.5 109.88,-284.5 109.88,-284.5 109.88,-278.5 115.88,-272.5 121.88,-272.5 121.88,-272.5 203.47,-272.5 203.47,-272.5 209.47,-272.5 215.47,-278.5 215.47,-284.5 215.47,-284.5 215.47,-296.5 215.47,-296.5 215.47,-302.5 209.47,-308.5 203.47,-308.5\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"120.68\" y=\"-291.05\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Unused tax loss\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"145.8\" y=\"-281.95\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">300,000\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg