1,-75 111,-69 111,-69 111,-57 111,-57 111,-51 117,-45 123,-45 123,-45 203.4,-45 203.4,-45 209.4,-45 215.4,-51 215.4,-57 215.4,-57 215.4,-69 215.4,-69 215.4,-75 209.4,-81 203.4,-81\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"125.7\" y=\"-64\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Contingent liab.\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"146.32\" y=\"-54.95\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">disclose\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\n\u003cg id=\"node11\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>oRm\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#f3f4f6\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,2\" d=\"M203.4,-36C203.4,-36 123,-36 123,-36 117,-36 111,-30 111,-24 111,-24 111,-12 111,-12 111,-6 117,0 123,0 123,0 203.4,0 203.4,0 209.4,0 215.4,-6 215.4,-12 215.4,-12 215.4,-24 215.4,-24 215.4,-30 209.4,-36 203.4,-36\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"146.32\" y=\"-14.12\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\">Nothing\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\n\n\n\n\u003cg id=\"node13\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>iPb\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e6f4f1\" stroke=\"#0f766e\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M314.4,-126C314.4,-126 234,-126 234,-126 228,-126 222,-120 222,-114 222,-114 222,-102 222,-102 222,-96 228,-90 234,-90 234,-90 314.4,-90 314.4,-90 320.4,-90 326.4,-96 326.4,-102 326.4,-102 326.4,-114 326.4,-114 326.4,-120 320.4,-126 314.4,-126\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"234.82\" y=\"-109\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Contingent asset\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"257.32\" y=\"-99.95\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">disclose\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\n\n\u003cg id=\"node14\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>iPs\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#f3f4f6\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,2\" d=\"M314.4,-81C314.4,-81 234,-81 234,-81 228,-81 222,-75 222,-69 222,-69 222,-57 222,-57 222,-51 228,-45 234,-45 234,-45 314.4,-45 314.4,-45 320.4,-45 326.4,-51 326.4,-57 326.4,-57 326.4,-69 326.4,-69 326.4,-75 320.4,-81 314.4,-81\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"257.32\" y=\"-59.12\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\">Nothing\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\n\u003cg id=\"node15\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>iRm\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#f3f4f6\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,2\" d=\"M314.4,-36C314.4,-36 234,-36 234,-36 228,-36 222,-30 222,-24 222,-24 222,-12 222,-12 222,-6 228,0 234,0 234,0 314.4,0 314.4,0 320.4,0 326.4,-6 326.4,-12 326.4,-12 326.4,-24 326.4,-24 326.4,-30 320.4,-36 314.4,-36\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"257.32\" y=\"-14.12\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\">Nothing\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\n\n\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"type":"mcq","bucket":"classify","blabel":"contingent assets","lo":33,"q":"An entity is claiming $90,000 from its insurer for storm damage. The insurer has accepted liability in writing and agreed the amount, but hasn’t paid by year end. How is the claim treated?","options":[{"t":"Recognise a {a|receivable} of $90,000","ok":true,"why":"The inflow is virtually certain (accepted and agreed), so it is no longer a contingent asset. Recognise it."},{"t":"Disclose a contingent asset only","why":"That is the treatment when the inflow is probable but not virtually certain. Written acceptance of an agreed amount takes it beyond that."},{"t":"Nothing until the cash arrives","why":"Recognition doesn’t wait for cash. Virtually certain is enough."},{"t":"Net the $90,000 off the {l|storm-damage repair provision}","why":"There is nothing to net it against here, and reimbursements are shown as a {a|separate asset} anyway."}],"id":"mcq-4xyi4g","sect":3,"part":"Classify · contingent assets"},{"type":"compare","bucket":"classify","preamble":"Unlike a financial liability (a contract to pay a set amount of cash), a provision is uncertain in **timing or amount**, and that uncertainty drives the whole chapter.","blabel":"contingent assets","lo":33,"special":"Here “classify” means sorting by **likelihood**: {l|provision} (recognise), contingent liability (disclose) or nothing; and a contingent asset is disclosed when probable, recognised only when virtually certain.","id":"compare-1kumyt","sect":3,"part":"Classify · contingent assets"},{"type":"map","id":"map-4-recognise","bucket":"recognise","blabel":"the four tests","sect":4,"part":"Recognise · the four tests"},{"type":"think","bucket":"recognise","blabel":"the four tests","lo":32,"scenario":"Orchard Fashion’s website promises: “Changed your mind? Full refund within 60 days, no questions asked.” Singapore law only requires refunds for faulty goods. Orchard has always honoured its promise.","prompt":"The law doesn’t make Orchard refund change-of-mind returns. Does it still have an obligation at year end for sales made in the last 60 days?","answer":["Yes. Its **published policy** and **past practice** have created a **valid expectation** in customers that it will refund them. That is a **constructive obligation**.","The obligating event is the **sale**. Orchard has no realistic alternative but to refund if customers return goods, so it provides for expected refunds."],"id":"think-oqo71x","sect":4,"part":"Recognise · the four tests"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"recognise","blabel":"the four tests","lo":32,"title":"Recognise a provision only if all four tests pass","body":["Classifying told us what a {l|provision} is. Now the gate: Orchard’s refund promise passes it, and these four tests are why.","1. **Present obligation**, either **legal** (contract, law) or **constructive** (past practice, a published policy or a statement that creates a **valid expectation** in others).","2. **From a past event**: the **obligating event** has happened, leaving **no realistic alternative** but to settle. Future plans or intentions don’t count.","3. **Probable outflow**: more likely than not (> 50%) that resources will leave the entity.","4. **Reliable estimate**: almost always possible; only in extremely rare cases can no estimate be made.","+ Memory hook from your notes: **“PPO + estimate”**: Present obligation, Past event, Outflow probable, and a reliable estimate."],"id":"rule-10z935","sect":4,"part":"Recognise · the four tests"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"recognise","blabel":"the four tests","lo":32,"title":"Where does an obligation come from?","intro":"Tests 1 and 2 together. Two routes lead to a present obligation; a plan or intention leads nowhere.","notes":{"legal":"Legal: from a contract, legislation or other operation of law. A signed warranty or a clean-up law.","constr":"Constructive: from the entity’s own conduct, e.g. a published refund policy, an established pattern of past practice, or a specific current statement.","valid":"The entity has shown others it will accept the responsibility, so they validly expect it to.","intent":"A board decision, a budget or a management intention. The entity could still change its mind.","event":"The obligating event: after it, the entity has no realistic alternative but to settle (because of law, or because of the valid expectation).","pres":"Present obligation: tests 1 and 2 pass. Now ask whether the outflow is probable and can be estimated.","none":"If the entity can avoid the cost by its own future actions (e.g. change its plans, stop operating), there is no present obligation."},"walk":[{"nodes":["legal","event"],"text":"Legal route: a contract or law, plus an event that has already happened."},{"nodes":["constr","valid","event"],"text":"Constructive route: the entity’s own conduct creates a valid expectation in others."},{"nodes":["pres"],"text":"Either route gives a present obligation from a past event."},{"nodes":["intent","none"],"text":"An intention alone is not an obligation: it can still be avoided."}],"caption":"Ask: could the entity still avoid this by its own future actions? If yes, no provision.","id":"diagram-xwxcs0","sect":4,"part":"Recognise · the four tests","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:452px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 411.00 248.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(14.4 233.4)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-14.4,14.4 -14.4,-233.4 396.38,-233.4 396.38,14.4 -14.4,14.4\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>legal\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#b45309\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M60.6,-158C60.6,-158 12,-158 12,-158 6,-158 0,-152 0,-146 0,-146 0,-134 0,-134 0,-128 6,-122 12,-122 12,-122 60.6,-122 60.6,-122 66.6,-122 72.6,-128 72.6,-134 72.6,-134 72.6,-146 72.6,-146 72.6,-152 66.6,-158 60.6,-158\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"22.05\" y=\"-140.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Legal\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"10.8\" y=\"-131.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">contract, law\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node5\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>event\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e8eef6\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M157.35,-97C157.35,-97 29.25,-97 29.25,-97 23.25,-97 17.25,-91 17.25,-85 17.25,-85 17.25,-73 17.25,-73 17.25,-67 23.25,-61 29.25,-61 29.25,-61 157.35,-61 157.35,-61 163.35,-61 169.35,-67 169.35,-73 169.35,-73 169.35,-85 169.35,-85 169.35,-91 163.35,-97 157.35,-97\"/>\n\u003ctext