class=\"cb-track\">\u003cspan class=\"seg x\" style=\"width:16.67%\">\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-year\">\u003cdiv class=\"cb-cap\">\u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">Provision\u003c/span> = lower of 80,000 and 50,000 = \u003cstrong>\u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">50,000\u003c/span>\u003c/strong>\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-track\">\u003cspan class=\"seg l\" style=\"width:16.67%\">\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\n    \u003cdiv class=\"cb-key\">\u003cspan>\u003ci class=\"seg i\">\u003c/i>\u003cspan class=\"el el-i\">revenue still to come\u003c/span> (covers part of the cost)\u003c/span>\u003cspan>\u003ci class=\"seg x\">\u003c/i>\u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">net cost of that exit\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan>\u003ci class=\"seg l\">\u003c/i>\u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">provision\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>","id":"visual-1omvgc","sect":6,"part":"Recognise · onerous contracts"},{"type":"compare","bucket":"recognise","blabel":"onerous contracts","lo":33,"special":"Four tests (present obligation, past event, probable outflow, reliable estimate) decide everything. Legal or **constructive**; never for intentions or future operating losses; yes for onerous contracts.","id":"compare-1kumyt-2","sect":6,"part":"Recognise · onerous contracts"},{"type":"map","id":"map-7-initial","bucket":"initial","blabel":"best estimate","sect":7,"part":"Initial measurement · best estimate"},{"id":"think-146ist","type":"think","bucket":"initial","blabel":"best estimate","lo":32,"scenario":"Kallang sells 1,000 ovens with a one-year warranty. Experience says 75% will have no defect, 20% will need a minor repair costing $100, and 5% a major repair costing $400.","prompt":"The most likely outcome for any one oven is “no defect”, so $0. Is the {l|provision} $0? If not, what?","answer":["No. With a **large population** of similar items, some ovens **will** break. Weight each outcome by its probability: the **expected value**.","1,000 × (20% × 100 + 5% × 400) = 1,000 × 40 = **$40,000**."],"sect":7,"part":"Initial measurement · best estimate"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"initial","blabel":"best estimate","lo":32,"title":"Measure at the best estimate","body":["Once a {l|provision} passes the tests, it needs a number. The warranty example showed that “most likely” can be badly wrong for a crowd of items, so the standard picks the method by the shape of the obligation.","+ The **best estimate** is the amount the entity would rationally pay to settle the obligation (or transfer it) at the reporting date.","1. **Large population** of similar items (e.g. warranties): the **expected value**, weighting every outcome by its probability.","2. **Single obligation** (e.g. one lawsuit): the **most likely outcome**, adjusted if the other outcomes are mostly higher or mostly lower.","3. **Discount** to present value when the time value of money is **material**.","- **Future events** (new technology, new laws) count only with sufficient objective evidence that they will happen.","- **Expected {i|gains}** on disposing of {a|assets} are ignored, even if the disposal is linked to the provision.","! Don’t use the most likely outcome for a population, or the expected value for a single obligation."],"id":"rule-18yxyv","sect":7,"part":"Initial measurement · best estimate"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"initial","blabel":"best estimate","lo":32,"title":"Expected value: building up the warranty provision","intro":"The example from your notes. Each outcome is weighted by its probability, then scaled up to the whole population.","notes":{"sold":"1,000 ovens sold this year, each with a one-year warranty. The sale is the obligating event.","ok":"75% need nothing: they contribute zero but still count in the probabilities.","mi":"20% × $100 = $20 per oven sold.","ma":"5% × $400 = $20 per oven sold.","per":"Expected cost per oven = 20 + 20 = $40.","prov":"1,000 × 40 = $40,000. Dr {x|Warranty expense}, Cr {l|Provision for warranties}."},"walk":[{"nodes":["sold"],"text":"Start from the population: every oven sold carries a warranty."},{"nodes":["ok","mi","ma"],"text":"Weight each outcome: probability × cost."},{"nodes":["per"],"text":"Add them up: $40 per oven."},{"nodes":["prov"],"text":"Scale up to all 1,000 ovens: $40,000."}],"caption":"Many similar items → expected value. One big item → most likely outcome.","id":"diagram-1314bo","sect":7,"part":"Initial measurement · best estimate","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:347px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 315.00 248.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(14.4 233.4)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-14.4,14.4 -14.4,-233.4 300.62,-233.4 300.62,14.4 -14.4,14.4\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>sold\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e8eef6\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M191.98,-219C191.98,-219 81.88,-219 81.88,-219 75.88,-219 69.88,-213 69.88,-207 69.88,-207 69.88,-195 69.88,-195 69.88,-189 75.88,-183 81.88,-183 81.88,-183 191.98,-183 191.98,-183 197.98,-183 203.98,-189 203.98,-195 203.98,-195 203.98,-207 203.98,-207 203.98,-213 197.98,-219 191.98,-219\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"96.05\" y=\"-201.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">1,000 units sold\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"80.68\" y=\"-192.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">each with a 1&#45;year warranty\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node2\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>ok\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#f3f4f6\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,2\" d=\"M59.85,-158C59.85,-158 12,-158 12,-158 6,-158 0,-152 0,-146 0,-146 0,-134 0,-134 0,-128 6,-122 12,-12