"unwinding","lo":32,"title":"Provision up, asset down, step by step","html":"\u003cp>Pasir Power again: $100,000 to clean up in 3 years, discounted at 10%. On day 1 the present value sits on \u003cstrong>both\u003c/strong> sides of the balance sheet. Step through the years and watch the two sides go opposite ways.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"wg\" data-wg=\"roll\" data-key=\"decom-b23\" data-cfg=\"{&quot;panels&quot;:[{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Decommissioning provision&quot;,&quot;sub&quot;:&quot;cash 100,000 in 3 years · 10%&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;l&quot;,&quot;bal&quot;:&quot;Provision&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:75131,&quot;startCap&quot;:&quot;Day 1: {l|provision} = 100,000 ÷ 1.10³ = {l|75,131}.&quot;,&quot;years&quot;:[{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Year 1&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;unwinding&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:7513,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;{x|Unwinding} = {l|opening 75,131} × 10% = {x|7,513}, so {l|closing} = {l|82,644}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Year 2&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;unwinding&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:8264,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;{x|Unwinding} = {l|opening 82,644} × 10% = {x|8,264}, so {l|closing} = {l|90,908}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Year 3&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;unwinding&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:9092,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;{x|Unwinding} = {l|opening 90,908} × 10% (rounded so it lands on the cash) = {x|9,092}, so {l|closing} = {l|100,000}. Exactly the cash to pay.&quot;}]}]},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Clean-up cost inside the plant&quot;,&quot;sub&quot;:&quot;same 75,131, depreciated over 3 years&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;bal&quot;:&quot;Carrying amount&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:75131,&quot;startCap&quot;:&quot;Day 1: the same {a|75,131} is added to the {a|plant’s cost}.&quot;,&quot;years&quot;:[{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Year 1&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-25044,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;{x|Depreciation} 75,131 ÷ 3 = {x|25,044}, leaving {a|50,087}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Year 2&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-25044,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;{x|Depreciation} 75,131 ÷ 3 = {x|25,044}, leaving {a|25,043}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Year 3&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-25043,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;{x|Depreciation} 75,131 ÷ 3 (rounded) = {x|25,043}, leaving {a|0}.&quot;}]}]}],&quot;notes&quot;:{&quot;start&quot;:&quot;Day 1: Dr {a|Property, plant and equipment}, Cr {l|Decommissioning provision} 75,131. The same number starts on both sides. Press Play or Next.&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[&quot;Each year the {l|provision} grows by the {x|unwinding} ({x|finance cost}) while the {a|asset} shrinks by {x|depreciation}.&quot;],&quot;end&quot;:&quot;**Two roads to P&amp;L.** The {l|provision} climbs to the {l|100,000} cash; the {a|asset} part falls to nil. Over 3 years P&amp;L bears {x|depreciation} 75,131 + {x|unwinding} 24,869 = **100,000**: the full clean-up cost, spread over the plant’s life.&quot;}}\">\u003c/div>","id":"visual-109qqj","sect":10,"part":"Subsequent measurement · unwinding"},{"type":"map","id":"map-11-subsequent","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"review","sect":11,"part":"Subsequent measurement · review"},{"id":"think-1paj13","type":"think","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"review","lo":32,"scenario":"Last year Marina Ferries provided $500,000 for a lawsuit by passengers injured when one of its gangways collapsed. This year end, after mediation, its lawyers now say the most likely settlement is $420,000.","prompt":"What happens to the {l|provision}, and should last year’s accounts be restated?","answer":["The {l|provision} is **reviewed at every reporting date** and adjusted to the current best estimate: down by $80,000, a credit to this year’s P&L.","No restatement: last year’s figure was the best estimate on the evidence then. A new estimate is a **change in estimate**, dealt with going forward."],"sect":11,"part":"Subsequent measurement · review"},{"id":"calc-19sgy9","type":"calc","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"review","lo":32,"q":"Last year Marina Ferries recognised a {l|provision} of $500,000 for a lawsuit. At this year end, after mediation, its lawyers revise the best estimate of the settlement to $420,000. By how much does this year’s profit increase?","answer":80000,"unit":"$","working":["Adjust the {l|provision} to the new best estimate: 500,000 − 420,000 = 80,000 decrease.","Dr {l|Provision for legal claims} 80,000, Cr {x|Legal claims expense} 80,000: profit rises by $80,000."],"sect":11,"part":"Subsequent measurement · review"},{"type":"mcq","bucket":"subsequent","blabel":"review","lo":32,"q":"Last year a company disclosed a lawsuit as a contingent liability (outflow possible). This year new evidence makes the outflow probable. What should it do?","options":[{"t":"Restate last year’s accounts to show a {l|provision}","why":"Last year’s judgement was right on the evidence then. This is a change in circumstances."},{"t":"Keep disclosing it until the case is decided","why":"Once the outflow is probable (and can be estimated), it must be recognised."},{"t":"Recognise a {l|provision} this year, through this year’s profit or loss","ok":true,"why":"Contingent liabilities are reassessed continually. When the outflow becomes probable, a {l|provision} is recognised in the period of the change."},{"t":"Recognise the {l|provision} directly in {e|retained earnings}","why":"It is a change in estimate, so it goes through this year’s P&L."}],"id":"mcq-1e02r1","sect":11,"part":"Subsequent measurement · review"},{"type":"map","id":"map-12-derecognise","bucket":"derecognise","blabel":"use or reverse","sect":12,"part":"Derecognise / transfer · use or reverse"},{"id":"think-l5kgn9","type":"think","bucket":"derecognise","blabel":"use or reverse","lo":33,"scenario":"Last year Kallang Kitchens provided $40,000 for one-year warranties on the ovens it sold. This year it paid $31,000 of repair claims, and the warranty period has now ended. Meanwhile it needs $20,000 for an unexpected legal bill.","prompt":"What happens to the $9,000 left in the {l|provision}? Could Kallang use it for the legal bill?","answer":["The repairs are charged **against** the {l|provision} (not to {x|expense} again). The warranties have expired, so the $9,000 left is no longer needed: **reverse** it to P&L.","And no, it can’t touch the legal bill. A {l|provision} may be used only for the expenditure it was **originally recognised for**. Otherwise provisions become a cookie jar for smoothing profits."],"sect":12,"part":"Derecognise / transfer · use or reverse"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"derecognise","blabel":"use or reverse","lo":33,"title":"Using and reversing a provision","body":["The {l|provision} has been recognised, measured and kept up to date. This is how it ends: spent on what it was for, or released.","1. **Use:** charge the actual spending against the {l|provision} it was set up for: Dr {l|provision}, Cr {a|Cash}.","2. **Reverse:** if an outflow is no longer probable, release the {l|provision}: Dr {l|provision}, Cr the {x|expense line} (a credit to P&L).","! A {l|provision} is used **only** for the expenditure it was originally recognised for. No moving it to cover something else."],"id":"rule-1s482v","sect":12,"part":"Derecognise / transfer · use or reverse"},{"type":"visual","bucket":"derecognise","blabel":"use or reverse","lo":33,"title":"A provision’s life: recognise, use, reverse","html":"\u003cp>Kallang’s oven warranties from start to finish: $40,000 provided when the ovens are sold, $31,000 of repairs paid next year, and the rest released when the warranties expire. Watch which steps touch P&amp;L and which are just \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">cash\u003c/span>.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"wg\" data-wg=\"roll\" data-key=\"use-b23\" data-cfg=\"{&quot;panels&quot;:[{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Kallang’s warranty provision&quot;,&quot;sub&quot;:&quot;1,000 ovens, one-year warranty&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;l&quot;,&quot;bal&quot;:&quot;Provision&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:0,&quot;startCap&quot;:&quot;Before the sales: no obligation, no {l|provision}.&quot;,&quot;years&quot;:[{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Year 1&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;provide&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:40000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Ovens sold with a warranty: Dr {x|Warranty expense}, Cr {l|Provision} {l|40,000} (the expected value).&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Year 2&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;used&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-31000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Repairs paid: Dr {l|Provision}, Cr {a|Cash} 31,000. No new {x|expense}. {l|9,000} is left.&quot;},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;reversed&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-9000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Warranties expired: the unused {l|9,000} is reversed, a credit to {x|Warranty expense}. {l|Provision} = 0.&quot;}]}]}],&quot;notes&quot;:{&quot;start&quot;:&quot;One {l|provision}, from birth to nil. Press Play or Next.&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[&quot;Recognise: charged to P&amp;L in the year of the sales.&quot;,&quot;Use: spending is charged against the {l|provision} ({a|cash} out, no P&amp;L).&quot;,&quot;Reverse: whatever is no longer needed goes back to P&amp;L.&quot;],&quot;end&quot;:&quot;**Net P&amp;L over the two years: 40,000 − 9,000 = {x|31,000}**, exactly the repairs actually paid. The estimate only moved the cost into the year of the sales. And the leftover can’t be redirected to anything else.&quot;}}\">\u003c/div>","id":"visual-1097jv","sect":12,"part":"Derecognise / transfer · use or reverse"},{"id":"je-p3e5y2","type":"je","bucket":"derecognise","blabel":"use or reverse","lo":33,"q":"Kallang has a {l|warranty provision} of $40,000. During the year it paid $31,000 of repair claims, and the warranty period has now ended. Record the repair payments and the release of the unused {l|provision}.","accounts":["Warranty expense","Provision for warranties","Legal claims expense","Provision for legal claims","Onerous contract expense","Provision for onerous contract","Restructuring expense","Restructuring provision","Decommissioning provision","Property, plant and equipment","Finance cost","Reimbursement receivable","Cash","Trade payables","Accruals","Retained earnings","Other income"],"lines":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Provision for warranties","amount":40000},{"side":"Cr","account":"Cash","amount":31000},{"side":"Cr","account":"Warranty expense","amount":9000}],"why":"31,000 of repairs is charged against the {l|provision}; the unused 9,000 is reversed, reducing this year’s {x|warranty expense}. The {l|provision} is now nil.","sect":12,"part":"Derecognise / transfer · use or reverse"},{"type":"map","id":"map-13-present","bucket":"present","sect":13,"part":"Present & disclose"},{"id":"think-1jsmmg","type":"think","bucket":"present","lo":34,"scenario":"You are a bank lending to Kallang. Its balance sheet shows one line: “{l|Provisions} $X”.","prompt":"What else would you want the notes to tell you?","answer":["How the number **moved** during the year (what was added, used, released). **What** each {l|provision} is for and **when** the cash will go out. How **uncertain** it is.","And the things **not** on the balance sheet: lawsuits that might go against Kallang (contingent liabilities), and claims it might win (contingent assets)."],"sect":13,"part":"Present & disclose"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"present","lo":34,"title":"Disclosure checklist","body":["A single “{l|Provisions}” line tells a reader almost nothing. The notes fill in what the bank asked for, including the items that never reach the balance sheet.","1. **{l|Provisions}, for each class:** a **reconciliation** of {l|opening} to {l|closing} (additions, amounts used, unused amounts reversed, unwinding of the discount). No comparatives are needed for this table.","2. **{l|Provisions}, for each class:** the nature of the obligation, the **expected timing** of outflows, the **uncertainties** about amount or timing (and key assumptions), and any expected **reimbursement**.","3. **Contingent liabilities, unless remote:** their nature and, where practicable, an estimate of the financial effect, the uncertainties and any possible reimbursement.","4. **Contingent assets, where an inflow is probable:** their nature and, where practicable, an estimate of the financial effect. Don’t make the {i|income} sound certain.","5. **Exemption:** in extremely rare cases where disclosure would **seriously prejudice** the entity’s position in a dispute, disclose only the general nature of the dispute and why the information isn’t given.","! A remote contingent liability needs no disclosure."],"id":"rule-rmzbio","sect":13,"part":"Present & disclose"},{"id":"visual-5uyi30","type":"visual","bucket":"present","lo":34,"title":"The provisions reconciliation","html":"\u003cp>Item 1 of the checklist in practice. Every movement you have met in this chapter (new provisions, spending, releases, unwinding) gets its own line, rolling the \u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">opening balance\u003c/span> to the \u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">closing balance\u003c/span>.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"tbl-wrap\">\u003ctable class=\"tbl num reveal-rows\">\u003cthead>\u003ctr>\u003cth>\u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">Warranty provision\u003c/span>\u003c/th>\u003cth>$\u003c/th>\u003c/tr>\u003c/thead>\u003ctbody>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">At 1 January\u003c/span>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>120,000\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>Additional provisions in the year\u003c/td>\u003ctd>45,000\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>Amounts used during the year\u003c/td>\u003ctd>(38,000)\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>Unused amounts reversed\u003c/td>\u003ctd>(12,000)\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>Unwinding of the discount\u003c/td>\u003ctd>6,000\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003cth scope=\"row\">\u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">At 31 December\u003c/span>\u003c/th>\u003ctd>\u003cb>121,000\u003c/b>\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n    \u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\u003c/div>\n    \u003cp class=\"cap\">One table for each class of provision. Comparatives are not required for it.\u003c/p>","sect":13,"part":"Present & disclose"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"present","lo":34,"title":"Where each line of the reconciliation comes from","intro":"Every movement in the provision has a home in the accounts. Tap a line to see the entry.","notes":{"open":"Last year’s {l|closing balance}: $120,000.","add":"New provisions and increases in estimates: Dr {x|expense}, Cr {l|provision} 45,000.","used":"Spending charged against the {l|provision}: Dr {l|provision}, Cr {a|Cash} 38,000. No P&L effect.","rev":"No longer needed: Dr {l|provision}, Cr {x|expense} 12,000. A credit to P&L.","unw":"The discount unwinding on long-dated provisions: Dr {x|Finance cost}, Cr {l|provision} 6,000.","close":"{l|Opening} 120,000 + additions 45,000 − used 38,000 − reversed 12,000 + {x|unwinding} 6,000 = {l|closing} $121,000.","pl":"Additions are charged to P&L (or to the {a|asset}, for decommissioning).","cash":"Using a {l|provision} is a {a|cash} payment, not a new {x|expense}.","cr":"Reversals reduce the {x|expense} in P&L.","fc":"Unwinding is a {x|finance cost}, shown with interest."},"walk":[{"nodes":["open"],"text":"Start from the {l|opening balance}."},{"nodes":["add","pl"],"text":"Additions: charged to P&L."},{"nodes":["used","cash"],"text":"Used: {a|cash} out, no P&L."},{"nodes":["rev","cr"],"text":"Reversed: a credit back to P&L."},{"nodes":["unw","fc"],"text":"Unwinding: {x|finance cost}."},{"nodes":["close"],"text":"{l|Closing balance} $121,000."}],"caption":"Additions and reversals hit operating P&L; unwinding is {x|finance cost}; usage is just {a|cash}.","id":"diagram-dfo4e2","sect":13,"part":"Present & disclose","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:278px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 253.00 370.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(14.4 355.4)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-14.4,14.4 -14.4,-355.4 238.88,-355.4 238.88,14.4 -14.4,14.4\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>open\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e8eef6\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M83.85,-341C83.85,-341 42,-341 42,-341 36,-341 30,-335 30,-329 30,-329 30,-317 30,-317 30,-311 36,-305 42,-305 42,-305 83.85,-305 83.85,-305 89.85,-305 95.85,-311 95.85,-317 95.85,-317 95.85,-329 95.85,-329 95.85,-335 89.85,-341 83.85,-341\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"40.8\" y=\"-323.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Opening\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"46.05\" y=\"-314.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">120,000\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node2\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>add\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#b45309\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M91.72,-280C91.72,-280 34.12,-280 34.12,-280 28.12,-280 22.12,-274 22.12,-268 22.12,-268 22.12,-256 22.12,-256 22.12,-250 28.12,-244 34.12,-244 34.12,-244 91.72,-244 91.72,-244 97.72,-244 103.72,-250 103.72,-256 103.72,-256 103.72,-268 103.72,-268 103.72,-274 97.72,-280 91.72,-280\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"32.92\" y=\"-262.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">+ Additions\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"