fl\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M262.01,-149.53C270.83,-139.95 281.45,-128.43 290.67,-118.42\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"292.08,-119.99 294.6,-114.15 288.99,-117.14 292.08,-119.99\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"293.02\" y=\"-127.28\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> yes \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node5\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>eq\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#f3eeff\" stroke=\"#6d28d9\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M69.03,-36.82C69.03,-36.82 12,-36.82 12,-36.82 6,-36.82 0,-30.82 0,-24.82 0,-24.82 0,-12.82 0,-12.82 0,-6.82 6,-0.82 12,-0.82 12,-0.82 69.03,-0.82 69.03,-0.82 75.03,-0.82 81.03,-6.82 81.03,-12.82 81.03,-12.82 81.03,-24.82 81.03,-24.82 81.03,-30.82 75.03,-36.82 69.03,-36.82\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"23.64\" y=\"-19.37\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Equity\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"8.64\" y=\"-10.27\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">ordinary shares\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge5\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>why&#45;&gt;eq\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M130.21,-75.27C121.92,-71.06 113.21,-66.45 105.26,-61.89 94.19,-55.53 82.38,-48.07 71.93,-41.22\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"73.37,-39.66 67.21,-38.1 71.06,-43.16 73.37,-39.66\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"133.39\" y=\"-52.39\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> no: residual \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node6\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>nf\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#f3f4f6\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M218.28,-37.64C218.28,-37.64 114.75,-37.64 114.75,-37.64 108.75,-37.64 102.75,-31.64 102.75,-25.64 102.75,-25.64 102.75,-12 102.75,-12 102.75,-6 108.75,0 114.75,0 114.75,0 218.28,0 218.28,0 224.28,0 230.28,-6 230.28,-12 230.28,-12 230.28,-25.64 230.28,-25.64 230.28,-31.64 224.28,-37.64 218.28,-37.64\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"111.39\" y=\"-23.87\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Non&#45;financial liability\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"136.14\" y=\"-14.77\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">provisions, tax,\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"131.26\" y=\"-5.77\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">contract liabilities\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge4\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>why&#45;&gt;nf\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M166.51,-75.44C166.51,-66.45 166.51,-55.28 166.51,-45.32\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"168.62,-45.5 166.52,-39.5 164.42,-45.5 168.62,-45.5\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"177.39\" y=\"-52.39\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> yes \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node7\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>s9\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#dcfce7\" stroke=\"#166534\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M376.4,-36.82C376.4,-36.82 264.62,-36.82 264.62,-36.82 258.62,-36.82 252.62,-30.82 252.62,-24.82 252.62,-24.82 252.62,-12.82 252.62,-12.82 252.62,-6.82 258.62,-0.82 264.62,-0.82 264.62,-0.82 376.4,-0.82 376.4,-0.82 382.4,-0.82 388.4,-6.82 388.4,-12.82 388.4,-12.82 388.4,-24.82 388.4,-24.82 388.4,-30.82 382.4,-36.82 376.4,-36.82\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"261.26\" y=\"-19.37\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">SFRS(I) 9\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"310.76\" y=\"-19.37\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\"> measurement\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"275.89\" y=\"-10.27\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">the rest of this chapter\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge6\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>fl&#45;&gt;s9\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M314.53,-74.32C315.52,-65.33 316.72,-54.39 317.79,-44.67\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"319.87,-44.9 318.44,-38.71 315.7,-44.44 319.87,-44.9\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"type":"mcq","bucket":"classify","lo":35,"q":"A company issues preference shares with a fixed 6% dividend. It must redeem them for cash at par in five years. How are they classified by the issuer?","options":[{"t":"Equity, because they are shares","why":"The label does not decide it. A mandatory cash redemption is an obligation the company cannot avoid."},{"t":"A financial liability","ok":true,"why":"The company has a contractual obligation to deliver cash (the redemption, and here the fixed dividends too). That is a {l|financial liability}."},{"t":"A provision under SFRS(I) 1-37","why":"The obligation comes from a contract to pay cash, and the amount and timing are fixed. It is a financial instrument."},{"t":"Equity until the redemption date, then a liability","why":"Classification is made when the shares are issued, based on the obligation that exists from day one."}],"id":"mcq-qbizi2","sect":1,"part":"Classify"},{"type":"think","bucket":"classify","lo":35,"scenario":"Remember the financial assets chapter: two tests (SPPI and the business model) sorted every asset into amortised cost, FVOCI or FVTPL. Now the company is the borrower: it has issued a plain 5-year bond and will pay the coupons and the face value as they fall due.","prompt":"Does it make sense to remeasure that bond to fair value every year? Would the company ever “sell” its own debt?","answer":["Mostly no. The company will just pay the contractual cash. Market price swings in its own bond are money it will never pay or save. So the useful number is **amortised cost**: what it borrowed, plus {x|interest}, less what it has paid.","That is why there is **no business model test** for liabilities. **Amortised cost is the default.** Fair value through P&L is the exception, for liabilities that really are traded (like derivatives) or that the company chooses to designate on day one."],"id":"think-1p9lpl","sect":1,"part":"Classify"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"classify","lo":35,"title":"Two categories: amortised cost (default) or FVTPL","body":["Once we know it is a {l|financial liability}, the next question is how to measure it. The think page showed why fair value rarely makes sense for debt you will simply repay, so the menu here is much shorter than for financial assets.","1. **Amortised cost:** the **default** for almost every {l|financial liability}: {l|loans}, {l|bonds}, {l|payables}.","2. **FVTPL**, only if:","- **held for trading** (e.g. {l|a derivative with a negative fair value}), or","- **designated** at FVTPL at initial recognition. The designation is irrevocable (typically to remove an accounting mismatch with related assets, or because the group is managed on a fair value basis).","+ There is **no FVOCI category** for liabilities and **no SPPI or business model test**.","! Designation happens on day one or never. A company cannot move its {l|loan} to FVTPL in year 2 because rates moved."],"id":"rule-6lsnup","sect":1,"part":"Classify"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"classify","lo":35,"title":"How a financial liability is measured","intro":"This is the chart from your notes. Take the walkthrough once; the rest of the chapter fills in each box.","notes":{"fl":"Recognised when the entity **becomes a party to the contract**: the {l|bond} is issued, the {l|loan} is drawn.","q":"The only classification question. **Held for trading** (e.g. a derivative) or **designated** at FVTPL on day one? There is no business model test for liabilities.","ac":"**Amortised cost**, the default. Start at fair value **minus** transaction costs. {x|Interest expense} = {l|opening carrying amount} × effective rate. Any {l|premium} or {l|discount} unwinds to face value by maturity.","fv":"**FVTPL.** Start at fair value; {x|transaction costs} **expensed**. Fair value changes to P&L, except that for **designated** liabilities the part caused by the entity’s own credit risk goes to OCI."},"walk":[{"nodes":["fl"],"text":"A {l|financial liability} is recognised when the entity becomes a party to the contract."},{"nodes":["fl","q"],"text":"Ask the one classification question: held for trading, or designated at FVTPL at the start?"},{"nodes":["q","ac"],"text":"**No** (the usual answer) → **amortised cost**. Costs deducted on day one; effective interest after that."},{"nodes":["q","fv"],"text":"**Yes** → **FVTPL**. Costs expensed; fair value changes to P&L, own credit to OCI if designated."}],"caption":"Default: amortised cost. Exception: FVTPL (trading or designated).","id":"diagram-12k3m5","sect":1,"part":"Classify","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:563px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 512.00 209.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(14.4 194.73)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-14.4,14.4 -14.4,-194.73 497.12,-194.73 497.12,14.4 -14.4,14.4\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>fl\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M341.6,-180.33C341.6,-180.33 144.5,-180.33 144.5,-180.33 138.5,-180.33 132.5,-174.33 132.5,-168.33 132.5,-168.33 132.5,-156.33 132.5,-156.33 13