ncial assets\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"41.64\" y=\"-309.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">SFRS(I) 9\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge7\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>fa&#45;&gt;own\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,2\" d=\"M112.59,-318C125.29,-318 138.95,-318 151.72,-318\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"151.61,-320.1 157.61,-318 151.61,-315.9 151.61,-320.1\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node9\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>ipfv\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#f3eeff\" stroke=\"#6d28d9\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M111.03,-286C111.03,-286 12,-286 12,-286 6,-286 0,-280 0,-274 0,-274 0,-262 0,-262 0,-256 6,-250 12,-250 12,-250 111.03,-250 111.03,-250 117.03,-250 123.03,-256 123.03,-262 123.03,-262 123.03,-274 123.03,-274 123.03,-280 117.03,-286 111.03,-286\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"8.64\" y=\"-268.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Investment property\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"28.89\" y=\"-259.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">fair value model\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge8\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>ipfv&#45;&gt;own\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,2\" d=\"M114.58,-286.48C126.77,-290.8 139.75,-295.41 151.92,-299.72\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"151.19,-301.69 157.54,-301.72 152.59,-297.74 151.19,-301.69\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"type":"mcq","bucket":"classify","lo":37,"q":"Which of these assets is tested for impairment under SFRS(I) 1-36?","options":[{"t":"Finished goods held in a warehouse","why":"{a|Inventory} is written down to net realisable value under SFRS(I) 1-2."},{"t":"An investment in listed shares measured at fair value through profit or loss","why":"A {a|financial asset} under SFRS(I) 9, already at fair value."},{"t":"An office building held to earn rent, measured under the cost model","ok":true,"why":"{a|Investment property} under the cost model is in scope: nothing else catches a fall in its value."},{"t":"A rented-out warehouse measured under the fair value model","why":"Fair-value investment property is remeasured every year end, with falls in P&L. SFRS(I) 1-36 doesn’t apply."}],"id":"mcq-1hbl77","sect":1,"part":"Classify"},{"id":"think-15tdk7","type":"think","bucket":"classify","lo":37,"scenario":"Kopi Corner Pte Ltd runs 30 cafés. One café’s {a|espresso machine} is getting old. The CFO wants to test it for impairment and asks for “the cash flows the espresso machine generates”.","prompt":"Can anyone actually produce those cash flows? If not, what would you test instead?","answer":["No. Customers pay for coffee, cakes and a seat, not for the machine. Its cash flows can’t be separated from the oven, the fit-out and the barista.","So test the **smallest group of assets that does produce its own cash inflows**: here, the **café**. That group is a **cash-generating unit (CGU)**.","Not the whole chain of 30, though: each café takes its own customers’ money, largely independently of the others."],"sect":1,"part":"Classify"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"classify","lo":37,"title":"Test the asset alone, or as a cash-generating unit","body":["We know *which* assets are tested. Now *at what level*: the test needs cash flows, and many assets don’t earn cash on their own, like the café’s espresso machine.","Estimate recoverable amount for the **individual asset** where possible.","If the asset doesn’t generate cash inflows largely independent of other assets, test its **cash-generating unit (CGU)**:","> CGU = the **smallest** identifiable group of assets that generates cash inflows **largely independent** of the cash inflows from other assets or groups","- **{a|Goodwill}** never generates cash on its own, so it is always tested as part of a CGU (or group of CGUs).","- Typical CGUs: a shop, a café, a factory line, a bus route network, a hotel.","! Your notes say the detail of CGUs goes beyond LO 37. Know the definition and the allocation order (later in this chapter); don’t lose sleep over the edge cases."],"id":"rule-134vih","sect":1,"part":"Classify"},{"id":"tree-owsszm","type":"tree","bucket":"classify","lo":37,"title":"Is it in scope, and at what level is it tested?","scenario":"Kopi Corner Pte Ltd runs 30 cafés, each taking its own customers’ money. Take the {a|espresso machine} in one café. It is {a|PPE} under the cost model, and its cash flows cannot be separated from the rest of the café. Tap your way to the answer.","expect":"cgu","start":"s1","nodes":{"s1":{"q":"What kind of asset is it?","why":"Assets with their own write-down rule stay out of SFRS(I) 1-36.","opts":[{"t":"Inventory","to":"inv"},{"t":"A financial asset","to":"fa"},{"t":"Investment property at fair value","to":"ipfv"},{"t":"Goodwill","to":"gw"},{"t":"PPE, intangible, ROU asset or IP at cost","to":"s2"}]},"s2":{"q":"Does it generate cash inflows largely independent of other assets?","why":"Recoverable amount needs cash flows. If the asset has none of its own, look at its group.","opts":[{"t":"Yes, on its own","to":"alone"},{"t":"No, only together with other assets","to":"cgu"}]},"inv":{"result":"Out of scope: SFRS(I) 1-2","body":["{a|Inventory} is held at the lower of cost and net realisable value. The NRV write-down does the job."]},"fa":{"result":"Out of scope: SFRS(I) 9","body":["{a|Financial assets} use expected credit losses or fair value."]},"ipfv":{"result":"Out of scope: SFRS(I) 1-40","body":["Already at fair value, with every change in P&L."]},"gw":{"result":"In scope, always tested within a CGU, every year","body":["{a|Goodwill} has no cash flows of its own. It is allocated to the CGUs that benefit from the business combination and tested with them, **annually**."]},"alone":{"result":"In scope: test the individual asset","body":["Estimate the asset’s own recoverable amount and compare it with its {a|carrying amount}. Example: a rented-out building under the cost model, with its own rent."]},"cgu":{"result":"In scope: test its cash-generating unit","body":["The {a|espresso machine} has no cash flows of its own, so test the **café**: the smallest group that earns cash largely independently.","- Any loss on the café is then allocated to its assets, the machine included."]}},"sect":1,"part":"Classify","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:640px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 842.00 246.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 235.69)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-235.69 831.33,-235.69 831.33,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>s1\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#b45309\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M483.78,-224.89C483.78,-224.89 377.25,-224.89 377.25,-224.89 371.25,-224.89 365.25,-218.89 365.25,-212.89 365.25,-212.89 365.25,-200.89 365.25,-200.89 365.25,-194.89 371.25,-188.89 377.25,-188.89 377.25,-188.89 483.78,-188.89 483.78,-188.89 489.78,-188.89 495.78,-194.89 495.78,-200.89 495.78,-200.89 495.78,-212.89 495.78,-212.89 495.78,-218.89 489.78,-224.89 483.78,-224.89\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"430.51\" y=\"-202.44\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">What kind of asset is it?\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node2\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>s2\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#b45309\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M173.03,-129.14C173.03,-129.14 50,-129.14 50,-129.14 44,-129.14 38,-123.14 38,-117.14 38,-117.14 38,-96.5 