y=\"-50.75\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\">with other assets \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"type":"compare","bucket":"classify","preamble":"Impairment isn’t a cousin of these assets but a check run on top of them. Inventory and financial assets are out of scope because they have their own write-down tests (NRV and expected credit losses).","lo":37,"special":"Impairment isn’t an asset class: it is a **test applied to other assets** ({a|PPE}, {a|intangibles}, {a|goodwill}, {a|IP at cost}, {a|ROU}), alone or grouped in a **cash-generating unit**.","id":"compare-1kumyt","sect":1,"part":"Classify"},{"type":"map","id":"map-2-recognise","bucket":"recognise","sect":2,"part":"Recognise"},{"id":"think-fzy7tz","type":"think","bucket":"recognise","lo":37,"scenario":"A listed group owns 4,000 assets: buses, depots, software, two brands with indefinite lives, a half-built app, and {a|goodwill} from three acquisitions.","prompt":"Should it calculate the recoverable amount of all 4,000 assets at every year end? If not, which ones would you insist on testing every year, and why those?","answer":["No: that would be a huge job with little payoff. Instead it **looks for signs of trouble** at each reporting date and tests only where there is an **indication** of impairment.","But three kinds of asset are tested **every year, indication or not**: **{a|goodwill}**, **{a|intangibles} with an indefinite useful life** (the two brands), and **{a|intangibles} not yet available for use** (the half-built app).","Why those? None of them is amortised, so nothing else chips away at their {a|carrying amount}, and their value is hard to observe. An annual test is the safety net."],"sect":2,"part":"Recognise"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"recognise","lo":37,"title":"When to test","body":["Scope and level are settled. Next: *when* do you actually run the test? Testing every asset every year would bury the accountants, so the rule asks for a trigger, with three exceptions.","An asset is **impaired** when its **{a|carrying amount} exceeds its recoverable amount**.","1. At **each reporting date**, assess whether there is **any indication** that an asset may be impaired.","2. Only if there is, estimate its **recoverable amount**.","3. **Test every year, even with no indication:**","- **G**oodwill acquired in a business combination","- **I**ntangible assets with an **indefinite** useful life","- intangible assets **N**ot yet available for use","+ Memory hook: **G-I-N**. Everything else is tested only when there is an indication.","! Don’t test every asset every year. Only G-I-N gets the annual test."],"id":"rule-1dcsdk","sect":2,"part":"Recognise"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"recognise","lo":37,"title":"The impairment test, step by step","intro":"The chart from your notes. It is the whole chapter on one page: we are at the top box now, and the next two sections fill in the rest.","notes":{"q1":"Look for indications at **every reporting date**. G-I-N assets skip the question: they are tested every year anyway.","stop1":"No indication (and not G-I-N): no test, no calculation. The asset stays as it is.","ra":"Recoverable amount = the **higher** of what you could sell it for (net of costs) and what using it is worth.","q2":"The real test: is the asset carried above its recoverable amount?","stop2":"An indication alone is not a loss. If recoverable amount is at or above {a|carrying amount}, nothing is written down.","loss":"Write down the excess. Cost model → P&L. Revalued → {e|surplus} first, then P&L. Then depreciate the {a|new, lower carrying amount}."},"walk":[{"nodes":["q1"],"text":"Step 1, every reporting date: is there any **indication** of impairment? (G-I-N assets: test anyway.)"},{"nodes":["stop1"],"text":"No indication → stop. Most assets, most years, end here."},{"nodes":["ra"],"text":"Step 2: estimate **recoverable amount**, the higher of fair value less costs of disposal and value in use."},{"nodes":["q2","stop2"],"text":"Step 3: compare with {a|carrying amount}. Not above? No impairment."},{"nodes":["loss"],"text":"Step 4: {a|carrying amount} above recoverable amount → **{x|impairment loss}**, and {x|depreciation} restarts from the {a|new amount}."}],"caption":"Indication → recoverable amount → compare → write down.","id":"diagram-1qpotz","sect":2,"part":"Recognise","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:495px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 450.00 220.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 209.58)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-209.58 439.45,-209.58 439.45,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>q1\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#b45309\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M166.53,-198.78C166.53,-198.78 27,-198.78 27,-198.78 21,-198.78 15,-192.78 15,-186.78 15,-186.78 15,-153.14 15,-153.14 15,-147.14 21,-141.14 27,-141.14 27,-141.14 166.53,-141.14 166.53,-141.14 172.53,-141.14 178.53,-147.14 178.53,-153.14 178.53,-153.14 178.53,-186.78 178.53,-186.78 178.53,-192.78 172.53,-198.78 166.53,-198.78\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"36.39\" y=\"-185.01\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">At each reporting date:\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"23.64\" y=\"-174.01\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">any \u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"43.89\" y=\"-174.01\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">indication\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"95.64\" y=\"-174.01\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\"