-111.89 241.88,-111.89 235.88,-111.89 229.88,-105.89 229.88,-99.89 229.88,-99.89 229.88,-77.25 229.88,-77.25 229.88,-71.25 235.88,-65.25 241.88,-65.25 241.88,-65.25 401.65,-65.25 401.65,-65.25 407.65,-65.25 413.65,-71.25 413.65,-77.25 413.65,-77.25 413.65,-99.89 413.65,-99.89 413.65,-105.89 407.65,-111.89 401.65,-111.89\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"249.01\" y=\"-98.12\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Loss\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"274.51\" y=\"-98.12\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\"> = carrying − recoverable\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"284.26\" y=\"-89.02\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">cost model → P&amp;L\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"252.76\" y=\"-80.02\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">revalued → surplus first, then P&amp;L\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"238.51\" y=\"-71.02\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">then depreciate the new carrying amount\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge4\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>q2&#45;&gt;loss\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M238.39,-36.53C250.55,-43.97 264.98,-52.8 278.39,-61.02\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"276.97,-62.6 283.18,-63.95 279.16,-59.02 276.97,-62.6\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"280\" y=\"-46.75\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> yes \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"type":"mcq","bucket":"recognise","lo":37,"q":"Which asset must be tested for impairment every year, even if there is no indication of impairment?","options":[{"t":"A factory building that is 30 years old","why":"Age alone isn’t a reason. {a|PPE} is tested only when there is an indication."},{"t":"Software under development that is not yet available for use","ok":true,"why":"{a|Intangible assets} not yet available for use are tested annually (the N in G-I-N)."},{"t":"A customer list with a finite useful life of 5 years","why":"A finite-life intangible is amortised and tested only when there is an indication."},{"t":"All PPE carried under the revaluation model","why":"Revalued {a|PPE} is tested only when there is an indication."}],"id":"mcq-bscyj7","sect":2,"part":"Recognise"},{"type":"think","bucket":"recognise","lo":38,"scenario":"Kranji Moulding Pte Ltd makes plastic parts on a specialised line. This year: (1) a rival launched a 3D-printing process that halves its customers’ costs; (2) the central bank pushed market interest rates up sharply; (3) Kranji’s market capitalisation fell below its net assets; (4) the line is a year older, and its resale price fell about as much as expected for one more year of use.","prompt":"Which of these are signs that the line might be impaired, and which are just life going on as normal?","answer":["1. **Yes:** a significant adverse change in **technology and the market**.","2. **Yes:** higher market interest rates raise the discount rate, which **lowers value in use**.","3. **Yes:** if the market values the whole company at less than its net assets, the assets may be overstated.","4. **No:** a fall in value that is **expected** from age and normal use is what {x|depreciation} is for. Only a fall **significantly more** than expected counts."],"id":"think-yapdo7","sect":2,"part":"Recognise"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"recognise","lo":38,"title":"Indicators of impairment","body":["“Test when there is an indication” only works if you know what an indication looks like. This is the checklist the previous page’s four Kranji events were sorted against.","**External** (outside the entity):","1. the asset’s **market value** has fallen significantly **more than expected** from age or normal use","2. significant **adverse changes** in technology, the market, the economy or the law","3. **market interest rates** have risen, raising the discount rate and lowering value in use","4. the entity’s **net assets exceed its market capitalisation**","**Internal** (inside the entity):","1. evidence of **obsolescence or physical damage**","2. significant adverse **changes in use**: the asset is idle, its operation is being discontinued or restructured, or it is to be sold early","3. internal reports show the asset’s **performance is, or will be, worse than expected**","- The list is a **minimum**: other evidence counts too.","- Even if no impairment results, an indicator may mean the **useful life, depreciation method or residual value** needs reviewing.","! An indicator triggers a **test**, not a write-down. The loss exists only if recoverable amount turns out to be **below** {a|carrying amount}."],"id":"rule-1fauoy","sect":2,"part":"Recognise"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"recognise","lo":38,"title":"Seven signs of trouble","intro":"Four signals from outside, three from inside. Any one of them sends the asset to the test, and may also prompt a review of its life.","notes":{"mv":"Only a fall **beyond** what age and normal use explain. An expected fall is just {x|depreciation}.","adv":"New technology, a lost market, a recession, a new law banning the product.","rate":"A higher discount rate means a lower present value, so value in use drops.","mcap":"The market says the whole company is worth less than its book net assets: something may be overstated.","dmg":"A flood-damaged warehouse, a machine made obsolete by a new model.","use":"Idle plant, a plan to discontinue or restructure, or a decision to dispose of the asset before the end of its expected life.","perf":"Management reports show cash flows or profits below budget, now or in the forecast.","ind":"Any one indicator is enough to require a test.","test":"The indicator says “check”, not “write down”. The numbers decide.","rev":"Even if there is no impairment, the useful life, depreciation method or residual value may need updating."},"walk":[{"nodes":["mv","adv","rate","mcap"],"text":"**External** signs: the market, technology, interest rates, and the company’s own share price."},{"nodes":["dmg","use","perf"],"text":"**Internal** signs: damage or obsolescence, a change in how the asset is used, poor performance."},{"nodes":["ind","test"],"text":"Any one of them → estimate the **recoverable amount**."},{"nodes":["rev"],"text":"Side effect: review the useful life, depreciation method and residual value, even if no loss arises."}],"caption":"An indicator opens the test; it doesn’t decide the result.","id":"diagram-1qusl9","sect":2,"part":"Recognise","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:542px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 493.00 425.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 413.8)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-413.8 482.39,-413.8 482.39,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\u003cg id=\"clust1\" class=\"cluster\">\n\u003ctitle>cluster_ext\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"white\" stroke=\"#b45309\" d=\"M20,-182C20,-182 160.53,-182 160.53,-182 166.53,-182 172.53,-188 172.53,-194 172.53,-194 172.53,-383 172.53,-383 172.53,-389 166.53,-395 160.53,-395 160.53,-395 20,-395 20,-395 14,-395 8,-389 8,-383 8,-383 8,-194 8,-194 8,-188 14,-182 20,-182\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"68.51\" y=\"-381.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\">External\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003cg id=\"clust2\" class=\"cluster\">\n\u003ctitle>cluster_int\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"white\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" d=\"M31.62