s costs of disposal) and (value in use)","> {x|Impairment loss} = {a|carrying amount} − recoverable amount (only if positive)","1. **Fair value less costs of disposal (FVLCOD):** the price in an orderly sale between market participants, **minus the costs of selling** (legal costs, removal costs). Not finance costs or income tax.","2. **Value in use (VIU):** the **present value** of the future cash flows from **using** the asset and from its **final disposal**.","- **Shortcut:** if **either** measure is above the {a|carrying amount}, there is **no impairment** and the other need not be calculated.","! Recoverable amount is the **higher** of the two, not the lower. Sell or use: the business picks the better one."],"id":"rule-l9d1g1","sect":3,"part":"Initial measurement"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"initial","lo":39,"title":"The notes’ machine: building the recoverable amount","intro":"Two routes to a value, one winner, one comparison.","notes":{"fv":"The price in an orderly sale between market participants.","cod":"Selling costs only: legal costs, removal costs. Not finance costs, not income tax.","fvlcod":"340,000 − 10,000 = 330,000.","viu":"Present value of the cash flows from using the machine and from its final disposal.","ra":"Higher of 330,000 and 350,000 = **350,000**.","ca":"What the machine is carried at today, after {x|depreciation}.","loss":"400,000 − 350,000 = 50,000. Positive, so the machine is impaired."},"walk":[{"nodes":["fv","cod","fvlcod"],"text":"The **sell** route: fair value less costs of disposal = 330,000."},{"nodes":["viu"],"text":"The **use** route: value in use = 350,000."},{"nodes":["ra"],"text":"Take the **higher**: recoverable amount = 350,000."},{"nodes":["ca","loss"],"text":"Compare with {a|carrying amount} 400,000: {x|loss} = **50,000**. Taking the lower by mistake would give 70,000."}],"caption":"Sell value vs use value: the higher wins, then compare with {a|carrying amount}.","id":"diagram-u2snjl","sect":3,"part":"Initial measurement"