itle>ca\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M325.03,-109.25C325.03,-109.25 243.25,-109.25 243.25,-109.25 237.25,-109.25 231.25,-103.25 231.25,-97.25 231.25,-97.25 231.25,-85.25 231.25,-85.25 231.25,-79.25 237.25,-73.25 243.25,-73.25 243.25,-73.25 325.03,-73.25 325.03,-73.25 331.03,-73.25 337.03,-79.25 337.03,-85.25 337.03,-85.25 337.03,-97.25 337.03,-97.25 337.03,-103.25 331.03,-109.25 325.03,-109.25\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"239.89\" y=\"-92.8\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"white\">Carrying amount\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"264.64\" y=\"-81.8\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"white\">400,000\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge6\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>ca&#45;&gt;loss\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M266.95,-73C257.59,-63.6 245.88,-51.85 235.78,-41.72\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"237.45,-40.42 231.73,-37.66 234.48,-43.39 237.45,-40.42\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"269.02\" y=\"-50.75\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> minus \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"type":"visual","bucket":"initial","lo":39,"title":"The notes’ machine as bars","html":"\u003cp>The same machine, drawn to scale from zero. Each bar is one number from the test. The top bar has two layers: the part of the \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">carrying amount\u003c/span> the machine can still recover (solid) and the \u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">impairment loss\u003c/span> that can’t be recovered (hatched). The sell bar loses its costs of disposal; the use bar is whole. The longer of the two sets the recoverable amount, and the gap to the top bar is the \u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">loss\u003c/span>.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"cbars\">\u003cdiv class=\"cb-year\">\u003cdiv class=\"cb-cap\">\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">Carrying amount\u003c/span> 400,000 = recoverable 350,000 + \u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">loss 50,000\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-track\">\u003ci class=\"seg a\" style=\"width:87.50%\">\u003c/i>\u003ci class=\"seg out-x\" style=\"width:12.50%\">\u003c/i>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-year\">\u003cdiv class=\"cb-cap\">Sell: fair value 340,000 − costs 10,000 = FVLCOD 330,000\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-track\">\u003ci class=\"seg n\" style=\"width:82.50%\">\u003c/i>\u003ci class=\"seg out-n\" style=\"width:2.50%\">\u003c/i>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-year\">\u003cdiv class=\"cb-cap\">Use: value in use \u003cstrong>350,000\u003c/strong> (the higher, so it wins)\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-track\">\u003ci class=\"seg a\" style=\"width:87.50%\">\u003c/i>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\n    \u003cdiv class=\"cb-key\">\u003cspan>\u003ci class=\"seg a\">\u003c/i>recoverable\u003c/span>\u003cspan>\u003ci class=\"seg out-x\">\u003c/i>\u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">impairment loss\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan>\u003ci class=\"seg n\">\u003c/i>FVLCOD\u003c/span>\u003cspan>\u003ci class=\"seg out-n\">\u003c/i>costs of disposal (leave)\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>","id":"visual-7ldi28","sect":3,"part":"Initial measurement"},{"id":"think-15iroc","type":"think","bucket":"initial","lo":39,"scenario":"Bedok Bakery is working out the value in use of an oven line. The forecast shows: net operating inflows $90,000 a year for 4 years; routine maintenance (already netted off); $20,000 from selling the line at the end; a cost saving from a restructuring the board is “considering”; a planned upgrade that would add capacity; {x|interest} on the {l|loan} that financed the line; and {x|income tax} on the profits.","prompt":"Value in use is meant to capture the asset **as it is today**, before financing and tax. Which of these lines belong in it?","answer":["**In:** the operating inflows, the maintenance needed to keep the line running, and the **final disposal** proceeds.","**Out:** the restructuring saving (not yet committed), and the **upgrade** (it would improve the asset beyond its current condition).","**Out:** {l|loan} **{x|interest}** (financing) and **{x|income tax}**. VIU looks at the asset, not how it was paid for or taxed."],"sect":3,"part":"Initial measurement"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"initial","lo":39,"title":"What goes into value in use","body":["Value in use is the harder of the two measures, because you build it from a forecast. The Bedok oven line showed the problem: forecasts contain things that don’t belong.","> VIU = present value of (cash inflows from continuing use − cash outflows needed to generate them + net cash from final disposal)","**Include:**","- cash inflows from using the asset","- cash outflows needed to keep it generating them (day-to-day servicing, maintenance)","- net cash from its **disposal** at the end of its life","**Exclude:**","1. future **restructurings** the entity is not yet committed to","2. spending that would **improve or enhance** the asset beyond its current condition","3. **financing** cash flows ({x|interest}, {l|loan} repayments)","4. **{x|income tax}** receipts and payments","+ Use the asset in its **current condition**: no wishful upgrades, no reorganisations that only exist in a slide deck."],"id":"rule-1m35k8","sect":3,"part":"Initial measurement"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"initial","lo":39,"title":"Value in use: in and out","intro":"What makes it into the present-value calculation, and what is left on the cutting-room floor.","notes":{"ops":"The cash the asset brings in by being used, as it is today.","maint":"Outflows needed to keep generating those inflows: these are deducted.","disp":"Whatever the asset fetches at the end of its life, net of disposal costs.","viu":"Discount all the included cash flows to present value.","restr":"Only once the entity is **committed** can its effects come in. A board “considering” it is not enough.","upg":"Would improve the asset beyond its **current condition**. Leave it out.","fin":"How the asset was paid for doesn’t change what it is worth to use.","tax":"VIU is measured before {x|tax}."},"walk":[{"nodes":["ops","maint","disp","viu"],"text":"**In:** cash from using it, the maintenance to keep it running, and the final disposal."},{"nodes":["restr","upg"],"text":"**Out:** anything that changes the asset from its current condition: uncommitted restructurings, upgrades."},{"nodes":["fin","tax"],"text":"**Out:** financing and income tax cash flows."}],"caption":"The asset as it stands today, before financing and tax.","id":"diagram-h19wq9","sect":3,"part":"Initial measurement","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:347px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 315.00 358.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 346.8)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-346.8 304.11,-346.8 304.11,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>ops\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e6f4f1\" stroke=\"#0f766e\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M102.78,-336C102.78,-336 17.25,-336 17.25,-336 11.25,-336 5.25,-330 5.25,-324 5.25,-324 5.25,-312 5.25,-312 5.25,-306 11.25,-300 17.25,-300 17.25,-300 102.78,-300 102.78,-300 108.78,-300 114.78,-306 114.78,-312 114.78,-312 114.78,-324 114.78,-324 114.78,-330 108.78,-336 102.78,-336\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"13.89\" y=\"-318.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Operating inflows\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"19.14\" y=\"-309.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#1