0.28,-36 274.28,-36\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"226.64\" y=\"-19.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Combine it with other\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"226.64\" y=\"-7.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">promises\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge2\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>n1&#45;&gt;comb\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M229.21,-256.17C232.21,-252.19 234.81,-247.9 236.64,-243.39 269.04,-163.3 250.48,-134.28 236.64,-49 236.35,-47.2 235.96,-45.36 235.51,-43.52\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"237.6,-43.18 233.94,-37.99 233.56,-44.33 237.6,-43.18\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"264\" y=\"-147.94\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> No \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node3\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>sep\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e6f4f1\" stroke=\"#0f766e\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M113.28,-36C113.28,-36 12,-36 12,-36 6,-36 0,-30 0,-24 0,-24 0,-12 0,-12 0,-6 6,0 12,0 12,0 113.28,0 113.28,0 119.28,0 125.28,-6 125.28,-12 125.28,-12 125.28,-24 125.28,-24 125.28,-30 119.28,-36 113.28,-36\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"62.64\" y=\"-19.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Separate performance\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"62.64\" y=\"-7.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">obligation\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge3\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>n2&#45;&gt;sep\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M76.1,-129.06C71.5,-125.49 67.4,-121.34 64.14,-116.5 49.74,-95.16 51.92,-64.77 56.06,-43.61\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"58.05,-44.33 57.26,-38.02 53.95,-43.44 58.05,-44.33\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"102.39\" y=\"-101.38\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> Yes: no\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"102.39\" y=\"-90.12\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\">significant\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"102.39\" y=\"-78.88\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\">integration, no\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"102.39\" y=\"-67.62\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\">modification, not\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"102.39\" y=\"-56.38\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\">highly dependent \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge4\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>n2&#45;&gt;comb\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M144.08,-129.08C143.63,-106.77 146.26,-72.14 163.89,-49 166.22,-45.94 168.95,-43.17 171.93,-40.68\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"172.79,-42.66 176.34,-37.39 170.27,-39.3 172.79,-42.66\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"200.26\" y=\"-107\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> No: it\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"200.26\" y=\"-95.75\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\">significantly\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"200.26\" y=\"-84.5\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\">customises the\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"200.26\" y=\"-73.25\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\">software or is an\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"200.26\" y=\"-62\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\">input into one\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"200.26\" y=\"-50.75\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\">combined item \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"type":"think","bucket":"pos","lo":40,"scenario":"Marina Mobile gives every phone a 1-year warranty that it works as specified. It also offers an optional “Care+” plan for $120 that covers accidental damage for 2 more years, which customers can buy or skip.","prompt":"Is either warranty something extra that Marina is selling, or just a promise that the phone is not faulty?","answer":["The **1-year warranty** only assures the phone works as promised. It is an **assurance** warranty: no separate obligation, just a {l|Warranty provision} under SFRS(I) 1-37 for the expected repair cost.","**Care+** is a **service** on top: customers can buy it separately, and it covers more than defects. It is a separate **performance obligation**: part of the price goes to it and is recognised over the 2 years."],"id":"think-1i8mal","sect":2,"part":"Performance obligations"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"pos","lo":40,"title":"Warranties","body":["Warranties are a classic step-2 puzzle: is the warranty something extra being sold, or just a promise that the product works? The answer decides whether it takes a slice of {i|revenue}.","- **Assurance warranty** (the product works as promised): not a performance obligation. Recognise a {l|Warranty provision} and {x|Warranty expense} under SFRS(I) 1-37.","- **Service warranty** (extra cover, often sold separately): a **separate performance obligation**. Allocate part of the price to it and recognise it as {i|revenue} over the cover period.","! The test is what the warranty gives the customer, not what it is called. “Extended” and sold separately → service."],"id":"rule-4bw46x","sect":2,"part":"Performance obligations"},{"id":"think-v1ttcr","type":"think","bucket":"pos","lo":40,"scenario":"TripLah runs a travel website. A customer pays TripLah $1,000 for a hotel night; TripLah passes $850 to the hotel. TripLah never books rooms in advance, isn’t responsible if the hotel is overbooked, and the hotel sets the price.","prompt":"Is TripLah’s {i|revenue} $1,000 or $150?","answer":["$150. TripLah never **controls** the hotel room before the customer gets it: no inventory risk, no pricing power, and the hotel fulfils the stay.","So TripLah is an **agent**: it arranges for another party to provide the service, and its {i|revenue} is the **net** commission, 1,000 − 850 = 150.","If TripLah bought rooms in bulk at its own risk and set the price, it would be the **principal** and report {i|$1,000} gross with an {x|$850 cost}. Same booking, very different top line."],"sect":2,"part":"Performance obligations"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"pos","lo":40,"title":"Principal or agent?","body":["TripLah showed that one booking can give two very different top lines. This rule decides whether the entity promised to provide the good itself, or only to arrange it.","Ask: does the entity **control** the good or service **before** it is transferred to the customer?","- **Yes → principal:** {i|revenue} **gross** (the full amount the customer pays); the payment to the supplier is a {x|cost}.","- **No → agent:** {i|revenue} **net** (its fee or commission only).","Signs that it is the principal:","1. it is **primarily responsible** for fulfilling the promise","2. it bears **inventory risk** before or after transfer","3. it has **discretion in setting the price**"],"id":"rule-1pe975","sect":2,"part":"Performance obligations"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"pos","lo":40,"title":"Same booking, two answers","intro":"TripLah’s $1,000 booking, drawn both ways. The cash flows are identical; only the {i|revenue} line changes.","notes":{"cust":"The customer’s {a|cash} is the same in both stories.","q":"The deciding question: control before transfer. Clues: primary responsibility, inventory risk, pricing discretion.","prin":"Bought the rooms at its own risk, sets the price, answers to the customer if things go wrong.","agent":"Just arranges the booking; the hotel provides the stay and sets the price.","pRev":"Gross: the full price is {i|Revenue}; the hotel’s share is {x|Cost of sales}.","aRev":"Net: only the commission is {i|Revenue}.","profit":"1,000 − 850 = 150 in both cases. Only the top line moves."},"walk":[{"nodes":["cust","q"],"text":"Start with one question: did TripLah control the room before the customer got it?"},{"nodes":["prin","pRev"],"text":"**Principal:** {i|revenue} 1,000 gross, {x|cost} 850."},{"nodes":["agent","aRev"],"text":"**Agent:** {i|revenue} 150 net."},{"nodes":["profit"],"text":"Profit is the same; {i|revenue} is not. Exam questions ask for **revenue**, so this matters."}],"caption":"Gross vs net changes {i|revenue}, never profit.","id":"diagram-9czn8s","sect":2,"part":"Performance obligations","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:283px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 257.00 345.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 334.33)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-334.33 246.35,-334.33 246.35,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>cust\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M158.66,-323.53C158.66,-323.53 85.88,-323.53 85.88,-323.53 79.88,-323.53 73.88,-317.53 73.88,-311.53 73.88,-311.53 73.88,-299.53 73.88,-299.53 73.88,-293.53 79.88,-287.53 85.88,-287.53 85.88,-287.53 158.66,-287.53 158.66,-287.53 164.66,-287.53 170.66,-2