cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M183.71,-83.91C187.8,-71.65 192.92,-56.33 197.16,-43.65\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"199.15,-44.32 199.05,-37.97 195.16,-42.99 199.15,-44.32\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"234.18\" y=\"-62\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> No: it only\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"234.18\" y=\"-50.75\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\">arranges the sale \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"id":"calc-9rp4f4","type":"calc","bucket":"pos","lo":40,"q":"GreenCart, an online marketplace, lists vegetables from independent farms. The farms set their prices, pack and ship the orders and handle complaints; GreenCart never holds the stock. This month it processes $400,000 of orders and keeps 12% commission. How much revenue does GreenCart recognise?","answer":48000,"unit":"$","working":["GreenCart is an **agent**: it never controls the vegetables.","{i|Revenue} = commission = 400,000 × 12% = **$48,000**."],"sect":2,"part":"Performance obligations"},{"type":"map","id":"map-3-price","bucket":"price","sect":3,"part":"Transaction price"},{"type":"think","bucket":"price","lo":41,"scenario":"Sentosa Engineering signs a contract for $1,000,000, plus a bonus of $50,000 if it finishes on time or $100,000 if it finishes early. From experience: 30% chance late (no bonus), 50% on time, 20% early.","prompt":"The bonus isn’t certain. Should Sentosa ignore it until it is earned, or build an estimate into the price now?","answer":["Build an estimate in now. The transaction price is what Sentosa **expects to be entitled to**, and it expects some bonus.","Two ways to estimate: weight every outcome by its probability (**expected value** = 45,000), or take the single **most likely** outcome (50,000).","Pick whichever predicts the amount better, then check it against the **constraint**: don’t include more than you are fairly sure won’t reverse."],"id":"think-1ud768","sect":3,"part":"Transaction price"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"price","lo":41,"title":"Step 3: variable consideration","body":["Step 3 puts a number on the contract. Sentosa’s bonus showed the price is not always fixed, so the standard says how to estimate the uncertain part.","The **transaction price** is the amount the entity expects to be entitled to for transferring the goods or services. It excludes amounts collected for third parties (such as GST).","**Variable consideration** is any part that can change: discounts, rebates, refunds, credits, performance bonuses, penalties, price concessions.","Estimate it with whichever method better predicts the amount:","1. **Expected value:** the probability-weighted sum of the possible amounts. Best with **many similar contracts** or many possible outcomes.","2. **Most likely amount:** the single most likely outcome. Best with **only two outcomes** (bonus or no bonus).","> Expected value = Σ (amount × probability)"],"id":"rule-6x2dzo","sect":3,"part":"Transaction price"},{"id":"visual-5gea16","type":"visual","bucket":"price","lo":41,"title":"Sentosa’s bonus, worked both ways","html":"\u003cp>Here is Sentosa’s bonus with both methods side by side: 1,000,000 fixed, plus 0, 50,000 or 100,000 depending on when it finishes. Each row weights one outcome by its probability.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"tbl-wrap\">\u003ctable class=\"tbl num reveal-rows\">\u003cthead>\u003ctr>\u003cth>Outcome\u003c/th>\u003cth>Bonus\u003c/th>\u003cth>Probability\u003c/th>\u003cth>Bonus × probability\u003c/th>\u003c/tr>\u003c/thead>\u003ctbody>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>Late\u003c/td>\u003ctd>0\u003c/td>\u003ctd>30%\u003c/td>\u003ctd>0\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\u003ctr>\u003ctd>On time\u003c/td>\u003ctd>50,000\u003c/td>\u003ctd>50%\u003c/td>\u003ctd>25,000\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\u003ctr>\u003ctd>Early\u003c/td>\u003ctd>100,000\u003c/td>\u003ctd>20%\u003c/td>\u003ctd>20,000\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003cb>Expected value\u003c/b>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>100%\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cb>45,000\u003c/b>\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003cb>Most likely amount\u003c/b>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cb>50,000\u003c/b>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>50%\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n    \u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\u003c/div>\n    \u003cp class=\"cap\">Transaction price: 1,045,000 (expected value) or 1,050,000 (most likely amount). With three outcomes, expected value usually predicts better.\u003c/p>","sect":3,"part":"Transaction price"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"price","lo":41,"title":"Two ways to estimate a bonus","intro":"Same three outcomes, two methods. Expected value blends them all; most likely amount picks one.","notes":{"late":"No bonus, 30% likely. It still counts in the expected value (as zero).","ontime":"The single most likely outcome, at 50%.","early":"The big bonus, but only 20% likely.","ev":"0 × 30% + 50,000 × 50% + 100,000 × 20% = 45,000. Not an amount that can actually happen, but a good predictor across many contracts.","ml":"Just the most probable outcome: 50,000. Fits a yes/no bonus best.","cons":"Whatever the method, include it only to the extent a significant reversal is **highly probable not** to happen."},"walk":[{"nodes":["late","ontime","early"],"text":"List the possible outcomes with their probabilities."},{"nodes":["ev"],"text":"**Expected value:** weight each one and add up: 45,000."},{"nodes":["ml"],"text":"**Most likely amount:** pick the likeliest outcome: 50,000."},{"nodes":["cons"],"text":"Then run the estimate past the **constraint** before it goes into the price."}],"caption":"Choose the method that predicts better; the question often tells you which one.","id":"diagram-yn3m59","sect":3,"part":"Transaction price","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:640px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 599.00 178.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 167.62)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-167.62 588.67,-167.62 588.67,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>late\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e8eef6\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M62.28,-98.82C62.28,-98.82 28.5,-98.82 28.5,-98.82 22.5,-98.82 16.5,-92.82 16.5,-86.82 16.5,-86.82 16.5,-74.82 16.5,-74.82 16.5,-68.82 22.5,-62.82 28.5,-62.82 28.5,-62.82 62.28,-62.82 62.28,-62.82 68.28,-62.82 74.28,-68.82 74.28,-74.82 74.28,-74.82 74.28,-86.82 74.28,-86.82 74.28,-92.82 68.28,-98.82 62.28,-98.82\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"34.14\" y=\"-82.37\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Late\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"25.14\" y=\"-71.37\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">0 × 30%\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node4\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>ev\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#dcfce7\" stroke=\"#166534\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M330.81,-101.64C330.81,-101.64 223.53,-101.64 223.53,-101.64 217.53,-101.64 211.53,-95.64 211.53,-89.64 211.53,-89.64 211.53,-74 211.53,-74 211.53,-68 217.53,-62 223.53,-62 223.53,-62 330.81,-62 330.81,-62 336.81,-62 342.81,-68 342.81,-74 342.81,-74 342.81,-89.64 342.81,-89.64 342.81,-95.64 336.81,-101.64 330.81,-101.64\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"237.42\" y=\"-87.87\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Expected value\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"260.67\" y=\"-76.87\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">45,000\u003c/text>\n\u003c