=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"168.26\" y=\"-25.87\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Revenue\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"165.64\" y=\"-14.87\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">200 a year\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"159.64\" y=\"-5.77\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">over 24 months\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge5\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>cl&#45;&gt;over\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M191.14,-76.42C191.14,-67.6 191.14,-57 191.14,-47.44\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"193.24,-47.55 191.14,-41.55 189.04,-47.55 193.24,-47.55\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"235.01\" y=\"-54.39\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> as service is given \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"id":"je-yfocrd","type":"je","bucket":"allocate","lo":40,"q":"Marina Mobile sells a phone plus a 24-month airtime plan for $1,000, paid up front. Sold separately, the phone is $750 and the plan $500. Record the day-1 entry: phone handed over, $1,000 received.","accounts":["Cash","Accounts receivable","Contract asset","Contract liability","Revenue","Refund liability","Right to recover returned goods","Inventory","Cost of sales","Provision for onerous contract","Loss on onerous contract","Warranty provision","Warranty expense","Interest income","Marketing expense"],"lines":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Cash","amount":1000,"el":"a"},{"side":"Cr","account":"Revenue","amount":600,"el":"i"},{"side":"Cr","account":"Contract liability","amount":400,"el":"l"}],"why":"Phone 600 is {i|revenue} now; the plan’s 400 is a {l|contract liability} until the service is given (200 a year). {a|Cash received} before you perform is a {l|liability}, not {i|revenue}.","sect":4,"part":"Allocate the price"},{"type":"visual","bucket":"allocate","lo":40,"title":"Marina’s contract liability over the plan","html":"\u003cp>Follow the plan’s 400 slice after day 1. It enters as a \u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">contract liability\u003c/span> (cash in, airtime still owed) and leaves as \u003cspan class=\"el el-i\">revenue\u003c/span> while the airtime is used. Step through it.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"wg\" data-wg=\"roll\" data-key=\"cl-c1\" data-cfg=\"{&quot;panels&quot;:[{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Contract liability&quot;,&quot;sub&quot;:&quot;plan slice of 1,000&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;l&quot;,&quot;bal&quot;:&quot;Contract liability&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:0,&quot;startCap&quot;:&quot;Before the sale: nothing owed.&quot;,&quot;years&quot;:[{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Day 1&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;cash for the plan&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:400,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Day 1: the plan’s {a|400} of the {a|cash} is for airtime not yet given, so the {l|contract liability} is {l|400}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Year 1&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;revenue&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;i&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-200,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 1: 12 of 24 months used, so {i|revenue} 400 × 12/24 = {i|200} and the {l|liability} falls to {l|200}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Year 2&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;revenue&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;i&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-200,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 2: the last 12 months, {i|revenue} {i|200}. The {l|liability} is {l|nil}: the promise is kept.&quot;}]}]}],&quot;notes&quot;:{&quot;start&quot;:&quot;The plan’s slice of the price, not the whole bundle. Press Play or Next.&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[&quot;Each step: a movement in the {l|contract liability}.&quot;],&quot;end&quot;:&quot;**Cash first, revenue later.** The 400 arrives on day 1 but becomes {i|revenue} at 200 a year, as the airtime is used.&quot;}}\">\u003c/div>","id":"visual-ss6r8z","sect":4,"part":"Allocate the price"},{"type":"calc","bucket":"allocate","lo":40,"q":"FitLah gym sells a 1-year package for $2,400: membership (SSP $1,800), 10 personal-training sessions (SSP $900) and a starter kit (SSP $300). How much of the price is allocated to the personal training?","answer":720,"unit":"$","working":["Total SSP = 1,800 + 900 + 300 = 3,000.","Training = 2,400 × 900 ÷ 3,000 = **$720**.","Check: membership 1,440 + training 720 + kit 240 = 2,400."],"id":"calc-usbpqr","sect":4,"part":"Allocate the price"},{"type":"mcq","bucket":"allocate","lo":40,"q":"A bundle of three products is sold at a discount to the sum of their stand-alone selling prices. There is no evidence the discount relates to any particular product. How is the discount allocated?","options":[{"t":"Entirely to the product with the highest SSP","why":"Without evidence it relates to one product, the discount is spread across all of them."},{"t":"Equally to each product","why":"Not equal shares: in proportion to SSP."},{"t":"Across all three in proportion to their stand-alone selling prices","ok":true,"why":"The relative SSP basis spreads the discount automatically."},{"t":"Expensed as a {x|selling cost}","why":"A discount reduces the price; it is not an {x|expense}."}],"id":"mcq-1fzr7z","sect":4,"part":"Allocate the price"},{"type":"map","id":"map-5-recognise","bucket":"recognise","sect":5,"part":"Recognise revenue"},{"type":"think","bucket":"recognise","lo":40,"scenario":"Four contracts: (1) an office-cleaning firm cleans a client’s office every night; (2) a builder builds an extension on the customer’s own land; (3) a shipyard builds a custom vessel to the buyer’s design, and if the buyer cancels it must pay for work done to date plus a margin; (4) a car dealer sells a car off the lot.","prompt":"For which of these does the customer gain control bit by bit as the work happens, and for which does control pass in one go?","answer":["**(1) Over time:** the client **receives and consumes** the clean office as the work is done.","**(2) Over time:** the extension is an asset the **customer controls** as it is built (it is on their land).","**(3) Over time:** the vessel has **no alternative use** to the shipyard and it has an **enforceable right to payment** for work to date.","**(4) Point in time:** none of the three tests is met, so {i|revenue} comes when control passes, at handover."],"id":"think-m5920i","sect":5,"part":"Recognise revenue"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"recognise","lo":40,"title":"Step 5: over time or at a point in time?","body":["Step 5 is where {i|revenue} finally hits P&L. The four contracts showed two patterns, bit by bit or all at once, and three tests decide which applies.","An obligation is satisfied **over time** if **any one** of these is met:","1. the customer **receives and consumes** the benefits as the entity performs (cleaning, a subscription)","2. the entity’s work **creates or enhances an asset the customer controls** as it is built (building on the customer’s land)","3. the asset has **no alternative use** to the entity **and** the entity has an **enforceable right to payment** for work done to date","Otherwise it is satisfied at a **point in time**: when control passes. Indicators:","- the entity has a present **right to payment**","- the customer has **legal title**","- the customer has **physical possession**","- the customer has the **significant risks and rewards** of ownership","- the customer has **accepted** the asset"],"id":"rule-gbqwyr","sect":5,"part":"Recognise revenue"},{"type":"tree","bucket":"recognise","lo":40,"title":"Over time or point in time?","scenario":"Tuas Marine builds a custom dredger to a buyer’s specification. It could not be sold to anyone else without major rework. The contract says that if the buyer cancels, it must pay for the work done to date plus a reasonable margin. The dredger is built in Tuas Marine’s own yard.","expect":"otC","start":"r1","nodes":{"r1":{"q":"Does the customer receive and consume the benefit as the entity performs?","why":"If the customer uses up the service as it is given, nobody would need to redo the work done so far.","opts":[{"t":"Yes (cleaning, subscriptions, payroll processing)","to":"otA"},{"t":"No","to":"r2"}]},"r2":{"q":"Does the work create or enhance an asset the customer controls as it is built?","why":"If the customer already controls the half-built asset, control is passing as you go.","opts":[{"t":"Yes (e.g. built on the customer’s land)","to":"otB"},{"t":"No (built in the entity’s own premises)","to":"r3"}]},"r3":{"q":"Does the asset have no alternative use to the entity?","why":"If it could easily be sold to someone else, the entity still effectively controls it.","opts":[{"t":"Right: it can’t be redirected to another customer","to":"r4"},{"t":"It could be sold to other customers","to":"pit"}]},"r4":{"q":"Does the entity have an enforceable right to payment for work done to date?","why":"Both halves are needed: no alternative use AND a right to be paid as you go.","opts":[{"t":"Yes, including a reasonable margin","to":"otC"},{"t":"No, payment only on delivery","to":"pit"}]},"otA":{"result":"Over time (customer consumes as you perform)","body":["Recognise {i|revenue} as the service is given, measuring progress (often straight-line by time)."]},"otB":{"result":"Over time (customer controls the asset as it is built)","body":["Recognise {i|revenue} as the work progresses, e.g. cost-to-cost."]},"otC":{"result":"Over time (no alternative use + right to payment)","body":["The dredger can’t go to anyone else and Tuas Marine is paid for work done if the buyer walks. Recognise {i|revenue} as it is built, measuring progress (e.g. {x|costs incurred to date} ÷ total costs)."]},"pit":{"result":"Point in time","body":["None of the three tests is met. Recognise {i|revenue} when control passes: look at legal title, physical possession, risks and rewards, acceptance and a present right to payment."]}},"id":"tree-95jm8b","sect":5,"part":"Recognise revenue","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:592px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 538.00 487.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 476.36)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-476.36 526.7,-476.36 526.7,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>r1\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#b45309\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M427.15,-465.56C427.15,-465.56 301.88,-465.56 301.88,-465.56 295.88,-465.56 289.88,-459.56 289.88,-453.56 289.88,-453.56 289.88,-432.92 289.88,-432.92 289.88,-426.92 295.88,-420.92 301.88,-420.92 301.88,-420.92 427.15,-420.92 427.15,-420.92 433.15,-420.92 439.15,-426.92 439.15,-432.92 439.15,-432.92 439.15,-453.56 439.15,-453.56 439.15,-459.56 433.15,-465.56 427.15,-465.56\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"364.51\" y=\"-450.79\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Does the customer receive\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"364.51\" y=\"-438.79\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">and consume the benefit as\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"364.51\" y=\"-426.79\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">the entity performs?\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node2\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>r2\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#b45309\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M341.03,-349.92C341.03,-349.92 230,-349.92 230,-349.92 224,-349.92 218,-343.92 218,-337.92 218,-337.92 218,-305.28 218,-305.28 218,-299.28 224,-293.28 230,-293.28 230,-293.28 341.03,-293.28 341.03,-293.