ext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"501.39\" y=\"-13.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Cease: expense from here\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge12\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>t5&#45;&gt;ceased\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M345.2,-108.57C347.96,-108.04 350.7,-107.51 353.39,-107 384.9,-101 395.89,-108.72 424.39,-94 448.52,-81.54 470.1,-59 484.23,-41.88\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"485.65,-43.47 487.78,-37.48 482.38,-40.83 485.65,-43.47\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"513.11\" y=\"-78.88\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> Substantially all\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"513.11\" y=\"-67.62\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\">the work is\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"513.11\" y=\"-56.38\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\">complete \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"type":"mcq","bucket":"classify","lo":43,"q":"Which of these is a qualifying asset under SFRS(I) 1-23?","options":[{"t":"Office computers delivered and set up the same week","why":"Ready for use almost as soon as acquired: no substantial period to get ready."},{"t":"An investment in {a|corporate bonds} bought with a {l|bank loan}","why":"{a|Financial assets} are never qualifying assets."},{"t":"A power station that will take three years to build","ok":true,"why":"It necessarily takes a substantial period to get ready for use, so it is a qualifying asset."},{"t":"Bread made daily in large quantities by an industrial bakery","why":"Made over a short period, in large quantities on a repetitive basis: not a qualifying asset."}],"id":"mcq-1nnwah","sect":1,"part":"Classify"},{"type":"compare","bucket":"classify","preamble":"Borrowing costs aren’t an asset of their own: they add to the cost of PPE, investment property or inventory that takes a long time to get ready.","lo":43,"special":"Borrowing costs don’t classify an asset into a standard: they ask whether the asset is **qualifying** (takes a substantial period to get ready). If yes, its interest joins its {a|cost} under its own standard.","id":"compare-1kumyt","sect":1,"part":"Classify"},{"type":"map","id":"map-2-recognise","bucket":"recognise","sect":2,"part":"Recognise"},{"id":"think-rmji93","type":"think","bucket":"recognise","lo":44,"scenario":"Tampines Depot Pte Ltd draws a $3,600,000 {l|loan} at 5% on 1 January to build a logistics depot. The money sits in its account until 1 March, when it pays the first contractor invoice and the builders arrive on site.","prompt":"From 1 January the company is paying interest on a {l|loan} taken out for the depot. Why not capitalise from day one?","answer":["Because in January and February nothing is being **built**. Interest on idle {a|cash} is not a cost of getting the depot ready.","Capitalisation starts only when **all three** have happened:","1. **expenditure** on the asset is being incurred (the first invoice on 1 March)","2. **borrowing costs** are being incurred (from 1 January)","3. **activities** to get the asset ready have begun (builders on site from 1 March)","The last of the three falls on 1 March, so that is when capitalisation commences. January and February’s interest is expensed as {x|interest expense}."],"sect":2,"part":"Recognise"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"recognise","lo":44,"title":"Commencement: all three at once","body":["We know *which* interest can be capitalised; next is *from when*. Borrowing early is common, so the standard needs a clear start date that ties the interest to actual building.","Capitalisation **commences** on the first date when **all three** conditions are met:","1. expenditure for the asset is incurred","2. borrowing costs are incurred","3. activities necessary to prepare the asset for its intended use or sale are under way","- \"Activities\" can include technical and administrative work **before** physical construction starts, such as getting permits.","- Merely **holding** {a|land}, with no development going on, is not such an activity.","! Borrowing early doesn’t start the clock. The latest of the three dates is the start date."],"id":"rule-1ojqw3","sect":2,"part":"Recognise"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"recognise","lo":44,"title":"The capitalisation window","intro":"The chart from your notes. Interest goes into the asset only while it is **inside the navy box**: after commencement, before completion, and not during an extended halt.","notes":{"a":"{l|Loan} drawn, but no spending or work yet: interest is **expensed**.","b":"Capitalisation starts when spending, borrowing costs **and** work are all under way.","c":"Active development: directly attributable borrowing costs are **capitalised** into the {a|asset}.","s":"An **extended** period with no active development: suspend, and expense the interest. Normal or necessary delays don’t count.","e":"Substantially all the work is done: capitalisation **ceases**. From here, interest is an {x|expense}."},"walk":[{"nodes":["a"],"text":"Before the project really starts, interest is just an {x|expense}."},{"nodes":["b"],"text":"The clock starts on the date when the **last** of the three conditions is met."},{"nodes":["c"],"text":"While the asset is actively being developed, interest is capitalised into its {a|cost}."},{"nodes":["s","c"],"text":"If work stops for an **extended** period, suspend; when active work resumes, so does capitalisation."},{"nodes":["e"],"text":"When the asset is substantially complete, stop. Every later dollar of {x|interest} goes to P&L."}],"caption":"Commence → (suspend) → cease. Only the navy stretch is capitalised.","id":"diagram-1tvomp","sect":2,"part":"Recognise","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:640px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 641.00 127.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(14.4 112.44)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-14.4,14.4 -14.4,-112.44 627.05,-112.44 627.05,14.4 -14.4,14.4\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>a\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#f3f4f6\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M86.85,-64C86.85,-64 12,-64 12,-64 6,-64 0,-58 0,-52 0,-52 0,-40 0,-40 0,-34 6,-28 12,-28 12,-28 86.85,-28 86.85,-28 92.85,-28 98.85,-34 98.85,-40 98.85,-40 98.85,-52 98.85,-52 98.85,-58 92.85,-64 86.85,-64\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"10.8\" y=\"-46.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Not yet started\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"31.8\" y=\"-37.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">expense\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node2\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>b\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#b45309\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M243.95,-65.54C243.95,-65.54 133.85,-65.54 133.85,-65.54 127.85,-65.54 121.85,-59.54 121.85,-53.54 121.85,-53.54 121.85,-38.46 121.85,-38.46 121.85,-32.46 127.85,-26.46 133.85,-26.46 133.85,-26.46 243.95,-26.46 243.95,-26.46 249.95,-26.46 255.95,-32.46 255.95,-38.46 255.95,-38.46 255.95,-53.54 255.95,-53.54 255.95,-59.54 249.95,-65.54 243.95,-65.54\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"159.27\" y=\"-51.05\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Commence\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"132.65\" y=\"-41.95\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">spending + borrowing costs\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"140.52\" y=\"-32.95\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">+ work begun (all three)\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge1\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>a&#45;&gt;b\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M99.28,-46C103.81,-46 108.48,-46 113.17,-46\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"113.14,-48.45 120.14,-46 113.14,-43.55 113.14,-48.45\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node3\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>c\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M392.05,-64C392.05,-64 290.95,-64 290.95,-64 284.95,-64 278.95,-58 278.95,-52 278.95,-52 278.95,-40 278.95,-40 278.95,-34 284.95,-28 290.95,-28 290.95,-28 392.05,-28 392.05,-28 398.05,-28 404.05,-34 404.05,-40 404.05,-40 404.05,-52 404.05,-52 404.05,-58 398.05,-64 392.05,-64\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"289.75\" y=\"-46.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"white\">Active development\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"322\" y=\"-37.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"white\">capitalise\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge2\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>b&#45;&gt;c\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M256.39,-46C261.02,-46 265.7,-46 270.35,-46\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"270.15,-48.45 277.15,-46 270.15,-43.55 270.15,-48.45\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node4\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>s\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#ffe4e6\" stroke=\"#be123c\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M600.65,-98.04C600.65,-98.04 473.3,-98.04 473.3,-98.04 467.3,-98.04 461.3,-92.04 461.3,-86.04 461.3,-86.04 461.3,-61.96 461.3,-61.96 461.3,-55.96 467.3,-49.96 473.3,-49.96 473.3,-49.96 600.65,-49.96 600.65,-49.96 606.65,-49.96 612.65,-55.96 612.65,-61.96 612.65,-61.96 612.65,-86.04 612.65,-86.04 612.65,-92.04 606.65,-98.04 600.65,-98.04\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"472.1\" y=\"-83.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Extended inactive period\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"499.48\" y=\"-74.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">suspend: expense\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"502.1\" y=\"-65.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">(not for normal or\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"499.85\" y=\"-56.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">necessary delays)\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge3\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>c&#45;&gt;s\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M404.52,-54.97C419.76,-57.18 436.34,-59.58 452.42,-61.91\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"451.99,-64.32 459.27,-62.9 452.7,-59.47 451.99,-64.32\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node5\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>e\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e6f4f1\" stroke=\"#0f766e\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M595.4,-36C595.4,-36 478.55,-36 478.55,-36 472.55,-36 466.55,-30 466.55,-24 466.55,-24 466.55,-12 466.55,-12 466.55,-6 472.55,0 478.55,0 478.55,0 595.4,0 595.4,0 601.4,0 607.4,-6 607.4,-12 607.4,-12 607.4,-24 607.4,-24 607.4,-30 601.4,-36 595.4,-36\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"477.35\" y=\"-18.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Substantially complete\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"484.1\" y=\"-9.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">cease: expense from here\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge5\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>c&#45;&gt;e\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M404.52,-37.03C421.58,-34.56 440.3,-31.85 458.13,-29.27\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"458.18,-31.73 464.75,-28.31 457.47,-26.89 458.18,-31.73\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge4\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>s&#45;&gt;c\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M476.79,-49.41C468.04,-46.66 459.03,-44.29 450.3,-42.75 438.2,-40.61 425.22,-39.78 412.61,-39.73\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"412.87,-37.28 405.9,-39.79 412.92,-42.18 412.87,-37.28\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"432.67\" y=\"-44.5\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> resume\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"type":"think","bucket":"recognise","lo":44,"scenario":"Two pauses on two building sites. (1) At Tampines Depot, work stops for two months in June and July because of a payment dispute with the main contractor; nobody is on site. (2) At another site, work pauses for three weeks while a concrete slab cures, exactly as planned in the build schedule.","prompt":"Should either company stop capitalising interest during its pause?","answer":["**(1) Yes: suspend.** The dispute causes an **extended period** in which active development stops. That interest is the cost of a stalled project, not of building the depot. Expense it.","**(2) No.** Curing concrete is a **necessary part of the process** of getting the asset ready. Capitalisation carries on.","Rule of thumb: a pause *in the plan* is part of building; a pause *from a problem* is not."],"id":"think-1xbihz","sect":2,"part":"Recognise"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"recognise","lo":44,"title":"Suspension: extended halts only","body":["Once the clock has started, it doesn’t always run smoothly. This rule decides which pauses stop it, so that the cost of a stalled project doesn’t end up in the asset.","**Suspend** capitalisation during **extended periods** in which active development of the asset is interrupted. Borrowing costs in that period are expensed.","Do **not** suspend:","- while substantial technical and administrative work is still being carried out","- for a **temporary delay that is a necessary part of the process** of getting the asset ready (curing concrete, or high water levels that are normal for the area and season)","+ Ask: is the delay part of the job, or is the job stuck?","! Suspending for a normal or necessary delay is a classic exam trap. So is carrying on capitalising through a long dispute."],"id":"rule-7fkfc7","sect":2,"part":"Recognise"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"recognise","lo":44,"title":"Tampines Depot: one year, month by month","intro":"The year from the two thinking pages, as a timeline. Interest runs at 15,000 a month all year; the question is only where each month lands.","notes":{"pre":"{l|Loan} drawn 1 Jan, but no spending and no work until 1 Mar. Not yet commenced: expense.","act1":"All three conditions met from 1 Mar. Capitalise.","halt":"Extended halt from a dispute, not a necessary part of building. Suspend: expense.","act2":"Work resumes in August; so does capitalisation, until the depot is substantially complete at the end of November.","post":"Substantially complete: capitalisation has ceased. December’s interest is an {x|expense}.","cap":"180,000 × 7/12 = 105,000 added to the {a|depot’s cost}.","pl":"180,000 − 105,000 = {x|75,000} in profit or loss."},"walk":[{"nodes":["pre","pl"],"text":"January and February: commencement hasn’t happened yet. Expense."},{"nodes":["act1","cap"],"text":"March to May: all three conditions met, active development. Capitalise."},{"nodes":["halt","pl"],"text":"June and July: an extended halt from a dispute. Suspend and expense."},{"nodes":["act2","cap"],"text":"August to November: building again. Capitalise."},{"nodes":["post","pl"],"text":"December: the depot is complete. Cease: expense."}],"caption":"7 months in the {a|asset}, 5 months in P&L.","id":"diagram-1wxwfb","sect":2,"part":"Recognise","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:606px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 551.00 187.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 176.62)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-176.62 540.48,-176.62 540.48,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>pre\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#f3f4f6\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M61.53,-51.32C61.53,-51.32 12,-51.32 12,-51.32 6,-51.32 0,-45.32 0,-39.32 0,-39.32 0,-12.68 0,-12.68 0,-6.68 6,-0.68 12,-0.68 12,-0.68 61.53,-0.68 61.53,-0.68 67.53,-0.68 73.53,-6.68 73.53,-12.68 73.53,-12.68 73.53,-39.32 73.53,-39.32 73.53,-45.32 67.53,-51.32 61.53,-51.32\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"14.64\" y=\"-37.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Jan–Feb\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"8.64\" y=\"-26.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">loan drawn,\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"17.64\" y=\"-15.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">no work\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"18.01\" y=\"-6.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">2 months\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node2\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>act1\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M143.31,-86.82C143.31,-86.82 103.53,-86.82 103.53,-86.82 97.53,-86.82 91.53,-80.82 91.53