size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">on unspent funds\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"166.42\" y=\"-5.87\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">40,000\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge3\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>inc&#45;&gt;net\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M233.14,-25.6C251.78,-27.41 273.31,-29.5 293.23,-31.44\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"292.81,-33.51 298.98,-32 293.21,-29.33 292.81,-33.51\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"266.94\" y=\"-32.09\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> minus \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node5\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>asset\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e6f4f1\" stroke=\"#0f766e\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M554.12,-58.64C554.12,-58.64 467.84,-58.64 467.84,-58.64 461.84,-58.64 455.84,-52.64 455.84,-46.64 455.84,-46.64 455.84,-29 455.84,-29 455.84,-23 461.84,-17 467.84,-17 467.84,-17 554.12,-17 554.12,-17 560.12,-17 566.12,-23 566.12,-29 566.12,-29 566.12,-46.64 566.12,-46.64 566.12,-52.64 560.12,-58.64 554.12,-58.64\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"464.48\" y=\"-44.87\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Warehouse under\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"477.61\" y=\"-33.87\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">construction\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"488.11\" y=\"-22.87\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">+260,000\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge4\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>net&#45;&gt;asset\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#0f766e\" d=\"M419.42,-37.82C428.91,-37.82 438.76,-37.82 448.32,-37.82\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#0f766e\" stroke=\"#0f766e\" points=\"448.05,-39.92 454.05,-37.82 448.05,-35.72 448.05,-39.92\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"id":"je-ncb8tk","type":"je","bucket":"initial","lo":44,"q":"Changi Cold Chain borrows $2,400,000 at 4.5% specifically to build a warehouse; work runs all year. During the year it debited the full interest to {x|Interest expense} and credited $15,000 earned on the unspent funds to {i|Investment income}. At year end, record the entry that puts the right amount into the {a|asset}.","accounts":["Building under construction","Asset under construction","Cash","Bank loan","Interest payable","Interest expense","Investment income","Depreciation expense","Retained earnings"],"lines":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Building under construction","amount":93000},{"side":"Dr","account":"Investment income","amount":15000},{"side":"Cr","account":"Interest expense","amount":108000}],"why":"Interest 2,400,000 × 4.5% = 108,000, less {i|investment income} 15,000 = 93,000 capitalised. Both the {x|interest} and the {i|income} are moved out of P&L and netted into the {a|asset}.","sect":3,"part":"Initial measurement"},{"id":"think-129cx2","type":"think","bucket":"initial","lo":44,"scenario":"A company has no loan earmarked for its new plant. It has a pool of {l|general borrowings}: $2,000,000 at 6% and $3,000,000 at 8%, both outstanding all year. It spends $1,000,000 on the plant on 1 January and $2,000,000 on 1 July.","prompt":"There is no \"plant loan\" to point at. How would you work out the interest that the plant really caused?","answer":["Two pieces:","1. **A rate:** what does the pool cost on average? Weight by the size of each {l|loan}: (120,000 + 240,000) ÷ 5,000,000 = **7.2%**. Not the simple average of the two rates.","2. **An amount:** how much money was tied up in the plant, and for how long? 1,000,000 for 12 months + 2,000,000 for 6 months = **2,000,000** for a full year.","Then rate × amount = 7.2% × 2,000,000 = **144,000**."],"sect":3,"part":"Initial measurement"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"initial","lo":44,"title":"General borrowings","body":["Specific loans are the easy case. Many companies just fund everything from one pool of loans, so there is no loan to point at, and the standard needs a formula to work out the asset’s share.","When funds come from a **general** pool of borrowings:","> {a|Capitalised} = capitalisation rate × expenditure on the asset (weighted by time)","> Capitalisation rate = borrowing costs on {l|general borrowings} ÷ average {l|general borrowings} outstanding","1. Work out the **weighted average** cost of the general pool (exclude {l|loans} taken specifically for a qualifying asset).","2. **Time-weight** the expenditure: each amount × months outstanding ÷ 12.","3. Multiply, then **cap** it: the amount capitalised can’t exceed the borrowing costs actually incurred in the period.","! Two classic slips: a simple average of the interest rates, and forgetting to weight the spending by time."],"id":"rule-2zstml","sect":3,"part":"Initial measurement"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"initial","lo":44,"title":"General borrowings: rate × weighted spend","intro":"Two streams meet: the pool gives you a **rate**, the {a|asset} gives you a **weighted spend**. Multiply, check the cap, and the rest stays in P&L.","notes":{"l1":"2,000,000 × 6% = 120,000.","l2":"3,000,000 × 8% = 240,000.","rate":"A **weighted** average: total cost of the pool ÷ average pool outstanding. Not (6% + 8%) ÷ 2.","e1":"Tied up in the asset for the whole year.","e2":"Tied up for only half the year, so it counts half.","wexp":"1,000,000 + 1,000,000 = 2,000,000.","amt":"7.2% × 2,000,000 = 144,000.","capchk":"You can never capitalise more than the borrowing costs actually incurred in the period.","asset":"Capitalised into the {a|plant’s cost}.","pl":"360,000 − 144,000 = {x|216,000} stays in profit or loss."},"walk":[{"nodes":["l1","l2","rate"],"text":"Stream 1: the pool’s weighted average cost, 7.2%."},{"nodes":["e1","e2","wexp"],"text":"Stream 2: spending weighted by how long it was tied up, 2,000,000."},{"nodes":["amt","capchk"],"text":"Multiply: 144,000. Check it against the actual cost of the pool, 360,000: below, so no cap."},{"nodes":["asset","pl"],"text":"144,000 into the {a|plant}; the other 216,000 stays as an {x|expense}."}],"caption":"General pool: weighted rate × weighted spend, capped at actual cost.","id":"diagram-1ekhuv","sect":3,"part":"Initial measurement","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:537px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 488.00 354.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 343.61)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-343.61 477.33,-343.61 477.33,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>l1\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e8eef6\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M84.03,-332.81C84.03,-332.81 12,-332.81 12,-332.81 6,-332.81 0,-326.81 0,-320.81 0,-320.81 0,-305.17 0,-305.17 0,-299.17 6,-293.17 12,-293.17 12,-293.17 84.03,-293.17 84.03,-293.17 90.03,-293.17 96.03,-299.17 96.03,-305.17 96.03,-305.17 96.03,-320.81 96.03,-320.81 96.03,-326.81 90.03,-332.81 84.03,-332.81\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"29.64\" y=\"-319.04\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Loan A\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"8.64\" y=\"-308.04\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">2,000,000 at 6%\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"21.76\" y=\"-298.94\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">cost 120,000\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node3\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>rate\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M210.15,-266.17C210.15,-266.17 117.87,-266.17 117.87,-266.17 111.87,-266.17 105.87,-260.17 105.87,-254.17 105.87,-254.17 105.87,-236.53 105.87,-236.53 105.87,-230.53 111.87,-224.53 117.87,-224.53 117.87,-224.53 210.15,-224.53 210.15,-224.53 216.15,-224.53 222.15,-230.53 222.15,-236.53 222.15,-236.53 222.15,-254.17 222.15,-254.17 222.15,-260.17 216.15,-266.17 210.15,-266.17\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"116.39\" y=\"-252.4\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"white\">Capitalisation rate\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"114.51\" y=\"-241.4\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"white\">360,000 ÷ 5,000,000\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"146.76\" y=\"-230.4\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"white\">= 7.2%\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge1\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>l1&#45;&gt;rate\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M82.19,-292.65C94.6,-285.63 108.76,-277.62 121.78,-270.25\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"122.56,-272.22 126.75,-267.44 120.49,-268.56 122.56,-272.22\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node2\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>l2\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e8eef6\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M202.03,-332.81C202.03,-332.81 130,-332.81 130,-332.81 124,-332.81 118,-326.81 118,-320.81 118,-320.81 118,-305.17 118,-305.17 118,-299.17 124,-293.17 130,-293.17 130,-293.17 202.03,-293.17 202.03,-293.17 208.03,-293.17 214.03,-299.17 214.03,-305.17 214.03,-305.17 214.03,-320.81 214.03,-320.81 214.03,-326.81 208.03,-332.81 202.03,-332.81\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"147.26\" y=\"-319.04\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" fo