e=\"#166534\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M424.59,-36C424.59,-36 309.06,-36 309.06,-36 303.06,-36 297.06,-30 297.06,-24 297.06,-24 297.06,-12 297.06,-12 297.06,-6 303.06,0 309.06,0 309.06,0 424.59,0 424.59,0 430.59,0 436.59,-6 436.59,-12 436.59,-12 436.59,-24 436.59,-24 436.59,-30 430.59,-36 424.59,-36\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"331.58\" y=\"-18.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">OCI: recycled\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"305.7\" y=\"-9.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">FVOCI reserve → P&amp;L on sale\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge10\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>fd&#45;&gt;oy\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M239.88,-18C255.3,-18 272.62,-18 289.35,-18\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"288.97,-20.1 294.97,-18 288.97,-15.9 288.97,-20.1\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"id":"je-q54i3n","type":"je","bucket":"oci","lo":45,"q":"A company uses the revaluation model for its head-office building: {a|cost} $800,000, {a|accumulated depreciation} $160,000. It is revalued to fair value $880,000. Record the revaluation: eliminate the {a|accumulated depreciation} and take the {a|building} to fair value. Ignore tax.","accounts":["Cash","Share capital","Share premium","Treasury shares","Capital reserve","Retained earnings","Revaluation surplus (OCI)","FVOCI reserve","Dividend payable","Building (PPE)","Accumulated depreciation: building","Share issue expense","Gain on treasury shares","Revaluation gain (P&L)","Dividend expense","Gain on disposal of investment"],"lines":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Accumulated depreciation: building","amount":160000},{"side":"Dr","account":"Building (PPE)","amount":80000},{"side":"Cr","account":"Revaluation surplus (OCI)","amount":240000}],"why":"{a|Carrying amount} 800,000 − 160,000 = 640,000. Increase to 880,000 = 240,000, credited to OCI and built up in the {e|revaluation surplus}. The {a|building} account rises by 880,000 − 800,000 = 80,000.","sect":3,"part":"OCI: what goes there"},{"type":"visual","bucket":"oci","lo":45,"title":"The revaluation as two bars","html":"\u003cp>What the entry you just made does, drawn to scale. \u003cstrong>Before:\u003c/strong> the \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">building\u003c/span> at \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">cost\u003c/span> 800,000, with 160,000 of \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">accumulated depreciation\u003c/span> (a \u003cstrong>contra-asset\u003c/strong>, so asset-coloured) taken off it, leaves a \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">carrying amount\u003c/span> of 640,000. \u003cstrong>After:\u003c/strong> the \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">accumulated depreciation\u003c/span> is wiped out and the \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">building\u003c/span> goes up to fair value; the extra 240,000 on top of the old \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">carrying amount\u003c/span> is matched by the \u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">revaluation surplus\u003c/span> in \u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">equity\u003c/span>.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"cbars\">\n    \u003cdiv class=\"cb-key\">\u003cspan>\u003cspan class=\"seg a\">\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">carrying amount\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan>\u003cspan class=\"seg out-a\">\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">accumulated depreciation\u003c/span> (taken off)\u003c/span>\u003cspan>\u003cspan class=\"seg e\">\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">revaluation surplus\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\n    \u003cdiv class=\"cb-year\">\u003cdiv class=\"cb-cap\">Before: \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">cost 800,000\u003c/span> − \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">160,000\u003c/span> = \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">640,000\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-track\">\u003cspan class=\"seg a\" style=\"flex:none;width:72.73%\">\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"seg out-a\" style=\"flex:none;width:18.18%\">\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\n    \u003cdiv class=\"cb-year\">\u003cdiv class=\"cb-cap\">After: \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">640,000\u003c/span> + \u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">240,000\u003c/span> = \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">fair value 880,000\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-track\">\u003cspan class=\"seg a\" style=\"flex:none;width:72.73%\">\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"seg e\" style=\"flex:none;width:27.27%\">\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\n  \u003c/div>\u003cp class=\"cap\">The \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">building\u003c/span> account itself moves from 800,000 to 880,000 (+80,000); with the 160,000 \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">accumulated depreciation\u003c/span> removed, the \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">carrying amount\u003c/span> rises by 240,000.\u003c/p>","id":"visual-1hlslo","sect":3,"part":"OCI: what goes there"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"oci","lo":45,"title":"The revaluation surplus: where it is not","body":["You have just recorded the {e|surplus}. Exams test it by offering tempting wrong homes, so here are the three to rule out.","A revaluation increase on PPE is **credited to OCI and accumulated in equity** under {e|Revaluation surplus (OCI)}.","It is **not**:","1. {i|income} in **profit or loss**","2. credited **straight to {e|retained earnings}**","3. **{l|deferred income}** waiting for a sale","- Exception: if the same {a|asset} had an earlier revaluation **{x|decrease}** in P&L, the increase goes to P&L up to that amount first.","- **{x|Tax}** on OCI items is shown with OCI: either each item net of tax, or gross with a tax line for each group.","! Practice Q29 offers all three wrong homes. Only “OCI, accumulated in equity” is right."],"id":"rule-1p3mgk","sect":3,"part":"OCI: what goes there"},{"type":"mcq","bucket":"oci","lo":45,"q":"Which of these gains is recognised in other comprehensive income?","options":[{"t":"A fair value gain on {a|investment property} under the fair value model","why":"{a|Investment property} {i|gains} go to profit or loss."},{"t":"A fair value gain on {a|shares held for trading}","why":"Held for trading means FVTPL: profit or loss."},{"t":"A fair value gain on {a|shares} the entity elected to measure at FVOCI","ok":true,"why":"That election sends fair value changes to OCI, and they are never recycled."},{"t":"A gain on reissuing {e|treasury shares} above cost","why":"Not {i|income} at all: it stays in {e|equity} as a transaction with owners."}],"id":"mcq-lm3had","sect":3,"part":"OCI: what goes there"},{"type":"map","id":"map-4-recycle","bucket":"recycle","sect":4,"part":"Recycle or not"},{"id":"think-1dn9zl","type":"think","bucket":"recycle","lo":45,"scenario":"A company sells two investments, both at FVOCI. (1) A {a|government bond} (debt): $12,000 of gains have built up in OCI. (2) {a|Shares in a supplier} (equity, FVOCI elected): $20,000 of gains have built up in OCI.","prompt":"When each is sold, should the gains sitting in OCI now pass through profit or loss?","answer":["**The {a|bond}: yes.** {a|Debt} at FVOCI is **recycled**: the 12,000 is reclassified from OCI to P&L on sale, so total profit over the bond’s life matches amortised cost.","**The {a|shares}: no.** That was the deal when the company made the FVOCI election: {i|gains} on those shares **never** reach P&L. The 20,000 may simply be transferred to {e|Retained earnings} within {e|equity}."],"sect":4,"part":"Recycle or not"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"recycle","lo":45,"title":"Two groups of OCI","body":["The {a|bond} and the {a|shares} behaved differently on sale: one passed through profit, the other never will. That difference is why OCI is presented in two groups.","Present OCI in **two groups**:","1. Items that **will not** be reclassified to profit or loss: {e|revaluation surplus}, FVOCI {a|equity investments}, own credit risk on FVTPL {l|liabilities}.","2. Items that **may** be reclassified to profit or loss: FVOCI {a|debt instruments} (in this syllabus).","- **Reclassification (recycling):** an amount recognised in OCI earlier is moved into profit or loss now, e.g. when a FVOCI {a|bond} is sold.","- Items in group 1 can still be **transferred to {e|retained earnings}** within {e|equity}. That is not recycling: it never passes through P&L or OCI.","! The {e|revaluation surplus} is **never** recycled. Exam options love to send it to P&L on disposal."],"id":"rule-6abpxh","sect":4,"part":"Recycle or not"},{"id":"tree-1bfb8q","type":"tree","bucket":"recycle","lo":45,"title":"Where does this change in equity go?","scenario":"A company sells a {a|bond} it held at FVOCI (a debt instrument). $18,000 of fair value gains are sitting in its {e|FVOCI reserve}. Where does that 18,000 go now? Tap your way down.","expect":"debt","start":"n1","nodes":{"n1":{"q":"What kind of movement is it?","why":"Owner transactions and reserve transfers never touch P&L or OCI. Everything else is performance.","opts":[{"t":"A transaction with owners (shares, buy-backs, dividends)","to":"n2"},{"t":"A move between two {e|equity reserves}","to":"xfer"},{"t":"{i|Income} or an {x|expense}","to":"n3"}]},"n2":{"q":"Which owner transaction?","why":"All of them sit directly in equity; the entries differ.","opts":[{"t":"Issuing shares (with issue costs)","to":"issue"},{"t":"Buying back or reissuing own shares","to":"ts"},{"t":"Declaring a dividend","to":"div"},{"t":"A bonus issue","to":"bonus"}]},"n3":{"q":"Does a standard send it to OCI?","why":"Profit or loss is the default. OCI is only for items a standard names.","opts":[{"t":"No","to":"pl"},{"t":"Yes","to":"n4"}]},"n4":{"q":"Which OCI item is it?","why":"The item decides which OCI group it sits in, and whether it can be recycled.","opts":[{"t":"{e|Revaluation surplus} on {a|PPE} or {a|intangibles}","to":"reval"},{"t":"Fair value change on {a|equity investments} elected at FVOCI","to":"fvoe"},{"t":"Fair value change on a {a|debt instrument} at FVOCI","to":"n5"},{"t":"Own credit risk on a {l|liability} designated at FVTPL","to":"own"}]},"n5":{"q":"Is the {a|debt instrument} being derecognised (sold or redeemed)?","why":"FVOCI debt gains wait in OCI until the instrument goes; then they are recycled.","opts":[{"t":"No, it is a year-end fair value change","to":"debtYr"},{"t":"Yes, it is sold","to":"debt"}]},"xfer":{"result":"Directly in equity: total unchanged","body":["E.g. {e|revaluation surplus} → {e|retained earnings} (excess depreciation or on disposal). Shown as a transfer line in the SOCE.","! Not through P&L or OCI, and not a change in {e|total equity}."]},"issue":{"result":"Directly in equity: share capital (and premium)","body":["Dr {a|Cash} / Cr {e|Share capital}. Issue costs are deducted from {e|equity}, net of tax."]},"ts":{"result":"Directly in equity: treasury shares","body":["A deduction from {e|equity}. No {i|gain} or {x|loss} in P&L on buying, reissuing or cancelling."]},"div":{"result":"Directly in equity: retained earnings","body":["Dr {e|Retained earnings} / Cr {l|Dividend payable} when declared. Declared after year end → not a {l|liability}; disclose."]},"bonus":{"result":"Directly in equity: total unchanged","body":["Reserves → {e|Share capital}. No {a|cash} moves."]},"pl":{"result":"Profit or loss","body":["The default for {i|income} and {x|expenses}: {i|sales}, {x|wages}, {x|depreciation}, {a|investment property} fair value changes, FVTPL {i|gains}."]},"reval":{"result":"OCI: will not be reclassified","body":["Built up in {e|Revaluation surplus (OCI)}. May be transferred to {e|Retained earnings} as the {a|asset} is used or sold. Never recycled."]},"fvoe":{"result":"OCI: will not be reclassified","body":["Built up in the {e|FVOCI reserve}. On sale it may be transferred to {e|Retained earnings}. Never recycled."]},"own":{"result":"OCI: will not be reclassified","body":["The part of the fair value change caused by the entity’s own credit risk. Never recycled."]},"debtYr":{"result":"OCI: may be reclassified","body":["The year’s fair value change goes to OCI and builds up 