\"middle\" x=\"187.28\" y=\"-152.11\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> ✗ never \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node3\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>fd\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#dcfce7\" stroke=\"#166534\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M95.65,-36C95.65,-36 26.62,-36 26.62,-36 20.62,-36 14.62,-30 14.62,-24 14.62,-24 14.62,-12 14.62,-12 14.62,-6 20.62,0 26.62,0 26.62,0 95.65,0 95.65,0 101.65,0 107.65,-6 107.65,-12 107.65,-12 107.65,-24 107.65,-24 107.65,-30 101.65,-36 95.65,-36\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"23.26\" y=\"-18.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">FVOCI reserve\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"27.39\" y=\"-9.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">debt instruments\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge3\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>fd&#45;&gt;pl\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#166534\" d=\"M108.03,-19.86C142.51,-21.9 190.72,-26.11 232.28,-34.75 240.79,-36.52 249.69,-38.89 258.26,-41.47\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#166534\" stroke=\"#166534\" points=\"257.58,-43.45 263.93,-43.22 258.82,-39.44 257.58,-43.45\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"187.28\" y=\"-36.5\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> on sale: recycled \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"id":"think-1mw68h","type":"think","bucket":"recycle","lo":45,"scenario":"A company’s head-office building ({a|cost} $800,000, 20-year life, straight line) had a {a|carrying amount} of $640,000 after 4 years and was revalued to $880,000, with a {e|revaluation surplus} of $240,000 and 16 years of life left. Before the revaluation, {x|depreciation} was $40,000 a year ({a|cost} 800,000 ÷ 20). After it, it is 880,000 ÷ 16 = $55,000.","prompt":"Profit is now hit by the higher {x|depreciation} every year, but the {e|surplus} that caused it just sits in {e|equity}. Is there a way to tidy that up?","answer":["Yes. Each year the company **may** transfer the **excess depreciation**, 55,000 − 40,000 = **15,000**, from the {e|revaluation surplus} to {e|retained earnings}.","Over the 16 remaining years that moves the whole 240,000 (15,000 × 16) as the {a|building} is used up.","It goes **directly within {e|equity}**: not through profit or loss, not through OCI. The {e|surplus} quietly moves house as the building gets older."],"sect":4,"part":"Recycle or not"},{"id":"calc-umbnij","type":"calc","bucket":"recycle","lo":45,"q":"A building cost $800,000 and was depreciated straight line over 20 years. After 4 years ({a|carrying amount} $640,000) it is revalued to $880,000, with 16 years of life left. The company transfers the excess depreciation to {e|retained earnings} each year. What is the balance on the {e|revaluation surplus} at the end of the first year after the revaluation? (Ignore tax.)","answer":225000,"unit":"$","working":["Excess depreciation = 55,000 − 40,000 = 15,000 (also 240,000 ÷ 16).","{e|Surplus} = 240,000 − 15,000 = **$225,000**."],"sect":4,"part":"Recycle or not"},{"id":"je-i9plrd","type":"je","bucket":"recycle","lo":45,"q":"A head-office building with a {a|carrying amount} of $640,000 was revalued to $880,000, creating a {e|revaluation surplus} of $240,000, with 16 years of life left. {x|Depreciation} was $40,000 a year before the revaluation and is $55,000 a year after it. The company transfers the excess depreciation from the {e|revaluation surplus} to {e|retained earnings} each year. Record this year’s transfer.","accounts":["Cash","Share capital","Share premium","Treasury shares","Capital reserve","Retained earnings","Revaluation surplus (OCI)","FVOCI reserve","Dividend payable","Building (PPE)","Accumulated depreciation: building","Share issue expense","Gain on treasury shares","Revaluation gain (P&L)","Dividend expense","Gain on disposal of investment"],"lines":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Revaluation surplus (OCI)","amount":15000},{"side":"Cr","account":"Retained earnings","amount":15000}],"why":"15,000 moves from one {e|reserve} to another, within {e|equity}. Not through P&L or OCI; {e|total equity} unchanged.","sect":4,"part":"Recycle or not"},{"type":"visual","bucket":"recycle","lo":45,"title":"The surplus moves house, year by year","html":"\u003cp>The head office again: a \u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">revaluation surplus\u003c/span> of 240,000, 16 years of life left, and an excess depreciation transfer of 15,000 a year. Step through the first 5 years.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"wg\" data-wg=\"roll\" data-key=\"surplus-c3\" data-cfg=\"{&quot;notes&quot;:{&quot;start&quot;:&quot;Start: {a|carrying amount} 640,000 revalued to {a|880,000}, so the {e|surplus} opens at {e|240,000}. Press Play or Next.&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[&quot;Each year the excess depreciation (55,000 new − 40,000 old = 15,000, also 240,000 ÷ 16) leaves the {e|surplus} for {e|retained earnings}: Dr {e|Revaluation surplus (OCI)} / Cr {e|Retained earnings}.&quot;],&quot;end&quot;:&quot;After 5 years 75,000 has moved and **{e|165,000}** is left. None of it touched P&amp;L or OCI, and {e|total equity} never moved: one pocket down, the other up. Carry on for all 16 years and the {e|surplus} reaches zero just as the {a|building} is fully depreciated.&quot;},&quot;panels&quot;:[{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Revaluation surplus&quot;,&quot;sub&quot;:&quot;−15,000 a year&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;e&quot;,&quot;bal&quot;:&quot;Revaluation surplus&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:240000,&quot;startCap&quot;:&quot;Revaluation: {a|880,000} − {a|640,000} = {e|240,000}, credited to OCI and built up in the {e|surplus}.&quot;,&quot;years&quot;:[{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Yr 1&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;transfer to retained earnings&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;e&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-15000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 1: {x|depreciation} 55,000 − 40,000 = 15,000 excess, moved to {e|retained earnings}. {e|Surplus} now {e|225,000}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Yr 2&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;transfer to retained earnings&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;e&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-15000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 2: {x|depreciation} 55,000 − 40,000 = 15,000 excess, moved to {e|retained earnings}. {e|Surplus} now {e|210,000}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Yr 3&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;transfer to retained earnings&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;e&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-15000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 3: {x|depreciation} 55,000 − 40,000 = 15,000 excess, moved to {e|retained earnings}. {e|Surplus} now {e|195,000}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Yr 4&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;transfer to retained earnings&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;e&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-15000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 4: {x|depreciation} 55,000 − 40,000 = 15,000 excess, moved to {e|retained earnings}. {e|Surplus} now {e|180,000}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Yr 5&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;transfer to retained earnings&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;e&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-15000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Year 5: {x|depreciation} 55,000 − 40,000 = 15,000 excess, moved to {e|retained earnings}. {e|Surplus} now {e|165,000}.&quot;}]}]}]}\">\u003c/div>","id":"visual-1ivxrk","sect":4,"part":"Recycle or not"},{"id":"mcq-3ow7n0","type":"mcq","bucket":"recycle","lo":45,"q":"A company revalued its head office (a {e|revaluation surplus} of $240,000) and has transferred the excess depreciation to {e|retained earnings} each year. Five years later it sells the building, with $165,000 still in the {e|revaluation surplus}. What happens to that $165,000?","options":[{"t":"It is reclassified to profit or loss as part of the {i|gain on disposal}","why":"The {e|revaluation surplus} is never recycled to P&L."},{"t":"It may be transferred directly to {e|retained earnings}","ok":true,"why":"The {a|asset} is gone, so the {e|surplus} is realised. It moves within equity, never through P&L."},{"t":"It is shown as a negative item in OCI for the year","why":"A transfer within equity is not an OCI item."},{"t":"It must stay in the {e|revaluation surplus} permanently","why":"The transfer is allowed (not required) once the {a|asset} is derecognised."}],"sect":4,"part":"Recycle or not"},{"type":"map","id":"map-5-soce","bucket":"soce","sect":5,"part":"Statement of changes in equity"},{"id":"think-bbkapn","type":"think","bucket":"soce","lo":45,"scenario":"An investor wants to know why a company’s {e|retained earnings} went up but its {e|revaluation surplus} went down, and whether any shares were issued this year.","prompt":"Which statement answers all three questions at once, and how would you lay it out?","answer":["The **statement of changes in equity (SOCE)**. It has a **column for each component** of {e|equity} and reconciles each one from {e|opening} to {e|closing}.","Rows show profit, each OCI item, total comprehensive income, transactions with owners, and transfers between reserves. The transfer row is where a {e|surplus} goes down while {e|retained earnings} go up, with a zero in the total column."],"sect":5,"part":"Statement of changes in equity"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"soce","lo":45,"title":"Statement of changes in equity","body":["Every movement in this chapter ends up in one statement. Here is what it must show for each component of {e|equity}.","For **each component of {e|equity}**, reconcile the {e|opening and closing balances}, showing separately:","1. **profit or loss**","2. **each item of OCI**","3. **total comprehensive income** (with any split between owners of the parent and non-controlling interests)","4. **transactions with owners**: contributions (share issues) and distributions (dividends, buy-backs)","5. **transfers** between {e|reserves}","- Also the effect of **retrospective restatements** (see E1), and dividends per share (in the SOCE or the notes).","> {e|Closing equity} = {e|opening} + TCI + contributions − distributions (transfers net to nil)"],"id":"rule-1oe4xw","sect":5,"part":"Statement of changes in equity"},{"id":"visual-1wbhf6","type":"visual","bucket":"soce","lo":45,"title":"Example SOCE ($’000)","html":"\u003cp>The rule as a table, using the example from your notes. One column per component of \u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">equity\u003c/span>, one row per kind of movement. Tap to reveal the rows one by one.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"tbl-wrap\">\u003ctable class=\"tbl num reveal-rows\">\u003cthead>\u003ctr>\u003cth>\u003c/th>\u003cth>\u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">Share capital\u003c/span>\u003c/th>\u003cth>\u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">Revaluation surplus\u003c/span>\u003c/th>\u003cth>\u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">Retained earnings\u003c/span>\u003c/th>\u003cth>\u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">Total\u003c/span>\u003c/th>\u003c/tr>\u003c/thead>\u003ctbody>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">Opening balance\u003c/span>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>300\u003c/td>\u003ctd>60\u003c/td>\u003ctd>140\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cb>500\u003c/b>\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>Profit for the year\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>80\u003c/td>\u003ctd>80\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>OCI: \u003cspan class=\"el el-i\">revaluation gain\u003c/span>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>20\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>20\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003cb>Total comprehensive income\u003c/b>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>20\u003c/td>\u003ctd>80\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cb>100\u003c/b>\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>Issue of shares\u003c/td>\u003ctd>50\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>50\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>Dividends\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>(30)\u003c/td>\u003ctd>(30)\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>Transfer: excess depreciation\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>(5)\u003c/td>\u003ctd>5\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cb>0\u003c/b>\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003cb>\u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">Closing balance\u003c/span>\u003c/b>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cb>350\u003c/b>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cb>75\u003c/b>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cb>195\u003c/b>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cb>620\u003c/b>\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n    \u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\u003c/div>\n    \u003cp class=\"cap\">Read across the transfer row: one column down, one up, \u003cstrong>zero\u003c/strong> in the total. That is the row exam options love to count twice.\u003c/p>","sect":5,"part":"Statement of changes in equity"},{"type":"visual","bucket":"soce","lo":45,"title":"Two columns, step by step","html":"\u003cp>The same SOCE ($’000), column by column. The \u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">revaluation surplus\u003c/span> gets the OCI; \u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">retained earnings\u003c/span> get profit and lose the dividends. Watch the last step: the transfer takes 5 out of one column and puts it into the other.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"wg\" data-wg=\"roll\" data-key=\"soce-c3\" data-cfg=\"{&quot;notes&quot;:{&quot;start&quot;:&quot;Opening balances from the SOCE. Press Play or Next.&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[&quot;Total comprehensive income first: profit to {e|retained earnings}, OCI to the {e|revaluation surplus}.&quot;,&quot;Then the owners: the dividend comes out of {e|retained earnings}.&quot;,&quot;Last, the transfer: out of one column, into the other, **zero** in the total.&quot;],&quot;end&quot;:&quot;Closing: {e|surplus} 75, {e|retained earnings} 195. Both columns moved by 5 on the transfer, in opposite directions, so {e|total equity} only felt profit, OCI, the share issue and the dividend.&quot;},&quot;panels&quot;:[{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Revaluation surplus&quot;,&quot;sub&quot;:&quot;$’000&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;e&quot;,&quot;bal&quot;:&quot;Revaluation surplus&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:60,&quot;startCap&quot;:&quot;{e|Opening surplus} 60.&quot;,&quot;years&quot;:[{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;This year&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;OCI&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;i&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:20,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;OCI {i|revaluation gain} +20 → {e|80}.&quot;},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;dividends&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;e&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:0,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;No change: dividends come out of {e|retained earnings}, not the {e|surplus}. Still {e|80}.&quot;},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;transfer out&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;e&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-5,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Excess depreciation −5 to {e|retained earnings} → {e|closing 75}.&quot;}]}]},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Retained earnings&quot;,&quot;sub&quot;:&quot;$’000&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;e&quot;,&quot;bal&quot;:&quot;Retained earnings&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:140,&quot;startCap&quot;:&quot;{e|Opening retained earnings} 140.&quot;,&quot;years&quot;:[{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;This year&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;profit&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;i&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:80,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Profit +80 → {e|220}.&quot;},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;dividends&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;e&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-30,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Dividends −30: a distribution to owners, not an {x|expense} → {e|190}.&quot;},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;transfer in&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;e&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:5,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;Transfer in +5 from the {e|surplus} → {e|closing 195}.&quot;}]}]}]}\">\u003c/div>","id":"visual-igxg5y","sect":5,"part":"Statement of changes in equity"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"soce","lo":45,"title":"The total column as a bridge","intro":"The total column of the example SOCE, drawn as a bridge from {e|opening} to {e|closing} ($’000).","notes":{"open":"{e|Total equity} at the start of the year: all columns added up.","tci":"Performance: profit 80 plus OCI 20 = total comprehensive income 100.","own":"Transactions with owners: +50 share issue, −30 dividends.","xf":"Moves between columns but adds nothing to the total. Dashed because it changes nothing here.","close":"500 + 100 + 50 − 30 = 620."},"walk":[{"nodes":["open"],"text":"Start with {e|opening equity}: 500."},{"nodes":["tci"],"text":"Add **TCI**: profit and OCI together, 100."},{"nodes":["own"],"text":"Add contributions from owners and subtract distributions to them."},{"nodes":["xf"],"text":"**Transfers between reserves: zero.** Skip them in the total."},{"nodes":["close"],"text":"{e|Closing equity}: **620**."}],"caption":"“TCI or owners”: the only two things that move the total.","id":"diagram-16qyxr","sect":5,"part":"Statement of changes in equity","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:120px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 109.00 307.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 295.72)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-295.72 97.83,-295.72 97.83,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>open\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M62.28,-284.92C62.28,-284.92 24.75,-284.92 24.75,-284.92 18.75,-284.92 12.75,-278.92 12.75,-272.92 12.75,-272.92 12.75,-260.92 12.75,-260.92 12.75,-254.92 18.75,-248.92 24.75,-248.92 24.75,-248.92 62.28,-248.92 62.28,-248.92 68.28,-248.92 74.28,-254.92 74.28,-260.92 74.28,-260.92 74.28,-272.92 74.28,-272.92 74.28,-278.92 68.28,-284.92 62.28,-284.92\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"21.39\" y=\"-268.47\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"white\">Opening\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"34.52\" y=\"-257.47\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"white\">500\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node2\" class=\