l","why":"That goes straight to P&L, not OCI."},{"t":"A {i|fair value gain} on an {a|equity investment} designated at FVOCI","why":"OCI, but never reclassified to P&L."}],"id":"mcq-al3ggd","sect":3,"part":"Profit or loss, OCI and equity"},{"id":"think-171p0m","type":"think","bucket":"pl","lo":46,"scenario":"Kranji Furniture buys timber, pays carpenters, runs a factory, and sells finished tables. At year end it has timber in the yard, half-built tables on the floor, and finished tables in the showroom.","prompt":"A retailer has one {a|inventory} line. How many does Kranji have, and how would you get to its {x|cost of sales}?","answer":["Three: **{a|raw materials}**, **{a|work in progress}** and **{a|finished goods}**.","{x|Cost of sales} is built in two layers: first the **cost of goods manufactured** (what the factory finished this year), then adjust for {a|finished goods} in and out of the showroom."],"sect":3,"part":"Profit or loss, OCI and equity"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"pl","lo":46,"title":"Retail, service and manufacturing","body":["The P&L layout is the same for everyone, but how you reach {x|cost of sales} depends on what the business does. A manufacturer has two extra layers.","- **Retail:** one {a|inventory} (merchandise). {x|Cost of sales} = {a|opening inventory} + {x|purchases} − {a|closing inventory}.","- **Service:** little or no {a|inventory}; {i|revenue} is mostly fees over time and costs mainly staff. {a|Contract assets} and {l|contract liabilities} are common.","- **Manufacturing:** three {a|inventories}, and a cost of goods manufactured schedule:","> Raw materials used = {a|opening raw materials} + {x|purchases} − {a|closing raw materials}","> Cost of goods manufactured = raw materials used + direct labour + production overheads + {a|opening WIP} − {a|closing WIP}","> {x|Cost of sales} = {a|opening finished goods} + cost of goods manufactured − {a|closing finished goods}","! {x|Factory depreciation} is a **production overhead** (into {x|cost of sales}), not an {x|admin expense}."],"id":"rule-1p7wwi","sect":3,"part":"Profit or loss, OCI and equity"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"pl","lo":46,"title":"Kranji’s cost of sales, built up","intro":"Two layers: the factory first, then the showroom.","notes":{"rm":"Raw materials used = {a|opening 20,000} + {x|purchases} 150,000 − {a|closing 25,000} = $145,000.","dl":"Wages of the carpenters who make the tables: $90,000.","oh":"Factory rent, power, supervision and {x|factory depreciation} ($15,000 of it): $60,000.","wip":"Add half-built tables brought forward ({a|opening WIP} $18,000), take off those still half-built at year end ({a|closing WIP} $22,000).","cogm":"145,000 + 90,000 + 60,000 + 18,000 − 22,000 = $291,000: what the factory finished this year.","fg":"Add finished tables brought forward ({a|opening finished goods} $40,000), take off those still unsold ({a|closing finished goods} $35,000).","cos":"40,000 + 291,000 − 35,000 = $296,000, the {x|cost of sales} line in P&L."},"walk":[{"nodes":["rm"],"text":"Raw materials used: the retailer formula, applied to timber."},{"nodes":["dl","oh"],"text":"Add the factory’s labour and overheads, including {x|factory depreciation}."},{"nodes":["wip","cogm"],"text":"Adjust for {a|work in progress} to get the cost of goods manufactured."},{"nodes":["fg","cos"],"text":"Then adjust for {a|finished goods}: that is {x|cost of sales}."}],"caption":"Same opening + in − closing pattern, three times.","id":"diagram-1lvhk8","sect":3,"part":"Profit or loss, OCI and equity","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:640px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 662.00 181.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(14.4 166.4)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-14.4,14.4 -14.4,-166.4 647.75,-166.4 647.75,14.4 -14.4,14.4\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"nod