\">Cost of sales\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"387.8\" y=\"-9.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"white\">296,000\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge5\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>cogm&#45;&gt;cos\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M340.16,-57.43C349,-52.17 358.8,-46.33 368.04,-40.83\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"369.24,-42.96 374,-37.28 366.73,-38.76 369.24,-42.96\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node6\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>fg\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#f3f4f6\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,2\" d=\"M569.35,-94C569.35,-94 430,-94 430,-94 424,-94 418,-88 418,-82 418,-82 418,-70 418,-70 418,-64 424,-58 430,-58 430,-58 569.35,-58 569.35,-58 575.35,-58 581.35,-64 581.35,-70 581.35,-70 581.35,-82 581.35,-82 581.35,-88 575.35,-94 569.35,-94\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"454.68\" y=\"-76.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#374151\">± Finished goods\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"428.8\" y=\"-67.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#374151\">+ opening 40,000 − closing 35,000\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge6\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>fg&#45;&gt;cos\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M469.88,-57.43C460.86,-52.12 450.84,-46.22 441.43,-40.66\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"442.95,-38.72 435.67,-37.27 440.46,-42.94 442.95,-38.72\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"id":"calc-1kpmqi","type":"calc","bucket":"pl","lo":46,"q":"Kranji Furniture makes tables. Its {a|raw materials} were $20,000 at the start of the year and $25,000 at the end; it bought $150,000 of timber. Direct labour was $90,000, production overheads $60,000, {a|opening WIP} $18,000 and {a|closing WIP} $22,000. What is the cost of goods manufactured?","answer":291000,"unit":"$","working":["Raw materials used = 20,000 + 150,000 − 25,000 = 145,000.","COGM = 145,000 + 90,000 + 60,000 + 18,000 − 22,000 = $291,000."],"sect":3,"part":"Profit or loss, OCI and equity"},{"id":"calc-1d0f1g","type":"calc","bucket":"pl","lo":46,"q":"Kranji Furniture, a table maker: its {a|finished goods} were $40,000 at the start of the year and $35,000 at the end. Using the cost of goods manufactured of $291,000, what is {x|cost of sales}?","answer":296000,"unit":"$","working":["40,000 + 291,000 − 35,000 = $296,000.","{a|Finished goods} fell over the year, so {x|cost of sales} is a little more than what the factory made."],"sect":3,"part":"Profit or loss, OCI and equity"},{"id":"think-1hxi61","type":"think","bucket":"pl","lo":46,"scenario":"Marina Services made a profit of $120,000, revalued its {a|office} upward by $30,000 (in OCI), issued $100,000 of {e|new shares} and paid {e|dividends} of $40,000.","prompt":"Which of these appear in the P&L, and which only in the statement of changes in equity?","answer":["Profit is in P&L, the revaluation is in OCI, and both reach equity through total comprehensive income.","The {e|share issue} and the {e|dividend} are **transactions with owners**. They never touch P&L or OCI: they go straight to the statement of changes in equity."],"sect":3,"part":"Profit or loss, OCI and equity"},{"id":"visual-1oyvmx","type":"visual","bucket":"pl","lo":46,"title":"Marina Services: statement of changes in equity","html":"\u003cp>Marina’s year in equity. One column per component of \u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">equity\u003c/span>, one row per kind of movement: opening, the year’s activity, closing.\u003c/p>\n    \u003cdiv class=\"tbl-wrap\">\u003ctable class=\"tbl num reveal-rows\">\u003cthead>\u003ctr>\u003cth>\u003c/th>\u003cth>\u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">Share capital\u003c/span>\u003c/th>\u003cth>\u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">Retained earnings\u003c/span>\u003c/th>\u003cth>\u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">Revaluation surplus\u003c/span>\u003c/th>\u003cth>Total\u003c/th>\u003c/tr>\u003c/thead>\u003ctbody>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">Opening\u003c/span>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>500,000\u003c/td>\u003ctd>300,000\u003c/td>\u003ctd>50,000\u003c/td>\u003ctd>850,000\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>Profit for the year\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>120,000\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>120,000\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>OCI: revaluation\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>30,000\u003c/td>\u003ctd>30,000\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">Shares issued\u003c/span>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>100,000\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>100,000\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">Dividends\u003c/span>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>(40,000)\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>(40,000)\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003cth scope=\"row\">\u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">Closing\u003c/span>\u003c/th>\u003ctd>\u003cb>600,000\u003c/b>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cb>380,000\u003c/b>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cb>80,000\u003c/b>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cb>1,060,000\u003c/b>\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n    \u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\u003c/div>\n    \u003cp class=\"cap\">Total comprehensive income 150,000 = profit 120,000 + OCI 30,000. OCI goes to \u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">its own reserve\u003c/span>, not to \u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">Retained earnings\u003c/span>.\u003c/p>","sect":3,"part":"Profit or loss, OCI and equity"},{"type":"visual","bucket":"pl","lo":46,"title":"Profit and OCI land in different reserves","html":"\u003cp>The SOCE table as two moving balances. Left: \u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">retained earnings\u003c/span> take the profit and lose the \u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">dividend\u003c/span>. Right: the \u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">revaluation surplus\u003c/span> takes the OCI and nothing else. Same year, two separate reserves.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"wg\" data-wg=\"roll\" data-key=\"eq-d1\" data-cfg=\"{&quot;panels&quot;:[{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;{e|Retained earnings}&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;e&quot;,&quot;bal&quot;:&quot;Retained earnings&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:300000,&quot;startCap&quot;:&quot;{e|Opening retained earnings} {e|300,000}.&quot;,&quot;years&quot;:[{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;The year&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;profit&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;i&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:120000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;+ profit for the year 120,000: {e|420,000}.&quot;},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;dividends&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;e&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-40000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;− {e|dividends} 40,000, straight from equity, never P&amp;L: {e|closing 380,000}.&quot;}]}]},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;{e|Revaluation surplus}&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;e&quot;,&quot;bal&quot;:&quot;Revaluation surplus&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:50000,&quot;startCap&quot;:&quot;{e|Opening revaluation surplus} {e|50,000}.&quot;,&quot;years&quot;:[{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;The year&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;OCI&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;i&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:30000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;+ OCI revaluation gain 30,000: {e|closing 80,000}.&quot;}],&quot;hold&quot;:&quot;No dividends come out of the {e|revaluation surplus}: it stays at {e|80,000}.&quot;}]}],&quot;notes&quot;:{&quot;start&quot;:&quot;Two components of {e|equity}, side by side. Press Play or Next.&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[&quot;Total comprehensive income splits: profit to {e|retained earnings}, OCI to {e|its own reserve}.&quot;,&quot;Transactions with owners ({e|dividends}) go straight through equity.&quot;],&quot;end&quot;:&quot;**OCI is not retained earnings.** Total comprehensive income 150,000 = profit 120,000 + OCI 30,000, but the two halves land in different columns. (The {e|share issue} of 100,000 lands in a third, {e|share capital}.)&quot;}}\">\u003c/div>","id":"visual-eujmiq","sect":3,"part":"Profit or loss, OCI and equity"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"pl","lo":46,"title":"SOCE and the notes","body":["Marina showed that profit and OCI reach equity through total comprehensive income, while owners’ transactions skip the P&L entirely. The SOCE is where all of it meets, and the notes back it up.","- **SOCE:** for each component of equity, opening to closing: profit, OCI, transactions with owners ({e|share issues}, {e|dividends}), and retrospective adjustments.","- **{e|Dividends}** are a distribution to owners: in the SOCE, never an {x|expense} in P&L.","- **Notes, in order:** 1. statement of compliance with SFRS(I); 2. significant accounting policies; 3. supporting detail for each line; 4. other disclosures.","- Also disclose **key judgements** and **sources of estimation uncertainty**.","! OCI is not {e|retained earnings}. A {i|revaluation gain} goes to the {e|revaluation surplus} column."],"id":"rule-y9ttu4","sect":3,"part":"Profit or loss, OCI and equity"},{"id":"mcq-b0vxd0","type":"mcq","bucket":"pl","lo":46,"q":"During the year a company declared and paid a {e|dividend} of $40,000. Where is it presented?","options":[{"t":"As an {x|expense} in profit or loss","why":"{e|Dividends} are distributions to owners, not {x|expenses}."},{"t":"As a deduction in other comprehensive income","why":"OCI is for specific gains and losses, not owner transactions."},{"t":"In the statement of changes in equity, as a reduction of {e|retained earnings}","ok":true,"why":"Transactions with owners go straight through equity."},{"t":"Only in the notes","why":"It changes equity, so it appears in the SOCE (and as a cash outflow in the cash flow statement)."}],"sect":3,"part":"Profit or loss, OCI and equity"},{"type":"map","id":"map-4-sfp","bucket":"sfp","sect":4,"part":"Financial position: current or not"},{"id":"think-1xfh6s","type":"think","bucket":"sfp","lo":46,"scenario":"Lion City Venture’s (LCV’s) {l|bond payable} has sat in {l|non-current liabilities} for years. At 31 December 20X5 it is due for repayment on 31 March 20X6.","prompt":"Is it still non-current? What decides it?","answer":["**Current.** It is due within 12 months of the reporting date, and LCV has no right to defer it.","Same bond, new label: a {l|long-term debt} becomes current in its final year. Nothing about the bond changed except the calendar."],"sect":4,"part":"Financial position: current or not"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"sfp","lo":46,"title":"Current or non-current: the tests","body":["The statement of financial position splits every balance by timing, so users can see what turns into cash soon and what must be paid soon. The bond shows the label can change with nothing but the calendar.","**An {a|asset} is current if any one of these is true:**","1. It will be realised, sold or used in the **normal operating cycle**.","2. It is held mainly **for trading**.","3. It will be realised within **12 months** after the reporting date.","4. It is **{a|cash}** or a {a|cash equivalent}, not restricted for 12+ months.","**A {l|liability} is current if any one of these is true:**","1. It will be settled in the **normal operating cycle**.","2. It is held mainly **for trading**.","3. It is due within **12 months** after the reporting date.","4. The entity has **no right, at the reporting date,** to defer settlement for at least 12 months.","+ Everything else is non-current."],"id":"rule-1vfjww","sect":4,"part":"Financial position: current or not"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"sfp","lo":46,"title":"Current or non-current?","intro":"The chart from your notes (master.pdf): any one “yes” makes it current.","notes":{"a1":"{a|Inventory} and {a|trade receivables} are current even if realised after more than 12 months, because they are part of the operating cycle.","a2":"Held for trading, e.g. {a|FVTPL shares} bought to sell soon. LCV plans to sell its {a|marketable securities} in 20X6, so they are current.","a3":"Realised within 12 months after the reporting date, e.g. a {a|loan receivable} due next year.","a4":"{a|Cash and cash equivalents}, unless restricted from use for at least 12 months.","ac":"Any “yes” above: {a|current asset}.","an":"All “no”: non-current. {a|PPE}, {a|investment property}, {a|intangibles}, {a|long-term financial assets}, {a|deferred tax assets}.","l1":"{l|Trade payables} and {l|accrued operating costs} are current, as part of the operating cycle.","l2":"Held for trading, e.g. {l|derivative liabilities} held for trading.","l3":"Due within 12 months: this year’s {l|loan instalment}, a {l|bond} maturing next March, {l|accrued interest}, {l|tax payable}.","l4":"Even if due within 12 months, it stays non-current only if the entity has a right at the reporting date to defer settlement for 12+ months. A refinancing agreed after year end doesn’t count.","lc":"{l|Current liability}.","ln":"{l|Non-current liability}: {l|long-term borrowings}, the non-current part of {l|lease liabilities}, {l|deferred tax}, {l|long-term provisions}."},"walk":[{"nodes":["a1","a2","a3","a4","ac"],"text":"{a|Assets}: four tests. Any “yes” makes it current."},{"nodes":["an"],"text":"Four “no”s: non-current."},{"nodes":["l1","l2","l3"],"text":"{l|Liabilities}: operating cycle, trading, then due within 12 months?"},{"nodes":["l4","lc","ln"],"text":"Due within 12 months is current unless, at the reporting date, there is a right to defer for 12+ months."}],"caption":"Judge it at the reporting date. What happens after year end can’t rescue a {l|liability}.","id":"diagram-1cixz3","sect":4,"part":"Financial position: current or not","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:640px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 600.00 397.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(14.4 382.4)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-14.4,14.4 