rmation, or a new choice of method","to":"n2"}]},"n1b":{"q":"Which period’s statements contain the mistake?","why":"Only errors in statements already issued are prior period errors. A mistake caught before this year’s statements are authorised is simply corrected.","opts":[{"t":"A prior period whose statements have been issued","to":"err"},{"t":"This period, and the statements are not yet authorised","to":"cur"}]},"n2":{"q":"Does it change the principle, basis or rule (recognition, measurement basis, presentation, cost formula)? Or only an input or technique for an uncertain amount?","why":"A policy is the *rule*; an estimate is a *number* the rule needs. Useful life, residual value, depreciation method and bad debt rates are all inputs or techniques.","opts":[{"t":"The principle, basis or rule changes","to":"n3"},{"t":"Only an input or technique (life, residual, depreciation method, bad debt %)","to":"est"},{"t":"I honestly can’t tell","to":"est"}]},"n3":{"q":"Is the policy for transactions that are new, different in substance from before, or were immaterial before?","why":"Adopting a policy for something you never had to account for is not a *change*: there is nothing to restate.","opts":[{"t":"Yes","to":"notpol"},{"t":"No, the same transactions as before","to":"n4"}]},"n4":{"q":"Is it the first adoption of the revaluation model for {a|PPE} or {a|intangibles}?","why":"This is the one policy change with its own treatment: it is accounted for as a revaluation, not restated.","opts":[{"t":"Yes","to":"reval"},{"t":"No","to":"n5"}]},"n5":{"q":"Is the change required by an SFRS(I), or does it give reliable and more relevant information?","why":"Those are the only two allowed reasons. Consistency matters, so policies don’t change on a whim.","opts":[{"t":"Yes","to":"pol"},{"t":"No: it just gives a nicer profit, or the CFO prefers it","to":"bad"}]},"err":{"result":"Prior period error: retrospective restatement","body":["Restate the comparatives for the period(s) the error happened in. If it began before the earliest period presented, restate the **opening** balances of that earliest period.","- Net of tax. Never through this year’s profit."]},"cur":{"result":"Current-period error: just correct it","body":["Found before the statements are authorised, in the period it happened: correct it in this year’s statements. It is **not** a prior period error, so nothing is restated."]},"est":{"result":"Change in accounting estimate: prospective","body":["Recognise the effect in **profit or loss** of the period of change and future periods. No restatement, no {e|opening retained earnings} adjustment.","- If you can’t tell policy from estimate, the standard says treat it as an **estimate**."]},"notpol":{"result":"Not a change in accounting policy","body":["A policy for transactions that differ in substance from before, are new, or were immaterial before is simply **adopted** going forward. Nothing to restate."]},"reval":{"result":"Policy change, but treated as a revaluation","body":["Switching to the revaluation model for {a|PPE} or {a|intangibles} **is** a change in policy, but it is accounted for as a revaluation under SFRS(I) 1-16 / 1-38 from now on, **not** retrospectively under 1-8."]},"pol":{"result":"Change in accounting policy: retrospective application","body":["Use the standard’s transitional provisions if it has any. Otherwise apply it as if it had **always** applied:","1. adjust the {e|opening balance} of each affected {e|component of equity} for the **earliest prior period presented**","2. restate the comparatives"]},"bad":{"result":"Not allowed: keep the old policy","body":["A policy may change only if a standard requires it or it gives **reliable and more relevant** information. “Higher profit” and “management prefers it” fail both tests."]}},"sect":1,"part":"Policy, estimate or error?","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:640px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 638.00 707.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" 