 Bukit Timah’s crypto tokens), there is a pecking order for where to look.","1. If an SFRS(I) applies to the item, **use it**.","2. If none applies, management uses **judgement** to give information that is **relevant** and **reliable** (faithful, reflecting substance, neutral, prudent and complete).","3. In that judgement, look first at SFRS(I)s on **similar issues**, then at the **Conceptual Framework**.","4. It **may** also consider other standard setters with a similar framework, other literature and accepted industry practice, if consistent with steps 1–3.","- Apply policies **consistently** to similar transactions, unless a standard allows different categories.","+ Hierarchy: **Standard → similar standards → Framework → others (optional).**"],"id":"rule-xpptec","sect":2,"part":"Policy change: retrospective"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"policy","lo":49,"title":"The policy hierarchy as a ladder","intro":"Climb down only as far as you need to. Most items stop at the first rung.","notes":{"s1":"Always the first question. If a standard covers it, there is no choice to make (beyond options the standard itself offers).","use":"Use the standard. Job done.","judge":"No standard? Management must judge, aiming for information that is **relevant** and **reliable**.","sim":"First port of call: standards that deal with **similar or related** issues.","fw":"Then the **Conceptual Framework**: the definitions of {a|assets}, {l|liabilities}, {i|income} and {x|expenses}, and its recognition and measurement concepts.","oth":"Optional, and only if consistent with the rungs above: other standard setters, accounting literature, industry practice.","cons":"Whatever is chosen, apply it **consistently** to similar items."},"walk":[{"nodes":["s1","use"],"text":"If an SFRS(I) applies, **use it**."},{"nodes":["judge"],"text":"If not, management uses **judgement**: relevant and reliable information."},{"nodes":["sim","fw"],"text":"Judgement has a pecking order: **similar standards** first, then the **Framework**."},{"nodes":["oth"],"text":"Other sources **may** be considered, but only if consistent with the rungs above."},{"nodes":["cons"],"text":"Then apply it **consistently**."}],"caption":"Standard → similar standards → Framework → others (optional).","id":"diagram-vickqz","sect":2,"part":"Policy change: retrospective","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:354px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 322.00 395.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 383.94)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-383.94 311.33,-383.94 311.33,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>s1\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#b45309\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M191.9,-373.14C191.9,-373.14 80.88,-373.14 80.88,-373.14 74.88,-373.14 68.87,-367.14 68.87,-361.14 68.87,-361.14 68.87,-349.14 68.87,-349.14 68.87,-343.14 74.87,-337.14 80.87,-337.14 80.87,-337.14 191.9,-337.14 191.9,-337.14 197.9,-337.14 203.9,-343.14 203.9,-349.14 203.9,-349.14 203.9,-361.14 203.9,-361.14 203.9,-367.14 197.9,-373.14 191.9,-373.14\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"77.51\" y=\"-356.69\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Does an SFRS(I) apply\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"107.51\" y=\"-345.69\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">to this item?\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node2\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>use\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#dcfce7\" stroke=\"#166534\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M102.78,-299.89C102.78,-299.89 12,-299.89 12,-299.89 6,-299.89 0,-293.89 0,-287.89 0,-287.89 0,-275.89 0,-275.89 0,-269.89 6,-263.89 12,-263.89 12,-263.89 102.78,-263.89 102