4,-61 609.62,-61 609.62,-61 615.62,-61 621.62,-67 621.62,-73 621.62,-73 621.62,-86.64 621.62,-86.64 621.62,-92.64 615.62,-98.64 609.62,-98.64\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"524.48\" y=\"-84.87\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">SFP 31 Dec 20X4\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"534.61\" y=\"-75.77\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">inventory −4,000\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"532.73\" y=\"-66.77\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">deferred tax −680\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge5\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>cum&#45;&gt;sfp\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" stroke-dasharray=\"1,5\" d=\"M447.48,-59.31C469.22,-63.02 494.02,-67.25 515.43,-70.9\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"481.09\" y=\"-69.26\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> mirrors \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node7\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>cur\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,2\" d=\"M610.37,-38.82C610.37,-38.82 527.09,-38.82 527.09,-38.82 521.09,-38.82 515.09,-32.82 515.09,-26.82 515.09,-26.82 515.09,-14.82 515.09,-14.82 515.09,-8.82 521.09,-2.82 527.09,-2.82 527.09,-2.82 610.37,-2.82 610.37,-2.82 616.37,-2.82 622.37,-8.82 622.37,-14.82 622.37,-14.82 622.37,-26.82 622.37,-26.82 622.37,-32.82 616.37,-38.82 610.37,-38.82\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"540.23\" y=\"-21.37\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#6b7280\">20X5 profit\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"523.73\" y=\"-12.27\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#6b7280\">untouched by the past\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge6\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>cum&#45;&gt;cur\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,2\" d=\"M447.48,-40.64C466.49,-37.51 487.84,-33.99 507.22,-30.8\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"507.46,-32.88 513.04,-29.84 506.78,-28.74 507.46,-32.88\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"481.09\" y=\"-41.17\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> ✗ \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"type":"visual","bucket":"policy","lo":50,"title":"One inventory cut, three layers","html":"\u003cp>Same switch: \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">inventory\u003c/span> is lower under WA by 2,000 at 31 Dec 20X3 and 4,000 at 31 Dec 20X4, tax 17%. The 4,000 that comes off \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">inventory\u003c/span> has to land somewhere. It splits into three layers: the \u003cstrong>\u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">tax effect\u003c/span>\u003c/strong>, the slice for the years \u003cstrong>before\u003c/strong> 20X4 (\u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">opening retained earnings\u003c/span>), and the slice for \u003cstrong>20X4 itself\u003c/strong> (the restated comparative profit).\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"cbars\">\u003cdiv class=\"cb-key\">\u003cspan>\u003ci class=\"seg out out-a\">\u003c/i>\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">inventory removed\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan>\u003ci class=\"seg e\">\u003c/i>\u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">retained earnings\u003c/span> (two slices)\u003c/span>\u003cspan>\u003ci class=\"seg l\">\u003c/i>\u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">deferred tax\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-year\">\u003cdiv class=\"cb-cap\">\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">Inventory\u003c/span> down 4,000 at 31 Dec 20X4\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-track\">\u003ci class=\"seg out out-a\" style=\"width:100.00%\">\u003c/i>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-year\">\u003cdiv class=\"cb-cap\">= \u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">opening RE\u003c/span> 1,660 + \u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">20X4 profit\u003c/span> 1,660 + \u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">deferred tax\u003c/span> 680\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-track\">\u003ci class=\"seg e\" style=\"width:41.50%\">\u003c/i>\u003ci class=\"seg e\" style=\"width:41.50%\">\u003c/i>\u003ci class=\"seg l\" style=\"width:17.00%\">\u003c/i>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\u003cp class=\"cap\">Both \u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">retained earnings\u003c/span> slices are after tax: 2,000 × 83% = 1,660, and (4,000 − 2,000) × 83% = 1,660. 20X5 profit gets no slice at all.\u003c/p>","id":"visual-foql9n","sect":2,"part":"Policy change: retrospective"},{"id":"je-18ivgn","type":"je","bucket":"policy","lo":50,"q":"Your turn. Simei Trading switches from FIFO to weighted average in 20X5 (comparatives 20X4). WA is lower than FIFO by 5,000 at 31 Dec 20X3 and by 8,000 at 31 Dec 20X4. Tax 17%, booked to {l|deferred tax}. Record the adjustment at 1 Jan 20X5.","accounts":["Inventory","Plant and equipment","Accumulated depreciation","Cash","Retained earnings","Revaluation surplus (OCI)","Deferred tax liability","Current tax payable","Cost of sales","Depreciation expense","Repairs expense","Tax expense"],"lines":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Retained earnings","amount":6640},{"side":"Dr","account":"Deferred tax liability","amount":1360},{"side":"Cr","account":"Inventory","amount":8000}],"why":"The cumulative difference at 31 Dec 20X4 is 8,000. {l|Tax effect} 1,360; the rest, 6,640, comes off {e|opening retained earnings}. Nothing goes to 20X5 {x|cost of sales}.","sect":2,"part":"Policy change: retrospective"},{"id":"calc-lusvqs","type":"calc","bucket":"policy","lo":50,"q":"Simei Trading switches from FIFO to weighted average in 20X5 (comparatives 20X4). WA is lower than FIFO by 5,000 at 31 Dec 20X3 and by 8,000 at 31 Dec 20X4. Tax 17%. By how much is {e|retained earnings} at 1 Jan 20X4 (the start of the earliest period presented) reduced in the restated statements?","answer":4150,"unit":"$","working":["Only the years **before** 20X4 count here: the difference at 31 Dec 20X3, 5,000.","After tax at 17%: 5,000 − 850 = **4,150**.","The extra 3,000 belongs to 20X4 and shows up in the restated 20X4 profit instead."],"sect":2,"part":"Policy change: retrospective"},{"id":"mcq-1riyu1","type":"mcq","bucket":"policy","lo":49,"q":"Paya Lebar Pte Ltd has carried its {a|land} at cost. In 20X5 it adopts the revaluation model for the first time. How is the change accounted for?","options":[{"t":"Retrospectively: restate 20X4 and adjust {e|opening retained earnings} at 1 Jan 20X4","why":"This is the exception. First adoption of the revaluation model is not applied retrospectively under 1-8."},{"t":"As a revaluation under SFRS(I) 1-16 from 20X5, with the increase to the {e|revaluation surplus}","ok":true,"why":"It is a change in policy, but it is accounted for as a revaluation under 1-16 from now on, not by restating the past."},{"t":"Prospectively, as a change in accounting estimate","why":"It is a policy change (a different measurement basis), not an estimate. It just has its own treatment."},{"t":"It is not allowed: an entity cannot move away from the cost model","why":"It is allowed if it gives reliable and more relevant information. 1-16 offers both models."}],"sect":2,"part":"Policy change: retrospective"},{"id":"tree-1pcccg","type":"tree","bucket":"policy","lo":49,"title":"Which is it? A new inventory formula","scenario":"Changi Retail has used weighted average for years. Its prices now move sharply, and it switches to FIFO because FIFO gives a {a|closing inventory} figure much closer to current cost: reliable and more relevant information. It is the same stock as before. Tap your way to the answer.","expect":"pol","start":"n1","nodes":{"n1":{"q":"Is it fixing a mistake: reliable information was available but was ignored or misused?","why":"Errors are the only change that is about getting it *wrong*. New information or a new choice is never an error.","opts":[{"t":"Yes, it is a mistake","to":"n1b"},{"t":"No: new information, or a new choice of method","to":"n2"}]},"n1b":{"q":"Which period’s statements contain the mistake?","why":"Only errors in statements already issued are prior period errors. A mistake caught before this year’s statements are authorised is simply corrected.","opts":[{"t":"A prior period whose statements have been issued","to":"err"},{"t":"This period, and the statements are not yet authorised","to":"cur"}]},"n2":{"q":"Does it change the principle, basis or rule (recognition, measurement basis, presentation, cost formula)? Or only an input or technique for an uncertain amount?","why":"A policy is the *rule*; an estimate is a *number* the rule needs. Useful life, residual value, depreciation method and bad debt rates are all inputs or techniques.","opts":[{"t":"The principle, basis or rule changes","to":"n3"},{"t":"Only an input or technique (life, residual, depreciation method, bad debt %)","to":"est"},{"t":"I honestly can’t tell","to":"est"}]},"n3":{"q":"Is the policy for transactions that are new, different in substance from before, or were immaterial before?","why":"Adopting a policy for something you never had to account for is not a *change*: there is nothing to restate.","opts":[{"t":"Yes","to":"notpol"},{"t":"No, the same transactions as before","to":"n4"}]},"n4":{"q":"Is it the first adoption of the revaluation model for {a|PPE} or {a|intangibles}?","why":"This is the one policy change with its own treatment: it is accounted for as a revaluation, not restated.","opts":[{"t":"Yes","to":"reval"},{"t":"No","to":"n5"}]},"n5":{"q":"Is the change required by an SFRS(I), or does it give reliable and more relevant information?","why":"Those are the only two allowed reasons. Consistency matters, so policies don’t change on a whim.","opts":[{"t":"Yes","to":"pol"},{"t":"No: it just gives a nicer profit, or the CFO prefers it","to":"bad"}]},"err":{"result":"Prior period error: retrospective restatement","body":["Restate the comparatives for the period(s) the error happened in. If it began before the earliest period presented, restate the **opening** balances of that earliest period.","- Net of tax. Never through this year’s profit."]},"cur":{"result":"Current-period error: just correct it","body":["Found before the statements are authorised, in the period it happened: correct it in this year’s statements. It is **not** a prior period error, so nothing is restated."]},"est":{"result":"Change in accounting estimate: prospective","body":["Recognise the effect in **profit or loss** of the period of change and future periods. No restatement, no {e|opening retained earnings} adjustment.","- If you can’t tell policy from estimate, the standard says treat it as an **estimate**."]},"notpol":{"result":"Not a change in accounting policy","body":["A policy for transactions that differ in substance from before, are new, or were immaterial before is simply **adopted** going forward. Nothing to restate."]},"reval":{"result":"Policy change, but treated as a revaluation","body":["Switching to the revaluation model for {a|PPE} or {a|intangibles} **is** a change in policy, but it is accounted for as a revaluation under SFRS(I) 1-16 / 1-38 from now on, **not** retrospectively under 1-8."]},"pol":{"result":"Change in accounting policy: retrospective application","body":["Use the standard’s transitional provisions if it has any. Otherwise apply it as if it had **always** applied:","1. adjust the {e|opening balance} of each affected {e|component of equity} for the **earliest prior period presented**","2. restate the comparatives"]},"bad":{"result":"Not allowed: keep the old policy","body":["A policy may change only if a standard requires it or it gives **reliable and more relevant** information. “Higher profit” and “management prefers it” fail both tests."]}},"sect":2,"part":"Policy change: retrospective","svg":"\u003csvg