339.78,-40.32 333.78,-40.32\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"276.39\" y=\"-23.87\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Not allowed: keep the old\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"276.39\" y=\"-11.87\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">policy\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge13\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>n5&#45;&gt;bad\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M221.45,-103.8C233.58,-86.03 249.1,-63.3 260.55,-46.52\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"262.07,-48.02 263.72,-41.89 258.6,-45.66 262.07,-48.02\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"293.33\" y=\"-81.89\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> No: it just gives\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"293.33\" y=\"-70.64\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\">a nicer profit, or\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"293.33\" y=\"-59.39\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\">the CFO prefers it \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"type":"map","id":"map-3-estimate","bucket":"estimate","sect":3,"part":"Estimate change: prospective"},{"id":"think-xk7s57","type":"think","bucket":"estimate","lo":50,"scenario":"A {a|machine} cost $120,000 on 1 Jan 20X1: 10-year life, no residual value, straight-line. On 1 Jan 20X4, an engineer reports that its remaining life is only 4 years, and it will fetch $4,000 as scrap at the end.","prompt":"Were the 20X1–20X3 {x|depreciation} charges wrong? What should 20X4’s charge be?","answer":["They weren’t wrong. They were the best estimate with what was known then. That is why an estimate change **doesn’t restate** anything.","{a|Carrying amount} at 1 Jan 20X4 = 120,000 − 3 × 12,000 = 84,000. Spread what’s left to depreciate over what’s left of the life: (84,000 − 4,000) ÷ 4 = **20,000** a year.","No catch-up for past years. The past keeps its old numbers; the future gets the new ones."],"sect":3,"part":"Estimate change: prospective"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"estimate","lo":50,"title":"Estimate changes: prospective","body":["The machine’s past charges weren’t wrong, so there is nothing to restate. The new estimate simply takes over from the date of change. Here is the rule, and the formula you will use every time.","Recognise the effect of a change in estimate **prospectively**:","1. in **profit or loss** of the period of change, if it affects only that period, or","2. of the period of change **and future periods**, if it affects both (e.g. {x|depreciation}).","- If it changes an {a|asset}, {l|liability} or {e|equity} item, adjust that item’s **{a|carrying amount}** in the period of change.","- **No** restatement of comparatives, **no** {e|opening retained earnings} adjustment.","> {x|New depreciation} = ({a|carrying amount} at date of change − new residual value) ÷ remaining useful life","! Start from the **{a|carrying amount}**, not the {a|original cost}, and divide by the **remaining** life, not the total. No catch-up for the years already gone."],"id":"rule-12n5ir","sect":3,"part":"Estimate change: prospective"},{"type":"visual","bucket":"estimate","lo":50,"title":"What the new depreciation spreads","html":"\u003cp>The formula as bars, for a \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">machine\u003c/span> that cost 120,000 on 1 Jan 20X1 (10-year life, no residual), revised on 1 Jan 20X4 to 4 years left and a residual of 4,000. Two layers: first peel off what is already gone (\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">accumulated depreciation\u003c/span>, a contra account against the asset), then split what is left into the residual you keep and the amount still to depreciate.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"cbars\">\u003cdiv class=\"cb-key\">\u003cspan>\u003ci class=\"seg out out-a\">\u003c/i>\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">gone already (accumulated depreciation)\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan>\u003ci class=\"seg a\">\u003c/i>\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">carrying amount\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan>\u003ci class=\"seg n\">\u003c/i>\u003cspan class=\"el el-n\">residual value\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan>\u003ci class=\"seg x\">\u003c/i>\u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">one year of new depreciation\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-year\">\u003cdiv class=\"cb-cap\">\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">Cost\u003c/span> 120,000 = \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">accumulated depreciation\u003c/span> 36,000 + \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">carrying amount\u003c/span> 84,000\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-track\">\u003ci class=\"seg out out-a\" style=\"width:30.00%\">\u003c/i>\u003ci class=\"seg a\" style=\"width:70.00%\">\u003c/i>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-year\">\u003cdiv class=\"cb-cap\">\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">Carrying amount\u003c/span> 84,000 = residual 4,000 + to depreciate 80,000\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-track\">\u003ci class=\"seg n\" style=\"width:3.33%\">\u003c/i>\u003ci class=\"seg x\" style=\"width:16.67%\">\u003c/i>\u003ci class=\"seg x\" style=\"width:16.67%\">\u003c/i>\u003ci class=\"seg x\" style=\"width:16.67%\">\u003c/i>\u003ci class=\"seg x\" style=\"width:16.67%\">\u003c/i>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-year\">\u003cdiv class=\"cb-cap\">To depreciate 80,000 ÷ 4 years = \u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">20,000\u003c/span> a year (one block each)\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-track\">\u003ci class=\"seg x\" style=\"width:16.67%\">\u003c/i>\u003ci class=\"seg x\" style=\"width:16.67%\">\u003c/i>\u003ci class=\"seg x\" style=\"width:16.67%\">\u003c/i>\u003ci class=\"seg x\" style=\"width:16.67%\">\u003c/i>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\u003cp class=\"cap\">The years already gone stay gone: they are never re-spread. Only the remaining blocks are charged, one per remaining year.\u003c/p>","id":"visual-1too4k","sect":3,"part":"Estimate change: prospective"},{"id":"worked-1m5zzk","type":"worked","bucket":"estimate","lo":50,"title":"Worked example: revised useful life and residual value","q":"{a|Machine} cost $120,000 on 1 Jan 20X1, 10-year life, no residual. On 1 Jan 20X4 the remaining life is revised to 4 years and the residual value to $4,000.","intro":["A typical exam question: an asset’s cost, life and residual, then a revised life or residual at some date; give the new {x|depreciation} or the entry. Remember two things:","- Start from the **{a|carrying amount}** at the date of change, not the {a|cost}.","- Spread it over the **remaining** life, down to the **new** residual. No catch-up for the years already gone.","Then follow these steps: old depreciation → carrying amount at the change → new depreciation → entry."],"steps":[{"h":"Work out the old depreciation.","t":"{a|120,000} ÷ 10 = **{x|12,000}** a year, charged for 20X1, 20X2 and 20X3."},{"h":"Find the carrying amount at the date of change.","t":"{a|Carrying amount at 1 Jan 20X4} = {a|120,000} − 3 × {x|12,000} = **{a|84,000}**."},{"h":"Calculate the new depreciation.","t":"({a|84,000} − residual 4,000) ÷ 4 remaining years = **{x|20,000}** a year from 20X4."},{"h":"Record the 20X4 depreciation.","je":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Depreciation expense","amount":20000,"el":"x"},{"side":"Cr","account":"Accumulated depreciation","amount":20000,"el":"a"}],"after":"Check: after 4 years at {x|20,000}, the {a|carrying amount} is {a|4,000}, exactly the new residual. Nothing is done to 20X1–20X3; the change is disclosed."}],"sect":3,"part":"Estimate change: prospective"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"estimate","lo":50,"title":"The machine on a timeline","intro":"The worked example as a timeline. The past is frozen; the change only bends the line from the date of change.","notes":{"past":"120,000 ÷ 10 = 12,000 a year. These {x|depreciation} charges stay exactly as reported.","chg":"The date of change. {a|Carrying amount} 120,000 − 36,000 = 84,000: this is the new starting point.","fut":"(84,000 − 4,000) ÷ 4 = 20,000 a year, to {x|Depreciation expense} in profit or loss.","end":"The {a|machine} lands exactly on its new residual value.","norestate":"The old estimate was reasonable when it was made, so the past isn’t touched."},"walk":[{"nodes":["past"],"text":"20X1–20X3: 12,000 a year of {x|depreciation} on the old estimate."},{"nodes":["norestate"],"text":"Those years are **not** restated. Nothing was wrong with them."},{"nodes":["chg"],"text":"1 Jan 20X4: start again from the **{a|carrying amount}**, 84,000."},{"nodes":["fut","end"],"text":"Spread 84,000 − 4,000 over the **remaining** 4 years: 20,000 a year, landing on the residual."}],"caption":"Prospective: new estimate from the date of change onwards.","id":"diagram-byktvx","sect":3,"part":"Estimate change: prospective","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:640px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 643.00 140.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 129.62)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-129.62 632.42,-129.62 632.42,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>past\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e8eef6\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M111.78,-118.82C111.78,-118.82 52.5,-118.82 52.5,-118.82 46.5,-118.82 40.5,-112.82 40.5,-106.82 40.5,-106.82 40.5,-91.18 40.5,-91.18 40.5,-85.18 46.5,-79.18 52.5,-79.18 52.5,-79.18 111.78,-79.18 111.78,-79.18 117.78,-79.18 123.78,-85.18 123.78,-91.18 123.78,-91.18 123.78,-106.82 123.78,-106.82 123.78,-112.82 117.78,-118.82 111.78,-118.82\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"53.64\" y=\"-105.05\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">20X1–20X3\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"49.14\" y=\"-94.05\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">12,000 a year\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"57.39\" y=\"-84.95\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">old estimate\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node2\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>chg\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M381.81,-118.82C381.81,-118.82 281.28,-118.82 281.28,-118.82 275.28,-118.82 269.28,-112.82 269.28,-106.82 269.28,-106.82 269.28,-91.18 269.28,-91.18 269.28,-85.18 275.28,-79.18 281.28,-79.18 281.28,-79.18 381.81,-79.18 381.81,-79.18 387.81,-79.18 393.81,-85.18 393.81,-91.18 393.81,-91.18 393.81,-106.82 393.81,-106.82 393.81,-112.82 387.81,-118.82 381.81,-118.82\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"303.42\" y=\"-105.05\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"white\">1 Jan 20X4\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"306.05\" y=\"-94.05\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"white\">CA 84,000\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"277.92\" y=\"-84.95\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"white\">4 years left, residual 4,000\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge1\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>past&#45;&gt;chg\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M124.27,-99C161.63,-99 217.47,-99 261.64,-99\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"261.38,-101.1 267.38,-99 261.38,-96.9 261.38,-101.1\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"216.78\" y=\"-100.75\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> new information \u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node5\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>norestate\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,2\" d=\"M152.28,-36C152.28,-36 12,-36 12,-36 6,-36 0,-30 0,-24 0,-24 0,-12 0,-12 0,-6 6,0 12,0 12,0 152.28,0 152.28,0 158.28,0 164.28,-6 164.28,-12 164.28,-12 164.28,-24 164.28,-24 164.28,-30 158.28,-36 152.28,-36\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"42.01\" y=\"-18.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#6b7280\">No restatement\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"8.64\" y=\"-9.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#6b7280\">no catch&#45;up, no opening RE change\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge4\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>past&#45;&gt;norestate\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,2\" d=\"M82.14,-78.93C82.14,-64.74 82.14,-50.55 82.14,-36.35\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node3\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>fut\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e6f4f1\" stroke=\"#0f766e\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M496.09,-118.82C496.09,-118.82 436.81,-118.82 436.81,-118.82 430.81,-118.82 424.81,-112.82 424.81,-106.82 424.81,-106.82 424.81,-91.18 424.81,-91.18 424.81,-85.18 430.81,-79.18 436.81,-79.18 436.81,-79.18 496.09,-79.18 496.09,-79.18 502.09,-79.18 508.09,-85.18 508.09,-91.18 508.09,-91.18 508.09,-106.82 508.09,-106.82 508.09,-112.82 502.09,-118.82 496.09,-118.82\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"437.95\" y=\"-105.05\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">20X4–20X7\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"433.45\" y=\"-94.05\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">20,000 a year\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"439.45\" y=\"-84.95\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">new estimate\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge2\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>chg&#45;&gt;fut\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M394.33,-99C401.95,-99 409.66,-99 417.05,-99\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"416.8,-101.1 422.8,-99 416.8,-96.9 416.8,-101.1\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node4\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>end\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e8eef6\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M609.62,-118.82C609.62,-118.82 551.09,-118.82 551.09,-118.82 545.09,-118.82 539.09,-112.82 539.09,-106.82 539.09,-106.82 539.09,-91.18 539.09,-91.18 539.09,-85.18 545.09,-79.18 551.09,-79.18 551.09,-79.18 609.62,-79.18 609.62,-79.18 615.62,-79.18 621.62,-85.18 621.62,-91.18 621.62,-91.18 621.62,-106.82 621.62,-106.82 621.62,-112.82 615.62,-118.82 609.62,-118.82\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"548.48\" y=\"-105.05\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">31 Dec 20X7\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"557.86\" y=\"-94.05\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">CA 4,000\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"547.73\" y=\"-84.95\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">= residual value\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge3\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>fut&#45;&gt;end\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M508.48,-99C515.88,-99 523.64,-99 531.21,-99\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"531.19,-101.1 537.19,-99 531.19,-96.9 531.19,-101.1\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"type":"visual","bucket":"estimate","lo":50,"title":"The revision, step by step","html":"\u003cp>The same \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">machine\u003c/span> (cost 120,000, 10-year life, no residual), followed from 1 Jan 20X3 in two versions: the old estimate kept, and the estimate revised on 1 Jan 20X4 to 4 years left and a residual of 4,000. Step through and watch where the lines split.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"wg\" data-wg=\"roll\" data-key=\"est-e1\" data-cfg=\"{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;v&quot;:4000,&quot;label&quot;:&quot;new residual 4,000&quot;},&quot;panels&quot;:[{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Old estimate kept&quot;,&quot;sub&quot;:&quot;10-year life, no residual&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;bal&quot;:&quot;Carrying amount&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:96000,&quot;startCap&quot;:&quot;1 Jan 20X3: {a|cost 120,000} − 2 years × {x|12,000} = {a|96,000}.&quot;,&quot;years&quot;:[{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X3&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-12000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;20X3: {x|depreciation} 120,000 ÷ 10 = {x|12,000}, so {a|closing carrying amount} {a|84,000}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X4&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-12000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;20X4: {x|depreciation} 120,000 ÷ 10 = {x|12,000}, so {a|closing carrying amount} {a|72,000}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X5&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-12000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;20X5: {x|depreciation} 120,000 ÷ 10 = {x|12,000}, so {a|closing carrying amount} {a|60,000}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X6&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-12000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;20X6: {x|depreciation} 120,000 ÷ 10 = {x|12,000}, so {a|closing carrying amount} {a|48,000}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X7&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-12000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;20X7: {x|depreciation} 120,000 ÷ 10 = {x|12,000}, so {a|closing carrying amount} {a|36,000}. Under the old estimate there would still be 3 years to go.&quot;}]}]},{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Revised on 1 Jan 20X4&quot;,&quot;sub&quot;:&quot;4 years left, residual 4,000&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;a&quot;,&quot;bal&quot;:&quot;Carrying amount&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:96000,&quot;startCap&quot;:&quot;1 Jan 20X3: {a|cost 120,000} − 2 years × {x|12,000} = {a|96,000}.&quot;,&quot;years&quot;:[{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X3&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-12000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;20X3: {x|depreciation} 120,000 ÷ 10 = {x|12,000}, so {a|closing carrying amount} {a|84,000}. Still the old estimate: it was the best one at the time.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X4&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-20000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;New information: ({a|84,000} − residual 4,000) ÷ 4 = {x|20,000} a year. {a|Closing} {a|64,000}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X5&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-20000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;20X5: {x|20,000} again, {a|closing} {a|44,000}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X6&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-20000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;20X6: {x|20,000} again, {a|closing} {a|24,000}.&quot;}]},{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;20X7&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;depreciation&quot;,&quot;el&quot;:&quot;x&quot;,&quot;v&quot;:-20000,&quot;cap&quot;:&quot;20X7: {x|20,000} again, {a|closing} {a|4,000}. It lands exactly on the new residual.&quot;}]}]}],&quot;notes&quot;:{&quot;start&quot;:&quot;Same {a|machine}, two stories. Left: nobody revises anything. Right: on 1 Jan 20X4 an engineer says only 4 years are left, with a scrap value of 4,000. Press Play or Next.&quot;,&quot;parts&quot;:[&quot;Each step is one year’s {x|depreciation}, leaving the {a|carrying amount}.&quot;],&quot;end&quot;:&quot;**Prospective.** 20X3 is identical in both panels: the past is never restated, and there is no catch-up. From 1 Jan 20X4 the right-hand line just bends steeper ({x|20,000} instead of {x|12,000} a year) and lands on the new residual, {a|4,000}, at 31 Dec 20X7.&quot;}}\">\u003c/div>","id":"visual-1a4ohi","sect":3,"part":"Estimate change: prospective"},{"id":"calc-nkmraf","type":"calc","bucket":"estimate","lo":50,"q":"Now with the first steps shown. A {a|machine} cost $250,000 on 1 Jan 20X1: 8-year life, residual value $10,000, straight-line. On 1 Jan 20X4 the remaining life is revised to 3 years and the residual value to $16,000. What is the {x|depreciation} for 20X4?","answer":48000,"unit":"$","given":2,"working":["Old {x|depreciation}: (250,000 − 10,000) ÷ 8 = 30,000 a year.","{a|Carrying amount} at 1 Jan 20X4: 250,000 − 3 × 30,000 = 160,000.","New {x|depreciation}: (160,000 − 16,000) ÷ 3 = **48,000**."],"sect":3,"part":"Estimate change: prospective"},{"id":"calc-115eh9","type":"calc","bucket":"estimate","lo":50,"q":"A blank one. {a|Equipment} cost $600,000 on 1 Jan 20X1, 12-year life, no residual value, straight-line. On 1 Jan 20X5 management concludes it will last another 10 years (residual still nil). What is the {x|depreciation} for 20X5?","answer":40000,"unit":"$","working":["Old {x|depreciation}: 600,000 ÷ 12 = 50,000 a year, for 4 years (20X1–20X4).","{a|Carrying amount} at 1 Jan 20X5: 600,000 − 200,000 = 400,000.","New {x|depreciation}: 400,000 ÷ 10 = **40,000**. A longer life means a lower charge from now on, and no reversal of past {x|depreciation}."],"sect":3,"part":"Estimate change: prospective"},{"id":"think-k4e644","type":"think","bucket":"estimate","lo":50,"scenario":"At 31 Dec 20X6, a distributor’s {a|receivables} are $900,000. Its {a|allowance for doubtful debts} has been 2%. News of a downturn in its customers’ industry leads it to raise the {a|allowance} to 5%.","prompt":"Does the extra {a|allowance} belong to 20X6, or should it be pushed back into earlier years?","answer":["It is a change in **estimate**, triggered by new information. The whole increase, 45,000 − 18,000 = 27,000, goes to **20X6 profit or loss**, and the {a|allowance} is adjusted in 20X6.","Earlier years are not touched. The downturn is news this year, not a mistake last year."],"sect":3,"part":"Estimate change: prospective"},{"type":"mcq","bucket":"estimate","lo":50,"q":"Which statement about a change in accounting estimate is correct?","options":[{"t":"Comparatives are restated so the new estimate applies to all periods presented","why":"That is retrospective treatment, used for policies and errors, not estimates."},{"t":"The cumulative effect on prior years is taken to {e|opening retained earnings}","why":"Estimates are never pushed back into {e|retained earnings}."},{"t":"The effect is recognised in profit or loss of the period of change, and of future periods if they are affected","ok":true,"why":"Prospective: the period of change and, where relevant, future periods."},{"t":"It is treated as a prior period error if the old estimate turns out to be different from the outcome","why":"An estimate that later proves inaccurate is not an error, as long as it used the information available at the time."}],"id":"mcq-1e6gjq","sect":3,"part":"Estimate change: prospective"},{"type":"map","id":"map-4-error","bucket":"error","sect":4,"part":"Prior period error: restate"},{"id":"think-1a0hmm","type":"think","bucket":"error","lo":50,"scenario":"While preparing its 20X5 statements, a company finds that 20X4 {x|depreciation} of $10,000 was never recorded. The 20X4 statements have already been issued. Tax is 17%.","prompt":"Why not just charge the 10,000 in 20X5 and move on?","answer":["Because then **both** years are wrong: 20X4 profit stays overstated, and 20X5 profit gets an {x|expense} that doesn’t belong to it. Users comparing the two years would be misled twice.","So the error is fixed in the period it belongs to: **restate 20X4**. {x|Depreciation} up 10,000, {x|tax} down 1,700, profit down **8,300**.","In the 20X5 books, the fix runs through **{e|opening retained earnings}**, not this year’s profit."],"sect":4,"part":"Prior period error: restate"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"error","lo":50,"title":"Prior period errors: retrospective restatement","body":["Charging the missed {x|depreciation} in 20X5 would leave both years wrong. So errors go back in time like policy changes, under their own name: **restatement**. First, what counts as an error.","A **prior period error** is an omission or misstatement in earlier statements because reliable information that was available (and could reasonably have been obtained) was ignored or misused.","- Examples: arithmetic mistakes, misapplying a policy or standard, oversights, misreading facts, **fraud**.","Correct it by **retrospective restatement**:","1. restate the comparatives for the prior period(s) in which the error happened;","2. if it happened **before** the earliest period presented, restate the {a|**opening** assets}, {l|liabilities} and {e|equity} of that earliest period.","- Errors found in the **current** period, before the statements are authorised, are simply corrected in the current statements. They are **not** prior period errors.","- **Third statement of financial position** at the start of the preceding period if that date is **materially** affected.","! Don’t correct a prior period error through this year’s profit, and don’t forget the **tax effect**."],"id":"rule-17g3la","sect":4,"part":"Prior period error: restate"},{"id":"visual-lfrfll","type":"visual","bucket":"error","lo":50,"title":"Restating the 20X4 comparatives","html":"\u003cp>Back to the missed 20X4 \u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">depreciation\u003c/span> of 10,000. This is what the restated comparative column looks like, line by line: the \u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">expense\u003c/span> goes in, the \u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">tax\u003c/span> comes down, and the balance sheet follows.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"tbl-wrap\">\u003ctable class=\"tbl num reveal-rows\">\u003cthead>\u003ctr>\u003cth>20X4 comparative\u003c/th>\u003cth>As reported\u003c/th>\u003cth>Correction\u003c/th>\u003cth>Restated\u003c/th>\u003c/tr>\u003c/thead>\u003ctbody>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>Profit before tax\u003c/td>\u003ctd>200,000\u003c/td>\u003ctd>(10,000)\u003c/td>\u003ctd>190,000\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">Tax expense\u003c/span> (17%)\u003c/td>\u003ctd>(34,000)\u003c/td>\u003ctd>1,700\u003c/td>\u003ctd>(32,300)\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003cb>Profit for the year\u003c/b>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cb>166,000\u003c/b>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cb>(8,300)\u003c/b>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cb>157,700\u003c/b>\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">PPE\u003c/span>, 31 Dec 20X4\u003c/td>\u003ctd>400,000\u003c/td>\u003ctd>(10,000)\u003c/td>\u003ctd>390,000\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">Retained earnings\u003c/span>, 31 Dec 20X4\u003c/td>\u003ctd>500,000\u003c/td>\u003ctd>(8,300)\u003c/td>\u003ctd>491,700\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n    \u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\u003c/div>\u003cp class=\"cap\">The missed \u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">depreciation\u003c/span> of 10,000 costs only 8,300 of profit, because \u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">tax\u003c/span> falls by 1,700. The error began in 20X4, so the 1 Jan 20X4 balances are untouched and no third statement of financial position is needed for it.\u003c/p>","sect":4,"part":"Prior period error: restate"},{"id":"je-sxm3tc","type":"je","bucket":"error","lo":50,"q":"While preparing its 20X5 statements, a company finds that 20X4 {x|depreciation} of $10,000 was never recorded; the 20X4 statements have already been issued. Record the correction in the 20X5 books (tax 17%, booked to {l|deferred tax}, as in your notes).","accounts":["Inventory","Plant and equipment","Accumulated depreciation","Cash","Retained earnings","Revaluation surplus (OCI)","Deferred tax liability","Current tax payable","Cost of sales","Depreciation expense","Repairs expense","Tax expense"],"lines":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Retained earnings","amount":8300},{"side":"Dr","account":"Deferred tax liability","amount":1700},{"side":"Cr","account":"Accumulated depreciation","amount":10000}],"why":"{a|Accumulated depreciation} is put right (10,000). The 20X4 profit effect, net of tax, comes off **{e|opening retained earnings}** (8,300), not 20X5 {x|depreciation expense}. The {l|tax effect} is 1,700.","sect":4,"part":"Prior period error: restate"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"error","lo":50,"title":"When did the error happen?","intro":"The answer decides what gets restated. Statements for 20X5, comparatives for 20X4.","notes":{"start":"Found while the 20X5 statements are being prepared, before they are authorised.","q":"The period the error **belongs to** decides the treatment, not the period it was found in.","cur":"A current-period error is not a prior period error. Just fix it before the statements go out.","cmp":"Restate the 20X4 comparatives. In the books, the fix goes through {e|opening retained earnings} at 1 Jan 20X5.","early":"The error is older than anything presented, so it lands in the **opening** balances of the earliest period presented: 1 Jan 20X4.","sfp":"A balance sheet at the start of the preceding period, when the restatement materially affects it.","tax":"Restate the {l|tax effect} too. The after-tax amount hits {e|retained earnings}."},"walk":[{"nodes":["start","q"],"text":"Ask which period the error **belongs** to."},{"nodes":["cur"],"text":"This year, and the statements aren’t out yet → just **correct it**. Not a prior period error."},{"nodes":["cmp"],"text":"Last year → **restate the comparatives**."},{"nodes":["early","sfp"],"text":"Before last year → restate the **opening balances** of the earliest period, and present a **third SFP** if material."},{"nodes":["tax"],"text":"Either way: **net of tax**, and never through this year’s profit."}],"caption":"The period the error belongs to decides what is restated.","id":"diagram-e36j1v","sect":4,"part":"Prior period error: restate","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:536px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 487.00 258.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 247.69)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-247.69 476.08,-247.69 476.08,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>start\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M305.78,-236.89C305.78,-236.89 167,-236.89 167,-236.89 161,-236.89 155,-230.89 155,-224.89 155,-224.89 155,-212.89 155,-212.89 155,-206.89 161,-200.89 167,-200.89 167,-200.89 305.78,-200.89 305.78,-200.89 311.78,-200.89 317.78,-206.89 317.78,-212.89 317.78,-212.89 317.78,-224.89 317.78,-224.89 317.78,-230.89 311.78,-236.89 305.78,-236.89\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"163.64\" y=\"-220.44\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"white\">Error found while preparing\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"186.89\" y=\"-209.44\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"white\">the 20X5 statements\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node2\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>q\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#b45309\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M316.65,-173.89C316.65,-173.89 156.12,-173.89 156.12,-173.89 150.12,-173.89 144.12,-167.89 144.12,-161.89 144.12,-161.89 144.12,-149.89 144.12,-149.89 144.12,-143