art\" x=\"345.32\" y=\"-152.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Non&#45;adjusting\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"344.57\" y=\"-143.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">disclose if material\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge6\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>b2&#45;&gt;b3\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M288.8,-152C301.33,-152 315.01,-152 327.91,-152\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"327.89,-154.1 333.89,-152 327.89,-149.9 327.89,-154.1\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"adjusting","lo":52,"title":"The usual adjusting events","body":["One test is enough in theory, but the exam leans on a short list of classic cases. Here are the adjusting ones: each is new evidence about something already true at year end.","Six families to know by heart:","1. A **court case settles** after year end, confirming an obligation that existed at year end → adjust (or recognise) the {l|Provision for legal claim}.","2. A **customer goes bankrupt** → usually shows the {a|Trade receivables} were already impaired at year end.","3. Year-end **{a|inventory} is sold below cost** → evidence of its NRV at the reporting date.","4. The **cost** of an {a|asset} bought, or the **proceeds** of an {a|asset} sold, **before** year end is finalised. e.g. a machine bought in December at a provisional $200,000, final invoice $207,500 → add $7,500 to its {a|cost}.","5. **Bonus or profit-share** amounts are determined, for an obligation that existed at year end. e.g. a 2% bonus pool on profit of $3,500,000 → accrue a {l|bonus liability} of $70,000.","6. **Fraud or errors** are discovered that show the FS are wrong.","+ Every one of them is new **information** about something that was already true at the reporting date."],"id":"rule-dpixjs","sect":2,"part":"Adjusting events"},{"type":"tree","bucket":"adjusting","lo":52,"title":"Classify it: the customer’s bankruptcy","scenario":"Year end 31 Dec 20X5; FS authorised 15 Mar 20X6. On 20 Feb 20X6 a customer that owed $40,000 at year end is declared bankrupt after months of losses and late payments. Tap your way to the answer.","expect":"adj","start":"w","nodes":{"w":{"q":"When did the event happen?","why":"SFRS(I) 1-10 only covers events between the reporting date and the date the FS are authorised for issue.","opts":[{"t":"Between the reporting date and authorisation","to":"gc"},{"t":"After the FS were authorised for issue","to":"late"},{"t":"On or before the reporting date","to":"early"}]},"gc":{"q":"Does it mean management intends to liquidate or stop trading, or has no realistic alternative?","why":"Going concern is checked first: if it fails, the whole basis of the FS changes and everything else is secondary.","opts":[{"t":"Yes","to":"nogc"},{"t":"No","to":"dv"}]},"dv":{"q":"Is it a dividend declared to shareholders after the reporting date?","why":"Dividends have their own rule: no obligation existed at the reporting date, however much the profits “belong” to that year.","opts":[{"t":"Yes","to":"div"},{"t":"No","to":"cond"}]},"cond":{"q":"Does it give evidence of a condition that already existed at the reporting date?","why":"This is the heart of the standard: the timing of the **condition**, not of the event, decides.","opts":[{"t":"Yes: it was already true at year end, we just found out later","to":"adj"},{"t":"No: the condition arose after year end","to":"mat"}]},"mat":{"q":"Is it material?","why":"Non-adjusting events never change the numbers. Materiality only decides whether the notes must mention it.","opts":[{"t":"Yes","to":"nonD"},{"t":"No","to":"nonN"}]},"late":{"result":"Outside these FS","body":["Once the FS are authorised for issue, the window has closed. The event is dealt with in **next year’s** FS."]},"early":{"result":"Not an event after the reporting period","body":["It happened during the year, so it is an ordinary transaction of that year: record it in the normal way."]},"nogc":{"result":"Don’t use the going concern basis","body":["The one post-year-end event that changes the **whole basis** of the FS, not just one balance.","- Disclose that the FS are not on a going concern basis, the basis used, and why."]},"div":{"result":"Not a liability: disclose in the notes","body":["No obligation existed at the reporting date, so there is no {l|Dividend payable} and no {x|expense}.","- Disclose the dividend in the notes. It becomes a {l|liability} in the year it is declared."]},"adj":{"result":"Adjusting event: change the amounts","body":["The event is better evidence about a balance that existed at the reporting date, so update that balance.","- e.g. impair the {a|receivable}, write {a|inventory} down to NRV, adjust the {l|provision}."]},"nonD":{"result":"Non-adjusting: disclose, don’t adjust","body":["Leave the year-end amounts alone. In the notes give the event’s **nature** and an **estimate of its financial effect** (or say that no estimate can be made)."]},"nonN":{"result":"Non-adjusting and immaterial: nothing needed","body":["No adjustment, and too small to need a note."]}},"id":"tree-1amtta","sect":2,"part":"Adjusting events","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:640px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 707.00 530.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 519.22)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-519.22 696.2,-519.22 696.2,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>w\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#b45309\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M561.28,-508.42C561.28,-508.42 430,-508.42 430,-508.42 424,-508.42 418,-502.42 418,-496.42 418,-496.42 418,-484.42 418,-484.42 418,