ld\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">20X5 profit\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"305.58\" y=\"-72.37\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">−71,000\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge4\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>b1&#45;&gt;pl\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M241.09,-124.88C254.12,-118.15 268.9,-110.52 282.35,-103.57\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"283.12,-105.53 287.49,-100.91 281.19,-101.8 283.12,-105.53\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge5\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>b2&#45;&gt;pl\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M256.72,-81.82C264.75,-81.82 272.96,-81.82 280.78,-81.82\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"280.31,-83.92 286.31,-81.82 280.31,-79.72 280.31,-83.92\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge6\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>b3&#45;&gt;pl\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" d=\"M243.72,-40.12C256.07,-46.5 269.74,-53.56 282.27,-60.03\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"281.07,-61.78 287.37,-62.66 283,-58.05 281.07,-61.78\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"type":"visual","bucket":"adjusting","lo":52,"title":"What each adjustment does to its balance","html":"\u003cp>The same three adjustments, drawn as bars. Two balances shrink: the \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">receivable\u003c/span> is reduced by an \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">allowance\u003c/span> (a contra account that sits against it, so it takes the asset’s colour), and the \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">inventory\u003c/span> is written down to NRV. One grows: the \u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">provision\u003c/span> is topped up to the settlement. Each hatched or extra piece is a 20X5 \u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">expense\u003c/span>.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"cbars\">\n    \u003cdiv class=\"cb-year\">\u003cdiv class=\"cb-cap\">\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">Trade receivables\u003c/span> 40,000 − \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">allowance\u003c/span> 36,000 = \u003cstrong>\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">net 4,000\u003c/span>\u003c/strong>\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-track\">\u003cspan class=\"seg a\" style=\"width:5.00%\">\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"seg out-a\" style=\"width:45.00%\">\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\n    \u003cdiv class=\"cb-year\">\u003cdiv class=\"cb-cap\">\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">Inventory\u003c/span> at cost 25,000 − \u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">write-down\u003c/span> 5,000 = \u003cstrong>\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">NRV 20,000\u003c/span>\u003c/strong>\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-track\">\u003cspan class=\"seg a\" style=\"width:25.00%\">\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"seg out-x\" style=\"width:6.25%\">\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\n    \u003cdiv class=\"cb-year\">\u003cdiv class=\"cb-cap\">\u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">Provision\u003c/span> 50,000 + \u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">extra legal expense\u003c/span> 30,000 = \u003cstrong>\u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">80,000\u003c/span>\u003c/strong>\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"cb-track\">\u003cspan class=\"seg l\" style=\"width:62.50%\">\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"seg x\" style=\"width:37.50%\">\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\n    \u003cdiv class=\"cb-key\">\u003cspan>\u003ci class=\"seg a\">\u003c/i>\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">what the asset is really worth\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan>\u003ci class=\"seg out-a\">\u003c/i>\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">Allowance for doubtful debts\u003c/span> (contra account)\u003c/span>\u003cspan>\u003ci class=\"seg out-x\">\u003c/i>\u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">write-down\u003c/span>: leaves the asset\u003c/span>\u003cspan>\u003ci class=\"seg l\">\u003c/i>\u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">year-end provision\u003c/span>\u003c/span>\u003cspan>\u003ci class=\"seg x\">\u003c/i>\u003cspan class=\"el el-x\">top-up\u003c/span>: added to the liability\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\n  \u003c/div>\n    \u003cp class=\"cap\">Hatched = leaves the asset. Total hit to 20X5 profit: 36,000 + 5,000 + 30,000 = \u003cstrong>71,000\u003c/strong>.\u003c/p>","id":"visual-1mma3r","sect":2,"part":"Adjusting events"},{"id":"mcq-iwj28e","type":"mcq","bucket":"adjusting","lo":52,"q":"While finalising the 20X5 FS in January 20X6, before they are authorised, the accountant finds that a $12,000 {l|tax payable} had been posted to {e|Share capital} in error. What should be done?","options":[{"t":"Nothing in 20X5: it was found after year end, so correct it in 20X6","why":"Discovering an error before authorisation is an **adjusting** event: the FS were wrong at year end."},{"t":"Correct it in the 20X5 FS: Dr {e|Share capital} 12,000, Cr {l|Tax payable} 12,000","ok":true,"why":"The discovery of an error that shows the FS are incorrect is adjusting. Move the amount back to where it belongs."},{"t":"Disclose it as a non-adjusting event","why":"The FS were wrong at the reporting date, so this is adjusting: fix the numbers."},{"t":"Correct it in the 20X5 FS: Dr {l|Tax payable} 12,000, Cr {e|Share capital} 12,000","why":"Backwards. {e|Share capital} is overstated and {l|tax payable} understated, so debit share capital and credit tax payable."}],"sect":2,"part":"Adjusting events"},{"type":"map","id":"map-3-nonadj","bucket":"nonadj","sect":3,"part":"Non-adjusting events"},{"id":"think-zuuf55","type":"think","bucket":"nonadj","lo":52,"scenario":"Year end 31 Dec 20X5. In February 20X6 the stock market falls sharply and the company’s {a|listed investments} (carried at fair value) drop by 30%. The same month it announces a plan to close a factory.","prompt":"Both make the company look worse. Should either be reflected in the 31 December numbers?","answer":["Neither. The fair value at 31 December was the price **on 31 December**. The February fall reflects conditions that arose **after** year end.","The closure was only **announced** after year end, so there was no {l|obligation} at 31 December to provide for.","Both are **non-adjusting**: leave the numbers alone, and disclose them if material."],"sect":3,"part":"Non-adjusting events"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"nonadj","lo":52,"title":"The usual non-adjusting events","body":["Now the other side of the test: news about conditions that arose **after** year end. These classics leave the numbers alone.","- A **fall in the market value** of {a|investments} after year end","- A **fire or flood** that destroys a {a|plant} or {a|inventory}","- A **major acquisition**, or the disposal of a subsidiary","- A **restructuring** announced after year end (no obligation existed at year end)","- A **large share issue** or share buy-back","- **Tax rates or laws changed** after year end: current and deferred tax keep using the rates enacted (or substantively enacted) at year end; disclose the change","- **Dividends** declared for the year just ended (their own step next)","! A non-adjusting event is **never** booked in this year’s numbers, however huge it is. Size only decides whether it is **disclosed**. The one exception is going concern."],"id":"rule-16sf28","sect":3,"part":"Non-adjusting events"},{"id":"tree-2okcin","type":"tree","bucket":"nonadj","lo":52,"title":"Classify it: the warehouse fire","scenario":"Year end 31 Dec 20X5; FS authorised 15 Mar 20X6. On 3 Feb 20X6 a fire destroys the Jurong warehouse and {a|inventory} with a {a|carrying amount} of $1.2 million. The amount is material. Tap your way to the answer.","expect":"nonD","start":"w","nodes":{"w":{"q":"When did the event happen?","why":"SFRS(I) 1-10 only covers events between the reporting date and the date the FS are authorised for issue.","opts":[{"t":"Between the reporting date and authorisation","to":"gc"},{"t":"After the FS were authorised for issue","to":"late"},{"t":"On or before the reporting date","to":"early"}]},"gc":{"q":"Does it mean management intends to liquidate or stop trading, or has no realistic alternative?","why":"Going concern is checked first: if it fails, the whole basis of the FS changes and everything else is secondary.","opts":[{"t":"Yes","to":"nogc"},{"t":"No","to":"dv"}]},"dv":{"q":"Is it a dividend declared to shareholders after the reporting date?","why":"Dividends have their own rule: no obligation existed at the reporting date, however much the profits “belong” to that year.","opts":[{"t":"Yes","to":"div"},{"t":"No","to":"cond"}]},"cond":{"q":"Does it give evidence of a condition that already existed at the reporting date?","why":"This is the heart of the standard: the timing of the **condition**, not of the event, decides.","opts":[{"t":"Yes: it was already true at year end, we just found out later","to":"adj"},{"t":"No: the condition arose after year end","to":"mat"}]},"mat":{"q":"Is it material?","why":"Non-adjusting events never change the numbers. Materiality only decides whether the notes must mention it.","opts":[{"t":"Yes","to":"nonD"},{"t":"No","to":"nonN"}]},"late":{"result":"Outside these FS","body":["Once the FS are authorised for issue, the window has closed. The event is dealt with in **next year’s** FS."]},"early":{"result":"Not an event after the reporting period","body":["It happened during the year, so it is an ordinary transaction of that year: record it in the normal way."]},"nogc":{"result":"Don’t use the going concern basis","body":["The one post-year-end event that changes the **whole basis** of the FS, not just one balance.","- Disclose that the FS are not on a going concern basis, the basis used, and why."]},"div":{"result":"Not a liability: disclose in the notes","body":["No obligation existed at the reporting date, so there is no {l|Dividend payable} and no {x|expense}.","- Disclose the dividend in the notes. It becomes a {l|liability} in the year it is declared."]},"adj":{"result":"Adjusting event: change the amounts","body":["The event is better evidence about a balance that existed at the reporting date, so update that balance.","- e.g. impair the {a|receivable}, write {a|inventory} down to NRV, adjust the {l|provision}."]},"nonD":{"result":"Non-adjusting: disclose, don’t adjust","body":["Leave the year-end amounts alone. In the notes give the event’s **nature** and an **estimate of its financial effect** (or say that no estimate can be made)."]},"nonN":{"result":"Non-adjusting and immaterial: nothing needed","body":["No adjustment, and too small to need a note."]}},"sect":3,"part":"Non-adjusting events","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:640px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 707.00 530.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 519.22)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-519.22 696.2,-519.22 696.2,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>w\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#b45309\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M561.28,-508.42C561.28,-508.42 430,-508.42 430,-508.42 424,-508.42 418,-502.42 418,-496.42 418,-496.42 418,-484.42 418,-484.42 418,-478.42 424,-472.42 430,-472.42 430,-472.42 561.28,-472.42 561.28,-472.42 567.28,-472.42 573.28,-478.42 573.28,-484.42 573.28,-484.42 573.28,-496.42 573.28,-496.42 573.28,-502.42 567.28,-508.42 561.28,-508.42\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"495.64\" y=\"-485.97\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">When did the event happen?\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node2\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>gc\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#b45309\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M415.15,-412.67C415.15,-412.67 292.12,-412.67 292.12,-412.67 286.12,-412.67 280.12,-406.67 280.12,-400.67 280.12,-400.67 280.12,-368.03 280.12,-368.03 280.12,-362.03 286.12,-356.03 292.12,-356.03 292.12,-356.03 415.15,-356.03 415.15,-356.03 421.15,-356.03 427.15,-362.03 427.15,-36