urt case \u003cstrong>settles\u003c/strong>, confirming an obligation at year end\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cstrong>Adjusting\u003c/strong>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Confirms the present \u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">obligation\u003c/span>\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>A customer goes \u003cstrong>bankrupt\u003c/strong>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cstrong>Adjusting\u003c/strong>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">Receivable\u003c/span> usually already impaired\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>Year-end \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">inventory\u003c/span> \u003cstrong>sold below cost\u003c/strong>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cstrong>Adjusting\u003c/strong>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Evidence of NRV at year end\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003cstrong>Cost or proceeds\u003c/strong> of a pre-year-end purchase or sale finalised\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cstrong>Adjusting\u003c/strong>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>The transaction was before year end\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003cstrong>Bonus\u003c/strong> for the year determined\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cstrong>Adjusting\u003c/strong>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>The \u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">obligation\u003c/span> existed at year end\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003cstrong>Fraud or error\u003c/strong> discovered\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cstrong>Adjusting\u003c/strong>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>The FS were wrong at year end\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003cstrong>Market value\u003c/strong> of \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">investments\u003c/span> falls\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Non-adjusting\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Conditions after year end\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003cstrong>Fire or flood\u003c/strong>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Non-adjusting\u003c/td>\u003ctd>The damage happened after year end\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>Major \u003cstrong>acquisition\u003c/strong> or disposal of a subsidiary\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Non-adjusting\u003c/td>\u003ctd>A new transaction\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003cstrong>Restructuring\u003c/strong> announced\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Non-adjusting\u003c/td>\u003ctd>No \u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">obligation\u003c/span> at year end\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>Large \u003cstrong>share issue\u003c/strong> or buy-back\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Non-adjusting\u003c/td>\u003ctd>A new \u003cspan class=\"el el-e\">equity\u003c/span> transaction\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003cstrong>Tax rates or laws\u003c/strong> change\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Non-adjusting\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Use the rates enacted at year end\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003cstrong>Dividends declared\u003c/strong> for the year\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Non-adjusting\u003c/td>\u003ctd>No \u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">obligation\u003c/span> at year end\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n    \u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\u003c/div>\n    \u003cp class=\"cap\">Tap to reveal row by row. Cover the middle column and test yourself first.\u003c/p>","sect":3,"part":"Non-adjusting events"},{"id":"mcq-hk0in1","type":"mcq","bucket":"nonadj","lo":52,"q":"A company’s year ends 31 December 20X5 and its {l|deferred tax liability} is measured at the 17% rate enacted at that date. On 20 February 20X6, before the FS are authorised, the government enacts a cut in the rate to 15%. How is the {l|deferred tax liability} measured at 31 December 20X5?","options":[{"t":"At 15%, because the new rate is known before the FS are authorised","why":"The rate change happened after year end: a non-adjusting event. Use the rate enacted (or substantively enacted) at the reporting date."},{"t":"At 17%, with the rate change disclosed if its effect is material","ok":true,"why":"Tax rate changes after the reporting date are non-adjusting. Measure at the year-end rate and disclose the change."},{"t":"At the average of 17% and 15%","why":"There is no averaging. The year-end enacted rate applies."},{"t":"At 17%, and no disclosure is ever needed for tax changes","why":"A material non-adjusting event must be disclosed, with its estimated effect."}],"sect":3,"part":"Non-adjusting events"},{"type":"mcq","bucket":"nonadj","lo":52,"q":"On 10 February 20X6 the board of Pasir Panjang Ltd (year end 31 December 20X5) approves and announces a plan to close its Tuas factory. Nothing had been decided or communicated before year end. How does this affect the 20X5 FS?","options":[{"t":"Recognise a {l|restructuring provision} at 31 December 20X5","why":"There was no obligation at 31 December: the plan was only approved and announced in February."},{"t":"Recognise the closure costs as an {x|expense} in 20X5 but no {l|provision}","why":"No obligation at year end means nothing is recognised in 20X5, as a provision or otherwise."},{"t":"No adjustment; disclose the restructuring if material","ok":true,"why":"A restructuring announced after year end is non-adjusting. Disclose its nature and estimated financial effect."},{"t":"No adjustment and no disclosure, because it relates to 20X6","why":"If material, a non-adjusting event must be disclosed."}],"id":"mcq-1g0w2u","sect":3,"part":"Non-adjusting events"},{"type":"map","id":"map-4-dividends","bucket":"dividends","sect":4,"part":"Dividends declared after year end"},{"id":"think-zm726a","type":"think","bucket":"dividends","lo":52,"scenario":"Marina Ltd’s year ends 31 December 20X5. On 20 February 20X6 the board declares a final dividend of 6 cents a share on its 8,000,000 shares, “out of the 20X5 profits”. The FS are authorised on 15 March 20X6 and the dividend is paid on 10 May 20X6.","prompt":"The dividend is “for” 20X5. Should Marina show a $480,000 {l|liability} at 31 December 20X5?","answer":["No. At 31 December nobody had declared anything, so Marina had **no obligation** to pay. No obligation, no {l|liability}.","Labelling it “for 20X5” doesn’t travel back in time. It is a **non-adjusting** event: disclose it in the notes.","And never as an {x|expense}: a dividend is a distribution to owners, so when it is recognised (in 20X6) it comes out of {e|Retained earnings}, not profit."],"sect":4,"part":"Dividends declared after year end"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"dividends","lo":52,"title":"Dividends declared after the reporting date","body":["Dividends get their own rule because they feel as if they belong to the year whose profits pay them. The test is the same as ever: was there an {l|obligation} at the reporting date?","- If dividends are declared **after** the reporting date, **don’t** recognise them as a {l|liability} at the reporting date: no obligation existed then.","- **Disclose** them in the notes.","- They are recognised as a {l|liability} in the period they are **declared**:","> Dr {e|Retained earnings} / Cr {l|Dividend payable}","! Two wrong turns the exam loves: recording a {l|Dividend payable} at year end, and putting the dividend through **profit or loss** as an {x|expense}. A dividend never touches P&L."],"id":"rule-1g4bod","sect":4,"part":"Dividends declared after year end"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"dividends","lo":52,"title":"Marina’s dividend on a timeline","intro":"Follow the dividend from declaration to payment, and see which year’s FS carry what.","notes":{"ye":"At the reporting date no dividend had been declared, so there was no obligation.","dec":"6 cents × 8,000,000 shares = 480,000. The {l|obligation} arises **today**, in 20X6.","au":"The declaration was inside the window, so the 20X5 FS must deal with it, by disclosure.","pay":"Payment settles the 20X6 {l|liability}: Dr {l|Dividend payable} / Cr {a|Cash}.","n5":"The 20X5 notes disclose the 480,000 dividend. No {l|liability}, no {x|expense}.","n6":"Recognised in 20X6 when declared, straight against {e|Retained earnings}: shown in the statement of changes in equity, never P&L."},"walk":[{"nodes":["ye"],"text":"At 31 December: nothing declared, so nothing owed."},{"nodes":["dec","au"],"text":"The board declares in February, inside the window."},{"nodes":["n5"],"text":"The 20X5 FS **disclose** it in the notes: a non-adjusting event."},{"nodes":["n6","pay"],"text":"The {l|liability} belongs to **20X6**, debited to {e|retained earnings}, and settled in May."}],"caption":"Declared after year end: a note in 20X5, a liability in 20X6.","id":"diagram-9et88u","sect":4,"part":"Dividends declared after year end","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:640px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 590.00 189.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 178.62)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-178.62 579.17,-178.62 579.17,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>ye\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M88.53,-106.64C88.53,-106.64 12,-106.64 12,-106.64 6,-106.64 0,-100.64 0,-94.64 0,-94.64 0,-79 0,-79 0,-73 6,-67 12,-67 12,-67 88.53,-67 88.53,-67 94.53,-67 100.53,-73 100.53,-79 100.53,-79 100.53,-94.64 100.53,-94.64 100.53,-100.64 94.53,-106.64 88.53,-106.64\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"18.39\" y=\"-92.87\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"white\">31 Dec 20X5\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"16.89\" y=\"-81.87\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"white\">reporting date\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"8.64\" y=\"-72.77\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"white\">nothing declared yet\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node2\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>dec\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#e8eef6\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M237.81,-106.64C237.81,-106.64 139.53,-106.64 139.53,-106.64 133.53,-106.64 127.53,-100.64 127.53,-