node\">\n\u003ctitle>pres\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#f3f4f6\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,2\" d=\"M310.98,-36C310.98,-36 197.12,-36 197.12,-36 191.12,-36 185.12,-30 185.12,-24 185.12,-24 185.12,-12 185.12,-12 185.12,-6 191.12,0 197.12,0 197.12,0 310.98,0 310.98,0 316.98,0 322.98,-6 322.98,-12 322.98,-12 322.98,-24 322.98,-24 322.98,-30 316.98,-36 310.98,-36\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"195.93\" y=\"-18.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Presentation currency\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"227.8\" y=\"-9.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">a free choice\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge8\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>fc&#45;&gt;pres\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,2\" d=\"M254.05,-72.27C254.05,-63.9 254.05,-53.79 254.05,-44.63\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"256.5,-44.75 254.05,-37.75 251.6,-44.75 256.5,-44.75\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"middle\" x=\"281.05\" y=\"-50.75\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"10.00\" fill=\"#374151\"> may print in\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"type":"mcq","bucket":"functional","lo":55,"q":"Which of these is a **primary** indicator of an entity’s functional currency?","options":[{"t":"The currency in which it issues its {l|bonds}","why":"Financing is a secondary indicator, used only when the primary ones are mixed."},{"t":"The currency that mainly influences its {x|labour and material costs}","ok":true,"why":"Costs are one of the primary indicators, alongside sales prices and the market forces behind them."},{"t":"The currency in which it keeps its {a|operating receipts}","why":"Retained receipts are a secondary indicator."},{"t":"The currency of the country where it is listed","why":"Not an indicator at all. Listing or incorporation doesn’t set the economic environment."}],"id":"mcq-3l6fzh","sect":1,"part":"Functional currency"},{"type":"mcq","bucket":"functional","lo":55,"q":"Merlion Bunkers (functional currency US$) wants its financial statements in S$ for its Singapore investors. Can it do that?","options":[{"t":"No: statements must be in the functional currency","why":"The functional currency is fixed by the facts, but the presentation currency can be chosen."},{"t":"Yes: the presentation currency is a choice, separate from the functional currency","ok":true,"why":"It records transactions in US$ (functional) and may present in S$. Translating to a presentation currency is outside this LO; just know the two are different."},{"t":"Yes, by changing its functional currency to S$","why":"The functional currency changes only when the underlying conditions change, not by choice."},{"t":"Only if its shareholders vote for S$","why":"Shareholders’ preference is not an indicator, and the presentation currency needs no vote in the standard."}],"id":"mcq-1zcpy9","sect":1,"part":"Functional currency"},{"type":"map","id":"map-2-initial","bucket":"initial","sect":2,"part":"Day 1: spot rate"},{"type":"think","bucket":"initial","lo":56,"scenario":"Orchid Trading Pte Ltd (functional currency S$) imports kitchenware. On 1 March it buys goods from a US supplier for US$10,000 on credit. That day US$1 = S$1.36.","prompt":"Orchid’s ledger is in S$. What goes into it on 1 March, and at what rate?","answer":["Translate at the **spot rate on the transaction date**: US$10,000 × 1.36 = **S$13,600**.","Dr {a|Inventory} 13,600, Cr {l|Trade payable} 13,600. Both sides use the same rate, so day 1 never has an exchange difference.","What happens when the rate moves before Orchid pays? Hold that thought."],"id":"think-1ogj1v","sect":2,"part":"Day 1: spot rate"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"initial","lo":56,"title":"Initial recognition","body":["Orchid’s ledger only speaks S$, so every foreign invoice must be converted on day 1. This is the first of three dates in a transaction’s life, and the simplest one.","- Record a foreign currency transaction in the functional currency at the **spot rate on the transaction date**.","- An **average rate** for a week or month may be used if exchange rates don’t fluctuate significantly.","- Applies to every type: purchases, {i|sales}, {l|borrowings}, buying {a|PPE}, paying {x|expenses}.","! Not the closing rate, and not the rate on the day you pay. Those come later, and only for some items."],"id":"rule-dw0oos","sect":2,"part":"Day 1: spot rate"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"initial","lo":56,"title":"Three dates, three rates","intro":"Every foreign currency transaction lives on this timeline. The exchange differences pop out at the second and third boxes.","notes":{"t":"Translate at the spot rate on the date of the transaction. An average rate for a week or month is fine if rates don’t move much.","y":"Only items that will be settled in a fixed number of currency units ({l|payables}, {a|receivables}, {l|loans}, {a|cash}) are retranslated, at the closing rate.","s":"The {a|cash} actually paid or received, converted at the spot rate on the settlement day.","d1":"The {l|payable} or {a|receivable} moves to the closing rate; the change is an {i|exchange gain} or {x|loss} in profit or loss.","d2":"{a|Cash} paid or received minus the S$ carrying amount of the {l|payable} or {a|receivable}: another {i|gain} or {x|loss} in profit or loss."},"walk":[{"nodes":["t"],"text":"Day 1: record the transaction in S$ at the spot rate. {a|Inventory} and {l|payable} go in at the same amount."},{"nodes":["y","d1"],"text":"If a year end comes before payment, retranslate the monetary item at the closing rate. The difference goes to P&L."},{"nodes":["s","d2"],"text":"On settlement, the {a|cash} is whatever it is on the day. The gap with the {l|payable}’s {l|carrying amount} goes to P&L."},{"nodes":["t","s"],"text":"Paid before any year end? Skip the middle box: one difference, on settlement."}],"id":"diagram-fr8we6","sect":2,"part":"Day 1: spot rate","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:614px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 558.00 178.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(14.4 163.64)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-14.4,14.4 -14.4,-163.64 544,-163.64 544,14.4 -14.4,14.4\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>t\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M113.85,-108.08C113.85,-108.08 12,-108.08 12,-108.08 6,-108.08 0,-102.08 0,-96.08 0,-96.08 0,-81 0,-81 0,-75 6,-69 12,-69 12,-69 113.85,-69 113.85,-69 119.85,-69 125.85,-75 125.85,-81 125.85,-81 125.85,-96.08 125.85,-96.08 125.85,-102.08 119.85,-108.08 113.85,-108.08\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"19.43\" y=\"-93.59\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"white\">Transaction date\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"21.68\" y=\"-84.49\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"white\">spot rate on that day\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"10.8\" y=\"-75.49\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"white\">both sides recorded in S$\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node2\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>y\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#b45309\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M322.23,-108.08C322.23,-108.08 201.62,-108.08 201.62,-108.08 195.62,-108.08 189.62,-102.08 189.62,-96.08 189.62,-96.08 189.62,-81 189.62,-81 189.62,-75 195.62,-69 201.62,-69 201.62,-69 322.23,-69 322.23,-69 328.23,-69 334.23,-75 334.23,-81 334.23,-81 334.23,-96.08 334.23,-96.08 33