\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node5\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>d2\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#b45309\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M517.6,-36C517.6,-36 408.25,-36 408.25,-36 402.25,-36 396.25,-30 396.25,-24 396.25,-24 396.25,-12 396.25,-12 396.25,-6 402.25,0 408.25,0 408.25,0 517.6,0 517.6,0 523.6,0 529.6,-6 529.6,-12 529.6,-12 529.6,-24 529.6,-24 529.6,-30 523.6,-36 517.6,-36\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"407.05\" y=\"-18.55\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11.00\" fill=\"#111827\">Settlement difference\u003c/text>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"448.68\" y=\"-9.45\" font-family=\"Helvetica,sans-Serif\" font-size=\"9.00\" fill=\"#111827\">→ P&amp;L\u003c/text>\n\u003c/g>\n\n\u003cg id=\"edge5\" class=\"edge\">\n\u003ctitle>s&#45;&gt;d2\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,2\" d=\"M462.93,-70.24C462.93,-62.59 462.93,-53.43 462.93,-44.98\"/>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"#6b7280\" stroke=\"#6b7280\" points=\"465.38,-45.04 462.93,-38.04 460.48,-45.04 465.38,-45.04\"/>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\n"},{"id":"je-8vlanr","type":"je","bucket":"initial","lo":56,"q":"On 1 March Orchid Trading Pte Ltd (functional currency S$) buys goods from a US supplier for US$10,000 on credit. That day US$1 = S$1.36. Record the purchase.","accounts":["Inventory","Trade payable","Cash","Foreign exchange gain","Foreign exchange loss","Revaluation surplus (OCI)","Cost of sales","Loan payable"],"lines":[{"side":"Dr","account":"Inventory","amount":13600},{"side":"Cr","account":"Trade payable","amount":13600}],"why":"US$10,000 × 1.36 = S$13,600 on both sides. No exchange difference on day 1.","sect":2,"part":"Day 1: spot rate"},{"id":"calc-vrus58","type":"calc","bucket":"initial","lo":56,"unit":"$","q":"Orchid Trading (functional currency S$) sells goods to a Johor restaurant for RM50,000 on credit on 10 June, when RM1 = S$0.29. By 30 June, RM1 = S$0.30. What {i|revenue} does Orchid record for the sale (in S$)?","answer":14500,"working":["{i|Revenue} is translated at the spot rate on the **transaction date**: RM50,000 × 0.29 = S$14,500.","The 30 June rate is irrelevant to {i|revenue}. If it matters at all, it is for retranslating the {a|Trade receivable} at a reporting date."],"sect":2,"part":"Day 1: spot rate"},{"id":"mcq-btos40","type":"mcq","bucket":"initial","lo":56,"q":"Orchid Trading (functional currency S$) makes about 200 small US$ {i|sales} a month. The US$/S$ rate barely moved all month. Which rate may it use to record them?","options":[{"t":"The closing rate at the year end","why":"The closing rate is for retranslating monetary items at the reporting date, not for recording transactions."},{"t":"The rate on the date each invoice is paid","why":"Settlement is a later event. The sale is recorded when it happens."},{"t":"An average rate for the month","ok":true,"why":"Allowed as a practical shortcut when rates don’t fluctuate significantly."},{"t":"The rate on the first day of the financial year","why":"An out-of-date rate. Only a spot rate, or an average that approximates it, will do."}],"sect":2,"part":"Day 1: spot rate"},{"type":"map","id":"map-3-yearend","bucket":"yearend","sect":3,"part":"Year end: monetary or not?"},{"id":"think-tskxr0","type":"think","bucket":"yearend","lo":56,"scenario":"At its year end, Orchid Trading (functional currency S$) has: (a) an {l|unpaid US$ invoice}, (b) {a|US$ in a bank account}, (c) {a|kitchenware} bought in US$ still in the warehouse, (d) a {a|delivery van} bought in US$ last year. The S$ has moved since all of these were recorded.","prompt":"Which of these are now “worth” a different number of S$, and which aren’t? What is the difference between the two groups?","answer":["(a) and (b) are a fixed number of **US dollars** to pay or to receive. When the rate moves, their S$ value really changes. Retranslate them.","(c) and (d) are **things**. Orchid will never settle them in a fixed number of dollars; their S$ cost was fixed on the day they were bought. Leave them.","That is the whole chapter in one line: **monetary** items move with the rate, **non-monetary** items don’t."],"sect":3,"part":"Year end: monetary or not?"},{"type":"rule","bucket":"yearend","lo":56,"title":"Monetary items, and what happens at each reporting date","body":["Day 1 is done; now a year end arrives before anything is settled. The S$ has moved, and the last page asked which balances should move with it. One definition sorts them.","**Monetary** = a right to receive, or an obligation to pay, a **fixed or determinable number of currency units**.","At each reporting date:","1. **Monetary items** → retranslate at the **closing rate**. The difference goes to profit or loss.","2. **Non-monetary items at historical cost** → keep the **historical** (transaction-date) rate. No retranslation.","3. **Non-monetary items at fair value** → the rate on the **date fair value was measured**.","! {a|Prepayments} and {l|advances} are **non-monetary**: you will receive or deliver goods or services, not {a|cash}. {a|Equity shares} are non-monetary too, even though they are {a|financial assets}."],"id":"rule-x3d6ne","sect":3,"part":"Year end: monetary or not?"},{"id":"visual-1cx9uw","type":"visual","bucket":"yearend","lo":56,"title":"Monetary or non-monetary?","html":"\u003cp>The definition in practice: the usual suspects on each side. The tricky ones are \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">deposits\u003c/span>, \u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">advances\u003c/span> and \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">shares\u003c/span>, which look like money but aren’t a fixed number of dollars.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"tbl-wrap\">\u003ctable class=\"tbl reveal-rows\">\u003cthead>\u003ctr>\u003cth>Monetary (closing rate)\u003c/th>\u003cth>Non-monetary (historical, or FV-date rate)\u003c/th>\u003c/tr>\u003c/thead>\u003ctbody>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">Cash and bank balances\u003c/span>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">Property, plant and equipment\u003c/span>\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">Trade receivable\u003c/span>s and \u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">trade payable\u003c/span>s\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">Inventory\u003c/span>\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">Loans and borrowings\u003c/span>, \u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">bonds\u003c/span>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">Prepayment\u003c/span>s for goods and services\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">Provisions\u003c/span> settled in cash\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">Advances received\u003c/span> for goods (\u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">contract liability\u003c/span>)\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">Lease liabilities\u003c/span>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">Intangible assets\u003c/span>, \u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">goodwill\u003c/span>\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n      \u003ctr>\u003ctd>Accrued \u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">interest payable\u003c/span>, \u003cspan class=\"el el-l\">dividends payable\u003c/span>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003cspan class=\"el el-a\">Investments in equity shares\u003c/span>\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n    \u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\u003c/div>\n    \u003cp class=\"cap\">Test: will it be settled by a \u003cstrong>fixed or determinable number of currency units\u003c/strong>? Yes → monetary.\u003c/p>","sect":3,"part":"Year end: monetary or not?"},{"type":"diagram","bucket":"yearend","lo":56,"title":"Which rate at the year end? The chart","intro":"The chart from your notes. One question at the top decides almost everything: is it monetary?","notes":{"init":"Everything starts at the spot rate on the transaction date.","rep":"Monetary = a right to receive, or an obligation to pay, a fixed or determinable number of currency units.","mon":"Retranslate at the closing rate. The difference goes to P&L, every year, until it is settled.","basis":"Non-monetary items ask a second question: how is the item measured?","hist":"At cost: frozen at the historical rate. No retranslation, no exchange difference.","fv":"At fair value: the rate on the date fair value was measured. The FX part follows the item’s own gain: OCI or P&L."},"walk":[{"nodes":["init"],"text":"Start: every item went in at the spot rate on its transaction date."},{"nodes":["rep","mon"],"text":"Monetary items ({a|cash}, {a|receivables}, {l|payables}, {l|loans}) move to the closing rate. Difference → P&L."},{"nodes":["basis","hist"],"text":"Non-monetary at cost ({a|PPE}, {a|inventory}, {a|prepayments}) stays at the historical rate."},{"nodes":["fv"],"text":"Non-monetary at fair value uses the rate on the valuation date, and the FX tags along with the fair value gain."}],"id":"diagram-dmu0fl","sect":3,"part":"Year end: monetary or not?","svg":"\u003csvg width=\"100%\" style=\"min-width:589px\" role=\"img\"\n viewBox=\"0.00 0.00 535.00 273.00\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\u003cg id=\"graph0\" class=\"graph\" transform=\"scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(10.8 261.96)\">\n\u003ctitle>G\u003c/title>\n\u003cpolygon fill=\"white\" stroke=\"none\" points=\"-10.8,10.8 -10.8,-261.96 524.02,-261.96 524.02,10.8 -10.8,10.8\"/>\n\n\u003cg id=\"node1\" class=\"node\">\n\u003ctitle>init\u003c/title>\n\u003cpath fill=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" d=\"M187.98,-251.16C187.98,-251.16 34.38,-251.16 34.38,-251.16 28.38,-251.16 22.38,-245.16 22.38,-239.16 22.38,-239.16 22.38,-227.16 22.38,-227.16 22.38,-221.16 28.38,-215.16 34.38,-215.16 34.38,-215.16 187.98,-215.16 187.98,-215.16 193.98,-215.16 199.98,-221.16 199.98,-227.16 199.98,-227.16 199.98,-239.16 199.98,-239.16 199.98,-245.16 193.98,-251.16 187.98,-251.16\"/>\n\u003ctext xml:space=\"preserve\" text-anchor=\"start\" x=\"35.0